[{"sha":"954e2878bbd735839c13a5e4e7bd45c74648f549","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk1NGUyODc4YmJkNzM1ODM5YzEzYTVlNGU3YmQ0NWM3NDY0OGY1NDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-06T01:01:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-06T01:01:20Z"},"message":"[codex] Send Responses Lite transport header (#26542)\n\n## Summary\n\n- send `X-OpenAI-Internal-Codex-Responses-Lite: true` on HTTP Responses\nrequests and WebSocket upgrade requests when model metadata enables\nResponses Lite\n- use client metadata when sending it over the websocket\n\nThis PR is stacked on #26490.\n\n## Why\n\nThe Responses Lite marker is request-scoped for HTTP but\nconnection-scoped for Responses-over-WebSocket because it is carried on\nthe upgrade request. Reusing a cached socket opened for the opposite\nmode would therefore send the wrong transport contract.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core responses_lite`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresponses_websocket_reconnects_when_responses_lite_mode_changes`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"12d88fa3056fa093982ab480b5845af65feef8a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/12d88fa3056fa093982ab480b5845af65feef8a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/954e2878bbd735839c13a5e4e7bd45c74648f549","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqI3FgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAztoQADmV7oi4hKxfRTnBa2QyE/hE\nlp0Tgfbww7FLK5L8Gw/N4DscZDreByfOCwiS10L+4dJ3A+XJU42HydzY8lCN+Ddj\ni88s8DgFAKMg/zuxdlEY3bZ7lvU7YP3kI27OwM7gYVxm/nYLNqCDA3PFgoEVVlhZ\nWvrw/TseWfXOyq/83DZijz0/xZROc9NCzNAPXetQsplzXvR56JrnJqE8iopghqN1\n/uOm7jQ5LhBQ7NA4BG5knrrFukxtxtMWyRPzFYjcN8IVA+3mZKaQf3l6MMZ5sL8L\nzA3QSl4AzBN6nTF7JhWMu6qaYVQ6pbz1H7MwxyUr/uZi2NbKwlac4uV9BwLmUxCr\nn82Jk0vtifn9IYs34e3oBhSLTodSHwXpFPekaJ2R/OvRHldqTsLtssaMTJbnJRHT\nO7MTePd7zSdYe7JmfMGzM7gp592RWwhwtwPXHH8sv3YMRvLRJ3bEqNCvxRLud0YN\n+rnoCilXx6lVi/8dG2v/SZlOHkqRT8OhPw08nwZ7/U0W6VPZJIRHZwFUVmgfyRgO\nqIlpvyc1eGwATtzF59zof+ydT3a41zSCrSaIe1143UvUXfK3E/asi3zLm6q+Rd9u\nAv8KUkVKohwD1/Ge2rrlMElXmvMThPWjU2uZoVii/TSVsJ5eOc/DikZGgolV88BL\nSpkksHIpQJRLmZBSVcCx\n=H2Zs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 12d88fa3056fa093982ab480b5845af65feef8a7\nparent df7818c7d138ad081f5bd1fa584646c116da7022\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1780707680 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780707680 +0000\n\n[codex] Send Responses Lite transport header (#26542)\n\n## Summary\n\n- send `X-OpenAI-Internal-Codex-Responses-Lite: true` on HTTP Responses\nrequests and WebSocket upgrade requests when model metadata enables\nResponses Lite\n- use client metadata when sending it over the websocket\n\nThis PR is stacked on #26490.\n\n## Why\n\nThe Responses Lite marker is request-scoped for HTTP but\nconnection-scoped for Responses-over-WebSocket because it is carried on\nthe upgrade request. Reusing a cached socket opened for the opposite\nmode would therefore send the wrong transport contract.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core responses_lite`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nresponses_websocket_reconnects_when_responses_lite_mode_changes`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-06T01:01:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/954e2878bbd735839c13a5e4e7bd45c74648f549","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/954e2878bbd735839c13a5e4e7bd45c74648f549","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/954e2878bbd735839c13a5e4e7bd45c74648f549/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"df7818c7d138ad081f5bd1fa584646c116da7022","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df7818c7d138ad081f5bd1fa584646c116da7022","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/df7818c7d138ad081f5bd1fa584646c116da7022"}]},{"sha":"df7818c7d138ad081f5bd1fa584646c116da7022","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRmNzgxOGM3ZDEzOGFkMDgxZjViZDFmYTU4NDY0NmMxMTZkYTcwMjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"cooper-oai","email":"cooper@openai.com","date":"2026-06-06T00:36:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-06T00:36:18Z"},"message":"[codex-rs] support v2 personal access tokens (#25731)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add v2 personal access token support for `codex login\n--with-access-token` and `CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN`\n- classify opaque `at-` tokens separately from legacy Agent Identity\nJWTs\n- hydrate required ChatGPT account metadata through AuthAPI\n`/v1/user-auth-credential/whoami`\n- use PATs directly as bearer tokens while preserving existing ChatGPT\naccount surfaces\n- expose PAT-backed auth as the explicit `personalAccessToken`\napp-server auth mode\n\n## Implementation\n\nPAT auth is intentionally small and stateless. Loading a PAT performs\none AuthAPI metadata request, stores the hydrated metadata in the\nin-memory auth object, and redacts the secret from debug output. Legacy\nAgent Identity JWT handling remains unchanged. The shared access-token\nclassifier lives in a private neutral module because it dispatches\nbetween both credential types.\n\nPAT hydration fails closed when AuthAPI omits any required metadata,\nincluding email. Hydrated metadata is intentionally not persisted:\nstartup performs a live `whoami` preflight so revoked tokens or changed\naccount metadata are not accepted from a stale cache.\n\n## Workspace restriction scope\n\nThis change intentionally does **not** apply\n`forced_chatgpt_workspace_id` to PAT authentication. The setting is a\nclient-side config guardrail, not an authorization boundary, and PAT\ndoes not currently require workspace-ID parity. The PAT login and\n`CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN` paths therefore validate through AuthAPI without\nthreading workspace-restriction state through access-token loading.\nExisting workspace checks for non-PAT auth remain on their established\npaths.\n\n## App-server compatibility\n\nThe public app-server `AuthMode` is shared across v1 and v2, and\nPAT-backed auth reports `personalAccessToken` through both APIs.\nFollowing human review, this intentionally removes the temporary v1\ncompatibility mapping that reported PATs as `chatgpt`; the deprecated v1\nAPI is kept in parity with v2 rather than maintaining a separate closed\nenum. Clients with exhaustive auth-mode handling in either API version\nmust add the new case and should generally treat it as ChatGPT-backed\nunless they need PAT-specific behavior.\n\nThe v1 auth-status response still omits the raw PAT when `includeToken`\nis requested because that response cannot carry the account metadata\nneeded to reuse the credential safely. Persisted PAT auth also omits the\nnew enum value so older Codex builds can deserialize `auth.json` and\ninfer PAT auth from the credential field after a rollback.\n\n## Validation\n\nLatest review-fix validation:\n\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-login` (126 passed)\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-cli` (263 passed)\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-cli\nstored_auth_validation_handles_personal_access_token`\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-app-server-protocol` (226\npassed)\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-models-manager\nrefresh_available_models_uses_remote_only_catalog_for_chatgpt_auth`\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-tui\nexisting_non_oauth_chatgpt_login_counts_as_signed_in`\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just fix -p codex-login -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol -p codex-models-manager -p codex-tui -p\ncodex-cli`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe broader `codex-tui` suite previously compiled and ran 2,834 tests.\nThree unrelated environment-sensitive guardian/IDE-socket tests failed\nafter retries; the PAT-relevant TUI coverage passed.","tree":{"sha":"66932118d4fc7bf5d25e2d4b36dde9a6701f5c3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/66932118d4fc7bf5d25e2d4b36dde9a6701f5c3a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/df7818c7d138ad081f5bd1fa584646c116da7022","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqI2uCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1SYQAJOa3/dE8fMhICE9auTkVYJi\nWM/JVt3ph6PURsMgGnULyLWjwC3jUvGlzdaW86wMQYDbzL0NqAiut3f9UhbRGnYw\nOK89K9nYySuZTu2gZVqGgRs4iFcZF6C7/D3lbGFgAOiPtpOcSXQ7kq/RjDh9ocGW\nsYbLdWbHsryLtXudzEjvtYsplcg+NXtpTexOC3JWSbzxvolcm1hhOaa0FT9DIgC9\nxEY8joVukMt0AevOGzTXMn0dzyd91yP25Fif4pT99zbK5EdS6q1Q/lWVyALi4qty\nQNfY0kCqzIeMl0no55S7eQo7JB2W581q7/xjpLge4JujUTcOLf1ylLaoFS5gS3jZ\n91Dq2KpL340GJy8ICpfwWoWGcfxdHwr7ALD4KoES6NG3ey+405+hBNkpFZJa3kIu\n40gTbHEe1t7GBtFfkS/i1dDSiVYxUHcHaKR3LNCIg3SC4QYqMC+HH9h/67rmX9W2\n7p6BqmBeTO/B5zuIIDhpUgMUhxtyvHwIuQAB/b0K2RJHpIAcma5VRYcJ/Xh1Vga0\nJ4Epm9dulPCc1zli3y5EXenIGkAcOqQTS27nVuMFIFeDptOrV3VvdySkLcjA0TPz\nUeoQa1SLAFgy5R9qe341C9oX75jgAkqCALVnr9YSqzrEwepX95+U/UMPWlcruRRt\njwvt/hWn6D1b+otel766\n=vt9V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 66932118d4fc7bf5d25e2d4b36dde9a6701f5c3a\nparent 61a913d9c83928335b9503ad530caa9851bf5955\nauthor cooper-oai <cooper@openai.com> 1780706178 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780706178 -0700\n\n[codex-rs] support v2 personal access tokens (#25731)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add v2 personal access token support for `codex login\n--with-access-token` and `CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN`\n- classify opaque `at-` tokens separately from legacy Agent Identity\nJWTs\n- hydrate required ChatGPT account metadata through AuthAPI\n`/v1/user-auth-credential/whoami`\n- use PATs directly as bearer tokens while preserving existing ChatGPT\naccount surfaces\n- expose PAT-backed auth as the explicit `personalAccessToken`\napp-server auth mode\n\n## Implementation\n\nPAT auth is intentionally small and stateless. Loading a PAT performs\none AuthAPI metadata request, stores the hydrated metadata in the\nin-memory auth object, and redacts the secret from debug output. Legacy\nAgent Identity JWT handling remains unchanged. The shared access-token\nclassifier lives in a private neutral module because it dispatches\nbetween both credential types.\n\nPAT hydration fails closed when AuthAPI omits any required metadata,\nincluding email. Hydrated metadata is intentionally not persisted:\nstartup performs a live `whoami` preflight so revoked tokens or changed\naccount metadata are not accepted from a stale cache.\n\n## Workspace restriction scope\n\nThis change intentionally does **not** apply\n`forced_chatgpt_workspace_id` to PAT authentication. The setting is a\nclient-side config guardrail, not an authorization boundary, and PAT\ndoes not currently require workspace-ID parity. The PAT login and\n`CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN` paths therefore validate through AuthAPI without\nthreading workspace-restriction state through access-token loading.\nExisting workspace checks for non-PAT auth remain on their established\npaths.\n\n## App-server compatibility\n\nThe public app-server `AuthMode` is shared across v1 and v2, and\nPAT-backed auth reports `personalAccessToken` through both APIs.\nFollowing human review, this intentionally removes the temporary v1\ncompatibility mapping that reported PATs as `chatgpt`; the deprecated v1\nAPI is kept in parity with v2 rather than maintaining a separate closed\nenum. Clients with exhaustive auth-mode handling in either API version\nmust add the new case and should generally treat it as ChatGPT-backed\nunless they need PAT-specific behavior.\n\nThe v1 auth-status response still omits the raw PAT when `includeToken`\nis requested because that response cannot carry the account metadata\nneeded to reuse the credential safely. Persisted PAT auth also omits the\nnew enum value so older Codex builds can deserialize `auth.json` and\ninfer PAT auth from the credential field after a rollback.\n\n## Validation\n\nLatest review-fix validation:\n\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-login` (126 passed)\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-cli` (263 passed)\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-cli\nstored_auth_validation_handles_personal_access_token`\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-app-server-protocol` (226\npassed)\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-models-manager\nrefresh_available_models_uses_remote_only_catalog_for_chatgpt_auth`\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just test -p codex-tui\nexisting_non_oauth_chatgpt_login_counts_as_signed_in`\n- `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 just fix -p codex-login -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol -p codex-models-manager -p codex-tui -p\ncodex-cli`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nThe broader `codex-tui` suite previously compiled and ran 2,834 tests.\nThree unrelated environment-sensitive guardian/IDE-socket tests failed\nafter retries; the PAT-relevant TUI coverage passed.","verified_at":"2026-06-06T00:36:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df7818c7d138ad081f5bd1fa584646c116da7022","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/df7818c7d138ad081f5bd1fa584646c116da7022","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df7818c7d138ad081f5bd1fa584646c116da7022/comments","author":{"login":"cooper-oai","id":242064477,"node_id":"U_kgDODm2cXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/242064477?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/cooper-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cooper-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"61a913d9c83928335b9503ad530caa9851bf5955","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/61a913d9c83928335b9503ad530caa9851bf5955","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/61a913d9c83928335b9503ad530caa9851bf5955"}]},{"sha":"61a913d9c83928335b9503ad530caa9851bf5955","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYxYTkxM2Q5YzgzOTI4MzM1Yjk1MDNhZDUzMGNhYTk4NTFiZjU5NTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"vie-oai","email":"vie@openai.com","date":"2026-06-06T00:23:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-06T00:23:45Z"},"message":"[codex] Gate terminal visualization instructions in TUI (#26013)\n\n## Summary\n- add `Feature::TerminalVisualizationInstructions` as\n`UnderDevelopment`, disabled by default\n- keep terminal visualization instructions inside the TUI package\n- append them to existing developer instructions for TUI start, resume,\nand fork flows only when enabled\n- intentionally do not apply them to `codex exec`\n\n## Rollout\nControl behavior is unchanged. TUI dogfooders can enable\n`terminal_visualization_instructions`; no default user receives the new\nterminal-specific instructions.\n\nThe shared visualization-selection rule is supplied separately through\nthe `codex_proxy_model_3` Statsig layer for every target Codex model\nslug in the gated cohort. This TUI feature determines how to render an\nappropriate visualization on the terminal surface; the model-layer\ntreatment determines when to use one.\n\n## Validation\n- `cargo test -p codex-tui\nterminal_visualization_instructions_are_gated_for_all_tui_thread_flows\n--lib`\n- `cargo test -p codex-features --lib`\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\n- `git diff --check`\n- GPT-5.4 and GPT-5.5 real prompt-pipeline smoke tests: both visualized\nthe positive mapping case, abstained on the negative route case, and\npassed exact prompt-stack verification on CLI and App\n- refreshed onto current `main` with a clean merge and reran the focused\nvalidation\n\nThe full 53-probe all-model treatment comparison and requested\nproduction coding evals remain rollout gates before broadening beyond\nthe initial employee cohort.\n\nThis PR remains open for normal human review.","tree":{"sha":"9555e98ef4be133f162c63132e4199bfd5555289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9555e98ef4be133f162c63132e4199bfd5555289"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/61a913d9c83928335b9503ad530caa9851bf5955","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqI2iRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1nMQAB1HmE3G8UZmHWoySRRG076T\n+S8kYs5rQsQb+RR1NQMWoCmS0BfqlD6Lqrer1hhpZcDpfwDcuLOzbBDA/kMCBoda\n36e45UAI+8olsvOd6/TSPunVZVKwyd4J7R2AhsRSlsoHfR7PWsJFkapY7D43B15M\n3xY91Xnog+jKJNgmwgZ8mcQDn70ZR98HClERrFohtArkK8w6RVm9rHL4RKWmPseQ\nR+zxOZHEp6/b0TIcJHu/1hEokjiJz54jJ9QfBlnC5pAnpPCSxwNYEcGMolNb+Wcp\n+iVqiewm6NCCTq6sksPH3vBxdxJlozKO3Ra1i0CY8Jac+kjppcf08SlrrRTLZEop\nFs0n+9AttZHt7vcINQZT249vHOnJ7mul2tgrblvbOW7s0D9ZHFfiJfGDBBNVjqrR\nP9MV4O8ZGT2MGTGLGJJlDc1Yc4Hp7wxCugIhwxkL11sTUXIq3X/nDrx/OVaq0Zmj\ntLBWee9e7sloP++zZGGMGglzZX16QH+nngAA1sNi3JeLjDWnJx97+v0rMguaxC+Y\nAdxT/WsiJ/7V6P3jkyZOfEVbEMhSbPCja9rMzoiawRWTXKHI/30+kdOzTO4ypG3B\nhR2lcE96g3As0TWMMxP56exrN/FlVWWCAOfNnIYtzSUOhYicyuQ9V7mtHsWH638h\nMSmiAmtYnxFJ0Ac21pgm\n=AMF1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9555e98ef4be133f162c63132e4199bfd5555289\nparent ffe90cb5c37d4cf6ccfa9de0126a5ff61cb959e5\nauthor vie-oai <vie@openai.com> 1780705425 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780705425 -0700\n\n[codex] Gate terminal visualization instructions in TUI (#26013)\n\n## Summary\n- add `Feature::TerminalVisualizationInstructions` as\n`UnderDevelopment`, disabled by default\n- keep terminal visualization instructions inside the TUI package\n- append them to existing developer instructions for TUI start, resume,\nand fork flows only when enabled\n- intentionally do not apply them to `codex exec`\n\n## Rollout\nControl behavior is unchanged. TUI dogfooders can enable\n`terminal_visualization_instructions`; no default user receives the new\nterminal-specific instructions.\n\nThe shared visualization-selection rule is supplied separately through\nthe `codex_proxy_model_3` Statsig layer for every target Codex model\nslug in the gated cohort. This TUI feature determines how to render an\nappropriate visualization on the terminal surface; the model-layer\ntreatment determines when to use one.\n\n## Validation\n- `cargo test -p codex-tui\nterminal_visualization_instructions_are_gated_for_all_tui_thread_flows\n--lib`\n- `cargo test -p codex-features --lib`\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\n- `git diff --check`\n- GPT-5.4 and GPT-5.5 real prompt-pipeline smoke tests: both visualized\nthe positive mapping case, abstained on the negative route case, and\npassed exact prompt-stack verification on CLI and App\n- refreshed onto current `main` with a clean merge and reran the focused\nvalidation\n\nThe full 53-probe all-model treatment comparison and requested\nproduction coding evals remain rollout gates before broadening beyond\nthe initial employee cohort.\n\nThis PR remains open for normal human review.","verified_at":"2026-06-06T00:23:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/61a913d9c83928335b9503ad530caa9851bf5955","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/61a913d9c83928335b9503ad530caa9851bf5955","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/61a913d9c83928335b9503ad530caa9851bf5955/comments","author":{"login":"vie-oai","id":229210842,"node_id":"U_kgDODal62g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229210842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/vie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ffe90cb5c37d4cf6ccfa9de0126a5ff61cb959e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ffe90cb5c37d4cf6ccfa9de0126a5ff61cb959e5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ffe90cb5c37d4cf6ccfa9de0126a5ff61cb959e5"}]},{"sha":"ffe90cb5c37d4cf6ccfa9de0126a5ff61cb959e5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZmZTkwY2I1YzM3ZDRjZjZjY2ZhOWRlMDEyNmE1ZmY2MWNiOTU5ZTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-06T00:23:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-06T00:23:40Z"},"message":"[codex] Use standalone tools for Responses Lite (#26490)\n\n## Summary\n\nResponses Lite does not execute hosted Responses tools, so models using\nit must route web search and image generation through Codex-owned\nexecutors & standalone Response's API endpoints.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #26487.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-core responses_lite_ --lib`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nstandalone_executors_remain_hidden_without_flags_or_responses_lite\n--lib`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nhosted_tools_follow_provider_auth_model_and_config_gates --lib`\n- `cargo test -p codex-web-search-extension -p\ncodex-image-generation-extension`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server --test all standalone_`\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`","tree":{"sha":"df08792d0080822f29cdd44a3b0ce04ad826dc87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/df08792d0080822f29cdd44a3b0ce04ad826dc87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ffe90cb5c37d4cf6ccfa9de0126a5ff61cb959e5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqI2iMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtC0QAEDFrZRj8dcjrAFsJVoxPrto\n9Td04VAT4j3qJKKf7LPQWjXwK8ffFV1KuIQG7zeR8YIYMOJ1SIt8cWy/EGg3Fpos\n2ULqU5/senFOkFSUJh+3Rvv4txSuWGPrUl02m7Xvickx/E8nVVvehYquEt7PIRn4\nJnYOSuPKo/jVjsuLdKiv1CA74fD0RExjWGavYxryw1ulV9arAsIQVIPiP1QYlwwP\nqSbBMKgrxYO5ilLHVYdlvhgK6xZWdwWZq5bmFBFE6gPI3fupXSfW/jiS1TaYFL1o\nzYxhqCYLbWevKPpnlehaPlSq/UtE+atKORMHJrTRZ8nQucQhzzcRJpfqVzMpSyCf\n1pb+aKHadUTSJen05qh9oa9ZdlMW6L9fg12EVj/jK1u8Go6Bwv8VU4DpMeqpD2uu\ngpHaUcghVULOCATOkI5w/R/4wMFQos0bmq6p9vJNRJDzMw8wOeQo9OtUbHYkeKwQ\nCT9+Q1jzm9SvzhN49u9ArKwPTgTgVHiUs6TBxVCsuZxzvY0hQIEV/u0aLE86Kvxh\naHcOHhzXXsccZtVZtX3rmFZgwGMFGJ6W9xi/lzaZGyzKsbLadEp4iW01f/UZfu4N\nZn8dt5LxiZO0wlRRbblqPglQKDWf5+CpO8IGnm/aFt06dY9LDakpZ+L/G14ih+Zu\npWiK887acXBCKTSyrdV2\n=WUXi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree df08792d0080822f29cdd44a3b0ce04ad826dc87\nparent 4f655bc3b740bb1fec3744df4851f7eb1b95fbe9\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1780705420 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780705420 +0000\n\n[codex] Use standalone tools for Responses Lite (#26490)\n\n## Summary\n\nResponses Lite does not execute hosted Responses tools, so models using\nit must route web search and image generation through Codex-owned\nexecutors & standalone Response's API endpoints.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #26487.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-core responses_lite_ --lib`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nstandalone_executors_remain_hidden_without_flags_or_responses_lite\n--lib`\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nhosted_tools_follow_provider_auth_model_and_config_gates --lib`\n- `cargo test -p codex-web-search-extension -p\ncodex-image-generation-extension`\n- `cargo test -p codex-app-server --test all standalone_`\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-06T00:23:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ffe90cb5c37d4cf6ccfa9de0126a5ff61cb959e5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ffe90cb5c37d4cf6ccfa9de0126a5ff61cb959e5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ffe90cb5c37d4cf6ccfa9de0126a5ff61cb959e5/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4f655bc3b740bb1fec3744df4851f7eb1b95fbe9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4f655bc3b740bb1fec3744df4851f7eb1b95fbe9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4f655bc3b740bb1fec3744df4851f7eb1b95fbe9"}]},{"sha":"4f655bc3b740bb1fec3744df4851f7eb1b95fbe9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRmNjU1YmMzYjc0MGJiMWZlYzM3NDRkZjQ4NTFmN2ViMWI5NWZiZTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T23:33:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T23:33:01Z"},"message":"[codex] Remove legacy remote plugin startup sync (#25936)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Remove the legacy startup remote plugin sync path that called\n`/plugins/list` and reconciled curated plugin cache/config.\n- Remove the `sync_plugins_from_remote` API, its result/error types,\nstartup marker task, and tests that expected the legacy request.\n- Keep the current remote installed bundle sync and remote catalog flows\n(`/ps/plugins/installed` and `/ps/plugins/list`) intact.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `env HOME=/private/tmp/codex-xin-build-home\nUSERPROFILE=/private/tmp/codex-xin-build-home just test -p\ncodex-core-plugins`\n- Searched for legacy `/plugins/list` sync references; remaining matches\nare `/ps/plugins/list` catalog tests/code.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server plugin_list` is currently blocked\nbefore running filtered tests by an unrelated compile error in\n`app-server/tests/suite/v2/image_generation.rs`:\n`app_test_support::McpProcess` is not exported.","tree":{"sha":"53039569b1043799f3cc4a615c3303c6f51adc5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/53039569b1043799f3cc4a615c3303c6f51adc5f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4f655bc3b740bb1fec3744df4851f7eb1b95fbe9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqI1ytCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWl0QAI0342t3vPyxZti4Sk90kfkX\ngejNh6okBzccOhpFQ+e2LkVC4+PsY4O02NvTaf7GUbstXUB8hfBrNteINZdj7xLD\nOI+MmquD9EicPJfGSHQ9WBpB1aTe0xLrM1QjdN3VsUKm9fXlG/3W1ZE7xwMqOKh2\nL46fWsmOjtFwEeiAezgY2JmDXRDIi95Em6Dtim5kELxV5wKqF4RGfHlKQ+TUYqKH\ntXdc4/wjLE0LgY9ZmGZ3HS1k7hpQGUDCB5eF67eKjPBJurdfZ6nSp76HPpSFuWy9\nwg1qI44izQ6s1lWzFH81bbOvYHf/uDunYMLfkICs3ad69S8AGPGW1FtCQyk9huGc\niXMD7+IdnOOWutv04gsWXH/8B9C5duMN/knIlE6w1ScVyfU3nWYmwb/dK9DPaDFw\ndKoYblkQNUJYQJIOkjW0Et4wY/t9+VfHUuL4n4INe47CqzqhWjwaAe0RKzLG5Fic\npw/kLtSJ25gwLNNVYLQbPrxisntFvUFKqVoniRl9RGVABK0fyy2PCpqDowksQaIN\nXgZsc1TveLW4QRurlGdyOK9OAN87lgzGedLzpSN/UKzhFV7cyM/J3o1BLQ5nhv8E\nRBIupufB3jIBcWEQEmoi6IVH01jW6fv+PGXrBaLnhMA+IGXe3YM2eg4XhHi+0+Uz\nbqL49niNhoQ1f+oJkCrw\n=uRwy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 53039569b1043799f3cc4a615c3303c6f51adc5f\nparent c62d79259d0ccd83ad515d3444840e0e0e18059a\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780702381 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780702381 -0700\n\n[codex] Remove legacy remote plugin startup sync (#25936)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Remove the legacy startup remote plugin sync path that called\n`/plugins/list` and reconciled curated plugin cache/config.\n- Remove the `sync_plugins_from_remote` API, its result/error types,\nstartup marker task, and tests that expected the legacy request.\n- Keep the current remote installed bundle sync and remote catalog flows\n(`/ps/plugins/installed` and `/ps/plugins/list`) intact.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `env HOME=/private/tmp/codex-xin-build-home\nUSERPROFILE=/private/tmp/codex-xin-build-home just test -p\ncodex-core-plugins`\n- Searched for legacy `/plugins/list` sync references; remaining matches\nare `/ps/plugins/list` catalog tests/code.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server plugin_list` is currently blocked\nbefore running filtered tests by an unrelated compile error in\n`app-server/tests/suite/v2/image_generation.rs`:\n`app_test_support::McpProcess` is not exported.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T23:33:01Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4f655bc3b740bb1fec3744df4851f7eb1b95fbe9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4f655bc3b740bb1fec3744df4851f7eb1b95fbe9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4f655bc3b740bb1fec3744df4851f7eb1b95fbe9/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c62d79259d0ccd83ad515d3444840e0e0e18059a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c62d79259d0ccd83ad515d3444840e0e0e18059a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c62d79259d0ccd83ad515d3444840e0e0e18059a"}]},{"sha":"c62d79259d0ccd83ad515d3444840e0e0e18059a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM2MmQ3OTI1OWQwY2NkODNhZDUxNWQzNDQ0ODQwZTBlMGUxODA1OWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T22:54:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T22:54:46Z"},"message":"Block active goals after terminal turn errors (#26690)\n\n## Why\n\nTerminal turn errors can leave a goal active. Automatic goal\ncontinuation may then repeatedly hit a permanent failure, including\ncompaction requests rejected with HTTP 400, and consume excessive\ntokens.\n\nThis PR changes the goal extension to treat all turn-ending errors\n(including non-retryable errors and retryable errors that have exceeded\ntheir retry count) as \"blocking\" for the goal. The downside to this\nchange is that there are some errors that may eventually succeed (e.g. a\n429 due to a service outage), and previously the goal runtime would have\nkept the agent going in these situations.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Block the current active goal when a turn ends with an error other\nthan a usage-limit error.\n- Preserve the existing `usage_limited` transition for usage-limit\nerrors.\n- Share progress accounting, guarded state updates, metrics, and event\nemission in the goal runtime.","tree":{"sha":"2f9a01d9abdf5c69010bccdb7a75f88136d346b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2f9a01d9abdf5c69010bccdb7a75f88136d346b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c62d79259d0ccd83ad515d3444840e0e0e18059a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqI1O2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKC4QAKNbZYqJGODDmYhEfzx31wZI\n8u8Wj+smre0oIl7vTEOiu5vJA4une8ApYuLdQ+FaGFZXZroyy26jq/1j/8ADUD6K\nfE0h/K5acRagyGfhm1qeWDsfXaEpuJBk94GpOEEwI7HHElK5d0qfSta+qMoCmUwg\nhZW1uGd6w94BMH76IylyQ7CvakmmQ7HYj55IS5Se1GliNuwj//0aQZ+KxuAmiyYz\nfrWja/QR4L8CQdi9IkNBCZQ5OOwfv7jdgrIPY/Entn2X0GJaZ/JCfzlRTPuHPU1m\n3UapNpMdPuThBU/1VGLU7o9Tn5DRhpxWAf+t4B4U4cnePeZjZ3rgXJuWBk4jbeDb\n/3Yfb5PhyK8yPKvE7ANzjzT+abHAfTUiD5M8nJ/a2lPMq4ThyLpctiFrj3rp+9tj\nkq5v6dX+8al6bxj9M4gBsH5uiN+yGpNCHfOlHydtzoQbMVxfBZjkGmfh5Hyc15EI\n8z7OtEFQPa4t6UJVRiqAcgG8c4ec6DGkTrTqSv3w/mHkw3nnnC7Jp3K8V68FM83G\n79HfbS2PlsGaFsFmr1UuPIZDQLkI0g9400ZYtqnkhjMCTYi5iX/QYFqCeoFq0Ko8\nq9NR+snNwgESr5U6Yn4fClAOJp4aZlb1dcsoOACkj0TbE6XwZjrQuGRbVu9nKF/a\notHSGrUPGONkIDyc43mM\n=Iu/J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2f9a01d9abdf5c69010bccdb7a75f88136d346b6\nparent 470c20bf98ce35c8bcaa021e722f0a7074c4530b\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780700086 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780700086 -0700\n\nBlock active goals after terminal turn errors (#26690)\n\n## Why\n\nTerminal turn errors can leave a goal active. Automatic goal\ncontinuation may then repeatedly hit a permanent failure, including\ncompaction requests rejected with HTTP 400, and consume excessive\ntokens.\n\nThis PR changes the goal extension to treat all turn-ending errors\n(including non-retryable errors and retryable errors that have exceeded\ntheir retry count) as \"blocking\" for the goal. The downside to this\nchange is that there are some errors that may eventually succeed (e.g. a\n429 due to a service outage), and previously the goal runtime would have\nkept the agent going in these situations.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Block the current active goal when a turn ends with an error other\nthan a usage-limit error.\n- Preserve the existing `usage_limited` transition for usage-limit\nerrors.\n- Share progress accounting, guarded state updates, metrics, and event\nemission in the goal runtime.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T22:54:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c62d79259d0ccd83ad515d3444840e0e0e18059a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c62d79259d0ccd83ad515d3444840e0e0e18059a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c62d79259d0ccd83ad515d3444840e0e0e18059a/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"470c20bf98ce35c8bcaa021e722f0a7074c4530b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/470c20bf98ce35c8bcaa021e722f0a7074c4530b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/470c20bf98ce35c8bcaa021e722f0a7074c4530b"}]},{"sha":"470c20bf98ce35c8bcaa021e722f0a7074c4530b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ3MGMyMGJmOThjZTM1YzhiY2FhMDIxZTcyMmYwYTcwNzRjNDUzMGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T22:41:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T22:41:13Z"},"message":"protocol: remove submission-side serde from Op (#26674)\n\n## Why\n\nSubmission-side `Op` payloads are now an internal handoff inside the\nRust codebase, so keeping a stable serde contract there adds complexity\nwithout a real wire consumer.\n\n## What changed\n\n- remove serde/schema annotations from `Submission`, `Op`, and\nsubmission-only payload types like thread settings overrides, additional\ncontext, realtime conversation params, `TurnEnvironmentSelection`, and\n`RequestUserInputResponse`\n- delete the `Op` serialization tests and the now-unused double-option\nprompt serde helper\n- keep event/API-facing serialization where it is still required, and\nserialize the `request_user_input` tool output from its wire payload\ninstead of the core response struct\n- update `protocol_v1.md` to call out that events remain the serialized\ntransport surface while submission payloads are implementation details\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `cargo check -p codex-core -p codex-app-server -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just test -p codex-core request_user_input`","tree":{"sha":"d6497322b637dfdba7e828624094e3ffbcbe5740","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d6497322b637dfdba7e828624094e3ffbcbe5740"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/470c20bf98ce35c8bcaa021e722f0a7074c4530b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqI1CJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7z0QAAdZE1fKo2a4a1ypet5PL4Ks\nyLa+JxNnMhkuLP1zmngTZ/LhNcRHTUClilIdcxXzP2ctC8PTt7iX6f3iJANqPjtr\nm5YLqXkXLgKCN90SnxD72YNFGTf4Mt9mqEXQCm0tjlzirrIMDABUepmQeKO4XHIn\no9t7QGBTzgDrwBhBkzUnRCGNr3yFZ9tT/isy5Wf8Nx/Wju7SFVKwtjD8kJVkkufl\n1ESxdFyIJyu2wNh+dsN3XMWKrEx3qE4NnPRZjlGazmjxsEmAwismiAk5M7Wxcvs1\nqzP5hfypLhDWtGYF7T/ZUB208WkcSEWLsFe+/xcdety3pnYGatn1yxvdf2lpoEwk\nAPxjd2CL1SE3R8S/X4IsHkS14ftHHVGReiAX/aMI6+9nx4OyeX8QrusBMFa8XuI6\nmmEPyNYNQUpV3ObG8QAT9Uas9lCcyXp3HLDqDooBHIWQ8qvBrG59uPmEpKb3Bmga\nWknzaVRacVy4AcFC3Pc9dDfFISs2hCejbKtriTMqK87WQler807pnMVO+Itunmqv\nbS/P/HM0xTDzz4jz+0Xd1/t+NRZy0l8p1VGfWznfOZYLLyjRZzHlez53bJiOQfpi\nxC2FcCm3XfwNcPSx2DQo3MKIIbvAWf8V8ubAzj4cUYgMGym10RKBV9sfrayFbb4U\nO7IlUQ0lNOvr+cXK5QOq\n=lGHk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d6497322b637dfdba7e828624094e3ffbcbe5740\nparent 479a14cf592d5e0ca319942e6ba833ebaa1274e2\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780699273 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780699273 -0700\n\nprotocol: remove submission-side serde from Op (#26674)\n\n## Why\n\nSubmission-side `Op` payloads are now an internal handoff inside the\nRust codebase, so keeping a stable serde contract there adds complexity\nwithout a real wire consumer.\n\n## What changed\n\n- remove serde/schema annotations from `Submission`, `Op`, and\nsubmission-only payload types like thread settings overrides, additional\ncontext, realtime conversation params, `TurnEnvironmentSelection`, and\n`RequestUserInputResponse`\n- delete the `Op` serialization tests and the now-unused double-option\nprompt serde helper\n- keep event/API-facing serialization where it is still required, and\nserialize the `request_user_input` tool output from its wire payload\ninstead of the core response struct\n- update `protocol_v1.md` to call out that events remain the serialized\ntransport surface while submission payloads are implementation details\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `cargo check -p codex-core -p codex-app-server -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just test -p codex-core request_user_input`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T22:41:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/470c20bf98ce35c8bcaa021e722f0a7074c4530b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/470c20bf98ce35c8bcaa021e722f0a7074c4530b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/470c20bf98ce35c8bcaa021e722f0a7074c4530b/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"479a14cf592d5e0ca319942e6ba833ebaa1274e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/479a14cf592d5e0ca319942e6ba833ebaa1274e2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/479a14cf592d5e0ca319942e6ba833ebaa1274e2"}]},{"sha":"479a14cf592d5e0ca319942e6ba833ebaa1274e2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ3OWExNGNmNTkyZDVlMGNhMzE5OTQyZTZiYTgzM2ViYWExMjc0ZTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T21:17:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T21:17:30Z"},"message":"[2 of 2] Finish moving goal runtime to extension (#26548)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#26547](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26547) - [1 of 2] Align\ngoal extension with core behavior\n2. [#26548](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26548) - [2 of 2] Move\ngoal runtime to extension\n\n## Why\n\nThis PR completes the switch of the goal behavior to the\nextension-backed runtime and removes the old core goal implementation.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Installs the goal extension for app-server `ThreadManager` sessions.\n- Routes app-server thread goal `get`, `set`, and `clear` through\n`GoalService`.\n- Uses thread-idle lifecycle emission after goal resume and snapshot\nordering so the extension can decide whether to continue the goal.\n- Forwards extension goal updates through a FIFO async app-server\nnotification path so backpressure does not drop them or reorder updates.\n- Keeps review turns from enabling goal runtime behavior.\n- Plans extension tools before dynamic tools so built-in goal tool names\nkeep their old precedence when goals are enabled.\n- Removes the old core goal runtime, core goal tool handlers, and core\ngoal tool specs.\n- Updates tests that were coupled to the core-owned goal runtime while\nleaving the legacy `<goal_context>` compatibility path in core for old\nthreads.\n- Removes the stale cargo-shear ignore now that `codex-goal-extension`\nis used by the workspace.\n- Keeps realtime event matching exhaustive after removing the old\ngoal-specific realtime text path.\n\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran manual `/goal` runs in TUI. Validated time accounting matched\nwall-clock time and goal lifecycle state transitions.","tree":{"sha":"adeb025a4683635870e483e8aefd77efbad02115","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/adeb025a4683635870e483e8aefd77efbad02115"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/479a14cf592d5e0ca319942e6ba833ebaa1274e2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIzzqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ4AQAJ5a/M29i3lhXZQOT04qUc3t\nlGAEIrFJz6N0oPjSdvJycL3jRsItMyGs64qoTaUi1AGOscHAWMiR7bjylX6jfpPH\n1R5qDHF8rYd35GjMWHVhhXvnxhvij3bmIfwkOsYzRGiGEYzn2X8gMnPkk87mBi0i\nh+XSc9kA8fhuMWN2/wfLQujQ2VmZCj+JxX4p11zvgE30BepZsDXOwhpRP5+Qq0r9\nny3Omzz01FTjYZ4e86bOXSpbANeVTqipdvgm7r54aahs5kh+/hp/9p75xjq36lcD\niyb5LEixLclW6tB74ICMSqY6MFBQQ1+ESK/lkPYZ6XaqTMLe/rQejEXdJD2IvrNX\nWm4oSXwJtnoS9QQBjmXjUZnm85mp8QEFXQNOER4ePmrzGQSZXONWqoyBYQnbDi8M\nvvSEiEc1xyWbmLsy22jbLOMdoq5J1pOumjOekyl5WXFbIcWVr9BdYNL+EZezbCGS\n4P8y0xOpMZ5ns1QSJF73JiKn2Uckkz8gROCUgEfvdt6JZAaJXYadkWJJDAHfc58v\nl0Cbc/W++qGxknnsb/d2ho8lwLQjui2GtC83BdnSbsLy2CJDfvcRCfTOsMu+PMN5\n1x2gD1m/01WJjRsxgekDYc5jvuLIO9peea8NJmxGdtt5k3BcNNdDEeeivivIWcDE\nL5DRMqKHJ++82bfhipEA\n=XnZ8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree adeb025a4683635870e483e8aefd77efbad02115\nparent 679cc084451e2111ad946d0befe583b79e486ca9\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780694250 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780694250 -0700\n\n[2 of 2] Finish moving goal runtime to extension (#26548)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#26547](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26547) - [1 of 2] Align\ngoal extension with core behavior\n2. [#26548](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26548) - [2 of 2] Move\ngoal runtime to extension\n\n## Why\n\nThis PR completes the switch of the goal behavior to the\nextension-backed runtime and removes the old core goal implementation.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Installs the goal extension for app-server `ThreadManager` sessions.\n- Routes app-server thread goal `get`, `set`, and `clear` through\n`GoalService`.\n- Uses thread-idle lifecycle emission after goal resume and snapshot\nordering so the extension can decide whether to continue the goal.\n- Forwards extension goal updates through a FIFO async app-server\nnotification path so backpressure does not drop them or reorder updates.\n- Keeps review turns from enabling goal runtime behavior.\n- Plans extension tools before dynamic tools so built-in goal tool names\nkeep their old precedence when goals are enabled.\n- Removes the old core goal runtime, core goal tool handlers, and core\ngoal tool specs.\n- Updates tests that were coupled to the core-owned goal runtime while\nleaving the legacy `<goal_context>` compatibility path in core for old\nthreads.\n- Removes the stale cargo-shear ignore now that `codex-goal-extension`\nis used by the workspace.\n- Keeps realtime event matching exhaustive after removing the old\ngoal-specific realtime text path.\n\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran manual `/goal` runs in TUI. Validated time accounting matched\nwall-clock time and goal lifecycle state transitions.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T21:17:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/479a14cf592d5e0ca319942e6ba833ebaa1274e2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/479a14cf592d5e0ca319942e6ba833ebaa1274e2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/479a14cf592d5e0ca319942e6ba833ebaa1274e2/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"679cc084451e2111ad946d0befe583b79e486ca9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/679cc084451e2111ad946d0befe583b79e486ca9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/679cc084451e2111ad946d0befe583b79e486ca9"}]},{"sha":"679cc084451e2111ad946d0befe583b79e486ca9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY3OWNjMDg0NDUxZTIxMTFhZDk0NmQwYmVmZTU4M2I3OWU0ODZjYTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T21:09:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T21:09:40Z"},"message":"[codex] Bound WSL local curated discovery (#26669)\n\n## Context\nThe installed-app suggestion expansion added in #24996 reads plugin\ndetails for trusted file-backed marketplace candidates because the list\nresponse does not include app ids. On Windows-backed WSL mounts, the\nlocal `openai-curated` checkout lives under `$CODEX_HOME/.tmp/plugins`,\nand those per-plugin detail reads can be very slow.\n\nRemote curated already has cached app ids, so it does not need the same\nlocal filesystem traversal.\n\n## Summary\n- Keep only the WSL Windows-backed local `openai-curated` checkout on\nthe legacy fallback/configured discovery path.\n- Preserve installed-app expansion for non-WSL file-backed marketplaces\nand remote curated.\n- Add focused tests for the WSL local curated path predicate.\n\n## Test\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins discoverable`\n- `just test -p codex-core plugins::discoverable::tests`","tree":{"sha":"174ca1fe50960c350593ff4de96955eddf89f03a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/174ca1fe50960c350593ff4de96955eddf89f03a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/679cc084451e2111ad946d0befe583b79e486ca9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIzsUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1bcQAGN1GZbPrVXGt0sohMhoRkVu\nTjZVQb/b3V1ntS3p3Gqqwr+xe91qKbch8oY421xx24y7YfMW6RlOsqeDx4qtKfSd\nqtaeuhlehzIDVT5utBSua+uyYctkXYFPT40is8H+T598kK5Q5f3r3T+l+aohF3G+\nBOP6PRGVwKgzHwORDfas3D4eqZIMPhMAUvvqIju8FUEoKPgNFgSwlc0B8KHiin6Z\n1aZwrsPBuK298LrK/J0bDxw+yXWL7mEB1CIE9NjjJIfDzgb+gygOnPP60fb9d3ca\nmONBKh6Dg6FpcN4oMWyutZYvd4rEBveJVBzIhVDtjKo+LM9ZrZDmd9MR6PdVoRLn\nXpKO2J5zehzs8Blb3325Pdi5eZQh1i9DIK26QbSdBMzTUOy13yu6y0gM77H+gCCi\nyDXxRn6/C/sAshBqa/zMjIOZI7uXiujgxfUcyKEO9DS2H3bgEzhmJz8A+5SUZ+Zn\noPZki5kV2PeKIqYdFsU5m6NaXcXrvJmjPK/Nl3NH0JfqShEUlXaceOtUgFpSZ4fo\ngAceuC9QQB0XI+swtDVznX9XK92FaYpjL1zDlXtwT9cabaOTXSOm7zjDVEIiM1fz\nGpTNyhblnc0F6roJUDh/gjJCXU/KV32mb8TAH3YRmQrUtVxJH7kC/UImW7Unn9Q/\nq4FaXzlNZhsibyiW+l57\n=04Is\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 174ca1fe50960c350593ff4de96955eddf89f03a\nparent bb7d19bc245b9661fbf2391a2d02d9d9139c4fee\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1780693780 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780693780 -0700\n\n[codex] Bound WSL local curated discovery (#26669)\n\n## Context\nThe installed-app suggestion expansion added in #24996 reads plugin\ndetails for trusted file-backed marketplace candidates because the list\nresponse does not include app ids. On Windows-backed WSL mounts, the\nlocal `openai-curated` checkout lives under `$CODEX_HOME/.tmp/plugins`,\nand those per-plugin detail reads can be very slow.\n\nRemote curated already has cached app ids, so it does not need the same\nlocal filesystem traversal.\n\n## Summary\n- Keep only the WSL Windows-backed local `openai-curated` checkout on\nthe legacy fallback/configured discovery path.\n- Preserve installed-app expansion for non-WSL file-backed marketplaces\nand remote curated.\n- Add focused tests for the WSL local curated path predicate.\n\n## Test\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins discoverable`\n- `just test -p codex-core plugins::discoverable::tests`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T21:09:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/679cc084451e2111ad946d0befe583b79e486ca9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/679cc084451e2111ad946d0befe583b79e486ca9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/679cc084451e2111ad946d0befe583b79e486ca9/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bb7d19bc245b9661fbf2391a2d02d9d9139c4fee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bb7d19bc245b9661fbf2391a2d02d9d9139c4fee","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bb7d19bc245b9661fbf2391a2d02d9d9139c4fee"}]},{"sha":"bb7d19bc245b9661fbf2391a2d02d9d9139c4fee","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJiN2QxOWJjMjQ1Yjk2NjFmYmYyMzkxYTJkMDJkOWQ5MTM5YzRmZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"mpc-oai","email":"mpc@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T19:40:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T19:40:31Z"},"message":"Add JSON output for plugin subcommands (#26631)\n\n## Summary\n- Follow-up to #25330 and #26417\n- Add `--json` output for `codex plugin add` and `codex plugin remove`\n- Add `--json` output for `codex plugin marketplace\nadd/list/upgrade/remove`\n- Keep existing human-readable output unchanged\n- Keep existing error handling/stderr behavior unchanged; `--json`\nchanges successful stdout output only\n- Align marketplace add/remove JSON field names with the existing\napp-server protocol shape\n- Add CLI coverage for plugin and marketplace JSON outputs\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-cli`\n- `just test -p codex-cli`","tree":{"sha":"622d8fddb60a49d52c4eab20bcf924d5d43f53bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/622d8fddb60a49d52c4eab20bcf924d5d43f53bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bb7d19bc245b9661fbf2391a2d02d9d9139c4fee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIyYvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANtMQABKxPXUUIKI1QFvYmBmVBsyl\n/SRZ4jiVvXdL/WErfEcVEGbWwGaiPQFIgLLNpr3/2xE5JvEYGCI0Z0MKOnJBs4eH\nizIHj3A0RpOr6o/j+rA3hfjm7Qw0tvqpTsq9UB50HFIz6NyYUIDftkTeZyzkhXQy\nK+qUV2pyNaER4ixM13GDNxXURN5OShqFwgGSoSOTOdirPK/aPthYA+oUqe6LZU5T\ny/ka8H3+lmMMRGZMELhnIKC7bEqGj+zBpEkT8jZs+g/sJONFhUSM1mSFonAMHk/3\nO5qH5w/uENBUZzdhGheYh215p0o2XBedXBhRrcsi7Y+F0IULbVJ4diHgJqCmaaoC\ncBiXH6pgaryWKBqNAJaCDnXjKZHf27fEks146Cd1NsEytKX/pMHXBc6IKNtTvEet\nqP9xnuvdPvDlrWEsSB0mWkRJuHGo8HIYOW8rGkxBBmcsGYkJ56HLXGz7DzaExL1L\nZKjG+aDWu2z56Sek3L7IqbP8kDWgCRioLiW25uM8IJpMa6tgmUHIed29sVqjT61a\nw6DHoE6Dg0Jn7+jMlladaO2+1svaKEP4NOGDuABio+CQlLcz4tt0HrxBGXtt5X6/\n5dSj9uX2HUom+/22mf52nubDNlZLcVwJYtIFTxHRUpo5bklm4cykgWS13hoyThEK\nQXQ0fyfYdseN3vpDKcGj\n=kEPL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 622d8fddb60a49d52c4eab20bcf924d5d43f53bd\nparent 055c7a7c53d46517e95f24147980b4523da279db\nauthor mpc-oai <mpc@openai.com> 1780688431 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780688431 -0500\n\nAdd JSON output for plugin subcommands (#26631)\n\n## Summary\n- Follow-up to #25330 and #26417\n- Add `--json` output for `codex plugin add` and `codex plugin remove`\n- Add `--json` output for `codex plugin marketplace\nadd/list/upgrade/remove`\n- Keep existing human-readable output unchanged\n- Keep existing error handling/stderr behavior unchanged; `--json`\nchanges successful stdout output only\n- Align marketplace add/remove JSON field names with the existing\napp-server protocol shape\n- Add CLI coverage for plugin and marketplace JSON outputs\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-cli`\n- `just test -p codex-cli`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T19:40:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bb7d19bc245b9661fbf2391a2d02d9d9139c4fee","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bb7d19bc245b9661fbf2391a2d02d9d9139c4fee","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bb7d19bc245b9661fbf2391a2d02d9d9139c4fee/comments","author":{"login":"mpc-oai","id":278119679,"node_id":"U_kgDOEJPE_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/278119679?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/mpc-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"055c7a7c53d46517e95f24147980b4523da279db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/055c7a7c53d46517e95f24147980b4523da279db","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/055c7a7c53d46517e95f24147980b4523da279db"}]},{"sha":"055c7a7c53d46517e95f24147980b4523da279db","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA1NWM3YTdjNTNkNDY1MTdlOTVmMjQxNDc5ODBiNDUyM2RhMjc5ZGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Charlie Marsh","email":"charliemarsh@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T19:32:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T19:32:43Z"},"message":"Speed up TUI startup by reusing plugin discovery (#26469)\n\n## Summary\n\nTUI startup loads related plugin data from `hooks/list`, session MCP\ninitialization, and plugin skill warmup. These paths repeated filesystem\ndiscovery and emitted the same plugin warnings, while `hooks/list` and\naccount/model bootstrap ran serially.\n\nThis change:\n\n- Reuses one immutable plugin load outcome across startup consumers.\n- Keys the cache only on plugin-relevant configuration.\n- Single-flights concurrent plugin loads and prevents invalidated loads\nfrom repopulating the cache.\n- Runs hook discovery and account/model bootstrap concurrently.\n- Preserves configuration-migration ordering, hook review behavior, and\naccurate startup telemetry.\n\nIn 10 alternating release-build launches in the Ruff repository with the\nexisting `~/.codex` configuration, median time to the first editable\ncomposer decreased from 833ms to 504ms. The branch was faster in 9 of 10\npairs, with a paired median improvement of 312ms.","tree":{"sha":"1ad2fefbf83043c14cb604f263687704a3f79497","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1ad2fefbf83043c14cb604f263687704a3f79497"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/055c7a7c53d46517e95f24147980b4523da279db","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIyRbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI6MQAHuJVLIaP8BPg1DhYVmjpIeC\nGZkNlpm8K3ZkeCf7Uy0gsncNGcai6Kiat9iCaYkwAOlkqLFZTFeCqTOf6374VtVQ\n4fMlSJXWiwc/hadBczTRAq+MuNFmkJLr7PxoPCQz5I49JWGjvQJlFi36iBub8ldy\nVnWT0GKEbGzxW7RamDUuDsNsSOoSJz+WxLDGlQhYAHOnlj6su0gJ6T6jri9yhUIC\nxm9Bo8nZ08sO0BgIA/KXpxcXhOYJBHSSJDgDb8ZaReVRqFcztDXF36guaLY03+4b\nWMt8TkcWncgK7h/BcjKWr7jvb7xiM97jcISHlkUzKfvfTqwyiQ8quJZGlXEfSIrm\nOg3HkYbFnOeayLN2lfSiSG1Nym5cDBWLY6BoRqSxnDFDqNuhlDtU4xhzTeZIcGLP\nRGVSuX5QYFcwaYS7g/Fbm6Mv6SVH48h69jzF+REytgLmCAqzWkoHrsxQZbH82Y9W\nFXFWsFkhMHfx5Hiy3VuTyxsOzhptJnoWoItgHMz/5aylQ/EZ4qlIlAd3q9j7SieW\nI3tdMWvbiFRW+UIIHW0okUR3l770daGYxk8Wh9++zo0y/B9cKXpEOyFZbU8W5pto\nMylQJv/zdtQ4ilbBnEElAhZMw/25oXyay9I4zZg7r7mFOiSosA5xdBomCfsdiAii\n/a2Ea/lPDq/6miSVj1Tx\n=/yMJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1ad2fefbf83043c14cb604f263687704a3f79497\nparent 345cf6e8d06b0d6890e68dc5fd80227f2fbb4e71\nauthor Charlie Marsh <charliemarsh@openai.com> 1780687963 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780687963 -0400\n\nSpeed up TUI startup by reusing plugin discovery (#26469)\n\n## Summary\n\nTUI startup loads related plugin data from `hooks/list`, session MCP\ninitialization, and plugin skill warmup. These paths repeated filesystem\ndiscovery and emitted the same plugin warnings, while `hooks/list` and\naccount/model bootstrap ran serially.\n\nThis change:\n\n- Reuses one immutable plugin load outcome across startup consumers.\n- Keys the cache only on plugin-relevant configuration.\n- Single-flights concurrent plugin loads and prevents invalidated loads\nfrom repopulating the cache.\n- Runs hook discovery and account/model bootstrap concurrently.\n- Preserves configuration-migration ordering, hook review behavior, and\naccurate startup telemetry.\n\nIn 10 alternating release-build launches in the Ruff repository with the\nexisting `~/.codex` configuration, median time to the first editable\ncomposer decreased from 833ms to 504ms. The branch was faster in 9 of 10\npairs, with a paired median improvement of 312ms.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T19:32:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/055c7a7c53d46517e95f24147980b4523da279db","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/055c7a7c53d46517e95f24147980b4523da279db","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/055c7a7c53d46517e95f24147980b4523da279db/comments","author":{"login":"charliemarsh-oai","id":282065134,"node_id":"U_kgDOEM_47g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282065134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/charliemarsh-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"345cf6e8d06b0d6890e68dc5fd80227f2fbb4e71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/345cf6e8d06b0d6890e68dc5fd80227f2fbb4e71","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/345cf6e8d06b0d6890e68dc5fd80227f2fbb4e71"}]},{"sha":"345cf6e8d06b0d6890e68dc5fd80227f2fbb4e71","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM0NWNmNmU4ZDA2YjBkNjg5MGU2OGRjNWZkODAyMjdmMmZiYjRlNzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Charlie Marsh","email":"charliemarsh@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:58:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:58:09Z"},"message":"Use state DB first for `resume --last` (#26462)\n\n## Summary\n\n`codex resume --last` currently lists sessions by updated time using\nscan-and-repair. Updated-time filesystem listing must stat every rollout\nbefore applying the cwd, provider, and source filters, so startup scales\nwith the entire local session history...\n\nThis change queries the state DB first for the latest matching session.\nFor local workspaces, we only accept the indexed result when its rollout\npath still exists; otherwise we retry with scan-and-repair. The same\nlookup path is shared by `fork --last`.\n\nI benchmarked the same `thread/list` request used by `resume --last` in\nmy local `ruff` checkout against a Codex home with 2,599 active rollouts\ntotaling 3.7 GiB, including 90 Ruff threads.\n\nAcross five fresh release app-server processes with warm filesystem\ncaches, the state-DB-only lookup had median latency of 0.37-0.44 ms,\nwhile scan-and-repair had median latency of 139-162 ms. First-request\nlatency was 0.7-1.7 ms versus 142-185 ms.\n\nSo this **removes roughly 140-160 ms from the `resume --last` lookup**\non this machine, and makes that lookup over 300x faster.\n\nThe tradeoff is that this does leave two correctness gaps:\n\n- If a newer matching rollout is missing from SQLite but an older\nmatching row exists, the fast path resumes the older thread and never\nfalls back to the filesystem scan.\n- If an existing row has stale filter or ordering metadata, the fast\npath can select a different thread from scan-and-repair. The rollout\ntests already demonstrate this for stale cwd metadata: state-DB-only\nreturns the stale match, while scan-and-repair removes and repairs it.\n\nSo you could end up seeing the \"wrong\" result in cases like...\n\n1. A crash or SQLite error occurs between Codex writing the conversation\nfile and updating SQLite, leaving the newer file unindexed.\n\n2. An older Codex version, restore, or manual copy adds a conversation\nfile after SQLite’s one-time backfill completed.\n\nThese seem pretty rare though (and sessions can always be recovered via\nother mechanisms -- `--last` is just a convenience feature), and I think\nthe tradeoffs are good here?","tree":{"sha":"8eb5dff7201d0347aecc5f8f99b124cdf964842b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8eb5dff7201d0347aecc5f8f99b124cdf964842b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/345cf6e8d06b0d6890e68dc5fd80227f2fbb4e71","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIxxBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVwkQAKRoJE9pqfFFDK0A0C2CSVgO\nkWL8pWBzswN8ZUE3nCj7fCC5lJTboTjyHlHBPbckM7c+8Vvz2J8AG1AwDoV5WI1n\nrsyw4Md8B1yV5Mu8HmrsPZjrvdO6bMyFxxt94stmgQiMQD2SBmT9Wx/XJdUaWAjF\n/nWmpLffqci3ZKvgkrZUJW+CcxyUtGvoxsCvUfZhrVbV8Wk7uODWvtZWhlJEaDHo\nFRPI4Fos7I1RrcfQ+B00fn4oHyutW/N0bMIHlASIhkqP2mKzA42ja7jomiWhfnZL\nL+hBuDtZ1L5sKAW1XsU7DFciRbJS3Ary/x6Yz5coKTtxNP8NxFPuu72YCgHJOqmq\nWZLXk/RsCkeyfzcDjv2QeMvAeILZg9lhLe3NHDxO0l7F3Q2pn7mLmR2IDBdhIbfU\nfu9XaXOn5GptCa/Ov92y8siYsWj6jdSPJAYYvojOtCFoaypv2SuaSiF0RMgGLsiB\nhpqHWKWbWs8yxV0gVnNh0f3PNsisqDCVUV8qWt6c8ZvpIfznrUaUsYebxc2wMaDL\nWnQO4PSgAYVER0IVtgrCONmp4/c/Fr5L43YYuuwF4C2ei1ypDZwEpB0aLv1b5JSX\nmNzQCZ2B9n1AFq4a1oVPQ9uRrwGuLYywtBqIevxfPUeEK+B0Um19w9cxp8UKkDQG\nkoQIyZUGoqxmwMENBZOJ\n=wcZq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8eb5dff7201d0347aecc5f8f99b124cdf964842b\nparent 76c0a5379c79cc6eafc3a041791201e849ad4c7f\nauthor Charlie Marsh <charliemarsh@openai.com> 1780685889 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780685889 -0400\n\nUse state DB first for `resume --last` (#26462)\n\n## Summary\n\n`codex resume --last` currently lists sessions by updated time using\nscan-and-repair. Updated-time filesystem listing must stat every rollout\nbefore applying the cwd, provider, and source filters, so startup scales\nwith the entire local session history...\n\nThis change queries the state DB first for the latest matching session.\nFor local workspaces, we only accept the indexed result when its rollout\npath still exists; otherwise we retry with scan-and-repair. The same\nlookup path is shared by `fork --last`.\n\nI benchmarked the same `thread/list` request used by `resume --last` in\nmy local `ruff` checkout against a Codex home with 2,599 active rollouts\ntotaling 3.7 GiB, including 90 Ruff threads.\n\nAcross five fresh release app-server processes with warm filesystem\ncaches, the state-DB-only lookup had median latency of 0.37-0.44 ms,\nwhile scan-and-repair had median latency of 139-162 ms. First-request\nlatency was 0.7-1.7 ms versus 142-185 ms.\n\nSo this **removes roughly 140-160 ms from the `resume --last` lookup**\non this machine, and makes that lookup over 300x faster.\n\nThe tradeoff is that this does leave two correctness gaps:\n\n- If a newer matching rollout is missing from SQLite but an older\nmatching row exists, the fast path resumes the older thread and never\nfalls back to the filesystem scan.\n- If an existing row has stale filter or ordering metadata, the fast\npath can select a different thread from scan-and-repair. The rollout\ntests already demonstrate this for stale cwd metadata: state-DB-only\nreturns the stale match, while scan-and-repair removes and repairs it.\n\nSo you could end up seeing the \"wrong\" result in cases like...\n\n1. A crash or SQLite error occurs between Codex writing the conversation\nfile and updating SQLite, leaving the newer file unindexed.\n\n2. An older Codex version, restore, or manual copy adds a conversation\nfile after SQLite’s one-time backfill completed.\n\nThese seem pretty rare though (and sessions can always be recovered via\nother mechanisms -- `--last` is just a convenience feature), and I think\nthe tradeoffs are good here?","verified_at":"2026-06-05T18:58:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/345cf6e8d06b0d6890e68dc5fd80227f2fbb4e71","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/345cf6e8d06b0d6890e68dc5fd80227f2fbb4e71","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/345cf6e8d06b0d6890e68dc5fd80227f2fbb4e71/comments","author":{"login":"charliemarsh-oai","id":282065134,"node_id":"U_kgDOEM_47g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282065134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/charliemarsh-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"76c0a5379c79cc6eafc3a041791201e849ad4c7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/76c0a5379c79cc6eafc3a041791201e849ad4c7f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/76c0a5379c79cc6eafc3a041791201e849ad4c7f"}]},{"sha":"76c0a5379c79cc6eafc3a041791201e849ad4c7f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc2YzBhNTM3OWM3OWNjNmVhZmMzYTA0MTc5MTIwMWU4NDlhZDRjN2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:36:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:36:53Z"},"message":"Make runtime workspace roots absolute in app-server API (#26552)\n\nStacked on #26532.\n\n## Why\n\n#26532 moves cwd normalization to the app-server/core boundary.\n`runtimeWorkspaceRoots` still accepted raw paths in v2 requests and in\n`ConfigOverrides`, which left core responsible for interpreting those\nroots later. This makes runtime workspace roots follow the same\nabsolute-path boundary as cwd.\n\n## What\n\n- Change v2 `runtimeWorkspaceRoots` request fields for `thread/start`,\n`thread/resume`, `thread/fork`, and `turn/start` to `AbsolutePathBuf`.\n- Deduplicate already-absolute runtime roots in app-server handlers and\npass them through `ConfigOverrides.workspace_roots` as\n`AbsolutePathBuf`.\n- Update TUI and exec client request builders to pass absolute runtime\nroots directly.\n- Update app-server docs, schema fixtures, and focused tests for\nabsolute runtime roots.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server runtime_workspace_roots`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsession_permission_profile_rebinds_runtime_workspace_roots`\n- `just test -p codex-tui app_server_session`\n- `just test -p codex-exec`","tree":{"sha":"6a8fa7df822c9246022e05b5c8a5aacac1dd7063","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6a8fa7df822c9246022e05b5c8a5aacac1dd7063"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/76c0a5379c79cc6eafc3a041791201e849ad4c7f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIxdFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD4MQABWM+Xp2JiOUwcQeE3Q/MIds\nACY9kNaN0p4eXSv0K8RkgaCg6V0M7Q0pOlbwSYkQDoZiRdj5iC82jkrorCDnU64x\nXJ3XmKU3nGVL9kZq82RT/pY59FcSPb/Jc+sVIxm4saSxvn3n7i2fQpBhYxht64i2\nUelXVCtL2g/LjGFSZvOcyqF00STW7J27FMeyL6YlzLw8vYQzG4I4Ugu/O7wsWYau\n/m2yQdWnePg2+Odcx9VTsUo2JSyY8Jqt407iT2sbAEIKBIKLYfwMNZt+Ws6NrE+u\nS7SwB5R6p/wH//KPQHmdBRNHXNXR2aWHxgJRQC/IpQkEI2DCH5buzMMZBos4Hg4A\n2uYaxlKFVtW7w/mGJDe+2YTF9dp1LPlP6JqT368xYwXGVQ/7Vik/DRxg2G2RHSAo\nYojQWPpvOjpWB4QuO5OHHn4PLSvyh9NVDHwNonXGmxyU6xzjbVWL+iJaTHmOuMWQ\ntW8C0f5t/J+9iy1HrSX8MY39anGZMycRxmlC8xlCslbSjPaGIkPQSrBr47VwWVKu\n84e6u9ZxB9XA0gQo6ANiIXEcNpZ+PpdVc+toUsmCFbbUall6uky5NhkGo796E5L6\nS3mvo9KOw/BWnqvRdnwou3BX1WI2x1vq75mQbvN8JuHvy7Z+1KC0qjhKh4S9N87N\nKtjwGlj8dtyYpuswYR7D\n=XS1a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6a8fa7df822c9246022e05b5c8a5aacac1dd7063\nparent 8d72fb6de92bf332b2ef4a4ccaf992021fbdf4ea\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780684613 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780684613 -0700\n\nMake runtime workspace roots absolute in app-server API (#26552)\n\nStacked on #26532.\n\n## Why\n\n#26532 moves cwd normalization to the app-server/core boundary.\n`runtimeWorkspaceRoots` still accepted raw paths in v2 requests and in\n`ConfigOverrides`, which left core responsible for interpreting those\nroots later. This makes runtime workspace roots follow the same\nabsolute-path boundary as cwd.\n\n## What\n\n- Change v2 `runtimeWorkspaceRoots` request fields for `thread/start`,\n`thread/resume`, `thread/fork`, and `turn/start` to `AbsolutePathBuf`.\n- Deduplicate already-absolute runtime roots in app-server handlers and\npass them through `ConfigOverrides.workspace_roots` as\n`AbsolutePathBuf`.\n- Update TUI and exec client request builders to pass absolute runtime\nroots directly.\n- Update app-server docs, schema fixtures, and focused tests for\nabsolute runtime roots.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server runtime_workspace_roots`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsession_permission_profile_rebinds_runtime_workspace_roots`\n- `just test -p codex-tui app_server_session`\n- `just test -p codex-exec`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T18:36:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/76c0a5379c79cc6eafc3a041791201e849ad4c7f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/76c0a5379c79cc6eafc3a041791201e849ad4c7f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/76c0a5379c79cc6eafc3a041791201e849ad4c7f/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8d72fb6de92bf332b2ef4a4ccaf992021fbdf4ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d72fb6de92bf332b2ef4a4ccaf992021fbdf4ea","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8d72fb6de92bf332b2ef4a4ccaf992021fbdf4ea"}]},{"sha":"8d72fb6de92bf332b2ef4a4ccaf992021fbdf4ea","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhkNzJmYjZkZTkyYmYzMzJiMmVmNGE0Y2NhZjk5MjAyMWZiZGY0ZWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:27:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:27:10Z"},"message":"[codex] Add turn profiling analytics (#26484)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd flat profiling fields to `codex_turn_event` so analytics can explain\nwhere turn wall-clock time is spent without changing tool execution\nbehavior.\n\nThe profile reports:\n- time before the first sampling request\n- sampling time across all attempts and follow-ups\n- overhead between sampling requests\n- time blocked in the post-sampling tool drain\n- time after the final sampling request\n- sampling request and retry counts\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Extend the existing turn timing state with constant-memory phase\naccounting and one RAII phase guard.\n- Observe sampling and the existing post-sampling drain only at turn\norchestration boundaries.\n- Keep tool runtime, tool futures, response item handling, and turn\nlifecycle values unchanged.\n- Add the profiling fields directly to the existing analytics turn event\nwithout changing app-server protocol or rollout persistence.\n- Use the existing turn `status` to distinguish completed, failed, and\ninterrupted profiles.\n\nExact sampling/tool overlap is intentionally omitted because measuring\ntool completion accurately would require hooks in the tool execution\npath.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Add app-server end-to-end coverage for a single-sampling turn with no\nblocking tool work.\n- Add app-server end-to-end coverage for `request_user_input` blocking\nfollowed by a second sampling request.\n- CI is running on the PR; tests were not executed locally per\nrepository guidance.","tree":{"sha":"39a7d445cd87bd3ffc49a1580d4df322bb13e928","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/39a7d445cd87bd3ffc49a1580d4df322bb13e928"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8d72fb6de92bf332b2ef4a4ccaf992021fbdf4ea","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIxT+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXe8QAAvSEgX44Ijz8gI68dlKdtLa\nGPwKIMUyMNCgbmt3WCbDTCL3xRUkeFKB20wJXpUyJV1ZFuV4XAhHAWbA9UL6rW8c\nI8ZAwO2j1elhnI8f4KNC6Rs5PuKZWL7M2hSdAWdw0gL/L4Yw/fU8nhM1SynaszDm\nq7cizkrOoHlY0xcjHgRQdGDgex0CD1hYgkkwThH7W85w6AiIyR1OdTHbx4Meuhe/\nT7cenx5S4n2fAuGxWZt/feHXiZH6KQIv07j7fFw+WSDn/iMVf7j+TPXs3KHc9J0r\nSCqeF2sa41wshbscrfetWTrcU0FqkLpjLkUqr5j/76cVTBdIVcqv62iErA5j1531\nmE+hx2zUXCxFhl0f1Wf6BA1JfxfHY4Oj9Z8VktBAu6qRQq080+S60wcZ4yBBWfM6\ngGWY5FWtLXx2pOrbh8jihw6HcLmCRK/UhHWkFqqWpg6ug9n+TbgHReqDrAdfh6O4\nyIa99MkSElSXb4VUHq2TM602jU4KOuG+MhVsvEjaBqN653H8ozo3j31EXjzsDx4N\nfF9q2s8ND74u92Ie6CnaPmebmQbg3hnLA6WOq+047DwCqoIdMBoeByxytgKuIKt7\ntMjy3F/MzeO1uW2TLv2WH5nfvlmHTjReTS1lefPvKvYmXbdyjWKr7C3oHBvYGiy8\naHRU08K5pSTCXbGEP85m\n=pUh4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 39a7d445cd87bd3ffc49a1580d4df322bb13e928\nparent 82b15b65e2303255e3e1a740d994c7e00250344a\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1780684030 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780684030 -0700\n\n[codex] Add turn profiling analytics (#26484)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd flat profiling fields to `codex_turn_event` so analytics can explain\nwhere turn wall-clock time is spent without changing tool execution\nbehavior.\n\nThe profile reports:\n- time before the first sampling request\n- sampling time across all attempts and follow-ups\n- overhead between sampling requests\n- time blocked in the post-sampling tool drain\n- time after the final sampling request\n- sampling request and retry counts\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Extend the existing turn timing state with constant-memory phase\naccounting and one RAII phase guard.\n- Observe sampling and the existing post-sampling drain only at turn\norchestration boundaries.\n- Keep tool runtime, tool futures, response item handling, and turn\nlifecycle values unchanged.\n- Add the profiling fields directly to the existing analytics turn event\nwithout changing app-server protocol or rollout persistence.\n- Use the existing turn `status` to distinguish completed, failed, and\ninterrupted profiles.\n\nExact sampling/tool overlap is intentionally omitted because measuring\ntool completion accurately would require hooks in the tool execution\npath.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Add app-server end-to-end coverage for a single-sampling turn with no\nblocking tool work.\n- Add app-server end-to-end coverage for `request_user_input` blocking\nfollowed by a second sampling request.\n- CI is running on the PR; tests were not executed locally per\nrepository guidance.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T18:27:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d72fb6de92bf332b2ef4a4ccaf992021fbdf4ea","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8d72fb6de92bf332b2ef4a4ccaf992021fbdf4ea","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d72fb6de92bf332b2ef4a4ccaf992021fbdf4ea/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"82b15b65e2303255e3e1a740d994c7e00250344a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/82b15b65e2303255e3e1a740d994c7e00250344a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/82b15b65e2303255e3e1a740d994c7e00250344a"}]},{"sha":"82b15b65e2303255e3e1a740d994c7e00250344a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDgyYjE1YjY1ZTIzMDMyNTVlM2UxYTc0MGQ5OTRjN2UwMDI1MDM0NGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:20:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:20:52Z"},"message":"[codex] Respect Windows sandbox backend in exec policy (#26307)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows managed filesystem permissions can now be backed by a real\nWindows sandbox. `exec-policy` was still treating the managed read-only\npolicy shape as if there were never a sandbox backend, so benign\nunmatched commands such as PowerShell directory listings could be\nrejected with `blocked by policy` even when `windows.sandbox` was\nenabled.\n\nThe inverse case still needs to stay conservative: when the Windows\nsandbox backend is disabled, managed filesystem restrictions are only\nconfiguration intent, not an enforced filesystem boundary. That applies\nto writable-root restricted profiles too, not just read-only profiles.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Thread the effective `WindowsSandboxLevel` into exec-policy approval\ndecisions for shell, unified exec, and intercepted shell exec paths.\n- Treat managed restricted filesystem profiles as lacking sandbox\nprotection only on Windows when `WindowsSandboxLevel::Disabled`.\n- Exclude full-disk-write profiles from that no-backend path because\nthey do not rely on filesystem sandbox enforcement.\n- Remove the cwd-sensitive read-only heuristic and the now-stale cwd\nplumbing from exec-policy approval contexts.\n- Add Windows coverage for both enabled-sandbox and disabled-backend\nbehavior, including a writable-root managed profile.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added/updated `exec_policy` coverage for managed filesystem\nrestrictions, full-disk-write exclusion, enabled Windows sandbox\nbehavior, and disabled-backend read-only/writable-root behavior.\n- `just test -p codex-core exec_policy` — 100 passed, 10 leaky\n- Empirical local `codex exec` probe with `--sandbox read-only -c\n'windows.sandbox=\"unelevated\"'`: PowerShell directory listing completed\nsuccessfully.\n- Disabled-backend control with Windows sandbox cleared: the same\ncommand was rejected with `blocked by policy`.","tree":{"sha":"93faf495da00bc0b165f9325bd34f82e7c0da0f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/93faf495da00bc0b165f9325bd34f82e7c0da0f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/82b15b65e2303255e3e1a740d994c7e00250344a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIxOECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVRcQABsXA3GlJVOIegSkYhW+Nl+O\nXFFbJ34qtCeYjyn2Cf74WmJbhtT9wbJeIQdqdOi2b+lk6TzGGX3WCwHE26ZErYkq\nWyXXm/pp3sYgrbU/CJowLqzFjqVo3Dk/NglOVrFW3l6mvjKZMM0NKWz/n/5pzks/\nhqefLo+ZYS4mAzVV+T7Zuk5eenX2pltSrWgj1Nwb/HOYZ05WlM5VAgIK3Oa1MEav\n7HR355xfth2y+EAscS3StuD4bf2LdGRbsOo5weqXxNSVcrM2eGoYb6gvc42DQn2/\nB/4PcgBfFi4wBo6HFYFAv7q4ATZMOKqK9pRKneljpnQ3Mw+/jiRf9z/PsQ12Qeuy\nE57uPoeGTjrhZAWPrw2gRkj+vxe0iZKZan+iatYQ40CgcnsIEGt1Dbry7fr3GZ8p\nJfmt/SIFSk750UfYntAChFX/LUIr35F+Wdt+bD/x2RoCvBSlMxakQ0wTCE9H25Dw\n5aHKJN4TSxlJhQdjjrgHXs2qn0YRJp3eGZMptw/jzcVddPoeNUeCV8607oP6hK4h\n+vc8w8/KEeB3boD8wOrmggnrZrdQCs9Rd7bj6Fz9mAFDatF5wE/zYk4O8KjNdrGl\nznNlUFQ3gy9wmtbfkl4CGASPTElrVHo28lfRc8+pu2fOs9XnpkHiQg2hFRHuzF4I\nwxG0PA9UzleUaG+nN/ox\n=QB32\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 93faf495da00bc0b165f9325bd34f82e7c0da0f0\nparent 679a944dbcdd5de1e745172268eb9e050d0d6034\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1780683652 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780683652 -0700\n\n[codex] Respect Windows sandbox backend in exec policy (#26307)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows managed filesystem permissions can now be backed by a real\nWindows sandbox. `exec-policy` was still treating the managed read-only\npolicy shape as if there were never a sandbox backend, so benign\nunmatched commands such as PowerShell directory listings could be\nrejected with `blocked by policy` even when `windows.sandbox` was\nenabled.\n\nThe inverse case still needs to stay conservative: when the Windows\nsandbox backend is disabled, managed filesystem restrictions are only\nconfiguration intent, not an enforced filesystem boundary. That applies\nto writable-root restricted profiles too, not just read-only profiles.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Thread the effective `WindowsSandboxLevel` into exec-policy approval\ndecisions for shell, unified exec, and intercepted shell exec paths.\n- Treat managed restricted filesystem profiles as lacking sandbox\nprotection only on Windows when `WindowsSandboxLevel::Disabled`.\n- Exclude full-disk-write profiles from that no-backend path because\nthey do not rely on filesystem sandbox enforcement.\n- Remove the cwd-sensitive read-only heuristic and the now-stale cwd\nplumbing from exec-policy approval contexts.\n- Add Windows coverage for both enabled-sandbox and disabled-backend\nbehavior, including a writable-root managed profile.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added/updated `exec_policy` coverage for managed filesystem\nrestrictions, full-disk-write exclusion, enabled Windows sandbox\nbehavior, and disabled-backend read-only/writable-root behavior.\n- `just test -p codex-core exec_policy` — 100 passed, 10 leaky\n- Empirical local `codex exec` probe with `--sandbox read-only -c\n'windows.sandbox=\"unelevated\"'`: PowerShell directory listing completed\nsuccessfully.\n- Disabled-backend control with Windows sandbox cleared: the same\ncommand was rejected with `blocked by policy`.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T18:20:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/82b15b65e2303255e3e1a740d994c7e00250344a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/82b15b65e2303255e3e1a740d994c7e00250344a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/82b15b65e2303255e3e1a740d994c7e00250344a/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"679a944dbcdd5de1e745172268eb9e050d0d6034","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/679a944dbcdd5de1e745172268eb9e050d0d6034","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/679a944dbcdd5de1e745172268eb9e050d0d6034"}]},{"sha":"679a944dbcdd5de1e745172268eb9e050d0d6034","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY3OWE5NDRkYmNkZDVkZTFlNzQ1MTcyMjY4ZWI5ZTA1MGQwZDYwMzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:10:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:10:13Z"},"message":"fix(tui): restore cancelled prompt cursor at end (#26457)\n\n## Why\n\nPressing `Esc` on a turn that produced no visible output restores the\nsubmitted prompt so the user can keep editing it. That restore path\npreserved the prompt content, images, and mention bindings, but left the\ncomposer cursor at the start of the restored text. The next edit\ntherefore inserted at the beginning instead of continuing from the end\nof the prompt.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Move the cursor to the end after\n`BottomPane::set_composer_text_with_mention_bindings` rehydrates a\nrestored draft.\n- Add test-only cursor accessors so restore tests can assert the\ncomposer state directly.\n- Extend the queued restore regression to assert the restored composer\ncursor is positioned at `text.len()`.\n\n## How to Test\n\nManual reviewer flow:\n\n1. Start Codex in the TUI.\n2. Submit a prompt that will take long enough to interrupt.\n3. Press `Esc` before any visible assistant output appears.\n4. Confirm the prompt is restored into the composer and the cursor is at\nthe end, so typing appends to the prompt.\n5. Repeat with a prompt that includes an attached image or resolved\nmention and confirm the restored content remains intact.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui\nchatwidget::tests::composer_submission::queued_restore_with_remote_images_keeps_local_placeholder_mapping`\n\nLint note:\n\n- `just argument-comment-lint` is blocked locally by the existing Bazel\n`compiler-rt` empty glob failure before analyzing touched code. The\ntouched Rust diff was manually inspected and adds no new opaque\npositional literal callsites.","tree":{"sha":"59e4c7ae0eb2cb627f1c6f20b08144c69dafd7a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/59e4c7ae0eb2cb627f1c6f20b08144c69dafd7a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/679a944dbcdd5de1e745172268eb9e050d0d6034","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIxEFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQfUQAAzhraZiiIiv4h8oHgMiRsdD\nQniCmylzKUZr11F8A5Y5cHF+upo4VeRTBBLoriUW8zMTyD4GlAZYG0+v7avTc723\n6jj1V4ELZw/4X0hESa6cs1T3+COJqrrKfatdytZBYNHF9QGx+9A4njAYR4tKzVFn\nQ1q3eyixaJHWtkP7/c3AmStklZuFGhrTEVCae90/guFsfdqFigx2tcv3uO1rvFvL\nzNTG896WrfQoL+RamKiRLjNudEAcGiSMf8xvYk0jV7aPebvmPCAGBIWPzhC6KRfb\nlvmBo2ET3KmrRuVWuiCVV4xMaouzydyEvFy5PvSpaNqjX8drcRKqImcmQZVz4VO/\nrXcp0YCsS2ylG45mK6YKbRXpPUydOge1aPhOs/RLRHdNDAv8SvSD//dFODMMTvPS\nz6m95rT/l0hzLUZ5eZPdmZNAQPymsZwz3S9jWbKoPFgMDFHtQPFtqOMprNgVDmJ+\n0Gj5W3CqpgDQXyu3yroRqW+YeRB70bLSFXcM5KcOPHowi+nsd+DVK4t2Nszxc3zw\nzPL1uNf1EcqO5CCrrI0YoQAyCy4zgAiukVth2hZlbzeJR0B0hYr/2YOcyYt2PiQ9\nREljnsFo6FDF2YejbZfHzfWiG28450UCjaaC7oGhKUTSganSA1RYUeq1nxnR7fNV\nAdYS9pXSnlHbf+Ig6+Ma\n=zsLf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 59e4c7ae0eb2cb627f1c6f20b08144c69dafd7a3\nparent 713192381b74f09f4b92f3ed410da067461d5cd0\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780683013 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780683013 -0300\n\nfix(tui): restore cancelled prompt cursor at end (#26457)\n\n## Why\n\nPressing `Esc` on a turn that produced no visible output restores the\nsubmitted prompt so the user can keep editing it. That restore path\npreserved the prompt content, images, and mention bindings, but left the\ncomposer cursor at the start of the restored text. The next edit\ntherefore inserted at the beginning instead of continuing from the end\nof the prompt.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Move the cursor to the end after\n`BottomPane::set_composer_text_with_mention_bindings` rehydrates a\nrestored draft.\n- Add test-only cursor accessors so restore tests can assert the\ncomposer state directly.\n- Extend the queued restore regression to assert the restored composer\ncursor is positioned at `text.len()`.\n\n## How to Test\n\nManual reviewer flow:\n\n1. Start Codex in the TUI.\n2. Submit a prompt that will take long enough to interrupt.\n3. Press `Esc` before any visible assistant output appears.\n4. Confirm the prompt is restored into the composer and the cursor is at\nthe end, so typing appends to the prompt.\n5. Repeat with a prompt that includes an attached image or resolved\nmention and confirm the restored content remains intact.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui\nchatwidget::tests::composer_submission::queued_restore_with_remote_images_keeps_local_placeholder_mapping`\n\nLint note:\n\n- `just argument-comment-lint` is blocked locally by the existing Bazel\n`compiler-rt` empty glob failure before analyzing touched code. The\ntouched Rust diff was manually inspected and adds no new opaque\npositional literal callsites.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T18:10:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/679a944dbcdd5de1e745172268eb9e050d0d6034","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/679a944dbcdd5de1e745172268eb9e050d0d6034","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/679a944dbcdd5de1e745172268eb9e050d0d6034/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"713192381b74f09f4b92f3ed410da067461d5cd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/713192381b74f09f4b92f3ed410da067461d5cd0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/713192381b74f09f4b92f3ed410da067461d5cd0"}]},{"sha":"713192381b74f09f4b92f3ed410da067461d5cd0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDcxMzE5MjM4MWI3NGYwOWY0YjkyZjNlZDQxMGRhMDY3NDYxZDVjZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:05:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T18:05:46Z"},"message":"fix(tui): Windows composer background (#26181)\n\n## Why\n\nOn Windows, the TUI could not shade the composer against the terminal\nbackground because `terminal_palette::default_colors()` always fell back\nto `None`. That preserved safety, but it also meant terminals that do\nsupport OSC 10/11 default color replies had no path to report their real\nbackground color.\n\nThis keeps the existing fallback behavior for unsupported terminals\nwhile allowing capable Windows terminals to report their default\nforeground/background colors during startup.\n\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| <img width=\"1235\" height=\"658\" alt=\"win-before\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ff756589-fcb3-43de-8f2a-ebc0369b30dd\"\n/> | <img width=\"1235\" height=\"658\" alt=\"win-after\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9563ff20-4be5-4608-9414-a2afb647e745\"\n/> |\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Moved the OSC 10/11 default color parser in\n`tui/src/terminal_probe.rs` out of the Unix-only implementation so it\ncan be reused by Windows.\n- Added a Windows-only bounded OSC 10/11 probe using raw console handles\nand the existing `windows-sys` dependency.\n- Added Windows palette caching in `tui/src/terminal_palette.rs` so\nstartup probe results, including `None`, are reused instead of probing\nagain later.\n- Wired the Windows color probe into TUI startup after the existing\nnon-Unix crossterm cursor and keyboard checks.\n- Added parser coverage for malformed, partial, and noisy OSC color\nreplies.\n\nIf the probe fails, times out, receives only one color, or receives\nmalformed data, the cache stores `None` and the composer keeps the\ncurrent behavior.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. On Windows, start Codex in a terminal that supports OSC 10/11 default\ncolor replies.\n2. Open the TUI composer.\n3. Confirm the composer/status area is painted using the terminal's\nreported default background, instead of leaving the background unshaded.\n4. Start Codex in a terminal that does not answer OSC 10/11, or\notherwise blocks terminal color replies.\n5. Confirm startup still succeeds and the composer uses the existing\nfallback behavior.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/private/tmp/codex-windows-osc-default-colors-target\njust test -p codex-tui terminal_probe`\n\nAdditional local verification:\n\n- `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/private/tmp/codex-windows-osc-default-colors-target\njust test -p codex-tui` was run; 2774 tests passed, and two unrelated\nGuardian feature-flag tests failed reproducibly when isolated.\n- `just argument-comment-lint` was attempted but blocked by the local\nBazel/LLVM `include/sanitizer/*.h` empty glob issue. Touched Rust\nliteral callsites were inspected manually.\n- `cargo check -p codex-tui --target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` was\nattempted after installing the target, but local macOS cross-checking is\nblocked by missing Windows C SDK headers in native dependencies\n(`ring`/`aws-lc-sys`).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kevin Bond <kbond@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cd256da678df8aef97674c214b1ac97ab01b73b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9cd256da678df8aef97674c214b1ac97ab01b73b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/713192381b74f09f4b92f3ed410da067461d5cd0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIw/6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQCkQADqI7dPAx+Vpe2moSrJDVPfs\n6p7RA0nYFKkghDKNNLs2s5CxXwCVK+WELXpb7bN0Oc75WAm/owYhdsMYOpOYBaW2\ngc8JjrNGECDO3PdjheHxl7WOnRDauxO+oDl+CsS3Abg2oI9VcopfSJruQj6Mhpmh\nZtnYl1UsBgQFV5dsueyME+SpgFKm9XvXSLSAvlvImXV7ed5HeEIBYpanR2xFtZw9\nkSa/6sJvCtu76ojwgmupPqivAKMtGze4MAMo3hOCiR4anXNMd1xGeShjXy7P+YFx\n/GB209tOjtBCNPXlX5n5jo/bKe5RtsITzUrdikke2d+7hPcC8L0ITJ9dS+yxCQON\ndaxf9rcPvWPBepkZsb8sgG6YfUFHfcnSxtAU7/Tf8Z/1QKgNu2FmsIT5kA2npHEE\nV9QG54W7WZIE6HTKf61QCdvU2flAy4d+vn94FW0LLBytY68HsHNWpdLfWLK3VraA\nopbFUSTI8V0azWAo6sDBOU1VflNEdEblXJB8J10DqDZYQZkHQePhgdPBlTWqxD7z\nblxaLbakvKhD9sUmwqHX7VxLjp+NxrmCyuP5wHzog454T0AbrpUxhU2KJJkhRtIh\n6KORdJxTCD7cZGyt51LMgtSSLGfTuS8hZXP2ACvOqdfN8luwuOGTO2FJzoQJ3v7w\nBagqUVATR1aEMAGkl5Ca\n=qDwg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9cd256da678df8aef97674c214b1ac97ab01b73b\nparent a8c95309111f1bb8b4864102a306d7e60a729ad0\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780682746 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780682746 -0700\n\nfix(tui): Windows composer background (#26181)\n\n## Why\n\nOn Windows, the TUI could not shade the composer against the terminal\nbackground because `terminal_palette::default_colors()` always fell back\nto `None`. That preserved safety, but it also meant terminals that do\nsupport OSC 10/11 default color replies had no path to report their real\nbackground color.\n\nThis keeps the existing fallback behavior for unsupported terminals\nwhile allowing capable Windows terminals to report their default\nforeground/background colors during startup.\n\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| <img width=\"1235\" height=\"658\" alt=\"win-before\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ff756589-fcb3-43de-8f2a-ebc0369b30dd\"\n/> | <img width=\"1235\" height=\"658\" alt=\"win-after\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9563ff20-4be5-4608-9414-a2afb647e745\"\n/> |\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Moved the OSC 10/11 default color parser in\n`tui/src/terminal_probe.rs` out of the Unix-only implementation so it\ncan be reused by Windows.\n- Added a Windows-only bounded OSC 10/11 probe using raw console handles\nand the existing `windows-sys` dependency.\n- Added Windows palette caching in `tui/src/terminal_palette.rs` so\nstartup probe results, including `None`, are reused instead of probing\nagain later.\n- Wired the Windows color probe into TUI startup after the existing\nnon-Unix crossterm cursor and keyboard checks.\n- Added parser coverage for malformed, partial, and noisy OSC color\nreplies.\n\nIf the probe fails, times out, receives only one color, or receives\nmalformed data, the cache stores `None` and the composer keeps the\ncurrent behavior.\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. On Windows, start Codex in a terminal that supports OSC 10/11 default\ncolor replies.\n2. Open the TUI composer.\n3. Confirm the composer/status area is painted using the terminal's\nreported default background, instead of leaving the background unshaded.\n4. Start Codex in a terminal that does not answer OSC 10/11, or\notherwise blocks terminal color replies.\n5. Confirm startup still succeeds and the composer uses the existing\nfallback behavior.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/private/tmp/codex-windows-osc-default-colors-target\njust test -p codex-tui terminal_probe`\n\nAdditional local verification:\n\n- `CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/private/tmp/codex-windows-osc-default-colors-target\njust test -p codex-tui` was run; 2774 tests passed, and two unrelated\nGuardian feature-flag tests failed reproducibly when isolated.\n- `just argument-comment-lint` was attempted but blocked by the local\nBazel/LLVM `include/sanitizer/*.h` empty glob issue. Touched Rust\nliteral callsites were inspected manually.\n- `cargo check -p codex-tui --target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` was\nattempted after installing the target, but local macOS cross-checking is\nblocked by missing Windows C SDK headers in native dependencies\n(`ring`/`aws-lc-sys`).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Kevin Bond <kbond@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-05T18:05:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/713192381b74f09f4b92f3ed410da067461d5cd0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/713192381b74f09f4b92f3ed410da067461d5cd0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/713192381b74f09f4b92f3ed410da067461d5cd0/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a8c95309111f1bb8b4864102a306d7e60a729ad0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a8c95309111f1bb8b4864102a306d7e60a729ad0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a8c95309111f1bb8b4864102a306d7e60a729ad0"}]},{"sha":"a8c95309111f1bb8b4864102a306d7e60a729ad0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE4Yzk1MzA5MTExZjFiYjhiNDg2NDEwMmEzMDZkN2U2MGE3MjlhZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:37:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:37:38Z"},"message":"[1 of 2] Align goal extension with core behavior (#26547)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#26547](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26547) - [1 of 2] Align\ngoal extension with core behavior\n2. [#26548](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26548) - [2 of 2] Move\ngoal runtime to extension\n\n## Why\n\nThe goal runtime is moving out of `codex-core` and into\n`codex-goal-extension`. This first PR brings the extension back in line\nwith the current core behavior before the follow-up PR switches\napp-server sessions over to the extension, so that review can focus on\nownership and wiring rather than hidden behavior drift.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Updates the extension `create_goal` and `update_goal` tool\nschemas/descriptions to match the current core wording for explicit\ntoken budgets, blocked-goal audits, resumed blocked goals, and\nsystem-owned budget/usage-limit transitions.\n- Marks `codex-goal-extension` as the live `/goal` extension crate\nrather than an unwired sketch.\n- Looks up the live thread before reading goal state for idle\ncontinuation, so continuation setup exits early when no live thread can\naccept the automatic turn.","tree":{"sha":"bc5421deaf2914ac781bb9a87321c850a9328517","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bc5421deaf2914ac781bb9a87321c850a9328517"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a8c95309111f1bb8b4864102a306d7e60a729ad0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIwliCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3M4QAIng3TNXk/gO6E4UA+0MiiF8\nzIkTpfaoZEwJI/LkTDEHrRhRB4xxBkhyylCcikSiHIGiWiyRDS2cvPzcZ+Pe00bd\nBGt9mOtHGrNup8XTlhgBiv4gn2Mri7n2LHu73NWFGdR8WyCTU9nMnoplEDZo/WAB\nRdPmY895rxLlozSeFaMh2X1jlFTr1I39njKUmKDxnnAFd2LK6fk73TCT7DP/0t8v\nXdsDiB3P3r4i+gnYQb16e+lAeMqqueUe0Gc1eUAW1D43aLiwlmsSa1mvurxggccf\nowyEcwUS7pVS7mHGnKU+SBAlVLgQzJ5mZv3TsP2/sZ8orTGarYEY7mlKfsyTDP1c\nrPW1WZOHyWfy8OxhEzyt4p8vKizQvKNjmT7qhY7/54nVeNTb6xaNjklhVTbn+6+V\nXxL/NCl7Rkg76O+DCfkX5OHZ+dd1oDyP91iZoTsiMnFqONB4quBbeZ/Zo8I6NePo\nooolMBmXHnAF0Kdc3gG8Q9fkmwR+nV70uvonanJOOSMxkp/XnxrTjLQ92vArpyUf\nqH3iBh0LNwF6G/kA1JtqXMA0wkY9hcn06Z9vMJMkPo2Umc4EPYcy/laws6Khv8O/\novQCzyuSGD2G4Ly0JSVu37cTjzHf8yvpaGrDrmJmLwQw6mcbSOS8CstTQ+RDlvd1\nmYocKNWRz4KPLatJ+qsS\n=XHhg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bc5421deaf2914ac781bb9a87321c850a9328517\nparent 78eba34b4148ec14493684ffc3a866415cbbbbd1\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780681058 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780681058 -0700\n\n[1 of 2] Align goal extension with core behavior (#26547)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#26547](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26547) - [1 of 2] Align\ngoal extension with core behavior\n2. [#26548](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26548) - [2 of 2] Move\ngoal runtime to extension\n\n## Why\n\nThe goal runtime is moving out of `codex-core` and into\n`codex-goal-extension`. This first PR brings the extension back in line\nwith the current core behavior before the follow-up PR switches\napp-server sessions over to the extension, so that review can focus on\nownership and wiring rather than hidden behavior drift.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Updates the extension `create_goal` and `update_goal` tool\nschemas/descriptions to match the current core wording for explicit\ntoken budgets, blocked-goal audits, resumed blocked goals, and\nsystem-owned budget/usage-limit transitions.\n- Marks `codex-goal-extension` as the live `/goal` extension crate\nrather than an unwired sketch.\n- Looks up the live thread before reading goal state for idle\ncontinuation, so continuation setup exits early when no live thread can\naccept the automatic turn.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T17:37:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a8c95309111f1bb8b4864102a306d7e60a729ad0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a8c95309111f1bb8b4864102a306d7e60a729ad0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a8c95309111f1bb8b4864102a306d7e60a729ad0/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"78eba34b4148ec14493684ffc3a866415cbbbbd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/78eba34b4148ec14493684ffc3a866415cbbbbd1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/78eba34b4148ec14493684ffc3a866415cbbbbd1"}]},{"sha":"78eba34b4148ec14493684ffc3a866415cbbbbd1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc4ZWJhMzRiNDE0OGVjMTQ0OTM2ODRmZmMzYTg2NjQxNWNiYmJiZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:36:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:36:14Z"},"message":"Clean up Rust release workflow (#26335)\n\n## Why\nPR #26252 moved macOS release signing into the tag-triggered\n`rust-release` workflow through the protected `codesigning` environment\nand Azure Key Vault. That leaves the old manual unsigned-build /\nsigned-promotion handoff as dead compatibility scaffolding: it makes the\nrelease DAG harder to reason about and keeps paths around that the\ncurrent release process no longer intends to operate.\n\n## What changed\n- Remove the manual `workflow_dispatch` inputs and validation for\n`build_unsigned`, `promote_signed`, and the deprecated `sign_macos`\nflag.\n- Drop the `stage-signed-macos` job and the promotion-specific artifact\ndownload, re-upload, pruning, and cleanup logic.\n- Make tag-pushed releases always follow the signed release path: build,\nsign, package, finalize, publish, and then run downstream release jobs\nfrom `release` success.\n- Remove stale `SIGN_MACOS` / `sign_macos` conditions and outputs,\nincluding downstream gates for npm, DotSlash, WinGet, dev website\ndeploy, and `latest-alpha-cli` branch updates.\n\n## Verification\n- `ruby -e 'require \"yaml\"; YAML.load_file(ARGV.fetch(0)); puts \"yaml\nok\"' .github/workflows/rust-release.yml`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `rg -n\n\"workflow_dispatch|inputs\\\\.|release_mode|build_unsigned|SIGN_MACOS|outputs\\\\.sign_macos|sign_macos\\\\b\"\n.github/workflows/rust-release.yml` returned no matches","tree":{"sha":"a7cc8a830d80fefe4da4591161a9d7756d17ef39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a7cc8a830d80fefe4da4591161a9d7756d17ef39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/78eba34b4148ec14493684ffc3a866415cbbbbd1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIwkOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWWgQAE8PvsR0lSEiBw1OW4IB0ZH0\nPXMfeEB2Db5AVrf8ja/Cwda+1Y32NhPE0od94RWtFsxWHp+vpSGtZfM9htufpTks\nl8bC/SMmYSJ/ZsQT8To+wMCGCvrereb65GUWLB1ptYpSmEORcrxzn4RZWSq11moZ\n6SY6MvuWNmYDsH7UWHnLDwMW/vfRW4kWRzQCMiiLlQTFsQtkzRKO/gglSEuUV4wf\nuqUGVOSuKg/XXDUI9k4Agm9PqIa+XE+2eZmmXhHv5gslwE2J6TzoEdlNW1XbTqL0\nxNDYzwHVT7N1UUvanHGWdN8HPWKyqPWHOoeZWqAed4TKWfyqC/5q+XCVeDdH16D0\nMoqN4GWneTl+Jjbsw1qq/oIGEb8VXBZ/dz6zs7gpdezXdlFoXleeDC5yW1p0YfXp\nUHLA2OwLFdf0kfc6T/0CdSAA50EeOgyEcgkql4nUD0Udp01H+A759GIWO+wlQttU\nDkiKwEFwQLl2nQvasSFsxzpocYOQq05yiKqO2t+yavGPJE/LKs3AmuUg5fXFL5n0\nJ9kpukYv5VjMGCxXdk2mbMl3d/2mvZCPBdnzxdJ0GhdRjBjKT3S0dEPn0LDXjFj5\nqEN557Q0A6Secf1Am7o3jTYEaxIJyUn9XuW+8tPU/4QvcMmpuC7RdlkSJqRl+VE7\ne/KYWGMv6nG/cd9gqqNB\n=aO50\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a7cc8a830d80fefe4da4591161a9d7756d17ef39\nparent 0177231ca055955bd553ac5f57d59f5df9639dd4\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1780680974 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780680974 -0700\n\nClean up Rust release workflow (#26335)\n\n## Why\nPR #26252 moved macOS release signing into the tag-triggered\n`rust-release` workflow through the protected `codesigning` environment\nand Azure Key Vault. That leaves the old manual unsigned-build /\nsigned-promotion handoff as dead compatibility scaffolding: it makes the\nrelease DAG harder to reason about and keeps paths around that the\ncurrent release process no longer intends to operate.\n\n## What changed\n- Remove the manual `workflow_dispatch` inputs and validation for\n`build_unsigned`, `promote_signed`, and the deprecated `sign_macos`\nflag.\n- Drop the `stage-signed-macos` job and the promotion-specific artifact\ndownload, re-upload, pruning, and cleanup logic.\n- Make tag-pushed releases always follow the signed release path: build,\nsign, package, finalize, publish, and then run downstream release jobs\nfrom `release` success.\n- Remove stale `SIGN_MACOS` / `sign_macos` conditions and outputs,\nincluding downstream gates for npm, DotSlash, WinGet, dev website\ndeploy, and `latest-alpha-cli` branch updates.\n\n## Verification\n- `ruby -e 'require \"yaml\"; YAML.load_file(ARGV.fetch(0)); puts \"yaml\nok\"' .github/workflows/rust-release.yml`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `rg -n\n\"workflow_dispatch|inputs\\\\.|release_mode|build_unsigned|SIGN_MACOS|outputs\\\\.sign_macos|sign_macos\\\\b\"\n.github/workflows/rust-release.yml` returned no matches","verified_at":"2026-06-05T17:36:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/78eba34b4148ec14493684ffc3a866415cbbbbd1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/78eba34b4148ec14493684ffc3a866415cbbbbd1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/78eba34b4148ec14493684ffc3a866415cbbbbd1/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0177231ca055955bd553ac5f57d59f5df9639dd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0177231ca055955bd553ac5f57d59f5df9639dd4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0177231ca055955bd553ac5f57d59f5df9639dd4"}]},{"sha":"0177231ca055955bd553ac5f57d59f5df9639dd4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDAxNzcyMzFjYTA1NTk1NWJkNTUzYWM1ZjU3ZDU5ZjVkZjk2MzlkZDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"hefuc-oai","email":"hefuc@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:33:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:33:56Z"},"message":"feat(app-server): add remote control pairing status RPC (#26450)\n\n## What\n\nExposes the pairing status transport as experimental app-server v2 RPC\n`remoteControl/pairing/status`.\n\n- Adds request/response protocol types for exactly one lookup key:\n`pairingCode` or `manualPairingCode`, returning `{ claimed }`.\n- Registers the RPC with `global_shared_read(\"remote-control-pairing\")`.\n- Wires the method through `MessageProcessor` and\n`RemoteControlRequestProcessor`.\n- Validates missing/conflicting pairing-code params as invalid requests.\n- Documents the RPC in `app-server/README.md`.\n- Adds processor, protocol export, and JSON-RPC integration coverage for\nboth code paths.\n\n## Why\n\nThis is the app-server surface the desktop app can poll while the\nQR/manual pairing modal is active.\n\nDepends on https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26449\nRelated backend change: https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/990244\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test --manifest-path app-server-protocol/Cargo.toml\nremote_control`\n- `cargo test --manifest-path app-server/Cargo.toml remote_control`\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"2c6679643b978b10f21f4a4a1f79bf9bd36eb896","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2c6679643b978b10f21f4a4a1f79bf9bd36eb896"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0177231ca055955bd553ac5f57d59f5df9639dd4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIwiECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqbQQAA5b8X+cuhKcFgWFgu647fkz\n7VN+PB5XIqfqWkX0qEICxNdo0ajYO6X373xs8uRGWH3HS0gsb4dup3PFnvBmvXAC\nXzxcxqGVJtby/aLdUbLS19QnxPF7Tp1qHpifXlwtzY+rvhr9c0qbbdIu0IjBjao1\nW1toS+Wy8mHKyfKdqq/Uei6XZEQz1YyuQMJmowx2KBHM7rFe6HNaSOXIWbHqdBF+\nabpcTiW7xAoM6RdRhe1sqt/dEyRs4vTmSEEUWh7+iuyujDkPL1aKx5uyqDiNlboS\nlaw2FdSFq8cBgAejEtCm3/Fw7BI2I40Lmmtw7UmzGr86bukJwPrPl6Yy14G7e/ux\ny7aGm66KPbxoiXAsnnSQI54j/ojwZjtFCCgFRBKNYEFzPd2FLa7Qrwk+kbgDO/Gs\n1pB2fwZ+MwiuvbIWqeE5WdNv0wycJGj9rAL6k6CiZ6C6AcovXaWe4KsQwCD+itxJ\nuubdLA04LbV60DVCpSLO5r/EpZJ5uBD2/NvjCnmK90ZuNzavbtCj3BOZdx6yMP0Y\nl+yzkGjmY93rUtvNLaKGH4ADW7Rsk1z+Vdvsjh9E5sAGyRBVOmvklfC8sWDTmz1V\nhSa63rW1Xw9YBhDFDQl7svrccr9RElk4FnSPFjBvtoE+Kmtaz5IYYdPPMLBHRQFS\ndc1qoqe+2mkkpddqGclH\n=TJOU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2c6679643b978b10f21f4a4a1f79bf9bd36eb896\nparent 841f057f2d2647441cfd3fa586f3f5d06f89d599\nauthor hefuc-oai <hefuc@openai.com> 1780680836 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780680836 -0700\n\nfeat(app-server): add remote control pairing status RPC (#26450)\n\n## What\n\nExposes the pairing status transport as experimental app-server v2 RPC\n`remoteControl/pairing/status`.\n\n- Adds request/response protocol types for exactly one lookup key:\n`pairingCode` or `manualPairingCode`, returning `{ claimed }`.\n- Registers the RPC with `global_shared_read(\"remote-control-pairing\")`.\n- Wires the method through `MessageProcessor` and\n`RemoteControlRequestProcessor`.\n- Validates missing/conflicting pairing-code params as invalid requests.\n- Documents the RPC in `app-server/README.md`.\n- Adds processor, protocol export, and JSON-RPC integration coverage for\nboth code paths.\n\n## Why\n\nThis is the app-server surface the desktop app can poll while the\nQR/manual pairing modal is active.\n\nDepends on https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/26449\nRelated backend change: https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/990244\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test --manifest-path app-server-protocol/Cargo.toml\nremote_control`\n- `cargo test --manifest-path app-server/Cargo.toml remote_control`\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T17:33:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0177231ca055955bd553ac5f57d59f5df9639dd4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0177231ca055955bd553ac5f57d59f5df9639dd4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0177231ca055955bd553ac5f57d59f5df9639dd4/comments","author":{"login":"hefuc-oai","id":289792942,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUXjrg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289792942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/hefuc-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"841f057f2d2647441cfd3fa586f3f5d06f89d599","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/841f057f2d2647441cfd3fa586f3f5d06f89d599","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/841f057f2d2647441cfd3fa586f3f5d06f89d599"}]},{"sha":"841f057f2d2647441cfd3fa586f3f5d06f89d599","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg0MWYwNTdmMmQyNjQ3NDQxY2ZkM2ZhNTg2ZjNmNWQwNmY4OWQ1OTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:33:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:33:31Z"},"message":"fix(tui): avoid doubled blank rows while streaming (#26636)\n\n## Summary\n\nDuring assistant-message streaming, blank markdown lines in the\ntransient active tail were prefixed with two spaces. Ratatui measured\nthose whitespace-only lines as two viewport rows, so list- and\ntable-heavy answers showed doubled vertical gaps while streaming and\nthen visibly compacted when finalized into scrollback.\n\n- keep whitespace-only `StreamingAgentTailCell` lines structurally empty\nwhile preserving nonblank message prefixes\n- clear impossible hyperlink metadata when normalizing a blank tail line\n- add an inline snapshot and height regression proving one blank\nmarkdown line occupies one viewport row\n\nRelated to #26618, but fixes a separate live-tail row-height issue\nrather than stale committed markdown content.\n\n## How to Test\n\nRecommended before/after reproduction:\n\n1. Start the latest Codex build without this change.\n2. Submit this exact prompt:\n\n> Send 20 different lists: bullets vs numbered, simple vs complex with\nparagraphs in between items, etc. Intertwine them with some tables and\nsome paragraphs.\n\n3. While the answer streams, observe duplicated vertical gaps around\nlist items and paragraphs. When the answer finishes, observe the spacing\ncompact.\n4. Start this branch with `just c` and submit the same prompt.\n5. Confirm each intended blank markdown line occupies one terminal row\nthroughout streaming and that the spacing does not compact or jump when\nthe answer finishes.\n6. As a focused regression, verify the sections after the first table,\nespecially loose lists with paragraphs between items; those blank rows\nshould remain stable throughout streaming.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui\nstreaming_agent_tail_blank_line_uses_one_viewport_row`\n- `just test -p codex-tui history_cell::tests`\n\n## Test Notes\n\n- Verified the exact prompt above in a real tmux TUI using latest Codex\nand this branch as the before/after comparison.\n- The full `just test -p codex-tui` run completed 2,782 of 2,784 tests\nsuccessfully. Two unrelated guardian feature-flag tests fail\nreproducibly in isolation because the expected `OverrideTurnContext`\nmessage is absent.\n- `just argument-comment-lint` is blocked locally by the existing Bazel\n`compiler-rt` missing-header glob error; the touched Rust diff was\ninspected manually for opaque positional literals.","tree":{"sha":"9c74d07bb34c901e05f59e7364b1f64c13ff8c37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9c74d07bb34c901e05f59e7364b1f64c13ff8c37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/841f057f2d2647441cfd3fa586f3f5d06f89d599","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIwhrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAewcQAF7suwxTT/KKP7sU7Tp+p+xG\nK8vNtH6f/jgDy6yEH0Ujf/SIdWIIik9hqn/rFADHqMKzibsH8/m8BQVpHt1R1qa6\nKFULqcvGEzNdgAjEZ/0IPQmtR7LVpZkehTJ5f6VrUEbbYU4+EAA1yHCoiFhnZf+t\nj/A9zItsSYqDwJgKEe7UnZq2tLo+6GHzuTnEiKIvf2wAylfKd4+PXiKWdCL5DGLV\nZSIHl4y1tJFhc1LLuR5tLpsKopcDUDD/SfHREPWCFXGR/zfRCs1rnmZxT/8YCznd\nB+yvI+P68wVi53DyFq2IG0DpI9hMgQEqygrbqv0T78OfMBSZErD5Mlh3aQ8qFNg5\nJUEodhuu/6BCQdHttZMsiG1tnGHxTNE/u1k+cs7wNiNSOnyjP56+6h6MDNY3ETCu\nAreSKKOhd/MIerLQfl5Q799xv0UAbRe0uxCAWeV34tDVOPGGgCeUuKIUxpujABpP\nCH8YjqPeaAtnEgMNkvUCAiNWNXdW31nU6bGjMl5AhL781AMqdhJeqrpowrZ0YWTM\nxooRq7yWQfiS/mGMUr8PfIWkSmHnLTYrexRU04vho6kCFBDZQNvnoAc+wQT0sE6b\n+LiOFbgT+QSYahEOFfC5fmKPcWOnR4GdIOVgQSjDP4+T4kjyv41WH4o8T1zPeQ4n\nkts/wUxkqO6H36J+plqC\n=cNql\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9c74d07bb34c901e05f59e7364b1f64c13ff8c37\nparent 86a1ddd0282f83f21d2e5743ffd1d6ba36725ed1\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780680811 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780680811 -0300\n\nfix(tui): avoid doubled blank rows while streaming (#26636)\n\n## Summary\n\nDuring assistant-message streaming, blank markdown lines in the\ntransient active tail were prefixed with two spaces. Ratatui measured\nthose whitespace-only lines as two viewport rows, so list- and\ntable-heavy answers showed doubled vertical gaps while streaming and\nthen visibly compacted when finalized into scrollback.\n\n- keep whitespace-only `StreamingAgentTailCell` lines structurally empty\nwhile preserving nonblank message prefixes\n- clear impossible hyperlink metadata when normalizing a blank tail line\n- add an inline snapshot and height regression proving one blank\nmarkdown line occupies one viewport row\n\nRelated to #26618, but fixes a separate live-tail row-height issue\nrather than stale committed markdown content.\n\n## How to Test\n\nRecommended before/after reproduction:\n\n1. Start the latest Codex build without this change.\n2. Submit this exact prompt:\n\n> Send 20 different lists: bullets vs numbered, simple vs complex with\nparagraphs in between items, etc. Intertwine them with some tables and\nsome paragraphs.\n\n3. While the answer streams, observe duplicated vertical gaps around\nlist items and paragraphs. When the answer finishes, observe the spacing\ncompact.\n4. Start this branch with `just c` and submit the same prompt.\n5. Confirm each intended blank markdown line occupies one terminal row\nthroughout streaming and that the spacing does not compact or jump when\nthe answer finishes.\n6. As a focused regression, verify the sections after the first table,\nespecially loose lists with paragraphs between items; those blank rows\nshould remain stable throughout streaming.\n\nTargeted tests:\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui\nstreaming_agent_tail_blank_line_uses_one_viewport_row`\n- `just test -p codex-tui history_cell::tests`\n\n## Test Notes\n\n- Verified the exact prompt above in a real tmux TUI using latest Codex\nand this branch as the before/after comparison.\n- The full `just test -p codex-tui` run completed 2,782 of 2,784 tests\nsuccessfully. Two unrelated guardian feature-flag tests fail\nreproducibly in isolation because the expected `OverrideTurnContext`\nmessage is absent.\n- `just argument-comment-lint` is blocked locally by the existing Bazel\n`compiler-rt` missing-header glob error; the touched Rust diff was\ninspected manually for opaque positional literals.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T17:33:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/841f057f2d2647441cfd3fa586f3f5d06f89d599","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/841f057f2d2647441cfd3fa586f3f5d06f89d599","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/841f057f2d2647441cfd3fa586f3f5d06f89d599/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"86a1ddd0282f83f21d2e5743ffd1d6ba36725ed1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/86a1ddd0282f83f21d2e5743ffd1d6ba36725ed1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/86a1ddd0282f83f21d2e5743ffd1d6ba36725ed1"}]},{"sha":"86a1ddd0282f83f21d2e5743ffd1d6ba36725ed1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg2YTFkZGQwMjgyZjgzZjIxZDJlNTc0M2ZmZDFkNmJhMzY3MjVlZDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:31:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:31:22Z"},"message":"Make turn diff tracker multi-env aware (#26433)\n\n## Why\n\nTurn diffs were tracked as one flat set of absolute paths. In\nmulti-environment turns, local and remote environments can report the\nsame path while representing different filesystems, so a single path key\ncan collapse distinct changes or attribute them to the wrong\nenvironment.\n\nThe environment name is **NOT** included in the generated unified diff.\nThis can come later.","tree":{"sha":"d65c049a5867794b30be02b4f3fbc322036aeac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d65c049a5867794b30be02b4f3fbc322036aeac2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/86a1ddd0282f83f21d2e5743ffd1d6ba36725ed1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIwfqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1uIQAA/G/7JjtRMWtGdXbvTpqgaq\nx3WDFHnPCLpxy4QeSMPFi4ykpKwAK/lYKvY8Wm83rtFGRWDZC77WJy/BgUI/Ldk3\nx6QJnBXgHKlxQ0kgyAdWcl/Tul6VFjFYe3BYSnt5ICfeqa6Y5DCCcberdWOFSojS\nWi0k7OUdnPcX2GgqcAzXrBNBuz1Ni9xHrsW8jWNxUBLr2T7BrASKKZ5Ojv05aAGe\nCNFdrtSLdj5cPUmCXzN6EM33x9DgGHq0N5Ce3zh0MH6RZUEKuwpPlyxk7fY09s+g\nx2ingwgIojjkI25BmuC9qkVqBYWbfDeL1G8o4oDgRqxgg4RfSypoy8fP2mhpucg/\nnw+yGGoFFCZWa0FcNiVEjymDbqMHD574UVjJbUil/yt7l4R5BI3fMKkYCvrg7CSl\nkyabaBh4cczNjH161sszqng+U6KOIAIjIn+O0fP817z2HJdyeu6If2Y5i7VIhrhW\nRcpA5SZsaODrPy6NsI0Jgw2YM5z7K+KAJog+79EvRrJR+nBtWWjyjanD1ZK1x+RL\nXWPYje/pmMas7lKhaPc/aBbjr9W2ME0gcVc+ICxvk9l3gtQLgifIzF47+vuG3lgu\nrmOvTfMcbSiyOvpD2YGS2F0Ybe8cwCNTMRZ9ztoLf9mLVn3kCx6xBhVO3L2V2iFR\nn462Vp6qJ3PYCPrTmZB1\n=EN3j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d65c049a5867794b30be02b4f3fbc322036aeac2\nparent da490ba9de80bf83ad04f8db4cf72b793e99967f\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780680682 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780680682 +0000\n\nMake turn diff tracker multi-env aware (#26433)\n\n## Why\n\nTurn diffs were tracked as one flat set of absolute paths. In\nmulti-environment turns, local and remote environments can report the\nsame path while representing different filesystems, so a single path key\ncan collapse distinct changes or attribute them to the wrong\nenvironment.\n\nThe environment name is **NOT** included in the generated unified diff.\nThis can come later.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T17:31:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/86a1ddd0282f83f21d2e5743ffd1d6ba36725ed1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/86a1ddd0282f83f21d2e5743ffd1d6ba36725ed1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/86a1ddd0282f83f21d2e5743ffd1d6ba36725ed1/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"da490ba9de80bf83ad04f8db4cf72b793e99967f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/da490ba9de80bf83ad04f8db4cf72b793e99967f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/da490ba9de80bf83ad04f8db4cf72b793e99967f"}]},{"sha":"da490ba9de80bf83ad04f8db4cf72b793e99967f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRhNDkwYmE5ZGU4MGJmODNhZDA0ZjhkYjRjZjcyYjc5M2U5OTk2N2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"hefuc-oai","email":"hefuc@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:07:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T17:07:25Z"},"message":"feat(remote-control): add pairing status transport (#26449)\n\n## What\n\nAdds transport support for checking remote-control pairing status\nagainst the backend.\n\n- Adds the normalized `server/pair/status` backend URL.\n- Adds backend request/response structs for exactly one lookup key:\n`pairing_code` or `manual_pairing_code`, returning `{ claimed }`.\n- Adds `RemoteControlEnrollment::pairing_status` and\n`RemoteControlHandle::pairing_status`.\n- Preserves auth refresh/retry behavior and backend error mapping.\n- Adds transport coverage for pending, claimed, manual-code payloads,\ntoken refresh, mapped backend errors, malformed responses, and URL\nnormalization.\n\n## Why\n\nDesktop needs a host-authenticated way to poll whether a QR or manual\npairing code has been claimed.\n\nRelated backend change: https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/990244\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test --manifest-path app-server-transport/Cargo.toml\nremote_control::tests::pairing_tests`\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"13397b76bba71be8324f60eabd55621578a890fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/13397b76bba71be8324f60eabd55621578a890fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/da490ba9de80bf83ad04f8db4cf72b793e99967f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIwJNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAF+cQAK68PnOylNacaDN2mZ6amoTB\njbo9oLH56HvKHgToZITaBtw0OMBjXY0ASwCuW2RhtqQfICExyzUtz7ITTHP3LepE\ngXTB0Y8lpJsp83/tlTEWzmyYk/myIDbFOTV4xseYmxaHQ/Gs4u5ZaYtqR4Q3wNYX\notGRyb/ntTD525aJwYWBN4S6Oej3hfjbB58eE5GFaNtM8VcNYgUekb1nVNPALL+A\nMnM2a+HXjmyMqVkKKnD+kusdHFLa1NZKLg7KfJ+Zmz70/Nrvx/OziQmfjrGO59Mp\nXYhvrmd/XVaFYHAzxKF1/K0uXYZ/Ufw7bLZb5ceHoNKxw+PuMuEW7vrWQnc2daAX\nkqKi9Qzyejn7DHgr6YcS8HW+uAIeCvjcsHUftQRMgptx9iZXbUNwE+2bbTAB82Di\nc638v5O8y5VYfgl92CQykxsR+ECK9dRTCHJniZ7/cR6wDSoDmM3LOInsOoiwFW9K\nXDZNYcz5I5K+cwGX2nnwRfDbGsMycLNtnjO1+ewnYp9xW6s7FJ3d3mpo4l+vr4z5\nk3QFZvHAvm2F568+74eoAcokkrdla8IB9RKmp+mDP74ASTcFxlFUMEz6Mi1aq4F4\n/37sHlvbJY2SU4MP67GbYMpp36ivdRY6akjS1p5lfECBK6cKcZtul6W5iV0+HC2+\nA5C3rD6v2/hJwlp2lsWe\n=2cBA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 13397b76bba71be8324f60eabd55621578a890fa\nparent 9ddb1de633bde6d3d3e9b8012f822eb447db5195\nauthor hefuc-oai <hefuc@openai.com> 1780679245 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780679245 -0700\n\nfeat(remote-control): add pairing status transport (#26449)\n\n## What\n\nAdds transport support for checking remote-control pairing status\nagainst the backend.\n\n- Adds the normalized `server/pair/status` backend URL.\n- Adds backend request/response structs for exactly one lookup key:\n`pairing_code` or `manual_pairing_code`, returning `{ claimed }`.\n- Adds `RemoteControlEnrollment::pairing_status` and\n`RemoteControlHandle::pairing_status`.\n- Preserves auth refresh/retry behavior and backend error mapping.\n- Adds transport coverage for pending, claimed, manual-code payloads,\ntoken refresh, mapped backend errors, malformed responses, and URL\nnormalization.\n\n## Why\n\nDesktop needs a host-authenticated way to poll whether a QR or manual\npairing code has been claimed.\n\nRelated backend change: https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/990244\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test --manifest-path app-server-transport/Cargo.toml\nremote_control::tests::pairing_tests`\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T17:07:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/da490ba9de80bf83ad04f8db4cf72b793e99967f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/da490ba9de80bf83ad04f8db4cf72b793e99967f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/da490ba9de80bf83ad04f8db4cf72b793e99967f/comments","author":{"login":"hefuc-oai","id":289792942,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUXjrg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289792942?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/hefuc-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hefuc-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9ddb1de633bde6d3d3e9b8012f822eb447db5195","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9ddb1de633bde6d3d3e9b8012f822eb447db5195","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9ddb1de633bde6d3d3e9b8012f822eb447db5195"}]},{"sha":"9ddb1de633bde6d3d3e9b8012f822eb447db5195","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDlkZGIxZGU2MzNiZGU2ZDNkM2U5YjgwMTJmODIyZWI0NDdkYjUxOTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T16:38:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T16:38:26Z"},"message":"[codex] Add /usr/bin/bash shell fallback (#26538)\n\n## Why\n\nSome Linux environments expose `bash` at `/usr/bin/bash` instead of\n`/bin/bash`. The shell detection fallback list should cover both\nstandard locations once PATH/user-shell probing fails.\n\nStacked on #26480.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `/usr/bin/bash` to the bash fallback path list in\n`codex-shell-command`.\n- Extend shell type detection coverage for `/usr/bin/bash`.\n- Add AGENTS.md testing guidance to avoid tests for statically defined\nvalues and negative tests for removed logic.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-shell-command`","tree":{"sha":"92157954ab283dd6b9e4c9ce0047a3cdf8a3c277","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/92157954ab283dd6b9e4c9ce0047a3cdf8a3c277"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9ddb1de633bde6d3d3e9b8012f822eb447db5195","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIvuDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9HQQAIHtFWn0sXVuQWScPt4luCtE\nFGBnKYd0zEziMZnZPCkaSeZrkTwxy1dZj5QiAKOVMgQHU22eFkF9k0u5hbOwRPcv\nQIiMNPCsLtqoNm9i7Jbm2UXcuNlmzNU+ip6BTnazxo5dvOQUMNSgbCcEmX4Av8f1\n6ceI535m/ltu0PEawJN1CNUHQ9FzFVbzQ9gvQDGP1lzbAQPQEUNr3c+gDfJUgCMp\nDvj7d/XUqEcegfCdLJgWWov7AVC7wBvX1Gy3XqTy5e9yUTho1ZA0xk2El77ZiAsi\nj9EU8yvddnIAekMg/CfdZ1XJ6OLwDiMT6ob5WjoyqAt+mS74YNowgMFydgKme4Mu\nIvosD3AsoediCUSksB8/l6cLGzCEgpoTQtP2u7KphpL8F/2f9zHzFxqdh6RN4uvC\n3vP1hC19y6rvAc8RA493VVofmC6q26lyUxueXb6nIfzRB9lGgFuQbbxQspiPX+Oe\nBvCPmJoYZ88jIJC9ydPK9EePHtJ09VEcQnZT608IjQAJU/W5Jy0juiguUytu4Ipj\nBHiDt2a94xrTbrmwRwFoxSNCbir8yall4uUqR88ZVmfAnoJXAzMxdYXN/SX2CBpK\nceL8N4EL4V/8XThGC9Q8Z323Sf2nPO7EByahaFRpIGSUlBgNGHZZWIDdoXW+DTej\n0ajNEgYh7KPRnBq/tvJX\n=1XBP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 92157954ab283dd6b9e4c9ce0047a3cdf8a3c277\nparent d40454522e2c6216eeeca5d97d39e991791ec664\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780677506 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780677506 -0700\n\n[codex] Add /usr/bin/bash shell fallback (#26538)\n\n## Why\n\nSome Linux environments expose `bash` at `/usr/bin/bash` instead of\n`/bin/bash`. The shell detection fallback list should cover both\nstandard locations once PATH/user-shell probing fails.\n\nStacked on #26480.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add `/usr/bin/bash` to the bash fallback path list in\n`codex-shell-command`.\n- Extend shell type detection coverage for `/usr/bin/bash`.\n- Add AGENTS.md testing guidance to avoid tests for statically defined\nvalues and negative tests for removed logic.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-shell-command`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T16:38:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9ddb1de633bde6d3d3e9b8012f822eb447db5195","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9ddb1de633bde6d3d3e9b8012f822eb447db5195","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9ddb1de633bde6d3d3e9b8012f822eb447db5195/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d40454522e2c6216eeeca5d97d39e991791ec664","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d40454522e2c6216eeeca5d97d39e991791ec664","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d40454522e2c6216eeeca5d97d39e991791ec664"}]},{"sha":"d40454522e2c6216eeeca5d97d39e991791ec664","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ0MDQ1NDUyMmUyYzYyMTZlZWVjYTVkOTdkMzllOTkxNzkxZWM2NjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T16:34:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T16:34:36Z"},"message":"[codex] Allow socketpair in proxy-routed Linux sandbox (#26625)\n\n## Summary\n\n- allow `socketpair(AF_UNIX, ...)` in the proxy-routed Linux seccomp\nmode\n- continue denying `socket(AF_UNIX, ...)` so user commands cannot create\npathname or abstract Unix sockets\n- extend the managed-proxy integration test to verify both behaviors\n\n## Root cause\n\n`NetworkSeccompMode::ProxyRouted` treated anonymous Unix socket pairs\nlike externally addressable Unix sockets and returned `EPERM`. This\nbreaks tools that use socket pairs for local child-process IPC even\nthough a socket pair cannot connect outside the sandbox or bypass the\nrouted proxy.\n\n`dangerously_allow_all_unix_sockets` controls Unix-socket requests\nforwarded by the managed network proxy; it does not currently configure\nthe Linux seccomp filter. Socket pairs should not require that dangerous\nsetting because they are unnamed, process-local IPC.\n\nRelated but independent: #26553 fixes host proxy bridge socket path\nlength handling.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"795d3314883b512f5166ea91e7baf9cf83a257b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/795d3314883b512f5166ea91e7baf9cf83a257b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d40454522e2c6216eeeca5d97d39e991791ec664","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIvqcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAobwQAKoPfaR0x3Yc0WZTOnrs+sda\nrN0e0N8zW2XM9JteQbdsodDCfQFTM05qgfh70IQEooYZMMb+Rkxw9vg/DBjmZCbY\np8k3Krn95rIGbCvmdGx8RbOZrOjrQgcoWROIVeu4c7wiO+JehdF8g1h1+9V+kUAf\nVNK03fUEZY6Kq9dZoxQ9SUK6rQti4cCgbhMxkNCTjuAuzOtrcuEc0ZjW1xKZxlsG\nyV/bd8J12peG61RMn60MCdb2O3yhfKejt0nPsYCUh+5FwSyIfkZ7pGSYYkNCxpkt\nN42vYcm+CwbSpALe+gIgDIBb5XaiBF/ZGF2il3PD2IeNJJhFChFsaedl4hrgly0C\nJqjqvORFOPhnkANeqCmCvgXb+A4jrdv8e1W3Zl6GXxe2sII3WCDeLvDhmrTVq6SG\nA5Fm0woRGR6oPJWB1Lj5VijUBWPAABl5DT5QVD2UKm2uMvyx44KCvElZvY8NOfX+\nIbLERU6i7j52cjbIODHCNSe0inH6ZruXyWYYq6LbShP8BPqLet9IlrZX98H841gu\ncKpZFd5tqFhz9MTVKiabrD1B58GRHJ9ELizOiUson5wh1k7GABIq9vfypVd/Sgos\n5n4llAsdiRhwF+qhejcVQ8dXQz5i6m9qa1zwgASvBbIa+iYKV0jSPi3GgqNnGFPy\nDW+CH1oqev/fySPjautQ\n=k+Pb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 795d3314883b512f5166ea91e7baf9cf83a257b3\nparent 40c8f1a0072e04f2df049c2233a28543604fc448\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1780677276 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780677276 -0700\n\n[codex] Allow socketpair in proxy-routed Linux sandbox (#26625)\n\n## Summary\n\n- allow `socketpair(AF_UNIX, ...)` in the proxy-routed Linux seccomp\nmode\n- continue denying `socket(AF_UNIX, ...)` so user commands cannot create\npathname or abstract Unix sockets\n- extend the managed-proxy integration test to verify both behaviors\n\n## Root cause\n\n`NetworkSeccompMode::ProxyRouted` treated anonymous Unix socket pairs\nlike externally addressable Unix sockets and returned `EPERM`. This\nbreaks tools that use socket pairs for local child-process IPC even\nthough a socket pair cannot connect outside the sandbox or bypass the\nrouted proxy.\n\n`dangerously_allow_all_unix_sockets` controls Unix-socket requests\nforwarded by the managed network proxy; it does not currently configure\nthe Linux seccomp filter. Socket pairs should not require that dangerous\nsetting because they are unnamed, process-local IPC.\n\nRelated but independent: #26553 fixes host proxy bridge socket path\nlength handling.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-05T16:34:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d40454522e2c6216eeeca5d97d39e991791ec664","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d40454522e2c6216eeeca5d97d39e991791ec664","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d40454522e2c6216eeeca5d97d39e991791ec664/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"40c8f1a0072e04f2df049c2233a28543604fc448","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/40c8f1a0072e04f2df049c2233a28543604fc448","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/40c8f1a0072e04f2df049c2233a28543604fc448"}]},{"sha":"40c8f1a0072e04f2df049c2233a28543604fc448","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQwYzhmMWEwMDcyZTA0ZjJkZjA0OWMyMjMzYTI4NTQzNjA0ZmM0NDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T16:29:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T16:29:15Z"},"message":"Require absolute cwd in thread settings (#26532)\n\n## Why\n\nThread settings cwd overrides are expected to be resolved before they\nenter core. Keeping this boundary as a plain `PathBuf` made it easy for\ncore/session code to keep fallback normalization and relative-path\nresolution logic in places that should only receive an already-resolved\ncwd.\n\nThis is intentionally the absolute-cwd-only slice: it does not change\nenvironment selection stickiness or cwd-to-default-environment fallback\nbehavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Changes `ThreadSettingsOverrides.cwd`,\n`CodexThreadSettingsOverrides.cwd`, and `SessionSettingsUpdate.cwd` to\nuse `AbsolutePathBuf`.\n- Removes core-side cwd normalization/resolution from session settings\nupdates.\n- Updates affected core/app-server test helpers and callsites to pass\nexisting absolute cwd values or use `abs()` helpers.\n\n## Validation\n\nOpening as draft so CI can start while local validation continues.","tree":{"sha":"65f96456153dfc2ff705d8f1ea7fd52690363a0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/65f96456153dfc2ff705d8f1ea7fd52690363a0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/40c8f1a0072e04f2df049c2233a28543604fc448","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIvlbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3xEQAH21Huk8l1gMd8SDMIbpYJHp\nDDeS/0MQALMp31m0CupJW45rBKZDvqTJWUzJkq+xnYnIjl6s3S3+M79qw74nZ9g3\nRnO2xZ2sWRqxpSZmsnQieChdoIx3lTxwlo4m7FQeVnM72flo0Z0ym0FYQPcBe4U1\n0sSKF189UDpGUbM0ippTitkgwZttOJgifvvSYfQ9l6MmdgeFv6RJ/XV0bM+KLc/P\nds08CYUkJrhyc+6HkWnyOiTrt0Ix36sIgJyc0Xe8p6TNpLb+o4E5iVfl0WnZDzKr\nBz/XZMqiky2wQ20nTbgnof1c0MqkTpxkkSk8bnlo8qWGSVpq1Ian/l9Vh217Jfet\nakoI6dD8ztriRv/YXUjKden0FYKkDwkBht0CPMpiNRlICWgJhkFIMXvurICUSbY3\nDdg7S7+F5Cv+ca0HOQrLGBAXwOPd3raq6UvSox9eVPEgzhBXfV83pouXNPzzbwht\naOxX5XxRXlK4FxPASc1jhA3WqLgY05006bEHONMd9Dv+fM4BMGpBR4O4b4ilEupM\nMvoUbloBk/qhtbMmAZd4t8OG4FaP3pN8FHeI92wR/voFdwlNy4evXQZnZlyMzF0a\nGYtakfhCgQvFIRFlMcKQ3IMI5GkxEw0/JOPt9zPZikUBF0u7WpBg1J0VqklrEboN\nrGAyW4xMgOsN6ckFNu1S\n=Tqps\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 65f96456153dfc2ff705d8f1ea7fd52690363a0a\nparent d5e4f01af4f7d3937ee4cd54ac27507fa421d755\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780676955 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780676955 -0700\n\nRequire absolute cwd in thread settings (#26532)\n\n## Why\n\nThread settings cwd overrides are expected to be resolved before they\nenter core. Keeping this boundary as a plain `PathBuf` made it easy for\ncore/session code to keep fallback normalization and relative-path\nresolution logic in places that should only receive an already-resolved\ncwd.\n\nThis is intentionally the absolute-cwd-only slice: it does not change\nenvironment selection stickiness or cwd-to-default-environment fallback\nbehavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Changes `ThreadSettingsOverrides.cwd`,\n`CodexThreadSettingsOverrides.cwd`, and `SessionSettingsUpdate.cwd` to\nuse `AbsolutePathBuf`.\n- Removes core-side cwd normalization/resolution from session settings\nupdates.\n- Updates affected core/app-server test helpers and callsites to pass\nexisting absolute cwd values or use `abs()` helpers.\n\n## Validation\n\nOpening as draft so CI can start while local validation continues.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T16:29:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/40c8f1a0072e04f2df049c2233a28543604fc448","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/40c8f1a0072e04f2df049c2233a28543604fc448","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/40c8f1a0072e04f2df049c2233a28543604fc448/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d5e4f01af4f7d3937ee4cd54ac27507fa421d755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d5e4f01af4f7d3937ee4cd54ac27507fa421d755","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d5e4f01af4f7d3937ee4cd54ac27507fa421d755"}]},{"sha":"d5e4f01af4f7d3937ee4cd54ac27507fa421d755","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ1ZTRmMDFhZjRmN2QzOTM3ZWU0Y2Q1NGFjMjc1MDdmYTQyMWQ3NTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T16:18:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T16:18:29Z"},"message":"feat: reload v2 agents on delivery (#26623)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis is the first small step toward making multi-agent v2 agents durable\nlogical agents whose `ThreadManager` residency is only an implementation\ndetail.\n\nThis PR adds a narrow v2 reload-on-delivery hook:\n\n- If a known v2 agent target is already loaded, delivery is unchanged.\n- If the target is still registered but missing from `ThreadManager`,\ndelivery reloads that exact v2 thread from durable rollout history\nbefore submitting the message.\n- If the target is unknown, closed, missing from storage, or not a v2\nthread, delivery still fails as not found.\n\nThe reload is wired only into existing-agent delivery paths: v2\n`send_message` / `followup_task`, and legacy `send_input` when its\ntarget is a known v2 agent.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **Reload on delivery**: load known unloaded v2 agents before\n`followup_task`, `send_message`, or `send_input` delivery. This PR.\n2. **Residency LRU**: unload idle resident v2 agents from\n`ThreadManager` without making them closed or unreachable.\n3. **Execution concurrency**: count active non-root turns, not logical\nagents or resident idle threads.\n4. **Close semantics**: make v2 close interrupt-only and leave durable\nagent identity intact.\n5. **Resume cleanup**: remove user-facing v2 resume semantics;\naddressing an unloaded durable agent reloads it implicitly.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `just fmt`.\n- Left broader tests and clippy to CI.","tree":{"sha":"f66a83e09749220d9cf7bb57ac442a6763f922f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f66a83e09749220d9cf7bb57ac442a6763f922f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d5e4f01af4f7d3937ee4cd54ac27507fa421d755","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIvbVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7aIQAFLMon0YxXwrNM1cJqsfJgLT\naA6Y9gWVTbaExn6NEM77NyCd7AVEVZBMbQyyHvajVu2CE3G26KlSPG4kuToxyPIi\n4ytkdIFwgd/sVgM9eYazzY++HFzsIWU94vjV2gDuFkvNYpMa8DfQez515UKwKKfj\n3m8HCxTPGhW7KyuCOwRTn0tbd645cAeb4sfx7xBoRQtbVly4gL19XKKM55glqINm\nS/cdzcowogzOyuJsxmJVl2wGhSLFTwxuyQod3FpGcsuzXtRlWgzH2cZnF04fbBOJ\nL/B/LhsPiMTZBW0Vo87lCkgNS10AZ0NywbMoKQpwQ2ZBrGkEW59BVKaPUJlZF7x8\nBLGzMEGd7Yg7Nn3aN8IhHziJfQ/crV4MdNRC51pp4e0yDikLoTAcBYO9iIBC8p1D\nfGcN2Yjyymvc7rQrK5ZzBFbQramfbPMNELfAthD+akhMcDQhL4XAAlaByQrnRZQX\n09BI319R0ABXgMpo1jevoE+U7bxPibWBSVFQ6ArSv4J+DKdC3rSxaKXoZ8b338Er\n6OHoOK3mi83SotwPp1f1mraWlBreaIooGUo90mkI9PIvC+M8W3oDjMgknwqoiQ5z\nDDQQoz2OsE/JTENQMjaoks+qfG/GwkAZ+y5uExFMTXjXz9HLSQCQ2r3KKUaSBoBm\nfQD9Uv7ewGGDToq2rVOY\n=YPRB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f66a83e09749220d9cf7bb57ac442a6763f922f5\nparent e5af672d730aa2a11c5e0ca5bc933f8c5195317a\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780676309 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780676309 +0200\n\nfeat: reload v2 agents on delivery (#26623)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis is the first small step toward making multi-agent v2 agents durable\nlogical agents whose `ThreadManager` residency is only an implementation\ndetail.\n\nThis PR adds a narrow v2 reload-on-delivery hook:\n\n- If a known v2 agent target is already loaded, delivery is unchanged.\n- If the target is still registered but missing from `ThreadManager`,\ndelivery reloads that exact v2 thread from durable rollout history\nbefore submitting the message.\n- If the target is unknown, closed, missing from storage, or not a v2\nthread, delivery still fails as not found.\n\nThe reload is wired only into existing-agent delivery paths: v2\n`send_message` / `followup_task`, and legacy `send_input` when its\ntarget is a known v2 agent.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. **Reload on delivery**: load known unloaded v2 agents before\n`followup_task`, `send_message`, or `send_input` delivery. This PR.\n2. **Residency LRU**: unload idle resident v2 agents from\n`ThreadManager` without making them closed or unreachable.\n3. **Execution concurrency**: count active non-root turns, not logical\nagents or resident idle threads.\n4. **Close semantics**: make v2 close interrupt-only and leave durable\nagent identity intact.\n5. **Resume cleanup**: remove user-facing v2 resume semantics;\naddressing an unloaded durable agent reloads it implicitly.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran `just fmt`.\n- Left broader tests and clippy to CI.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T16:18:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d5e4f01af4f7d3937ee4cd54ac27507fa421d755","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d5e4f01af4f7d3937ee4cd54ac27507fa421d755","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d5e4f01af4f7d3937ee4cd54ac27507fa421d755/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e5af672d730aa2a11c5e0ca5bc933f8c5195317a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e5af672d730aa2a11c5e0ca5bc933f8c5195317a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e5af672d730aa2a11c5e0ca5bc933f8c5195317a"}]},{"sha":"e5af672d730aa2a11c5e0ca5bc933f8c5195317a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU1YWY2NzJkNzMwYWEyYTExYzVlMGNhNWJjOTMzZjhjNTE5NTMxN2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:34:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:34:34Z"},"message":"Render code comment directives in TUI replay (#26554)\n\n## Summary\n\nResumed Codex App or VS Code review sessions can contain\n`::code-comment` directives that the TUI previously displayed verbatim\nbecause only rich clients interpret them.\n\nThis change rewrites valid line-start directives into readable Markdown\nduring assistant-message parsing, using the session working directory\nfor relative file paths. The fallback is applied consistently to live\nmessages, replayed transcripts, and resume previews while preserving\nmalformed directives and existing `::git-*` parsing.\n\n## Before\n\nThe TUI exposed the raw client directive:\n\n```text\n::code-comment{title=\"Fix body= parsing\" body=\"Keep role=\\\"tab\\\", ::git-stage{cwd=/tmp}, file=, and \\n literal.\" file=\"/repo/src/app.ts\" start=10 end=12 priority=\"P2\"}\n```\n\n## After\n\nThe same directive is rendered as readable review feedback:\n\n```text\n- [P2] Fix body= parsing — src/app.ts:10-12\n  Keep role=\"tab\", ::git-stage{cwd=/tmp}, file=, and \\n literal.\n```\n\nFixes #25658","tree":{"sha":"2125efc676d0ac331dd145d8dbc49fd4bc301d22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2125efc676d0ac331dd145d8dbc49fd4bc301d22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e5af672d730aa2a11c5e0ca5bc933f8c5195317a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIuyKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaG0QACN9sIfbAtctpoyWubkpFDVT\nL92uzVVBZuR8pqcb/KTzMZQrUT5hQDfSllPjc/7wenrlinC2LhQZgjThKeRpVnnh\n/dQGaDQdgna2BR/3tBrsK5wg8bp657EbSxlsJMzAKZGy1Uv5wwdmm/RumyX6VmoV\nSrjxCEDBxoJViUV6ez/FFdY9VB2RfkJ/VUZ099WkMv8va5KkIdGkz4sLlGH3taS6\nplWAMN+DdFyJgs6ja07HHAS2l8/Es4V69QJyYJu+eNJxOd8Bnd7dSrvQoG0CUAbR\niQ8vjqYwA8kDGye8tGwmA0nVwMexvxJIuPpujU2k9NMEYIeHfDdOpWQxaWkC6KWq\npz7W3LaIbplrBrvwf+2hKWl4uUVt54+9ukA8vEBHjg8tvBQqjr/WETlj77TZbi+m\nLe/IOZrf4Zdf38isF66oPfv3oCoxYkCSL8SXV6YPvxYfPpvqmseoDXhV3VLMpPrX\nBlAVw6/THUvAYEO6sPeDDKN1Fq/PASRdlNAt2C0gbiX7G1kP9ORNNYS8KsPC5YOu\n+d73JkY3hh8ifRa2ZoT05AhJpMicbKodx+qphNMDJRnwf4Us3fkAhCkm2TeslgxL\n0bIjHrLs8vPhtGFIIQj+hML8ZgYAYJYlG/MvJ80FnuCV4Inrh7GBb7snpY0Hn+mw\nbC2r5CuMlvV1Lj9SyNmy\n=yrxa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2125efc676d0ac331dd145d8dbc49fd4bc301d22\nparent fb0993dd3b68315408eaa109924c63f434e85382\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780673674 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780673674 -0700\n\nRender code comment directives in TUI replay (#26554)\n\n## Summary\n\nResumed Codex App or VS Code review sessions can contain\n`::code-comment` directives that the TUI previously displayed verbatim\nbecause only rich clients interpret them.\n\nThis change rewrites valid line-start directives into readable Markdown\nduring assistant-message parsing, using the session working directory\nfor relative file paths. The fallback is applied consistently to live\nmessages, replayed transcripts, and resume previews while preserving\nmalformed directives and existing `::git-*` parsing.\n\n## Before\n\nThe TUI exposed the raw client directive:\n\n```text\n::code-comment{title=\"Fix body= parsing\" body=\"Keep role=\\\"tab\\\", ::git-stage{cwd=/tmp}, file=, and \\n literal.\" file=\"/repo/src/app.ts\" start=10 end=12 priority=\"P2\"}\n```\n\n## After\n\nThe same directive is rendered as readable review feedback:\n\n```text\n- [P2] Fix body= parsing — src/app.ts:10-12\n  Keep role=\"tab\", ::git-stage{cwd=/tmp}, file=, and \\n literal.\n```\n\nFixes #25658","verified_at":"2026-06-05T15:34:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e5af672d730aa2a11c5e0ca5bc933f8c5195317a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e5af672d730aa2a11c5e0ca5bc933f8c5195317a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e5af672d730aa2a11c5e0ca5bc933f8c5195317a/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fb0993dd3b68315408eaa109924c63f434e85382","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fb0993dd3b68315408eaa109924c63f434e85382","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fb0993dd3b68315408eaa109924c63f434e85382"}]},{"sha":"fb0993dd3b68315408eaa109924c63f434e85382","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZiMDk5M2RkM2I2ODMxNTQwOGVhYTEwOTkyNGM2M2Y0MzRlODUzODI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:32:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:32:53Z"},"message":"Fix `/goal` usage text for control commands (#26551)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI's `/goal` usage text only advertised the objective form even\nthough `/goal clear`, `/goal edit`, `/goal pause`, and `/goal resume`\nare implemented. This made the lifecycle controls difficult to discover\nand allowed the duplicated help text to drift from actual behavior.\n\nFixes #25530.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Show the complete `/goal [<objective>|clear|edit|pause|resume]` syntax\nin usage messages.\n- Share one usage string across slash-command dispatch and goal-related\napp messages.\n- Add inline snapshot coverage for the control-command usage path.","tree":{"sha":"f71aaddcdefb3592ed36a2eb7b664101413a0b12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f71aaddcdefb3592ed36a2eb7b664101413a0b12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fb0993dd3b68315408eaa109924c63f434e85382","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIuwlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFNEQAFsRos0yLGhbU1dkcVY7k+JH\ns4HXfSJWiNIf0fnsNQYZiCJCYZu4vsKO2AFjiBzaV47xYyFdLDoICeEdvgVkZEle\nRcF7q95VSH2mwsEffvVDSwgsJ52EAGpXnArhf8bj2YO0ZW/ShD7ll3kOHCxfCeVB\nj74RnFug46foHgUPtBGqjJ4zFUnCOTjcU7eEy3Lu5ETr+H8x3ZMhwDu3/MoPToNv\njm4Q/47tjl0vDrqMgPCc7C9Ixx0Iwq/l8pHm+m+EUx3r5SAK23DWWdQPZUCd/9zM\n2SIJ/JsQ8uLAGCDgnVNZ+l3aXocvLwljWcv32FnkBzm6GfvpYXw6nVyKaYCmk0vF\n6UZAJk0/m1/UYZmKPSLxKVOzO1izmCL/mG8eyx8W8fTfPLk11lpY3qLN9jhx9HHW\ni5RTqSCH0b7fG5poXcGKR3YHuUiXmYr5FGI1+dQmfxfyVYYXpjvgjFgZTrUjo2gG\nyWYZspxKFn8cmpHOu3n3vDAAl8KOrZb+HeMskSUIIsaYZdntnfPdaKk4BYgr4u8T\nTqTfGxgMZb0mLQsbl6ZDRZNF/GuJiDJXeDrz2vpBUIidoC4gB04efu2g34xHUMIe\nwECS58xfhwskTDtt3zZs4jX8OC7QjDT0CB2gPg6SIsfHd0XiTFZvdW1tHCK/3vbx\nzc4Be3HzGVNblf5Qoi1P\n=CVgG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f71aaddcdefb3592ed36a2eb7b664101413a0b12\nparent e781816eadf1986c6ccb382b34a8d5bb4c23fb70\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780673573 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780673573 -0700\n\nFix `/goal` usage text for control commands (#26551)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI's `/goal` usage text only advertised the objective form even\nthough `/goal clear`, `/goal edit`, `/goal pause`, and `/goal resume`\nare implemented. This made the lifecycle controls difficult to discover\nand allowed the duplicated help text to drift from actual behavior.\n\nFixes #25530.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Show the complete `/goal [<objective>|clear|edit|pause|resume]` syntax\nin usage messages.\n- Share one usage string across slash-command dispatch and goal-related\napp messages.\n- Add inline snapshot coverage for the control-command usage path.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T15:32:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fb0993dd3b68315408eaa109924c63f434e85382","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fb0993dd3b68315408eaa109924c63f434e85382","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fb0993dd3b68315408eaa109924c63f434e85382/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e781816eadf1986c6ccb382b34a8d5bb4c23fb70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e781816eadf1986c6ccb382b34a8d5bb4c23fb70","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e781816eadf1986c6ccb382b34a8d5bb4c23fb70"}]},{"sha":"e781816eadf1986c6ccb382b34a8d5bb4c23fb70","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU3ODE4MTZlYWRmMTk4NmM2Y2NiMzgyYjM0YThkNWJiNGMyM2ZiNzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:32:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:32:42Z"},"message":"Open Windows app workspaces via deep link (#26500)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes #26423.\n\nOn Windows, `codex app PATH` detected Codex Desktop and launched the app\nshell target, then only printed a manual instruction to open the\nworkspace. The Desktop app already supports\n`codex://threads/new?path=...`, so the CLI can open the requested\nworkspace directly.\n\nThis updates the Windows launcher to normalize the workspace path,\nencode it into a `codex://threads/new` deep link, and open that URL when\nCodex Desktop is installed. The installer fallback still opens the\nWindows installer and prints the workspace path for after installation.","tree":{"sha":"c5cfa68dfac269442fa86e92d8700812f541f3c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c5cfa68dfac269442fa86e92d8700812f541f3c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e781816eadf1986c6ccb382b34a8d5bb4c23fb70","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIuwaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3U4QABUbXAd2rtK3EFj0LJWtfATS\n9KUQ1jmj1ny4T2QokwMKP2Q/J9bLmC3b6X68ldX1C+TsHXw8puiL0pb3oV65eesH\nq4E0d2SqlyE1AsgPjr9d0SVeDjlMLPJTVsQXGivVZViA0VlMkajLT7njHZd+D0sx\n9AY33zMa+h4fMaLUTIhDB0313NQapOgS2EHv0AO41+xFVtdWHQRJbTnlqUN3l8JP\nyPP2kbj72/ouSqbPkl72sRyTPBpaoeGog3vUEgW7HsYn4lc6WmYZaZo1dE9ku3CR\n1TWGdGbOs73r1OeYMWA748piVFcR38mPGQMK4w/aoBiNx9su1xODHqQ0H+kbrdti\naaheT6f3WUoOGEt9DfvRuqwQZtHzWN0Wx/3CMnkTcWpIpLtvyLunr1bmLCsm5Icm\n6JV05t6KlFRP57f8wnM0MnBaLmXIP4C98Yfbiu3IsqCf/DyuHE7NC75KW6Io/iP2\nZM85e0DrQ6LUCso19TqBK7wICWm4dA8dzgCr6JGAid3WnmIRzclrXS0ZrIB3IoAI\n7gDOXkTgX41Nk6Ne+Np9cHLFoMmgyvyaomdY1eFlj96fDt8imQjR83zBgtW3RbVj\nvKMzLLJzPZ00eOxIA6dJcLZpIRmzCYKC4r60BH8SJqBG3OleAXB1AVZ+wLwHWmNo\n5FcwxOJOGhLqXqKPtCbR\n=it+R\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c5cfa68dfac269442fa86e92d8700812f541f3c7\nparent 3acd71fedb1284e0f27f400e2d354a942b273421\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780673562 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780673562 -0700\n\nOpen Windows app workspaces via deep link (#26500)\n\n## Summary\n\nFixes #26423.\n\nOn Windows, `codex app PATH` detected Codex Desktop and launched the app\nshell target, then only printed a manual instruction to open the\nworkspace. The Desktop app already supports\n`codex://threads/new?path=...`, so the CLI can open the requested\nworkspace directly.\n\nThis updates the Windows launcher to normalize the workspace path,\nencode it into a `codex://threads/new` deep link, and open that URL when\nCodex Desktop is installed. The installer fallback still opens the\nWindows installer and prints the workspace path for after installation.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T15:32:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e781816eadf1986c6ccb382b34a8d5bb4c23fb70","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e781816eadf1986c6ccb382b34a8d5bb4c23fb70","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e781816eadf1986c6ccb382b34a8d5bb4c23fb70/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3acd71fedb1284e0f27f400e2d354a942b273421","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3acd71fedb1284e0f27f400e2d354a942b273421","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3acd71fedb1284e0f27f400e2d354a942b273421"}]},{"sha":"3acd71fedb1284e0f27f400e2d354a942b273421","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNhY2Q3MWZlZGIxMjg0ZTBmMjdmNDAwZTJkMzU0YTk0MmIyNzM0MjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:32:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:32:07Z"},"message":"Surface TUI config write error causes (#26537)\n\n## Summary\n\nTUI config writes currently wrap app-server failures with local context\nlike `config/batchWrite failed in TUI`, but several user-visible paths\nonly render the outer error. That hides the actionable app-server\nmessage, such as validation constraints or read-only `CODEX_HOME`\nfailures, leaving users with a dead-end diagnostic.\n\nThis change adds a small formatter next to the TUI config write helpers\nthat renders the error source chain, then uses it for model persistence,\nfeature persistence, project trust, status line writes, hook trust, and\nhook enablement.\n\nFixes #26077","tree":{"sha":"8299ad2641e1102872280b68d3e60ce7a38ba207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8299ad2641e1102872280b68d3e60ce7a38ba207"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3acd71fedb1284e0f27f400e2d354a942b273421","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIuv3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2YwQAKG+dFuvU4fXu2cyTSc0ECXC\nYWFSg0yDkVMDRFGywXlxxqoaIPNZoF+5qjXMVHVvHT4ymgGRmXpQznWACghMjROq\nFkFrZyMPCmpsySbgR96NB7gcrWfnGovYv3Kx+k/i02SFW53GAPqqu1wUhIzyX36a\nyLN4CyE1rV0IacOsKrQ91uoZjPGC1rYotZEC4a3eKFpD5sAi+7/m38+ESRhGzz3G\nJcIIEqfu5RB5SdUfcYw3I99uP8/N667784i1cBb/If7+M9zn/kU9O9qDsnKuC20p\ngXseeDW175metpQY+MUn2lp1HVT0ehwAnsLwsRfIqh4e1xlJwp9xyiTLhLlM2BB8\nUlpdu7JprHZbqxJmpovmM+mXBtZFGBFjxsoGP2CFn4rM7iUNG4H5cQ8ESdrapRmh\nrBZnqjwHXWB9v2jx+rkIO9atPZW8alxHpuZaubxvPcdT0S0VlQjsn3XclEFCtoSn\nBHIUvzxkFnRSAN0fl4tQYT3pWLo6W+sl/sO6XakLYt0Siql3PJ6JG3pnEctHSeJ3\n45bTKsV1By0VifSgGqLzBc7/4g5aDstYQr1z4gZT3K2n3SFAdZsKpn7z16MVERDy\nBF80fKeHCU4h1f+tPKo57y+bmrUDksrb2ggtSd1g4nqGm6n0hHGKeO/X1Dz1U/ZQ\nbeTymxyQW2TN2uCrIPhu\n=qnIs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8299ad2641e1102872280b68d3e60ce7a38ba207\nparent a14a73b54af26af4a5428ba2eb482a1ce54f8974\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780673527 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780673527 -0700\n\nSurface TUI config write error causes (#26537)\n\n## Summary\n\nTUI config writes currently wrap app-server failures with local context\nlike `config/batchWrite failed in TUI`, but several user-visible paths\nonly render the outer error. That hides the actionable app-server\nmessage, such as validation constraints or read-only `CODEX_HOME`\nfailures, leaving users with a dead-end diagnostic.\n\nThis change adds a small formatter next to the TUI config write helpers\nthat renders the error source chain, then uses it for model persistence,\nfeature persistence, project trust, status line writes, hook trust, and\nhook enablement.\n\nFixes #26077","verified_at":"2026-06-05T15:32:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3acd71fedb1284e0f27f400e2d354a942b273421","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3acd71fedb1284e0f27f400e2d354a942b273421","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3acd71fedb1284e0f27f400e2d354a942b273421/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a14a73b54af26af4a5428ba2eb482a1ce54f8974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a14a73b54af26af4a5428ba2eb482a1ce54f8974","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a14a73b54af26af4a5428ba2eb482a1ce54f8974"}]},{"sha":"a14a73b54af26af4a5428ba2eb482a1ce54f8974","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGExNGE3M2I1NGFmMjZhZjRhNTQyOGJhMmViNDgyYTFjZTU0Zjg5NzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:00:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T15:00:46Z"},"message":"[codex] Fix long proxy socket paths (#26553)\n\n## Summary\n\n- avoid generating host proxy bridge Unix socket paths that exceed\nLinux's `sockaddr_un.sun_path` limit\n- fall back from a long `$CODEX_HOME/tmp` path to the system temp\ndirectory, then `/tmp`\n- add focused unit coverage for short and overlong parent paths\n\n## Root cause\n\nWith a sufficiently long `CODEX_HOME`, the generated\n`proxy-route-*.sock` path exceeds Linux's 107-byte pathname limit. The\nhost bridge child exits before writing its readiness byte, so the parent\nreports the indirect error `failed to prepare host proxy routing bridge:\nfailed to fill whole buffer`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- reproduced the original error with a long `CODEX_HOME` using\n`codex-cli 0.138.0-alpha.4`\n- `cargo clippy -p codex-linux-sandbox --all-targets`\n- `just fix -p codex-linux-sandbox`\n- `just fmt`\n\nThe Linux-only unit test could not execute locally: the arm64 Docker\nbuild was repeatedly OOM-killed by `rustc` while compiling an unrelated\n`codex-app-server-protocol` dependency, before reaching the test.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"5e8dbbe125a4d5f549636f31833401ff3720c41b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5e8dbbe125a4d5f549636f31833401ff3720c41b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a14a73b54af26af4a5428ba2eb482a1ce54f8974","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIuSeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASBgQAB9uGHEKU7jp9sEAMbCSWHyw\nzdKdFYTZYLU68CdBzCV2NUXtMEru+7jJST9ng0GbycG+MsXZB/koC05CC9qeVqEe\n5ZaDqukqIzfiLOZkXXjIh62EVQzBpGGk7G3aljt8A36xH+kwJ7QgAcfczntEAmZs\nQeBnTQCK9ByxZKTzHPaJPWwgCEpEwD7Ie4HevHd+RMbQkPy3ZaJhjWpaqhoyUnJg\nGe3+mVi86DejIspD2sZjCwNmaJ34Qu5kbFRraNc0NxSm7f/QtF+kWBa5ngdBTWTv\nbA+g0nVkxD7uByugfNZAXV7HvRB2LcOSJZ8nSSH74s5SA7sG5XN8M/Hb/kM5zD6v\njD8VAP0QJQp/mFX4Q3ZUdeZyHotKY2WV5ASosPowpGRuAx5183DJkaoaXPrsZTnu\nIQg5D98ObUJ+ShieM2iqY6XKCj11H9059B8gsZ3naFB/omnSHDLjJDv25z+vIgBa\n3aHEEWQFLIKUdAaQOrgE5cZsLvb//rekNmefIWciqqmp9ocgnDH6RF9CXv7PAcVk\nFe1RTKd73WC4TbuSNlnyIBKxAgX2fxjcayHD8aZ4uMMdRwo4I9alzDKDWUBwyk05\nZxO8bDomH6gW+XJYM85j10qNq00Q2wFzZYDQZ9z1bY51wSgRxBR+S7dhLvpHWb6+\ne+9pm9dzmXBm9G3how2X\n=809J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5e8dbbe125a4d5f549636f31833401ff3720c41b\nparent 5e62c735b2b261e897276b4df544a197c49081d4\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1780671646 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780671646 -0700\n\n[codex] Fix long proxy socket paths (#26553)\n\n## Summary\n\n- avoid generating host proxy bridge Unix socket paths that exceed\nLinux's `sockaddr_un.sun_path` limit\n- fall back from a long `$CODEX_HOME/tmp` path to the system temp\ndirectory, then `/tmp`\n- add focused unit coverage for short and overlong parent paths\n\n## Root cause\n\nWith a sufficiently long `CODEX_HOME`, the generated\n`proxy-route-*.sock` path exceeds Linux's 107-byte pathname limit. The\nhost bridge child exits before writing its readiness byte, so the parent\nreports the indirect error `failed to prepare host proxy routing bridge:\nfailed to fill whole buffer`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- reproduced the original error with a long `CODEX_HOME` using\n`codex-cli 0.138.0-alpha.4`\n- `cargo clippy -p codex-linux-sandbox --all-targets`\n- `just fix -p codex-linux-sandbox`\n- `just fmt`\n\nThe Linux-only unit test could not execute locally: the arm64 Docker\nbuild was repeatedly OOM-killed by `rustc` while compiling an unrelated\n`codex-app-server-protocol` dependency, before reaching the test.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-05T15:00:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a14a73b54af26af4a5428ba2eb482a1ce54f8974","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a14a73b54af26af4a5428ba2eb482a1ce54f8974","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a14a73b54af26af4a5428ba2eb482a1ce54f8974/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5e62c735b2b261e897276b4df544a197c49081d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5e62c735b2b261e897276b4df544a197c49081d4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5e62c735b2b261e897276b4df544a197c49081d4"}]},{"sha":"5e62c735b2b261e897276b4df544a197c49081d4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVlNjJjNzM1YjJiMjYxZTg5NzI3NmI0ZGY1NDRhMTk3YzQ5MDgxZDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Felipe Coury","email":"felipe.coury@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T14:43:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T14:43:44Z"},"message":"feat(app-server): expose account token usage [1 of 2] (#25344)\n\n## Why\n\nToken activity is useful account-level context, but terminal clients\nneed a supported app-server path to fetch it without reaching into\nChatGPT backend details directly. The API should also live under the\nbroader account usage umbrella so future usage surfaces can be added\nwithout proliferating user-facing concepts.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add `codex-backend-client` support for the ChatGPT profile token-usage\npayload.\n- Add the v2 `account/usage/read` app-server RPC.\n- Map lifetime usage, peak daily usage, streak, longest task duration,\nand daily buckets into app-server protocol types.\n- Gate the request on Codex-backend auth, which supports ChatGPT auth\ntokens and AgentIdentity.\n- Regenerate the app-server JSON and TypeScript schema fixtures.\n\n## Token Count Source\n\n`account/usage/read` returns the token-usage aggregate supplied by the\nChatGPT profile backend. App-server maps that backend-owned aggregate\ninto protocol fields; it does not recompute cached-token treatment,\nusage multipliers, or raw input/output totals locally.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. feat(app-server): expose account token usage [1 of 2] (this PR)\n2. [#25345](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25345) feat(tui): add\ntoken activity command [2 of 2]\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Start an app-server client from this branch while authenticated with\nChatGPT or AgentIdentity.\n2. Call `account/usage/read`.\n3. Confirm the response includes `summary` and `dailyUsageBuckets`.\n4. Also verify a session without Codex-backend auth receives the\nexisting auth error path.\n\nTargeted tests:\n- `just test -p codex-backend-client -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`","tree":{"sha":"6156447ead93329c0e6dfae111a80392b9e05da0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6156447ead93329c0e6dfae111a80392b9e05da0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5e62c735b2b261e897276b4df544a197c49081d4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIuCgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsUYQADiHs1rNN9Wftu0CrzB5rq7h\nCZ7w8UqExvKMOuKmlb6/0lczAeAw2exX8lAuFtGvE//OTmBgStLf+9AG8DWgpr+F\nsAnvic2kordJgmZ3W11ka2SAxih2vIDW0uCyn4hcnkSTnRZHrkQVBpu0qhv3WnRm\npvvCkn8QmXztGUqQjefvFMxIOcryRBwBvVr2SYBLF+Sf7F6ttjQRPqPSUHvsFwID\nOPVNDqCPcGkvZvPwBiHV3BibjbvHN7J2bCex6aBNU+UWoOnCFh6xtwGYFT4GOS1o\nB2mQP8asrqSDAYgvdOMsnpyTfmBvIBK1N9hp8fR79DqaNNZqEXcXibkN9NyAiQRX\nXrU+5J9QRjk9Ci9QD+v6hkFfEMW7sk0QUYTuyXeLBQ4dOl2G/xdbK21kmnjufKof\nVfPT11F/sWegtJnvgYKTtZcE589EEj+pZnRy5qI8We6dvDPmh+LyHBwfwdfw1kLC\nfI7bng6WUrRRhOep8Z2ZffzgjH6fFbkmXLh/T4MoTDZ4nWPi67x/RoEeENqyKzTo\ngTV6lzjbsqpwMBsz/RXVTbk4MT7mHGErIbKr87tj8qX3yhja0SZpHd2cJgE9iuTU\nYVUU0esz6vIfGxiFIK9kZCyk53HdvC29teSrpJ2ZYpBUOVe6mqTl/oar9kLI54JS\nuYQ5anaRj4suyM+S8e6i\n=RMOG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6156447ead93329c0e6dfae111a80392b9e05da0\nparent 0b1512c2c83935af4eaa096ac7e434992f15b066\nauthor Felipe Coury <felipe.coury@openai.com> 1780670624 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780670624 +0000\n\nfeat(app-server): expose account token usage [1 of 2] (#25344)\n\n## Why\n\nToken activity is useful account-level context, but terminal clients\nneed a supported app-server path to fetch it without reaching into\nChatGPT backend details directly. The API should also live under the\nbroader account usage umbrella so future usage surfaces can be added\nwithout proliferating user-facing concepts.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Add `codex-backend-client` support for the ChatGPT profile token-usage\npayload.\n- Add the v2 `account/usage/read` app-server RPC.\n- Map lifetime usage, peak daily usage, streak, longest task duration,\nand daily buckets into app-server protocol types.\n- Gate the request on Codex-backend auth, which supports ChatGPT auth\ntokens and AgentIdentity.\n- Regenerate the app-server JSON and TypeScript schema fixtures.\n\n## Token Count Source\n\n`account/usage/read` returns the token-usage aggregate supplied by the\nChatGPT profile backend. App-server maps that backend-owned aggregate\ninto protocol fields; it does not recompute cached-token treatment,\nusage multipliers, or raw input/output totals locally.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. feat(app-server): expose account token usage [1 of 2] (this PR)\n2. [#25345](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25345) feat(tui): add\ntoken activity command [2 of 2]\n\n## How to Test\n\n1. Start an app-server client from this branch while authenticated with\nChatGPT or AgentIdentity.\n2. Call `account/usage/read`.\n3. Confirm the response includes `summary` and `dailyUsageBuckets`.\n4. Also verify a session without Codex-backend auth receives the\nexisting auth error path.\n\nTargeted tests:\n- `just test -p codex-backend-client -p codex-app-server-protocol -p\ncodex-app-server`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T14:43:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5e62c735b2b261e897276b4df544a197c49081d4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5e62c735b2b261e897276b4df544a197c49081d4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5e62c735b2b261e897276b4df544a197c49081d4/comments","author":{"login":"fcoury-oai","id":272635208,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAVSA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272635208?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fcoury-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fcoury-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0b1512c2c83935af4eaa096ac7e434992f15b066","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b1512c2c83935af4eaa096ac7e434992f15b066","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0b1512c2c83935af4eaa096ac7e434992f15b066"}]},{"sha":"0b1512c2c83935af4eaa096ac7e434992f15b066","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBiMTUxMmMyYzgzOTM1YWY0ZWFhMDk2YWM3ZTQzNDk5MmYxNWIwNjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T14:24:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T14:24:22Z"},"message":"refactor: split agent control modules (#26610)\n\n## Summary\n\nMechanically splits `AgentControl` into focused modules so later agent\nruntime changes are easier to review. The shared lookup, messaging, and\ncompletion logic remains in `control.rs`, while spawn-specific code and\nV1 legacy close/resume behavior move into dedicated files.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Extract spawn-agent code into `agent/control/spawn.rs`.\n- Extract V1-only legacy close/resume behavior into\n`agent/control/legacy.rs`.\n- Keep shared control-plane behavior in `agent/control.rs`.\n- Preserve existing behavior; this PR is intended to be mechanical.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. This PR - Mechanical `AgentControl` split: extracts spawn and V1\nlegacy code without behavior changes.\n2. #26614 - Execution slot accounting: separates logical agents from\nactive execution slots.\n3. #26611 - Residency and reload runtime: adds resident-agent LRU,\neviction/reload, durable lookup, and V2 delivery through reload.\n4. #26612 - V2 tool semantics: narrows `close_agent` to interrupt-only\nand updates V2 tool coverage.","tree":{"sha":"e307e74669b46ab7fd67cdeb9165a1ef644e4efc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e307e74669b46ab7fd67cdeb9165a1ef644e4efc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0b1512c2c83935af4eaa096ac7e434992f15b066","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqItwWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOVgQALADSE5YlZBgdHIB8Mr/0AG7\n2A8If311ASe9Fyo9ILUXOXZ7FjjUCow7GSXELo8La+GdNHo1Nai4lmk4YCyFA3Gk\nJ0FYgOTsJUTVuW5L60GGguBaaZuv6rAIlTLMeYxZDr5Snp5+9hvLpybMvJX0XrMU\nf1zog1pXQslX/YuZ0zlpgj5ydYIleocZEn7OmncT65MoHK0olq9xL2CdbolXPVBy\nY9jOGbuXzWVwZsd9kG5FF+Wv5rWmayKLiyZIfA95y/uFuE/U/Po2werR6Qn2goXu\nzn+FZyg3S/Rw8/QXZGcV1wAKJtQFSFl1Ca4233dCzo06bTrevDu4PnTGBPQZEB7R\n+lNKHZ5O9se0cnC6K2B4jsybu/YRrZdf8yIfFQWRy2i0Uelq6YyvN45bo5HsYLiQ\nUu9AE6zUghc8EIE8q7T840sfqMoWRITyumfXvuoU6g49HxThoWKY74R+knUZqbcQ\nXYgZiGJUd8Ol79JRNub1lLo5dcMO9uOujdLWPtfEAPVnKnxm6PIiGOxKkdAzrKqj\n2Zb3dji0pl7ahqfpLfaSvRBRS/ECVbQdewN3JCT6uNdLqk2SM4vjciDYamBBNVYd\neyJdN5NjFskukCmFsY/SvetN50QMFl14spKbbXJbKo8kA8V8OKFYdukq1wGXyV67\nPjNeHnUshfuBJsaqnAE1\n=ouE7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e307e74669b46ab7fd67cdeb9165a1ef644e4efc\nparent 66232220e21712604b0066f496e966c9a2c1bda8\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780669462 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780669462 +0200\n\nrefactor: split agent control modules (#26610)\n\n## Summary\n\nMechanically splits `AgentControl` into focused modules so later agent\nruntime changes are easier to review. The shared lookup, messaging, and\ncompletion logic remains in `control.rs`, while spawn-specific code and\nV1 legacy close/resume behavior move into dedicated files.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Extract spawn-agent code into `agent/control/spawn.rs`.\n- Extract V1-only legacy close/resume behavior into\n`agent/control/legacy.rs`.\n- Keep shared control-plane behavior in `agent/control.rs`.\n- Preserve existing behavior; this PR is intended to be mechanical.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. This PR - Mechanical `AgentControl` split: extracts spawn and V1\nlegacy code without behavior changes.\n2. #26614 - Execution slot accounting: separates logical agents from\nactive execution slots.\n3. #26611 - Residency and reload runtime: adds resident-agent LRU,\neviction/reload, durable lookup, and V2 delivery through reload.\n4. #26612 - V2 tool semantics: narrows `close_agent` to interrupt-only\nand updates V2 tool coverage.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T14:24:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b1512c2c83935af4eaa096ac7e434992f15b066","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0b1512c2c83935af4eaa096ac7e434992f15b066","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b1512c2c83935af4eaa096ac7e434992f15b066/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"66232220e21712604b0066f496e966c9a2c1bda8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/66232220e21712604b0066f496e966c9a2c1bda8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/66232220e21712604b0066f496e966c9a2c1bda8"}]},{"sha":"66232220e21712604b0066f496e966c9a2c1bda8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY2MjMyMjIwZTIxNzEyNjA0YjAwNjZmNDk2ZTk2NmM5YTJjMWJkYTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T12:52:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T12:52:51Z"},"message":"[codex] Keep v1 spawn metadata visible (#26599)\n\n## Summary\n- keep the legacy v1 `spawn_agent` role and model selectors visible\n- add regression coverage for the default v1 tool plan\n\n## Why\n`hide_spawn_agent_metadata` is a multi-agent v2 setting, but the v1\nplanning branch also consumed it. After the default changed to `true`,\nv1 stopped advertising `agent_type`, `model`, `reasoning_effort`, and\n`service_tier`, preventing configured agents from being selected.\n\nThis keeps the hidden-metadata default for v2 while opting v1 out of\nthat behavior.\n\nFixes #26363.\n\n## Validation\nNot run locally, per request; CI will validate the change.","tree":{"sha":"7e2e76dc3d8a29045ce5c839f76a4df414a3fd6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7e2e76dc3d8a29045ce5c839f76a4df414a3fd6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/66232220e21712604b0066f496e966c9a2c1bda8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIsajCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGXIQAEqc1T87xiAqRqZZ97QSm8VG\nYmhwA3rbymyqG2QijjDH2BczLvgyrypR8ZHFh2XygQ9+TnTiq2pxn0Tntf5Ny0BG\n5LuvF33pHIi0aUibIkf4dt4auGW+Xpfj7IMElqBsKmAv7VZKIp//sihL1WMDlLN8\nMVCjEJrOz4xJFcqshK4om71FgxNZX5A4zZdGNe+wi5ofVpkpMjdZ6do6aB5pdNvx\nQqyKx2EB5YnKteVynGyddJ5qZUBl4C7+Uu5WJVxX3lcQ5cl2j+JprdK+FiQhRXc1\nQZd8IH9/Mh7R/i/XoydGT7vzMnSKUr886BZEn29qxmcpjOX5glb6qaJ3NzezEzzP\nuVcXdtCm9nrE/i6h9F9Tzupm46Bu4cdatCScTTVKSTfSLP+e3sgEEyuFfxduIU3W\n4hH6/GlhPT+YDNSAugia5o0thp86zcXv6/BEIqL5N632OgCmRKa5meaobkx8EkxM\nvoaySmrh10FAoEyX+g6nfe7oNxU9kTzIRLSp6h0dFstkuHzSxn5OK0TyLWYOBfDv\nJ2uozKyipYvSeAYF5YTY5BEH3YX8IgNWiz5vFmyovf2tJXOMb75mUQPhrxPeZQ8M\n2aN6wxt52PaToWfE56/mvohL4egVV2LAoX8aJSRWKNnBju4v8CCfrdDS618vevbD\nnqK4wexTISKxzkxniefH\n=6V56\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7e2e76dc3d8a29045ce5c839f76a4df414a3fd6c\nparent 55aa071b17c825bdb66fac99cde2e7a7acfbdee7\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780663971 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780663971 +0200\n\n[codex] Keep v1 spawn metadata visible (#26599)\n\n## Summary\n- keep the legacy v1 `spawn_agent` role and model selectors visible\n- add regression coverage for the default v1 tool plan\n\n## Why\n`hide_spawn_agent_metadata` is a multi-agent v2 setting, but the v1\nplanning branch also consumed it. After the default changed to `true`,\nv1 stopped advertising `agent_type`, `model`, `reasoning_effort`, and\n`service_tier`, preventing configured agents from being selected.\n\nThis keeps the hidden-metadata default for v2 while opting v1 out of\nthat behavior.\n\nFixes #26363.\n\n## Validation\nNot run locally, per request; CI will validate the change.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T12:52:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/66232220e21712604b0066f496e966c9a2c1bda8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/66232220e21712604b0066f496e966c9a2c1bda8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/66232220e21712604b0066f496e966c9a2c1bda8/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"55aa071b17c825bdb66fac99cde2e7a7acfbdee7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/55aa071b17c825bdb66fac99cde2e7a7acfbdee7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/55aa071b17c825bdb66fac99cde2e7a7acfbdee7"}]},{"sha":"55aa071b17c825bdb66fac99cde2e7a7acfbdee7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU1YWEwNzFiMTdjODI1YmRiNjZmYWM5OWNkZTJlN2E3YWNmYmRlZTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"carlc-oai","email":"carlc@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T09:41:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T09:41:06Z"},"message":"[codex] Forward turn moderation metadata through app-server (#25710)\n\n## Why\nFirst-party backends can supply turn-scoped moderation metadata that\napp-server clients need for client-side presentation. Exposing this as\nan experimental typed notification lets opted-in clients consume it\nwithout interpreting raw Responses API events.\n\n## What changed\n- forward `response.metadata.openai_chatgpt_moderation_metadata` from\nResponses API SSE and WebSocket streams as turn-scoped moderation\nmetadata\n- emit the experimental app-server v2 `turn/moderationMetadata`\nnotification with `{ threadId, turnId, metadata }`\n- add app-server integration coverage for the typed moderation metadata\nnotification\n\n## Testing\n- `just test -p codex-core\nbuild_ws_client_metadata_includes_window_lineage_and_turn_metadata`\n- `just test -p codex-core` (fails locally: 46 failures and 1 timeout,\nprimarily missing `test_stdio_server` and shell snapshot timeouts)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nturn_moderation_metadata_emits_typed_notification_v2`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server` (fails locally: 792 passed, 10 failed,\nand 5 timed out; failures are in existing environment-sensitive tests,\nprimarily because nested macOS `sandbox-exec` is not permitted)\n- `just write-app-server-schema --experimental --schema-root\n/tmp/codex-app-server-schema-experimental`","tree":{"sha":"e5761f976d26f477f56a188ab45d34de4db1044f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e5761f976d26f477f56a188ab45d34de4db1044f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/55aa071b17c825bdb66fac99cde2e7a7acfbdee7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIpmyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaIQQAFNUB7/wrxe7T3BHMSDEr7TC\n8kEJxILMLv2aTOxNvYfN6XQfzBLXn3w02KcOeP56W0Vfua/8AtuGqmREKVHZccQs\nAgjivHH5u0BFg3fPLXy2nPySRZCPO9snh6mgPxlXFrOZ0k3R2v015ePxkBgOXus9\nNqDAZNCU1vkeNmhClz+fcm+v3cTyuP0adSL/sn5JFWM0w0+95l200yHnTLG6na1v\nRxMyef4k9YWn85R/fYyvi7XP6td0nn0mVuSz8iKeuqYdYFyJWAawdEGR1vBDbiyv\naF2g5JeEdm2RxeGKo1MJ+aMcK9OVQcqzAoGj/QH5S8Vbi2JYm1oc1NrwD+gVpK7x\niv8nSyC2R+DNz6R46+tmU4LERb7VrIATRxSQjOsI88b8wxzhyRHWLuBf6ogjfvSK\nx6oWy7yMdtL8DkIlom3h/R/JXYnU3m8CeZLqpUjHD6/lnSunhUSMFc+bWbJvTMaT\nII9l/WFE0FAOge3ZMBzfQjm7hYKlrPmruRsRrp7dXO6SA7H8jlBF6ph5pR3slxsK\nmcph6QARdvWvoK+EB5N0qufZnyMn0onQOW5HWpF53IJGK54IB2uMy5QRThXF7NZx\nQmYwS00YU6nNFWrPkVKz5NTVDT0xQn7gUDFqwQqCBmoe7gMvfcmpEmMlgFIjQhCP\nGcvjnYBO2xeXEib54J66\n=yN87\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e5761f976d26f477f56a188ab45d34de4db1044f\nparent 6dc28ba6e0acd391a1a006af8bd0237b61fd54a6\nauthor carlc-oai <carlc@openai.com> 1780652466 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780652466 -0700\n\n[codex] Forward turn moderation metadata through app-server (#25710)\n\n## Why\nFirst-party backends can supply turn-scoped moderation metadata that\napp-server clients need for client-side presentation. Exposing this as\nan experimental typed notification lets opted-in clients consume it\nwithout interpreting raw Responses API events.\n\n## What changed\n- forward `response.metadata.openai_chatgpt_moderation_metadata` from\nResponses API SSE and WebSocket streams as turn-scoped moderation\nmetadata\n- emit the experimental app-server v2 `turn/moderationMetadata`\nnotification with `{ threadId, turnId, metadata }`\n- add app-server integration coverage for the typed moderation metadata\nnotification\n\n## Testing\n- `just test -p codex-core\nbuild_ws_client_metadata_includes_window_lineage_and_turn_metadata`\n- `just test -p codex-core` (fails locally: 46 failures and 1 timeout,\nprimarily missing `test_stdio_server` and shell snapshot timeouts)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nturn_moderation_metadata_emits_typed_notification_v2`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server` (fails locally: 792 passed, 10 failed,\nand 5 timed out; failures are in existing environment-sensitive tests,\nprimarily because nested macOS `sandbox-exec` is not permitted)\n- `just write-app-server-schema --experimental --schema-root\n/tmp/codex-app-server-schema-experimental`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T09:41:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/55aa071b17c825bdb66fac99cde2e7a7acfbdee7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/55aa071b17c825bdb66fac99cde2e7a7acfbdee7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/55aa071b17c825bdb66fac99cde2e7a7acfbdee7/comments","author":{"login":"carlc-oai","id":242064971,"node_id":"U_kgDODm2eSw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/242064971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlc-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/carlc-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlc-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlc-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlc-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlc-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlc-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlc-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlc-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlc-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/carlc-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web