eb-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5f4d06ef186b896d316620556e561d59206c3ebf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5f4d06ef186b896d316620556e561d59206c3ebf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5f4d06ef186b896d316620556e561d59206c3ebf"}]},{"sha":"5f4d06ef186b896d316620556e561d59206c3ebf","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVmNGQwNmVmMTg2Yjg5NmQzMTY2MjA1NTZlNTYxZDU5MjA2YzNlYmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T08:25:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T08:25:57Z"},"message":"Encrypt multi-agent v2 message payloads (#26210)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 currently routes agent instructions through normal tool\narguments and inter-agent context. That means the parent model can emit\nplaintext task text, Codex can persist it in history/rollouts, and the\nrecipient can receive it as ordinary assistant-message JSON.\n\nThis changes the v2 path so agent instructions stay encrypted between\nmodel calls: Responses encrypts the `message` argument returned by the\nmodel, Codex forwards only that ciphertext, and Responses decrypts it\ninternally for the recipient model.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Mark the v2 `message` parameter as encrypted for `spawn_agent`,\n`send_message`, and `followup_task`.\n- Treat multi-agent v2 tool `message` values as ciphertext\nunconditionally.\n- Store v2 inter-agent task text in\n`InterAgentCommunication.encrypted_content` with empty plaintext\n`content`.\n- Convert encrypted inter-agent communications into the Responses\n`agent_message` input item before sending the child request.\n- Preserve `agent_message` items across history, rollout, compaction,\ntelemetry, and app-server schema paths.\n- Leave multi-agent v1 unchanged.\n\n## Message shape\n\nThe model still calls the v2 tools with a `message` argument, but that\nvalue is now ciphertext:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"spawn_agent\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"task_name\": \"worker\",\n    \"message\": \"<ciphertext>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCodex stores the task as encrypted inter-agent communication:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"author\": \"/root\",\n  \"recipient\": \"/root/worker\",\n  \"content\": \"\",\n  \"encrypted_content\": \"<ciphertext>\",\n  \"trigger_turn\": true\n}\n```\n\nWhen Codex builds the recipient request, it forwards the ciphertext\nusing the new Responses input item:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"agent_message\",\n  \"author\": \"/root\",\n  \"recipient\": \"/root/worker\",\n  \"content\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"encrypted_content\",\n      \"encrypted_content\": \"<ciphertext>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nResponses decrypts that item internally for the recipient model.\n\n## Context impact\n\n- Parent context no longer carries plaintext v2 agent task instructions\nfrom these tool arguments.\n- Codex rollout/history stores ciphertext for v2 agent instructions.\n- Recipient requests receive an `agent_message` item instead of\nassistant commentary JSON for encrypted task delivery.\n- Plaintext completion/status notifications are still plaintext because\nthey are Codex-generated status messages, not encrypted model tool\narguments.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tools`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout-trace`\n- `just test -p codex-otel`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`","tree":{"sha":"59931538bd56ed5d5af42111ca2f71475597391e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/59931538bd56ed5d5af42111ca2f71475597391e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5f4d06ef186b896d316620556e561d59206c3ebf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIogVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWd4QAC4aa29Qo4tPshHEcCGRzPkQ\nq7xSOojryvPNKp8hiHBnvaTa11JJgh37Mi3QFpbSoFdu1BvWfxDWAK+4euRHIt89\nbo+bIaX9rFdzXQ8mS+9fp8FwA/VJn//X1b8eIWmYGT1SHmKKqKBwbDwI1AVzZEJf\nrRJZZGq5I0aTNq6vtWKv1NPexVnQuAWv1BQnhuAOlhNwvjkk0jF2PGtMdy+AStRC\njjVi3BWmYUJn8Q6DlogQNYnPdHCu5Dp4cyNni90VCkAqQzSB+kil39m/mIee6ggS\nygCCOwBOfcCYImVfO1IjxCgJdZI2Mq8gVpO7p8/mXaXhw2vc1saq0XFS+ex92QeX\neDETG6yiN4Ym3GXxQvR0jNqRz8q8eZRKzGP4FSyRsMYLrrs6a7YHVRm11E8qPXLn\nafyg3L3sd9Uqz/G559lN9FIRKemzN89iIrL/VciDGVE5o2g1fBwAP+PpSG1zTGzS\nOqZr32aO/WIvjCoCEeS416neLeSI6tdXDdZuplp2V0/LxifjWFcpZs1X8GfKzQLy\nysXGiOlTeeF8JHrtkmqpF5H/Y8Dad7ZE440cS8DPF5Zdv5bG0SepwSHhbNgLu6WD\nI05CfJzxchQtujCwjzRP938nX4jBtkOUYf3VLMqxO53HZg2k8j9eHsdtIvEfRZrK\nWOkc6Fj1yyJuLmi4tfGh\n=YeOr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 59931538bd56ed5d5af42111ca2f71475597391e\nparent 6a6a5f925e97bee23d5d31938b5f9f9f38becb8a\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780647957 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780647957 +0200\n\nEncrypt multi-agent v2 message payloads (#26210)\n\n## Why\n\nMulti-agent v2 currently routes agent instructions through normal tool\narguments and inter-agent context. That means the parent model can emit\nplaintext task text, Codex can persist it in history/rollouts, and the\nrecipient can receive it as ordinary assistant-message JSON.\n\nThis changes the v2 path so agent instructions stay encrypted between\nmodel calls: Responses encrypts the `message` argument returned by the\nmodel, Codex forwards only that ciphertext, and Responses decrypts it\ninternally for the recipient model.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Mark the v2 `message` parameter as encrypted for `spawn_agent`,\n`send_message`, and `followup_task`.\n- Treat multi-agent v2 tool `message` values as ciphertext\nunconditionally.\n- Store v2 inter-agent task text in\n`InterAgentCommunication.encrypted_content` with empty plaintext\n`content`.\n- Convert encrypted inter-agent communications into the Responses\n`agent_message` input item before sending the child request.\n- Preserve `agent_message` items across history, rollout, compaction,\ntelemetry, and app-server schema paths.\n- Leave multi-agent v1 unchanged.\n\n## Message shape\n\nThe model still calls the v2 tools with a `message` argument, but that\nvalue is now ciphertext:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"spawn_agent\",\n  \"arguments\": {\n    \"task_name\": \"worker\",\n    \"message\": \"<ciphertext>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCodex stores the task as encrypted inter-agent communication:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"author\": \"/root\",\n  \"recipient\": \"/root/worker\",\n  \"content\": \"\",\n  \"encrypted_content\": \"<ciphertext>\",\n  \"trigger_turn\": true\n}\n```\n\nWhen Codex builds the recipient request, it forwards the ciphertext\nusing the new Responses input item:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"agent_message\",\n  \"author\": \"/root\",\n  \"recipient\": \"/root/worker\",\n  \"content\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"encrypted_content\",\n      \"encrypted_content\": \"<ciphertext>\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nResponses decrypts that item internally for the recipient model.\n\n## Context impact\n\n- Parent context no longer carries plaintext v2 agent task instructions\nfrom these tool arguments.\n- Codex rollout/history stores ciphertext for v2 agent instructions.\n- Recipient requests receive an `agent_message` item instead of\nassistant commentary JSON for encrypted task delivery.\n- Plaintext completion/status notifications are still plaintext because\nthey are Codex-generated status messages, not encrypted model tool\narguments.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tools`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout-trace`\n- `just test -p codex-otel`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T08:25:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5f4d06ef186b896d316620556e561d59206c3ebf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5f4d06ef186b896d316620556e561d59206c3ebf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5f4d06ef186b896d316620556e561d59206c3ebf/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6a6a5f925e97bee23d5d31938b5f9f9f38becb8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6a6a5f925e97bee23d5d31938b5f9f9f38becb8a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6a6a5f925e97bee23d5d31938b5f9f9f38becb8a"}]},{"sha":"6a6a5f925e97bee23d5d31938b5f9f9f38becb8a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZhNmE1ZjkyNWU5N2JlZTIzZDVkMzE5MzhiNWY5ZjlmMzhiZWNiOGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T05:36:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T05:36:25Z"},"message":"[codex] Add environment shell info (#26480)\n\n## Why\n\nShell detection needs to be available through the `Environment`\nabstraction so callers can ask the selected local or remote environment\nfor shell metadata without adding a separate HTTP endpoint or parallel\ninfo-source path. This keeps shell metadata shaped like the existing\nenvironment-owned filesystem capability and lets remote environments\nanswer through exec-server JSON-RPC.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `environment/info` to the exec-server protocol/client/server and\nexposed `Environment::info()`.\n- Added local and remote environment info providers on `Environment`,\nfollowing the existing capability-provider pattern used for filesystem\naccess.\n- Moved the shared shell detection logic into `codex-shell-command` and\nkept core shell APIs as wrappers around that implementation.\n- Returned shell metadata as `EnvironmentInfo { shell: ShellInfo }`\nusing the existing shell detection path.\n- Added a remote environment test that calls `Environment::info()`\nthrough an exec-server-backed environment.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-shell-command`\n- `just test -p codex-core -E 'test(/shell::tests::/)'`\\n- `just test -p\ncodex-exec-server environment`","tree":{"sha":"269643bffa5b87fcac680682306cf612d9075ef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/269643bffa5b87fcac680682306cf612d9075ef4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6a6a5f925e97bee23d5d31938b5f9f9f38becb8a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqImBZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAg7cQAC8Z4yq5wWEgh6KeTLW7jOlR\n5sKIjSu4q1Hyu0nTC0DknaV1LrKGrzIpZsO8cD0XeKBA/m/aJSkQ9ZbKrXYKDW2f\npt2X0WIJqrKdRoVNGVCYcb7lp8IIA/zzGhjkqLarg3b/hx1OlwQWl46VFZTs3y4i\nEA41ZOAmpXWNLkz1RpFks8RDMJ4VtaOnSATanWcAeqOaYWCB2JyOd1Av5ILiEAol\n+wLgkbuIlDQI8DQQfslg0erzW/4Oli1ocyVeqNJvvxcfugOBNBD0QD4SawKU12zg\nDywYy0Q2l0uRvrAYzoJFNZhVfNEBxL9Ebz3TJvUdNrTjFODRScYdygISNcahOx0p\nQehfFCR8vEqJmP5iegOueHSwX2lMCXyJlD+p6NFwXhnY5NLlxFP6VhzcCE91Vhvl\nVTUFQMh0gvP0CYjvIFcqB4lxlbVZrgaS6poJOiPQYkhfmMUx3mgsFujVEV7kJUVi\nNrv+gaFzbvX2dgSYF5T7xwH9frV+QJi2/THgaUEVpmYCjs4HwZ9056H7IE/o3ke8\nkh9XUwFfaz/SNDKlqAYghy1waSNgPEs3UH5KZqKkcbYOhkS2E83sSOS+l/dj/b+E\nrOtQzI3sCxnPVMAvhGa1y/oudnmdhDCnLOPjpEIJzlaUrwMtzBvKgENE2ySGvJI8\ndDw0u4cz0rcLHDyw4VHL\n=W30j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 269643bffa5b87fcac680682306cf612d9075ef4\nparent 64e0829cab9dccb14b8273a2ebea2eee9e06c12c\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780637785 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780637785 -0700\n\n[codex] Add environment shell info (#26480)\n\n## Why\n\nShell detection needs to be available through the `Environment`\nabstraction so callers can ask the selected local or remote environment\nfor shell metadata without adding a separate HTTP endpoint or parallel\ninfo-source path. This keeps shell metadata shaped like the existing\nenvironment-owned filesystem capability and lets remote environments\nanswer through exec-server JSON-RPC.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `environment/info` to the exec-server protocol/client/server and\nexposed `Environment::info()`.\n- Added local and remote environment info providers on `Environment`,\nfollowing the existing capability-provider pattern used for filesystem\naccess.\n- Moved the shared shell detection logic into `codex-shell-command` and\nkept core shell APIs as wrappers around that implementation.\n- Returned shell metadata as `EnvironmentInfo { shell: ShellInfo }`\nusing the existing shell detection path.\n- Added a remote environment test that calls `Environment::info()`\nthrough an exec-server-backed environment.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-shell-command`\n- `just test -p codex-core -E 'test(/shell::tests::/)'`\\n- `just test -p\ncodex-exec-server environment`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T05:36:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6a6a5f925e97bee23d5d31938b5f9f9f38becb8a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6a6a5f925e97bee23d5d31938b5f9f9f38becb8a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6a6a5f925e97bee23d5d31938b5f9f9f38becb8a/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"64e0829cab9dccb14b8273a2ebea2eee9e06c12c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/64e0829cab9dccb14b8273a2ebea2eee9e06c12c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/64e0829cab9dccb14b8273a2ebea2eee9e06c12c"}]},{"sha":"64e0829cab9dccb14b8273a2ebea2eee9e06c12c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY0ZTA4MjljYWI5ZGNjYjE0YjgyNzNhMmViZWEyZWVlOWUwNmMxMmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Anton Panasenko","email":"apanasenko@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T05:12:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T05:12:23Z"},"message":"feat(remote-control): allow pairing while disabled (#26215)\n\n## Why\n\n`remoteControl/pairing/start` creates authorization for future\nremote-control connections, so it should not require the live websocket\nto already be enabled. Requiring enable first made pairing depend on\npresence instead of the persisted server enrollment that pairing\nactually uses.\n\nPairing also needs to recover when that persisted server row is stale.\nIf `/server/pair` returns `404`, making the first pairing attempt fail\nforces a manual retry even though the client can clear the stale row and\ncreate a replacement enrollment immediately.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Allow `remoteControl/pairing/start` to reuse or create the persisted\nremote-control server enrollment while remote control is disabled.\n- Keep the selected in-memory enrollment across disable and share it\nwith websocket connect so a later enable uses the same selected server.\n- Thread the app-server client name through pairing so stdio persistence\nkeeps using the websocket-owned enrollment key.\n- Recover pairing server-token auth failures through the existing\nrefresh/auth-recovery path.\n- Recover stale pairing enrollment on `/server/pair` `404` by clearing\nthe stale selected enrollment, re-enrolling once, and retrying pairing\nonce.\n- Add focused disabled-pairing and stale-pairing recovery coverage.\n\n## Verification\n\n-\n`remote_control_pairing_start_returns_pairing_artifacts_while_disabled`\nexercises pairing before enable.\n- `remote_control_handle_reenrolls_after_stale_pairing_enrollment`\nexercises stale `/server/pair` `404` recovery without a manual retry.\n\nRelated: N/A","tree":{"sha":"c5286ee6e0e64e06e2f110f7ba15a0447e4bf1ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c5286ee6e0e64e06e2f110f7ba15a0447e4bf1ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/64e0829cab9dccb14b8273a2ebea2eee9e06c12c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIlq3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVoQQAHIQP8f4WzDCs2E/RsKQAXsK\nNCRvswKSsmoOZM0DL6DWxxkbNz8GYOyigLnBBEr1vEj3nUv62WxLoXykfg8Dfsrc\nHShnMfY5gJSd2E7jCqCuvK/0SJSWWzGU6Q12kKx3P6mBrg507FLPM0SJ/0St1Eny\nyndGtTBHB46cXD/wdo/ycPzhF3uUz12UQIN4diKIvlDhJu9poZduR6m7gAvn/GKU\ndFssXDfQoWJa5CuOs8tz/F5mW+oTCf8joE8lwe96hemMh2TRx5h8EQ2n3LylLq4c\nTm0wucIZ7dSlqpAZkEsOOYeFy3seQPCNKplp3QgAeXPBIw+kLlqF8C62K5lSdL27\nJvaGk9Wwh1EtSt0rplMIfFyysqqTrbf4b1nJ2qN05FqMhr1DLQyof01kG1bQ5/K9\neSp3M6lsWlEsDNc4mt1zT0ubDCr/zYpwmlJyRKbzW3OLfdnw2kF/17AFLM06JF2P\nAp72o0CD1r40KEA0sMnuaNOjGr/GjMsrXBQxI+7YZmWk8j9iYos24X7cqucus1O7\nLn8KRUPnfLOIddGQ42qGFERKbeXdGiEMZswbIb64QR9WklrGPQr//LaiS3FPx7GZ\nbSeuXTBiBZJNayBnW+EgwEhdtO2MAbxWOp6WqGI1IQnDntB8+DUWgk3p/tr5tjOD\nbYnH7t1b3thqGWIoo0mr\n=wv3O\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c5286ee6e0e64e06e2f110f7ba15a0447e4bf1ae\nparent a2f5874b7a2db79b46c60a73858ba4c4b4807c05\nauthor Anton Panasenko <apanasenko@openai.com> 1780636343 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780636343 +0000\n\nfeat(remote-control): allow pairing while disabled (#26215)\n\n## Why\n\n`remoteControl/pairing/start` creates authorization for future\nremote-control connections, so it should not require the live websocket\nto already be enabled. Requiring enable first made pairing depend on\npresence instead of the persisted server enrollment that pairing\nactually uses.\n\nPairing also needs to recover when that persisted server row is stale.\nIf `/server/pair` returns `404`, making the first pairing attempt fail\nforces a manual retry even though the client can clear the stale row and\ncreate a replacement enrollment immediately.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Allow `remoteControl/pairing/start` to reuse or create the persisted\nremote-control server enrollment while remote control is disabled.\n- Keep the selected in-memory enrollment across disable and share it\nwith websocket connect so a later enable uses the same selected server.\n- Thread the app-server client name through pairing so stdio persistence\nkeeps using the websocket-owned enrollment key.\n- Recover pairing server-token auth failures through the existing\nrefresh/auth-recovery path.\n- Recover stale pairing enrollment on `/server/pair` `404` by clearing\nthe stale selected enrollment, re-enrolling once, and retrying pairing\nonce.\n- Add focused disabled-pairing and stale-pairing recovery coverage.\n\n## Verification\n\n-\n`remote_control_pairing_start_returns_pairing_artifacts_while_disabled`\nexercises pairing before enable.\n- `remote_control_handle_reenrolls_after_stale_pairing_enrollment`\nexercises stale `/server/pair` `404` recovery without a manual retry.\n\nRelated: N/A","verified_at":"2026-06-05T05:12:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/64e0829cab9dccb14b8273a2ebea2eee9e06c12c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/64e0829cab9dccb14b8273a2ebea2eee9e06c12c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/64e0829cab9dccb14b8273a2ebea2eee9e06c12c/comments","author":{"login":"apanasenko-oai","id":228802911,"node_id":"U_kgDODaNBXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228802911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/apanasenko-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/apanasenko-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a2f5874b7a2db79b46c60a73858ba4c4b4807c05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a2f5874b7a2db79b46c60a73858ba4c4b4807c05","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a2f5874b7a2db79b46c60a73858ba4c4b4807c05"}]},{"sha":"a2f5874b7a2db79b46c60a73858ba4c4b4807c05","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEyZjU4NzRiN2EyZGI3OWI0NmM2MGE3Mzg1OGJhNGM0YjQ4MDdjMDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T04:48:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T04:48:45Z"},"message":"core: derive exec policy filesystem policy from profile (#26499)\n\n## Why\n\n`PermissionProfile` already owns the runtime filesystem sandbox policy\nthrough `file_system_sandbox_policy()`. Keeping a separate\n`FileSystemSandboxPolicy` on exec-policy fallback contexts made it\npossible for callers and tests to construct split states that the\nproduction permission model should not rely on.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Removed `file_system_sandbox_policy` from `UnmatchedCommandContext`,\n`ExecApprovalRequest`, and the intercepted Unix exec-policy context.\n- Derived filesystem sandbox policy inside unmatched-command decision\nlogic from `PermissionProfile::file_system_sandbox_policy()`.\n- Simplified shell/unified-exec callers and tests that were only\nplumbing the duplicate policy through.\n\n## Testing\n\nLocal tests not run per request; relying on remote CI.","tree":{"sha":"ee9428d4e3248295a778cb79b3f0bc638de46c69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ee9428d4e3248295a778cb79b3f0bc638de46c69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a2f5874b7a2db79b46c60a73858ba4c4b4807c05","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIlUtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwK8QADdyowxT4SeUtjAWiEd5F8uz\nrPynF0crBVb1rxpTQc2Ubx179CchdMOwB8+bMG6r/BXmK9/iCZlGf6dkxe9qRdix\nQfeEeUOH9syIGbaSKQc4M795C/lC6PkGs/OGTYXpHjLnU/5rH6OIDk8aitTG9SRh\nA0HfKReDRmxK7Jf66T+XNJB+mXkDxq898pAfBH5RM7sYYr/m2prjSkNNoETOLjFC\nsr18E/ByuIi60cR5I+fCfqlZSa9eK9Jzsvc8davEFSJWP8+Mw61Zz2R51zA4RScv\npfejHu8y3oarnuDOn6bjy+R+z+mNpynEQk+/9eBHFKp78YWM4WVoJa3cbnAUHEyf\nd77CHvLwdVL4BOjUsCs09ZynmCn2zksni3jY+4T4g/VHhKgENP7Ru9CFzzmHaeB6\ns7sZpgmfgGVayEXQ+kkJkgFEyPgGTk0/n8UeYUWexH0n0mi3+JdyNOlWqECa8AOI\nNg4wU4GWz5K8MHC1MBjzZckLzQW6stsCpfMPsXbM5YtASK0Vbsn74sTAUdGYazY6\ncko7677VsISseg+BYCVDxTSzubNqDRCvD6aFRUZmVYiR19cYZswOqHEyF/Tm0BA+\nAl0mnRCyIGw41a+ReKc16zH+6QusMWf8+24c4aauPMGyqwQJr/yeWvEeBdq2sPF7\nfO2+lMCCzD+0kCrCgTcM\n=/5o8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ee9428d4e3248295a778cb79b3f0bc638de46c69\nparent 1d9c9c9f33735223cc564ec942001c9141a11eb1\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780634925 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780634925 -0700\n\ncore: derive exec policy filesystem policy from profile (#26499)\n\n## Why\n\n`PermissionProfile` already owns the runtime filesystem sandbox policy\nthrough `file_system_sandbox_policy()`. Keeping a separate\n`FileSystemSandboxPolicy` on exec-policy fallback contexts made it\npossible for callers and tests to construct split states that the\nproduction permission model should not rely on.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Removed `file_system_sandbox_policy` from `UnmatchedCommandContext`,\n`ExecApprovalRequest`, and the intercepted Unix exec-policy context.\n- Derived filesystem sandbox policy inside unmatched-command decision\nlogic from `PermissionProfile::file_system_sandbox_policy()`.\n- Simplified shell/unified-exec callers and tests that were only\nplumbing the duplicate policy through.\n\n## Testing\n\nLocal tests not run per request; relying on remote CI.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T04:48:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a2f5874b7a2db79b46c60a73858ba4c4b4807c05","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a2f5874b7a2db79b46c60a73858ba4c4b4807c05","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a2f5874b7a2db79b46c60a73858ba4c4b4807c05/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1d9c9c9f33735223cc564ec942001c9141a11eb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1d9c9c9f33735223cc564ec942001c9141a11eb1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1d9c9c9f33735223cc564ec942001c9141a11eb1"}]},{"sha":"1d9c9c9f33735223cc564ec942001c9141a11eb1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFkOWM5YzlmMzM3MzUyMjNjYzU2NGVjOTQyMDAxYzkxNDFhMTFlYjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T03:23:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T03:23:37Z"},"message":"[codex] Keep Bazel startup options stable across commands (#26256)\n\n## Why\n\n`just bazel-clippy` ran target discovery with\n`--noexperimental_remote_repo_contents_cache`, then ran the build with\nthe workspace default `--experimental_remote_repo_contents_cache`. Bazel\ntherefore killed and restarted its server on each transition, slowing\nrepeated commands and discarding the in-memory analysis cache. An audit\nfound the same class of startup-option variation in several CI command\nsequences.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep local lint target-discovery queries on the workspace-default\nBazel server, while making CI target discovery explicitly use the CI\nstartup options.\n- Normalize GitHub Actions launches through the BuildBuddy wrapper to\nshare `BAZEL_OUTPUT_USER_ROOT` and\n`--noexperimental_remote_repo_contents_cache`.\n- Route the CI lockfile check and Windows test-shard query through the\nsame startup configuration.\n- Document the startup-option invariant and add wrapper regression\ncoverage.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Confirmed consecutive local clippy target-discovery runs retained the\nsame Bazel server PID.","tree":{"sha":"5473f4b378b38589b65c0d39c57f62336d80b67c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5473f4b378b38589b65c0d39c57f62336d80b67c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1d9c9c9f33735223cc564ec942001c9141a11eb1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIkE5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALcUQAEgV5elzVpMWBbSaBR+cSz4f\n8mi34UlF/wsaTrEj9p8PSaj0P5Or69L9kWYBJpVLQJ5misBdgsVjKBlVN9yLU0be\nEmZLyD/acqxM9gb/WBI+6jgnNns3CI44PsW87Z03kzlOAW9k55Sc0kwnTsvMAaBN\nH/Rnzl/1Bl56MtCHWH6VDLeyTJoelAJMtrtke9MV2k3pRuNUp1ywZhX4+bpGOk5L\nzoB+rg8JyQHG5T0vqUuPdBzpwETyPEoRyyln8OJh/6XWuWoD/la43mrSiSkbNnhV\nRRuDI9O49Z5Uzj3nwCZH6LmcjKpKb4Vt9W1YYkjRcRFtrg5VCl2pN6O2dOdu7d9y\nFD95VcstDHABr96zbUqGQRd05BlthNMK+VTgNP5udCjIWVUavRYCchR1EwGcCtdm\nhk+ahPq6pokD1VVOg1l7AYHgYOTB5K49JZJps14kf3l6M5V22IxAsHfCy0kgp9RW\nEIar78I7AG57/qvSUx57fDj/4Fsgo4eJ//A00LszRZUrgzp4cc4v1O8bv6cQfqWW\nKf+bQdBGBiUxZIF1/LHg/1naYe52eXckFjqUp7YrpctihZBG9gWXiNegCWM0MpIG\nNCXZjqhczi40+w8NyAHnoLJo8npDnVbeLjczbGZ1AAHxpXdEOxfA9Y/WK8jWw8Nb\nBUB3vHZqVFPKBWsFqsTN\n=CeZm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5473f4b378b38589b65c0d39c57f62336d80b67c\nparent 4de7a2b9d8eae19e00ca7f744647fa1aabdc204f\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780629817 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780629817 -0700\n\n[codex] Keep Bazel startup options stable across commands (#26256)\n\n## Why\n\n`just bazel-clippy` ran target discovery with\n`--noexperimental_remote_repo_contents_cache`, then ran the build with\nthe workspace default `--experimental_remote_repo_contents_cache`. Bazel\ntherefore killed and restarted its server on each transition, slowing\nrepeated commands and discarding the in-memory analysis cache. An audit\nfound the same class of startup-option variation in several CI command\nsequences.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep local lint target-discovery queries on the workspace-default\nBazel server, while making CI target discovery explicitly use the CI\nstartup options.\n- Normalize GitHub Actions launches through the BuildBuddy wrapper to\nshare `BAZEL_OUTPUT_USER_ROOT` and\n`--noexperimental_remote_repo_contents_cache`.\n- Route the CI lockfile check and Windows test-shard query through the\nsame startup configuration.\n- Document the startup-option invariant and add wrapper regression\ncoverage.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Confirmed consecutive local clippy target-discovery runs retained the\nsame Bazel server PID.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T03:23:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1d9c9c9f33735223cc564ec942001c9141a11eb1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1d9c9c9f33735223cc564ec942001c9141a11eb1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1d9c9c9f33735223cc564ec942001c9141a11eb1/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4de7a2b9d8eae19e00ca7f744647fa1aabdc204f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4de7a2b9d8eae19e00ca7f744647fa1aabdc204f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4de7a2b9d8eae19e00ca7f744647fa1aabdc204f"}]},{"sha":"4de7a2b9d8eae19e00ca7f744647fa1aabdc204f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRkZTdhMmI5ZDhlYWUxOWUwMGNhN2Y3NDQ2NDdmYTFhYWJkYzIwNGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T02:31:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T02:31:06Z"},"message":"fix(rmcp): refresh expired OAuth tokens before startup (#26482)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex persists OAuth expiry as an absolute `expires_at`, then\nreconstructs RMCP’s relative `expires_in` when credentials are loaded.\nFor an already-expired token, Codex reconstructed `expires_in` as\nmissing.\n\n[RMCP 0.15 treated a missing `expires_in` as zero when a refresh token\nwas\npresent](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/rust-sdk/blob/9cfc905a9ef17c8bba6748dc0a9bdd2452681733/crates/rmcp/src/transport/auth.rs#L704-L723),\nso this still triggered a refresh. [RMCP 1.7 treats missing expiry\ninformation as unknown and uses the access token\nas-is](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/rust-sdk/blob/3529c3675ff64db805bd947ca6ece6090809e43d/crates/rmcp/src/transport/auth.rs#L1233-L1265),\ncausing the stale token to be sent during `initialize`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Represent a known-expired persisted token as `expires_in = 0`,\npreserving `None` for genuinely unknown expiry.\n- Add Streamable HTTP coverage requiring the token to refresh before the\nstartup handshake.\n\n## Validation\n\n- The new regression test fails on RMCP 1.7 before the fix and passes\nafterward.\n- The same scenario passes on the commit immediately before the RMCP 1.7\nupdate, using RMCP 0.15.\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client` (63 passed).","tree":{"sha":"ee319c1e5180dca35e72fb8ced55f80f4fb39309","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ee319c1e5180dca35e72fb8ced55f80f4fb39309"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4de7a2b9d8eae19e00ca7f744647fa1aabdc204f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIjTqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAawcQAGVGWyTB3Etr14tOnHa7kd2B\nTfeGAVKkVDjFzbiWX3Gd8qKx3itjFdeSz7efLNUbKOMVEuwEKfm1P6RPezgfj1va\nEvOdMCWcS0cio/dGzMnHttxx9VwwKvh1F+Xpkl4PpDDsgUe6fes42ZB6AumaYMso\nkiuQhh5ZAAP+HCN3uiSBTe1Pf2ALLoLJ1JekcG1JsAoIYZjqajfA6+2iAyensovS\nwZXoqQ0njOpOVGpsfZgWnldPgSJb+Rko+C7N68y8NDMeXLakjvEerST1kuAV4LVg\nHYR8t3eEYPASE7SLxG34ri3j/X1lyEBMfYfKVOvE/mroSCeVc98kg2bQ4jrPgjPC\nMB1LmFVurEfz2LQ/Kqe1m0/u1FpKbTywItpwMI8J1LJqSYNEfdC/Fz1yiEhh64nL\n1N9XxaSoM6R5+qUK6LKHDs5Ut+cKrAlF3WkGT0qtLD7GjvtGgQK6gGVUoYW6LuLG\nEdqvT3yCxzAQ6fUlhycORirJG6Mdw/xs97fE4pfMPbDeJno6toTr5YjuTCgT2NoN\nxnOBqo3+J38Bi1i9tP3IiH740C9/jPOuWvh9uex1KWgMeKaH22xUynhOepKPx7OI\nP1CyX4uNMrsG1pRzOVU4IT7qS5s9ludj3BNPuvbbTmmz8t0JSlvm/CdvjoSCJ/iG\nWc3JZRDloiSTxjlclrIK\n=LE7U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ee319c1e5180dca35e72fb8ced55f80f4fb39309\nparent e0096db6dc8a2f89394986123802a676a1be20c5\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780626666 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780626666 +0000\n\nfix(rmcp): refresh expired OAuth tokens before startup (#26482)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex persists OAuth expiry as an absolute `expires_at`, then\nreconstructs RMCP’s relative `expires_in` when credentials are loaded.\nFor an already-expired token, Codex reconstructed `expires_in` as\nmissing.\n\n[RMCP 0.15 treated a missing `expires_in` as zero when a refresh token\nwas\npresent](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/rust-sdk/blob/9cfc905a9ef17c8bba6748dc0a9bdd2452681733/crates/rmcp/src/transport/auth.rs#L704-L723),\nso this still triggered a refresh. [RMCP 1.7 treats missing expiry\ninformation as unknown and uses the access token\nas-is](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/rust-sdk/blob/3529c3675ff64db805bd947ca6ece6090809e43d/crates/rmcp/src/transport/auth.rs#L1233-L1265),\ncausing the stale token to be sent during `initialize`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Represent a known-expired persisted token as `expires_in = 0`,\npreserving `None` for genuinely unknown expiry.\n- Add Streamable HTTP coverage requiring the token to refresh before the\nstartup handshake.\n\n## Validation\n\n- The new regression test fails on RMCP 1.7 before the fix and passes\nafterward.\n- The same scenario passes on the commit immediately before the RMCP 1.7\nupdate, using RMCP 0.15.\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client` (63 passed).","verified_at":"2026-06-05T02:31:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4de7a2b9d8eae19e00ca7f744647fa1aabdc204f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4de7a2b9d8eae19e00ca7f744647fa1aabdc204f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4de7a2b9d8eae19e00ca7f744647fa1aabdc204f/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e0096db6dc8a2f89394986123802a676a1be20c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0096db6dc8a2f89394986123802a676a1be20c5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e0096db6dc8a2f89394986123802a676a1be20c5"}]},{"sha":"e0096db6dc8a2f89394986123802a676a1be20c5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUwMDk2ZGI2ZGM4YTJmODkzOTQ5ODYxMjM4MDJhNjc2YTFiZTIwYzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T01:49:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T01:49:51Z"},"message":"[codex] Add use_responses_lite 'override' logic (#26487)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add a defaulted `ModelInfo.use_responses_lite` catalog field\n- support serializing `reasoning.context` while preserving the existing\neffort and summary path\n- has not been turned on for any models yet\n\nI've added an override to parallel tools if responses_lite is on. I've\nalso forced persistent reasoning when using responses_lite. It would be\nideal if we could centralize all the responses_lite plumbing, but I\nthink this is best for now to keep the plumbing & diffs small.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-protocol\nmodel_info_defaults_availability_nux_to_none_when_omitted`\n- `RUST_MIN_STACK=8388608 cargo test -p codex-core\nresponses_lite_sets_all_turns_context_and_disables_parallel_tool_calls`\n- `RUST_MIN_STACK=8388608 cargo test -p codex-core\nconfigured_reasoning_summary_is_sent`\n- `cargo check -p codex-core --tests`\n- `RUST_MIN_STACK=8388608 cargo clippy -p codex-core --tests` (passes\nwith pre-existing warnings in `codex-code-mode` and\n`codex-core-plugins`)","tree":{"sha":"35ba16c8e10610b1ef630c4d142fec3244bf87a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/35ba16c8e10610b1ef630c4d142fec3244bf87a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e0096db6dc8a2f89394986123802a676a1be20c5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIis/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeQ0QAFCCwqdRZw+lvBBwnegG2cRE\nbwtpAZ/HeZyPCYpGdHr1oDcVslBGBzdEqa/dLjTj9RGI6SyCPaMEAlatU7lBth4y\nYhClQNjmZBElbekEfmYz4TB7eABdI3Gz6IlzJVALH80oAhVCHZtwOun1M27u4obT\nfAfs1C2N427DuF6R5Th2m4drIuZYf/QD2yy96VnMla1kXK7ZO/WRid2Fh98d35Zw\nGNBUdW3G+kaXFbIBCoA1Ld3ppyX06RCwgXR4Y2KzprFfFxbuMLASSVF5s6DyXDmK\nLNxgmIwxjwB+6iJe6HOai9GUD8GXJVbn/+C6TlQf0Za7PXrPh6GA/Vr4XySV+Z3L\nkPIPDL6Zd/yXGgth8bncIcn95gGtPpnYNJn9gAzODpgkvM2Dj9+C2wiJvF+pWFJJ\nFOHJyuHsCpqkqdrwGZT8HN33lND3Oyx0M6u1zuIK4FwOHjlfHmJ3UMZu4rvfqIt1\nhYLmV1VZpCDaHCbr/GmHDbJcPFV1YZQphNzbJCaNEtlc0ecNkaJlJf2YT6qhrs+l\njveN4e4mvzHVCkJnCvngzjJVMOaTLZEIG1zATydxjHMD1KCYugBCsEjDTyg/5bd9\nzQFfa1+pbwDBLdU6hfLCwgPUwkFBTcqllRtCsfYxku6yjN424YDJ1UnQq4FTu8Db\n9mr3UULyCxRBZFxFP10+\n=C1O4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 35ba16c8e10610b1ef630c4d142fec3244bf87a8\nparent ecae41274091252f454eb5ed0507036ed4e6fc19\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1780624191 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780624191 -0700\n\n[codex] Add use_responses_lite 'override' logic (#26487)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add a defaulted `ModelInfo.use_responses_lite` catalog field\n- support serializing `reasoning.context` while preserving the existing\neffort and summary path\n- has not been turned on for any models yet\n\nI've added an override to parallel tools if responses_lite is on. I've\nalso forced persistent reasoning when using responses_lite. It would be\nideal if we could centralize all the responses_lite plumbing, but I\nthink this is best for now to keep the plumbing & diffs small.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-protocol\nmodel_info_defaults_availability_nux_to_none_when_omitted`\n- `RUST_MIN_STACK=8388608 cargo test -p codex-core\nresponses_lite_sets_all_turns_context_and_disables_parallel_tool_calls`\n- `RUST_MIN_STACK=8388608 cargo test -p codex-core\nconfigured_reasoning_summary_is_sent`\n- `cargo check -p codex-core --tests`\n- `RUST_MIN_STACK=8388608 cargo clippy -p codex-core --tests` (passes\nwith pre-existing warnings in `codex-code-mode` and\n`codex-core-plugins`)","verified_at":"2026-06-05T01:49:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0096db6dc8a2f89394986123802a676a1be20c5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e0096db6dc8a2f89394986123802a676a1be20c5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0096db6dc8a2f89394986123802a676a1be20c5/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ecae41274091252f454eb5ed0507036ed4e6fc19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ecae41274091252f454eb5ed0507036ed4e6fc19","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ecae41274091252f454eb5ed0507036ed4e6fc19"}]},{"sha":"ecae41274091252f454eb5ed0507036ed4e6fc19","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGVjYWU0MTI3NDA5MTI1MmY0NTRlYjVlZDA1MDcwMzZlZDRlNmZjMTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"rreichel3-oai","email":"rreichel3@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T00:58:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T00:58:14Z"},"message":"[codex] Emit sandbox outcome telemetry event (#25955)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a dedicated `codex.sandbox_outcome` telemetry event so we can query\nsandbox edge outcomes without threading sandbox metadata through\ntool-result output types.\n\nThis is meant to make sandbox failures and approved escalation retries\nvisible in OTEL while keeping the existing `codex.tool_result` event\nshape focused on tool completion data.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds `SessionTelemetry::sandbox_outcome(...)`, which emits\n`codex.sandbox_outcome` as both a log and trace event.\n- Records the tool name, call id, sandbox outcome, initial attempt\nduration, and escalated attempt duration when a retry runs.\n- Emits `denied` when the sandbox blocks execution and no retry is run.\n- Emits `timed_out` and `signal` when those sandbox errors surface from\ntool execution.\n- Emits `escalated` when the initial sandboxed attempt fails and the\napproved unsandboxed retry succeeds.\n- Adds OTEL coverage for the new event payload, including timing fields.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `RUST_MIN_STACK=8388608 just test -p codex-core\nsandbox_outcome_event_records_outcome\nhandle_sandbox_error_user_approves_retry_records_tool_decision`\n- `just test -p codex-otel\notel_export_routing_policy_routes_tool_result_log_and_trace_events\nruntime_metrics_summary_collects_tool_api_and_streaming_metrics`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-otel`","tree":{"sha":"512e0ea0eee2a43e1c44016a205fb40402ca6792","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/512e0ea0eee2a43e1c44016a205fb40402ca6792"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ecae41274091252f454eb5ed0507036ed4e6fc19","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIh8mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0owQABre0VPqTZ2k9pRB0XDzip+N\nn04yHFArJE8yWfBNm05t+GaW4GBogVN4bCk+Y4zFGTwgFuANqAezWkSg9FfBWaqh\nE8JvprKLJaqcdYx7BYpELef8qhc5qg+mNbkjmxqUJ4bLI6Ne92oh6bACGFgyrUL0\nk/NtJ7OlUC1Y3RxkJ9Um1KK23Lq2TW9p+NHG5wwdtieoIhNLYriUDJdWjRVipC0j\nmeOusWFWkb0GOWR5gvQVvImwkz+VO+0R3F4+HQ/Wg/NKv6InseLA8rrScWZf5uil\nLUQso1bYa/Ag/8ISE2x0D90bbBf4bOfskYXUprYtqNJJ+FmErtzK4MZA6TWq2le6\n0t0IMlSUCYU7h7t9LwkmCRH5tVYw1VWMXmzpWggFkywlpEJO5aLFluy/dcoc4b0Y\ncN8e93znn/FmftaBQxVaFI00a/vLeya6cMmPXcWbYKZI7yLZeobppxFGm8u64LXe\nERXRqVybCbxUut2dyZj7Ye3UFfuhFWgz0hJRVV3ptM+O1RbQC9pKDdqByg2WrfRI\ny4Q3rNwhTNm3JkyHElxGYamFa3C/qIz61/pNZwS4P3bweSapInFYJHLlYinD5/Uo\nOag2XlosaKTyfXWNTCQmbSUwTwlfAOlvLpRCVH6VwF+aRqoZQQnFD2N7JzlcRr+l\n0iZRQHn8rsk3tvLD1O/f\n=gLNs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 512e0ea0eee2a43e1c44016a205fb40402ca6792\nparent 4be1a168fc7ed3313ddc62031da036f0c50209b7\nauthor rreichel3-oai <rreichel3@openai.com> 1780621094 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780621094 -0400\n\n[codex] Emit sandbox outcome telemetry event (#25955)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a dedicated `codex.sandbox_outcome` telemetry event so we can query\nsandbox edge outcomes without threading sandbox metadata through\ntool-result output types.\n\nThis is meant to make sandbox failures and approved escalation retries\nvisible in OTEL while keeping the existing `codex.tool_result` event\nshape focused on tool completion data.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds `SessionTelemetry::sandbox_outcome(...)`, which emits\n`codex.sandbox_outcome` as both a log and trace event.\n- Records the tool name, call id, sandbox outcome, initial attempt\nduration, and escalated attempt duration when a retry runs.\n- Emits `denied` when the sandbox blocks execution and no retry is run.\n- Emits `timed_out` and `signal` when those sandbox errors surface from\ntool execution.\n- Emits `escalated` when the initial sandboxed attempt fails and the\napproved unsandboxed retry succeeds.\n- Adds OTEL coverage for the new event payload, including timing fields.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `RUST_MIN_STACK=8388608 just test -p codex-core\nsandbox_outcome_event_records_outcome\nhandle_sandbox_error_user_approves_retry_records_tool_decision`\n- `just test -p codex-otel\notel_export_routing_policy_routes_tool_result_log_and_trace_events\nruntime_metrics_summary_collects_tool_api_and_streaming_metrics`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-otel`","verified_at":"2026-06-05T00:58:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ecae41274091252f454eb5ed0507036ed4e6fc19","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ecae41274091252f454eb5ed0507036ed4e6fc19","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ecae41274091252f454eb5ed0507036ed4e6fc19/comments","author":{"login":"rreichel3-oai","id":247462724,"node_id":"U_kgDODr_7RA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247462724?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rreichel3-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rreichel3-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rreichel3-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rreichel3-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rreichel3-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rreichel3-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rreichel3-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rreichel3-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rreichel3-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rreichel3-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rreichel3-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4be1a168fc7ed3313ddc62031da036f0c50209b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4be1a168fc7ed3313ddc62031da036f0c50209b7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4be1a168fc7ed3313ddc62031da036f0c50209b7"}]},{"sha":"4be1a168fc7ed3313ddc62031da036f0c50209b7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRiZTFhMTY4ZmM3ZWQzMzEzZGRjNjIwMzFkYTAzNmYwYzUwMjA5Yjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T00:51:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T00:51:13Z"},"message":"ci: test windows cross build (#25000)\n\nWe cross build when using bazel for windows. This causes a couple\nhiccups in that v8 does a mksnapshot step that is expecting to snapshot\non the host arch which wasn't matching when we were doing the\ncrossbuild. This was causing segfault failiures when starting up\ncodemode from a cross built artifact.\n\nThis changes things such that we cross build the library and then run\nand link a snapshot on the host machine/arch which is windows. This\ngives us a functional snapshot and library that can start code-mode on\nwindows.\n\nThis fixes the build and then fixes two test regressions we had.","tree":{"sha":"72e4809962cb244a795a75039b3a54f31af1c6f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/72e4809962cb244a795a75039b3a54f31af1c6f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4be1a168fc7ed3313ddc62031da036f0c50209b7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIh2BCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAOwQAGzwOwvAQTbovqTIJyWWf+A8\n3Rsuaao8jLWNxn9R9vUdqwXfsrlS2tqk2NWGVp9QiS0q59G8ETKaysYfwgdF5EpV\n/B6hoanXXLf/XuBPms33S5R36Z7n6racHMC0euHR1GwP4Js0pB/4nFoWf+eN3GTF\n3klG31aq93UURKuZ7P+lQ7zUGhyOuDCNCZ/kB83Gh1lus/I5YjBxdHcYNgxNvFdz\nGc8V/wNNB+BFCxYzXvkO3gZIdXnH7qVonjxRP+rRp1/ldU8Rxh9cyDpabyi160CS\nX/KT7YQ0THzPqBXlqETR2xloDvsKwGiPvP/IYD+vt7Ih5/6Q0hGSZ84I0dYVpkay\n31FPMyMgGE8D2scDcA8fWkFWT0/0aHA0iP+j3Sa+ko3kufz7Jvs1d8iC65ig8pQ4\n6I0yflVeBDBspsPmQT70G3kHjAtbxwK6Xi2DTTjdc2awloM6JGuc/nM14tFu1QRT\nqRctOlX2XU3iPN9Kz9X9WEPFL/2IiFVQSpvQReYFgrq6lW6Drq5kPj4kDgGwXR7I\nbdTIlx9CALSyjSvO2zmsuMQUoR6TyxsUvHbHj60osNh2rZK6T89VRo/ymXEKgqHY\ncbDYCvq5npLocFSinTJMQ6RKu+HKfWFZN6WCzdnfKZO/K0ak5jN/OPH9X7m0jSa9\n9NNc7UJW7C+4g+xNsPEh\n=Vo29\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 72e4809962cb244a795a75039b3a54f31af1c6f0\nparent 72d0bfb6ba4b59ad78fbe012052a06a2c0874fc3\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1780620673 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780620673 -0700\n\nci: test windows cross build (#25000)\n\nWe cross build when using bazel for windows. This causes a couple\nhiccups in that v8 does a mksnapshot step that is expecting to snapshot\non the host arch which wasn't matching when we were doing the\ncrossbuild. This was causing segfault failiures when starting up\ncodemode from a cross built artifact.\n\nThis changes things such that we cross build the library and then run\nand link a snapshot on the host machine/arch which is windows. This\ngives us a functional snapshot and library that can start code-mode on\nwindows.\n\nThis fixes the build and then fixes two test regressions we had.","verified_at":"2026-06-05T00:51:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4be1a168fc7ed3313ddc62031da036f0c50209b7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4be1a168fc7ed3313ddc62031da036f0c50209b7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4be1a168fc7ed3313ddc62031da036f0c50209b7/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"72d0bfb6ba4b59ad78fbe012052a06a2c0874fc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/72d0bfb6ba4b59ad78fbe012052a06a2c0874fc3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/72d0bfb6ba4b59ad78fbe012052a06a2c0874fc3"}]},{"sha":"72d0bfb6ba4b59ad78fbe012052a06a2c0874fc3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDcyZDBiZmI2YmE0YjU5YWQ3OGZiZTAxMjA1MmEwNmEyYzA4NzRmYzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"beggers-openai","email":"beggers@openai.com","date":"2026-06-05T00:47:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-05T00:47:58Z"},"message":"Pull plugin service less frequently (#26431)\n\n# Summary\nReduce download traffic to `github.com/openai/plugins` while continuing\nto check for updates on every Codex startup.\n\n# Root cause\nThe startup sync replaced the local repository with a fresh shallow\nclone whenever the remote revision changed. At Codex's global scale,\nrepeatedly downloading the repository created excessive GitHub traffic.\n\n# Changes\n- Run `git ls-remote` on each startup to read the remote HEAD SHA.\n- Skip all repository downloads when the local and remote SHAs match.\n- Update existing checkouts with an exact-SHA shallow `git fetch`,\nfollowed by reset and clean.\n- Bootstrap new installations with `git init` plus the same shallow\nfetch, rather than cloning.\n- Keep the existing file lock so concurrent Codex processes serialize\nupdates and do not duplicate fetches.\n- Preserve the existing GitHub HTTP and export archive fallback\nbehavior.\n\n# Impact\nEach startup makes one lightweight remote HEAD check. Repository objects\nare downloaded only when the revision changes, and existing Git objects\nare reused during updates.\n\n# Validation\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins startup_sync` (15 tests passed)\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (201 tests passed)\n- `just clippy -p codex-core-plugins` (passes with one pre-existing\n`large_enum_variant` warning)\n- Production app-server smoke test against GitHub:\n  - Fresh home: `ls-remote`, `git init`, one exact-SHA shallow fetch\n- Unchanged restart: `ls-remote` and local `rev-parse` only; no fetch or\nclone\n- Bench smoke passed","tree":{"sha":"6bb159d682e87502d9db9420d1b8e7772d97ffe0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6bb159d682e87502d9db9420d1b8e7772d97ffe0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/72d0bfb6ba4b59ad78fbe012052a06a2c0874fc3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIhy+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+XEQAKWAEH6HrpgyUc37BtpWCcvZ\nDqOwOpUSM31RGjc516jCTDbKRn0/XQ0PBDhXWubdR9gszKHZGGRQRejgvAi5r+O5\nh/DrZ09VMigIKqXy9BKtbiiUw82NNxDoZFYwMqlXG0HiwHuQ+jgI0RMeDtH59zdw\n51IQCMGF581isZgR1PuS4GmNB7ozYAF4VSFnOQwsGgSJfSqLeHH76IK1CNGK4q6k\ndNOZ19fafrqJZxOGgodZBZQVIlg40SXPBYyQxV+e80LwwLytUANd5I/7q/10z59q\ngmJH9n+rXyxbW7Lg2aAx/BxsnaQrcN/Jicxan8LoUbiqGWPbUjOierFCwc+BthVu\nvXn7N1fARR1No93Qa6F3W3IR/kOfeGhcHECaDXruqX3JrbTxc5mA5vKu9X1R2OP6\n+/9tDkXJbjNpibAtLsYDgpAG/uyC0WX85nvAYProlBZx5L+nvYftjtItWHYotTMP\nhG5RBS4gqOFw0+R7L5aWVA2dYDdH7vVYlZSzkoMSURsGr/o+QosjkoTFHKqW23uL\n6bFSfJmNhPQg5ZxJGSFTfqJVq/C05CCabT9/eo4wmUlSAJm7UNbhKPg8lccu/Y7F\nmIkfa+FiXlfqIId26Cy88sjdF+XjgbjJWu9ZGuPoNCZ8mlUOWTgTGYSHZuttgaDZ\np68+9dgkMpmUl3lKS/M5\n=jsj8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6bb159d682e87502d9db9420d1b8e7772d97ffe0\nparent 0b2e7b5eb1cfa74e5807a84b291e6c900eeb197d\nauthor beggers-openai <beggers@openai.com> 1780620478 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780620478 -0700\n\nPull plugin service less frequently (#26431)\n\n# Summary\nReduce download traffic to `github.com/openai/plugins` while continuing\nto check for updates on every Codex startup.\n\n# Root cause\nThe startup sync replaced the local repository with a fresh shallow\nclone whenever the remote revision changed. At Codex's global scale,\nrepeatedly downloading the repository created excessive GitHub traffic.\n\n# Changes\n- Run `git ls-remote` on each startup to read the remote HEAD SHA.\n- Skip all repository downloads when the local and remote SHAs match.\n- Update existing checkouts with an exact-SHA shallow `git fetch`,\nfollowed by reset and clean.\n- Bootstrap new installations with `git init` plus the same shallow\nfetch, rather than cloning.\n- Keep the existing file lock so concurrent Codex processes serialize\nupdates and do not duplicate fetches.\n- Preserve the existing GitHub HTTP and export archive fallback\nbehavior.\n\n# Impact\nEach startup makes one lightweight remote HEAD check. Repository objects\nare downloaded only when the revision changes, and existing Git objects\nare reused during updates.\n\n# Validation\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins startup_sync` (15 tests passed)\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` (201 tests passed)\n- `just clippy -p codex-core-plugins` (passes with one pre-existing\n`large_enum_variant` warning)\n- Production app-server smoke test against GitHub:\n  - Fresh home: `ls-remote`, `git init`, one exact-SHA shallow fetch\n- Unchanged restart: `ls-remote` and local `rev-parse` only; no fetch or\nclone\n- Bench smoke passed","verified_at":"2026-06-05T00:47:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/72d0bfb6ba4b59ad78fbe012052a06a2c0874fc3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/72d0bfb6ba4b59ad78fbe012052a06a2c0874fc3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/72d0bfb6ba4b59ad78fbe012052a06a2c0874fc3/comments","author":{"login":"beggers-openai","id":175158901,"node_id":"U_kgDOCnC2dQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175158901?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beggers-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/beggers-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beggers-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beggers-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beggers-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beggers-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beggers-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beggers-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beggers-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beggers-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/beggers-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0b2e7b5eb1cfa74e5807a84b291e6c900eeb197d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b2e7b5eb1cfa74e5807a84b291e6c900eeb197d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0b2e7b5eb1cfa74e5807a84b291e6c900eeb197d"}]},{"sha":"0b2e7b5eb1cfa74e5807a84b291e6c900eeb197d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBiMmU3YjVlYjFjZmE3NGU1ODA3YTg0YjI5MWU2YzkwMGVlYjE5N2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T23:52:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T23:52:10Z"},"message":"Improve Windows sandbox setup refresh diagnostics (#26471)\n\n## Why\n\nUsers have been seeing opaque Windows sandbox setup refresh failures\nsuch as `windows sandbox: spawn setup refresh`, including reports in\n#24391 and #21208. The setup refresh path already runs the Windows\nsandbox setup helper, but it was not using the same structured\n`setup_error.json` reporting path that elevated setup uses. As a result,\nwhen the helper exited non-zero, Codex only surfaced a generic refresh\nstatus instead of the helper's `SetupFailure` code and message.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Clear stale `setup_error.json` before non-elevated setup refresh\nlaunches the helper.\n- When the refresh helper exits non-zero, read the helper-written report\nthrough the existing `report_helper_failure` path.\n- Keep a parent-side launch diagnostic for cases where the helper never\nstarts, including the helper path, cwd, sandbox log path, and spawn\nerror.\n- Clear the setup error report after a successful refresh.\n- Add regression coverage for report consumption and stale-report\navoidance.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-windows-sandbox setup::tests::`","tree":{"sha":"88401202a8795fd8ff86efe6ec9cf88e515b243e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/88401202a8795fd8ff86efe6ec9cf88e515b243e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0b2e7b5eb1cfa74e5807a84b291e6c900eeb197d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIg+qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlgcQAAIOjuS9Fjz5QUlMxZTkoohH\npYiGcC2w3IgD5LeU3KLFOt2tFA3bFEyZfEjBP+6aMBtvLR3YfEps8im0blK2KGXA\nMvFGNdD9fqHVP8YVcG4zvkXophM3f6d6egMFsYo/dYjD59JgO3ZN/40C7zOLIOm5\nK/cdwN/VOBPmy6F+Ffo+0z/cyUgQI9p+03hQt08hBV3/nC09S/cRtjOVMSt1jGqX\nFlLhsTbIieZW9ySutgEwm12MVnd9wBNQgytp2Ua0GE3O49xbS+90XARVKbyZA6Nt\ny8cZNT9a7S6avbcxzCbdjn7LCmblKwGQxzv/hQZ6VZdCdZkyySREH9KQppSrp6lG\nnQwXJ1RbuKmcuA1t8OyCO3H8VRfND9u6EzOi05HMzh5+0BE09diQX6J1WCJcUEFt\n9dzLuPQfQdBizgGSxliE5sl1VKuyBopfWlJG209Ss2EkRox4Mvy4g10FfkR0ALY2\nM5nPMvQXRgqJuBNgtLJ6VXpsRs9p7554Zp24bd7QTns2NaVbs8ZqC9lSziM33f/S\nGUyAuw25KRxILe06GRqf+HfyxHvCG9IdtSIVc55EWUO4m8mQZwptXEhKzcqgS9nT\n2jxP2Z5GN7QNEVtyDpu7zsra2zlAI47V8Jpp2riPqxKVwk1vGy4c6bh3SxyW0Qaj\ngoeA8H9hvvhE+FWhzOF0\n=RSaE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 88401202a8795fd8ff86efe6ec9cf88e515b243e\nparent b9ff4509029b40a0c10964aa751a1a006ab46359\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1780617130 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780617130 -0700\n\nImprove Windows sandbox setup refresh diagnostics (#26471)\n\n## Why\n\nUsers have been seeing opaque Windows sandbox setup refresh failures\nsuch as `windows sandbox: spawn setup refresh`, including reports in\n#24391 and #21208. The setup refresh path already runs the Windows\nsandbox setup helper, but it was not using the same structured\n`setup_error.json` reporting path that elevated setup uses. As a result,\nwhen the helper exited non-zero, Codex only surfaced a generic refresh\nstatus instead of the helper's `SetupFailure` code and message.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Clear stale `setup_error.json` before non-elevated setup refresh\nlaunches the helper.\n- When the refresh helper exits non-zero, read the helper-written report\nthrough the existing `report_helper_failure` path.\n- Keep a parent-side launch diagnostic for cases where the helper never\nstarts, including the helper path, cwd, sandbox log path, and spawn\nerror.\n- Clear the setup error report after a successful refresh.\n- Add regression coverage for report consumption and stale-report\navoidance.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-windows-sandbox setup::tests::`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T23:52:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b2e7b5eb1cfa74e5807a84b291e6c900eeb197d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0b2e7b5eb1cfa74e5807a84b291e6c900eeb197d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b2e7b5eb1cfa74e5807a84b291e6c900eeb197d/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b9ff4509029b40a0c10964aa751a1a006ab46359","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b9ff4509029b40a0c10964aa751a1a006ab46359","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b9ff4509029b40a0c10964aa751a1a006ab46359"}]},{"sha":"b9ff4509029b40a0c10964aa751a1a006ab46359","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI5ZmY0NTA5MDI5YjQwYTBjMTA5NjRhYTc1MWExYTAwNmFiNDYzNTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"charlesgong-openai","email":"charlesgong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T23:42:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T23:42:27Z"},"message":"[codex] Expose unavailable app templates in plugin detail (#26317)\n\n## Summary\n- Adds `unavailable_app_templates` to the app-server protocol and\ngenerated schemas/types.\n- Parses plugin-service `release.unavailable_app_templates` in the\nremote plugin client.\n- Maps remote unavailable templates into app-server `PluginDetail`.\n- Defaults local plugins to an empty unavailable app template list.\n\n## Validation\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `cargo +1.95.0 fmt --manifest-path codex-rs/Cargo.toml --all --check`\n- `cargo +1.95.0 test --manifest-path codex-rs/Cargo.toml -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol schema_fixtures`\n- `cargo +1.95.0 check --manifest-path codex-rs/Cargo.toml -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol -p codex-core-plugins -p codex-app-server`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nNote: default `cargo check` uses rustc 1.89 locally and failed because\ndependencies require newer Rust, so validation was rerun with installed\nRust 1.95.","tree":{"sha":"aa0e478ccf57f9fc65a19d7396033e4c6e34600a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/aa0e478ccf57f9fc65a19d7396033e4c6e34600a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b9ff4509029b40a0c10964aa751a1a006ab46359","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIg1jCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeHgQAGVyXNezkiuwcl4XXZv5Uil/\nIZNLol0mxdLwyNU3ODVdxFucLdrhIDLc81ubrQdjHCeQGRw2xBi+YbaK2mdE7+T5\nh3j58LtdEBQVwFuwan84JiwG4uAKwb43k2l5XLQc2rQYS5XtLma6cCJMHwwNL0zS\nI1Lo8j/qD2DvlevHbybAmrRAV95zK9w0RujN0iaIyv+VfX2wrAe41cex5rE8da8d\nHELCV4qAlUrBHYkQz+yXvn/m1TLXAjJUeZlBaQ8qXhUtoImCiEpXey6fIOyIjoun\nitfeUvZLqiPse7/liEkxvdrk9ncZu9r3MyMa9umrAFQOskdmkj2k0kFvNT/GSqRK\n9TJGfNOiFy+psgx148fphUVwK0xSRa/1Y8zvDxCYf5u4Lz94QbrnibqdVPw+dVig\noEEa2859fbq2d0xR2esmR7bp5brbMCzrTQ0f4BpTTiv0ywQPo7ZqCLXJzRLBdHzS\nq1D5Mx//kbCyRXlpdHI51jErZ8iOZna8CAI4bEX04rCbJFnpvOh3plbK9uzQVG/9\noFLQ7kBss9XJYtftxRB1hBUrZWeWaUtJ6XPq1jYqo5Jdk9deowEeFkVuZCtrFhP7\neoo3QBt8HdZqEWSvX7LC81oMxmHFE+Dnf52jfIzc2VGi6rEC6139VYtMflrBRX/P\nAim72PXdVeM7BhDxhqxV\n=vpaV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree aa0e478ccf57f9fc65a19d7396033e4c6e34600a\nparent e695ec8ec612f61f6150299cc5c0ec39138dc902\nauthor charlesgong-openai <charlesgong@openai.com> 1780616547 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780616547 +0000\n\n[codex] Expose unavailable app templates in plugin detail (#26317)\n\n## Summary\n- Adds `unavailable_app_templates` to the app-server protocol and\ngenerated schemas/types.\n- Parses plugin-service `release.unavailable_app_templates` in the\nremote plugin client.\n- Maps remote unavailable templates into app-server `PluginDetail`.\n- Defaults local plugins to an empty unavailable app template list.\n\n## Validation\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `cargo +1.95.0 fmt --manifest-path codex-rs/Cargo.toml --all --check`\n- `cargo +1.95.0 test --manifest-path codex-rs/Cargo.toml -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol schema_fixtures`\n- `cargo +1.95.0 check --manifest-path codex-rs/Cargo.toml -p\ncodex-app-server-protocol -p codex-core-plugins -p codex-app-server`\n- `git diff --check`\n\nNote: default `cargo check` uses rustc 1.89 locally and failed because\ndependencies require newer Rust, so validation was rerun with installed\nRust 1.95.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T23:42:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b9ff4509029b40a0c10964aa751a1a006ab46359","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b9ff4509029b40a0c10964aa751a1a006ab46359","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b9ff4509029b40a0c10964aa751a1a006ab46359/comments","author":{"login":"charlesgong-openai","id":200841148,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesgong-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e695ec8ec612f61f6150299cc5c0ec39138dc902","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e695ec8ec612f61f6150299cc5c0ec39138dc902","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e695ec8ec612f61f6150299cc5c0ec39138dc902"}]},{"sha":"e695ec8ec612f61f6150299cc5c0ec39138dc902","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU2OTVlYzhlYzYxMmY2MWY2MTUwMjk5Y2M1YzBlYzM5MTM4ZGM5MDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T22:40:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T22:40:16Z"},"message":"Add skill for pushing CI configuration changes (#26473)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex agents that modify GitHub Actions configuration need clear\nguidance when repository push protections require temporary approval.\nWithout it, an agent may pursue an unavailable exemption or stop before\nchecking whether the user already has access.\n\n## What\n\nAdd a `pushing-ci-changes` skill that explains the restriction, directs\nagents to attempt the push first, and tells them how to involve the user\nwhen approval is required.\n\n## Validation\n\nNot run; this change only adds skill documentation.","tree":{"sha":"2ddc16059dfaf63f6c7e2855e7e25d538ffe8618","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2ddc16059dfaf63f6c7e2855e7e25d538ffe8618"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e695ec8ec612f61f6150299cc5c0ec39138dc902","comment_count":3,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIf7QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAn20QABMTV3Isp7SGxQzZKdiZCpyN\nvtw84rrNxuhRNXCh7E8INwk2hbTGVKFRqw1cBiEpjeoaOeopTkwa4cGUBICJjhU7\na2V6Q80vRNpd7fJ62Cj/uNlt30Y63yO3vzW/bLUFQf3yq2jC8dnJvgW/p17nzZqI\n1AwdCMjS3iBopaGArNbKTPfg/SyBdKBLrwC+VBV7hPDI74y8Slqil/kurCt6ZElA\n+YahxK6aKoexDFBoiGY8tCjBzTnAMFYq6Aky0H7vi7nUh8k4G0V9eL10dJ3p3QPr\n+KBxCA+ZYSIwWsBtHsE6e6qlBDLMdyRaYSDwFC3DCJJhInNz9PwrNkHL3tbl0r8m\n60tL+Fj7Tp0Pj60UuPJE9zIP/YKnrTvckUyv2tyAg7p1zDqlucsnF7Ar/64UZvqX\naSurk0ZVPcM1t2wm2GUMBgcWcmiUM35QhE44TK0k8HerEC3DE89zetUPmm+KjtY4\nzEfL33/jcxaP5bndtChbxwmXC3BLzBzbPFoueJpaPgNwoNy39cwiBbwLRD9hhuup\ntkpa1Ctkzcfu4DWWk5ylhk4aWqj3YeQ2gkJHnTcDWt2shFtDv8lKbnaSUWWnxclV\n18AG0xx7bDOFUMrnPx9nKqvR4F/RN2AvBWsQPvjP7ptsLtYWZESYySlIzlc3kSnA\nIbLrucaZNyzqV0ZX8AHy\n=5x6G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2ddc16059dfaf63f6c7e2855e7e25d538ffe8618\nparent 769c231aa1d69e2482fda2a51444d7f7a2158e3a\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780612816 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780612816 -0700\n\nAdd skill for pushing CI configuration changes (#26473)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex agents that modify GitHub Actions configuration need clear\nguidance when repository push protections require temporary approval.\nWithout it, an agent may pursue an unavailable exemption or stop before\nchecking whether the user already has access.\n\n## What\n\nAdd a `pushing-ci-changes` skill that explains the restriction, directs\nagents to attempt the push first, and tells them how to involve the user\nwhen approval is required.\n\n## Validation\n\nNot run; this change only adds skill documentation.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T22:40:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e695ec8ec612f61f6150299cc5c0ec39138dc902","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e695ec8ec612f61f6150299cc5c0ec39138dc902","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e695ec8ec612f61f6150299cc5c0ec39138dc902/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"769c231aa1d69e2482fda2a51444d7f7a2158e3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/769c231aa1d69e2482fda2a51444d7f7a2158e3a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/769c231aa1d69e2482fda2a51444d7f7a2158e3a"}]},{"sha":"769c231aa1d69e2482fda2a51444d7f7a2158e3a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc2OWMyMzFhYTFkNjllMjQ4MmZkYTJhNTE0NDRkN2Y3YTIxNThlM2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Ning","email":"ericning@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T22:10:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T22:10:24Z"},"message":"fix(app-server): expose remote MCP servers in plugin read (#26453)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote plugin detail responses include MCP server metadata under\n`release.mcp_servers`, but Codex did not deserialize or propagate that\nfield. As a result, `plugin/read` always returned an empty `mcpServers`\nlist for remote plugins, so the plugin details pane omitted the MCP\nServers section even when the remote plugin declares one.\n\nThis affects uninstalled plugins as well: the remote detail API is the\nsource of truth and returns MCP server keys without requiring a local\nplugin bundle.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Deserialize MCP server entries from remote plugin detail responses.\n- Normalize their keys into a sorted, deduplicated list on\n`RemotePluginDetail`.\n- Return those keys from app-server `plugin/read` instead of hardcoding\nan empty list.\n- Add regression coverage proving an uninstalled remote plugin returns\nits MCP server names.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server plugin_read`","tree":{"sha":"cf07860ed40c49b5d38a8e9ba41153d9777d8425","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/cf07860ed40c49b5d38a8e9ba41153d9777d8425"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/769c231aa1d69e2482fda2a51444d7f7a2158e3a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIffQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbPgQAHeyNY/MeS5UG8Q+cvqcmahw\nh+uH5VVWp2zH3Fnm1OTWOInDrI8IUK1peUmVf3hxgFo/FFNy5s3Kl3wwHcxK91sh\n1gZ+QGHucHdUFWYmeAvyRMIhfGzSniBsv65ydQETp1DZvD9HhI3f9mCBLGSbDHJx\nJZXKEHdZoi786kiE80QvGKCO25y5STNJkIoEL/xBLurIe3JnWDHCQpOll4tpguwi\nUSM32xKzxEUkuYIolJvb3cm30UfoSvE1Myshgl8ZRryln9FaQcEp/SlHa5dTXkIv\nO3rzaHyDKJI2ZdBouMffGzc7hPk377A2riW0N0riJwRNZyRnCSIzhC+8Oul9mC8n\ny8P0NuHRmSn3PwrsBIDkaxbswnQeUcJhyYg+we633Pj2UD/MroYniRX+sIbQXgLd\nPnAT3A90TQFzA4tZ3fO6MosNjO2kEqUPA/dTWIYabAPniWiNTEtWWCb+F5VG+Fmd\n/jqCJoDCFHxJA7XZ9ggZDEUeBgFhbPtVqo6ybvfOprCtdYXAoC9zEahEgN6S2Ji5\nU0Mi1x/SeEROVrUTXu8hsoQ7feHuFQdPSVdIGDjD0l+tFTKvMJm82bgZnjuu9/P4\nzo/BFBP2jTXPq6tj+JPPYwID5RhxXmvLa/NdhfXxhjfGCHQ11vCpaP/ib23SSFZq\nz+WifAN3q1GWUoW26thM\n=kWFh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cf07860ed40c49b5d38a8e9ba41153d9777d8425\nparent 59ca34206b4606a8800a4e565d6006f02fa37206\nauthor Eric Ning <ericning@openai.com> 1780611024 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780611024 +0000\n\nfix(app-server): expose remote MCP servers in plugin read (#26453)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote plugin detail responses include MCP server metadata under\n`release.mcp_servers`, but Codex did not deserialize or propagate that\nfield. As a result, `plugin/read` always returned an empty `mcpServers`\nlist for remote plugins, so the plugin details pane omitted the MCP\nServers section even when the remote plugin declares one.\n\nThis affects uninstalled plugins as well: the remote detail API is the\nsource of truth and returns MCP server keys without requiring a local\nplugin bundle.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Deserialize MCP server entries from remote plugin detail responses.\n- Normalize their keys into a sorted, deduplicated list on\n`RemotePluginDetail`.\n- Return those keys from app-server `plugin/read` instead of hardcoding\nan empty list.\n- Add regression coverage proving an uninstalled remote plugin returns\nits MCP server names.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server plugin_read`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T22:10:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/769c231aa1d69e2482fda2a51444d7f7a2158e3a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/769c231aa1d69e2482fda2a51444d7f7a2158e3a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/769c231aa1d69e2482fda2a51444d7f7a2158e3a/comments","author":{"login":"ericning-o","id":182030612,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtmRFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182030612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o","html_url":"https://github.com/ericning-o","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"59ca34206b4606a8800a4e565d6006f02fa37206","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/59ca34206b4606a8800a4e565d6006f02fa37206","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/59ca34206b4606a8800a4e565d6006f02fa37206"}]},{"sha":"59ca34206b4606a8800a4e565d6006f02fa37206","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU5Y2EzNDIwNmI0NjA2YTg4MDBhNGU1NjVkNjAwNmYwMmZhMzcyMDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T22:08:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T22:08:52Z"},"message":"[codex] Preserve logical paths during AGENTS.md discovery (#26465)\n\n## Intent\n\nFollow up on #26205 by avoiding unnecessary filesystem canonicalization\nduring `AGENTS.md` discovery. The configured working directory is\nalready absolute, and canonicalization incorrectly switches symlinked\nworkspaces from their logical parent hierarchy to the target's\nhierarchy.\n\n## User-facing behavior\n\nFor a symlinked working directory such as:\n\n```text\ntest-root/\n|-- logical-repo/\n|   |-- AGENTS.md              (\"logical parent doc\")\n|   `-- workspace ------------> physical-repo/workspace/\n`-- physical-repo/\n    |-- AGENTS.md              (\"physical parent doc\")\n    `-- workspace/\n        `-- AGENTS.md          (\"workspace doc\")\n```\n\nBefore this change, Codex canonicalized `logical-repo/workspace` to\n`physical-repo/workspace` before discovery. It therefore loaded\n`physical-repo/AGENTS.md` and `physical-repo/workspace/AGENTS.md`,\nignoring the instructions from the repository through which the user\nentered the workspace.\n\nAfter this change, ancestor discovery walks the configured logical path,\nso Codex loads `logical-repo/AGENTS.md`. Opening\n`logical-repo/workspace/AGENTS.md` still follows the symlink through the\nhost filesystem, so the workspace document is also loaded.\n`physical-repo/AGENTS.md` is not loaded.\n\n## Implementation\n\nUse the logical absolute working directory when discovering project\ninstructions and reporting instruction sources. Filesystem reads still\nfollow the working-directory symlink, so an `AGENTS.md` in the target\nworkspace continues to load while ancestor discovery uses the symlink's\nparents.\n\n## Validation\n\nAdded integration coverage proving that discovery loads the logical\nparent's instructions and the target workspace's instructions, but not\nthe target parent's instructions.","tree":{"sha":"de054a59cb8237e9a46b1d7cdd151a8a8c13e5dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/de054a59cb8237e9a46b1d7cdd151a8a8c13e5dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/59ca34206b4606a8800a4e565d6006f02fa37206","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIfd0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc+MQAE/EbigTNimi5bvg26D8Defy\nDi5PgBeaOyKHkFw6nI42jvRN32r+1s5w7rmcV0HiFTC3zHAtNlPXY92lrU7OBi5+\naqHb76eUamLw5qcV4seM9ZSJrsxd5EgddweEJuIBVd43czKOg8WMwt1dCQ7Hb1uu\n9bHSWLJjsmQogncU7xqiyQKs3WLRSVJv9hT/s1U7oHZzLy/7OO1JE9IfdrgDqeYc\nvvluAMx60W/H6Xdxx+3Hk2tWo766xNEHwrfbXSAt5Ktyo2g0c76TXMPP4wBisgsi\nimWc4zHEbuVUuYjET1vKW2e3+zi6YKPIfGfzJIljq+vg/eID4jHiZTzqXRtNtUih\nfB/tltftUWlugU0LwI6B/dEuLMJYpsJ0DNuCr5XSVZDxDR/nhroJMmRXh8XQHB67\nFzsgTAgLdSv5xKWAh6ESCFEUMrU0k45ZCGKHC9XP14+LX3PH+7pVKmQwqvUtrvPv\n9BZKzJY1bN0wrA++vtTVfV+l0CDuF/5VGEKhWg7XyVFRfrq9ZV1NwfCI7xMpuGB6\nm49kksZh3Y/g8NGS/AmA3nz0ev9EbZ39C0XXQSNSDi59b0puILGkJny04Q6J9/o5\nVCPiWnnjy1TIHR86Tiya/NrejwMBVbHsePA3ey2n0lB8nArgO4bOf9HHrBDi8sZ/\nttZHBw3H5y/iAaLdLT1Q\n=jRLw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree de054a59cb8237e9a46b1d7cdd151a8a8c13e5dd\nparent 37c8aefa14e1a8bb817ee63ddc4561da04741082\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780610932 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780610932 -0700\n\n[codex] Preserve logical paths during AGENTS.md discovery (#26465)\n\n## Intent\n\nFollow up on #26205 by avoiding unnecessary filesystem canonicalization\nduring `AGENTS.md` discovery. The configured working directory is\nalready absolute, and canonicalization incorrectly switches symlinked\nworkspaces from their logical parent hierarchy to the target's\nhierarchy.\n\n## User-facing behavior\n\nFor a symlinked working directory such as:\n\n```text\ntest-root/\n|-- logical-repo/\n|   |-- AGENTS.md              (\"logical parent doc\")\n|   `-- workspace ------------> physical-repo/workspace/\n`-- physical-repo/\n    |-- AGENTS.md              (\"physical parent doc\")\n    `-- workspace/\n        `-- AGENTS.md          (\"workspace doc\")\n```\n\nBefore this change, Codex canonicalized `logical-repo/workspace` to\n`physical-repo/workspace` before discovery. It therefore loaded\n`physical-repo/AGENTS.md` and `physical-repo/workspace/AGENTS.md`,\nignoring the instructions from the repository through which the user\nentered the workspace.\n\nAfter this change, ancestor discovery walks the configured logical path,\nso Codex loads `logical-repo/AGENTS.md`. Opening\n`logical-repo/workspace/AGENTS.md` still follows the symlink through the\nhost filesystem, so the workspace document is also loaded.\n`physical-repo/AGENTS.md` is not loaded.\n\n## Implementation\n\nUse the logical absolute working directory when discovering project\ninstructions and reporting instruction sources. Filesystem reads still\nfollow the working-directory symlink, so an `AGENTS.md` in the target\nworkspace continues to load while ancestor discovery uses the symlink's\nparents.\n\n## Validation\n\nAdded integration coverage proving that discovery loads the logical\nparent's instructions and the target workspace's instructions, but not\nthe target parent's instructions.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T22:08:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/59ca34206b4606a8800a4e565d6006f02fa37206","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/59ca34206b4606a8800a4e565d6006f02fa37206","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/59ca34206b4606a8800a4e565d6006f02fa37206/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"37c8aefa14e1a8bb817ee63ddc4561da04741082","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/37c8aefa14e1a8bb817ee63ddc4561da04741082","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/37c8aefa14e1a8bb817ee63ddc4561da04741082"}]},{"sha":"37c8aefa14e1a8bb817ee63ddc4561da04741082","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM3YzhhZWZhMTRlMWE4YmI4MTdlZTYzZGRjNDU2MWRhMDQ3NDEwODI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T21:38:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T21:38:11Z"},"message":"Use Winget release environment secret (#26466)\n\n## Why\n`WINGET_PUBLISH_PAT` now lives as a GitHub environment secret under\n`mainline-release-winget`. The WinGet release job needs to enter that\nenvironment so `secrets.WINGET_PUBLISH_PAT` resolves during\nstable/mainline Rust releases.\n\n## What Changed\n- Attach the `winget` job in `.github/workflows/rust-release.yml` to the\n`mainline-release-winget` environment.\n- Set `deployment: false` so the job can read environment secrets\nwithout creating GitHub deployment records.\n\n## Operational Note\nThe `mainline-release-winget` environment must allow `rust-v*.*.*` tag\nrefs before this can run on release tags. The live environment currently\nhas a custom policy named `rust-v*.*.*` with type `branch`; add the\ncorresponding `tag` policy before relying on this path for a release.\n\n## Validation\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD --\n.github/workflows/rust-release.yml`\n- `ruby -e 'require \"yaml\"; ARGV.each { |f| YAML.load_file(f); puts\n\"yaml ok: #{f}\" }' .github/workflows/rust-release.yml`","tree":{"sha":"9644ac0fc755ebcb3ae7ff19182741c423841869","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9644ac0fc755ebcb3ae7ff19182741c423841869"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/37c8aefa14e1a8bb817ee63ddc4561da04741082","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIfBDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp2IQABqGuFz0B2UITmPhVPDna2v8\nn99uv2n0RLN4Tc17wYkBWgE3ho2SND0sBGk4QNtelxVNrV7t6w4JEeDMHp8I0Uju\njbb0k90sgF9ZDsOf1/R1hHMBsepaTtsZVT0QEQfqhBcNdwXIv4HcWAI/9R4UPK1g\nQ4pIjaPmH60XdaY7sftW4BgxbRrxHYns9Gr519JxoxPWzvd4HjVU3NnGJLVfQ7rn\nyERiBxIDyiNsFVmWgiZWcSx8LeGI/MO1+ckLWrOMs2fq7C3yIYBqZ1hMBfk4XI+o\nYxI8uuTVrhdzjaRozgtJYjKS3QthlDVtRldS4FnKzCqPcsMf1kgLBfErAhp3Q8ey\nK/FVZoxOqs7WjHPup44XevEqIR85YB9xsYyaGe9LXQPpTBLMaev1oR+XB559tdLd\njLHBbWt8C5m+dzvGcLAc1hTt7F6pr87amB8q4MfK3actTbgm66PpIv/kceeADwD3\n63bdZ01eLFO/jVQpl342ihNZy44Bz43wWb8WE7dtIvT7/R2/Nn7yrPeVxInjPC3k\n065DLB7YIwwm/R9h7dtzovjoOaa5HoKhCRblfaeEKpvW+/VcOKqZJekLooFu/L6c\nj+sxic9lgFcwjVBGtTjNdyy4ujjdLFbLVhBeWeETg358zTOIppXi2U043o3Ll3RM\nCQXxZoS9Z7vfNSFd5FAe\n=ITaC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9644ac0fc755ebcb3ae7ff19182741c423841869\nparent f6e529656f7ce4af6d146f4b0c8500a6d89221c2\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1780609091 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780609091 -0700\n\nUse Winget release environment secret (#26466)\n\n## Why\n`WINGET_PUBLISH_PAT` now lives as a GitHub environment secret under\n`mainline-release-winget`. The WinGet release job needs to enter that\nenvironment so `secrets.WINGET_PUBLISH_PAT` resolves during\nstable/mainline Rust releases.\n\n## What Changed\n- Attach the `winget` job in `.github/workflows/rust-release.yml` to the\n`mainline-release-winget` environment.\n- Set `deployment: false` so the job can read environment secrets\nwithout creating GitHub deployment records.\n\n## Operational Note\nThe `mainline-release-winget` environment must allow `rust-v*.*.*` tag\nrefs before this can run on release tags. The live environment currently\nhas a custom policy named `rust-v*.*.*` with type `branch`; add the\ncorresponding `tag` policy before relying on this path for a release.\n\n## Validation\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD --\n.github/workflows/rust-release.yml`\n- `ruby -e 'require \"yaml\"; ARGV.each { |f| YAML.load_file(f); puts\n\"yaml ok: #{f}\" }' .github/workflows/rust-release.yml`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T21:38:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/37c8aefa14e1a8bb817ee63ddc4561da04741082","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/37c8aefa14e1a8bb817ee63ddc4561da04741082","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/37c8aefa14e1a8bb817ee63ddc4561da04741082/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f6e529656f7ce4af6d146f4b0c8500a6d89221c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6e529656f7ce4af6d146f4b0c8500a6d89221c2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f6e529656f7ce4af6d146f4b0c8500a6d89221c2"}]},{"sha":"f6e529656f7ce4af6d146f4b0c8500a6d89221c2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY2ZTUyOTY1NmY3Y2U0YWY2ZDE0NmY0YjBjODUwMGE2ZDg5MjIxYzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T21:01:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T21:01:14Z"},"message":"[codex] Use model-advertised reasoning effort order (#26446)\n\n## Summary\n- preserve the model catalog order for app-server\n`supportedReasoningEfforts` and document that client contract\n- render TUI reasoning choices in the advertised order\n- step reasoning shortcuts by adjacent list position instead of deriving\norder from known effort names\n- anchor unsupported configured values to the advertised default, or the\nfirst option when needed\n- remove canonical effort ordering helpers and the unused upgrade effort\nmapping\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- Local tests and compilation were not run per request; relying on CI.\n\nStacked on #26444.","tree":{"sha":"c837f5dd3e150285bd010bae970b4d60bb5633fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c837f5dd3e150285bd010bae970b4d60bb5633fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f6e529656f7ce4af6d146f4b0c8500a6d89221c2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIeeaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANssQABiqurttDfTtVGzEpNbMPvgD\nXYCMEy0SLPafkYCFALkXlh/TW+tH/yjZBh/4gG0to2PhQ4CbljRpcVUGlG31E1li\n4IBuBMvaY74KzmctUNquB0w5WoqCUfGWLy1uoVJi2DEf4Ft8gtnCdQtZmpKQsPbY\nZI5jD6S87Nh19KYDoFZ3nOfN3DwV/5ekewj2KAFl3FRx74kiU+cPsZqUolzjXl69\nVZ+AIVL3Kje+QMUod+Z2LCUbp2Bq7BpjfMgTFg16Uzry+R+expYRxVP55zzNS4Fu\nc/tPatKSpFTL16eUq6g9V2lrhypw5ALR8rvuNgdrzkMoukuz5x4Y8/xZIzLxOUw9\nUu5Qn9UlWLmlh135DFM0FEIGaI4agHi/xfS6aXJrtUs2d1+X8Dys7Nva65Vkjp7u\n9EZJxGV7P09bcWLgCGm5hpVATx5tNSJhf37KDZHTUcznBfddRBWq/yzqNjqHtvE4\n/ZK1Y5qEK1NbyT06aoEnzyVy9DPSLG2rTxAsXdWItLlcIT4ptZX2ZqP7iX933rV8\nMOAYiMk6x7KdCsGKRQGvd+6MbOLkcxt79vxiTySqorBcWak2OTkiuP/6AVYdwNuS\nusDDy+LqXg52n6Vc0ct6+zfAvpzarFkXC2b0IXSv92onPWK92nvD1znqQGXhVq7K\nsJA6VzHfkQIy2ZLKuMVB\n=vq0q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c837f5dd3e150285bd010bae970b4d60bb5633fd\nparent 8ac304c2997529d3b6fe4be4ba032e0f2dac16af\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1780606874 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780606874 -0700\n\n[codex] Use model-advertised reasoning effort order (#26446)\n\n## Summary\n- preserve the model catalog order for app-server\n`supportedReasoningEfforts` and document that client contract\n- render TUI reasoning choices in the advertised order\n- step reasoning shortcuts by adjacent list position instead of deriving\norder from known effort names\n- anchor unsupported configured values to the advertised default, or the\nfirst option when needed\n- remove canonical effort ordering helpers and the unused upgrade effort\nmapping\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- Local tests and compilation were not run per request; relying on CI.\n\nStacked on #26444.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T21:01:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6e529656f7ce4af6d146f4b0c8500a6d89221c2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f6e529656f7ce4af6d146f4b0c8500a6d89221c2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6e529656f7ce4af6d146f4b0c8500a6d89221c2/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8ac304c2997529d3b6fe4be4ba032e0f2dac16af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ac304c2997529d3b6fe4be4ba032e0f2dac16af","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8ac304c2997529d3b6fe4be4ba032e0f2dac16af"}]},{"sha":"8ac304c2997529d3b6fe4be4ba032e0f2dac16af","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhhYzMwNGMyOTk3NTI5ZDNiNmZlNGJlNGJhMDMyZTBmMmRhYzE2YWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T20:36:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T20:36:24Z"},"message":"[codex] Support model-defined reasoning efforts (#26444)\n\n## Summary\n- accept non-empty model-defined reasoning effort values while\npreserving built-in effort behavior\n- propagate the non-Copy effort type through core, app-server, TUI,\ntelemetry, and persistence call sites\n- preserve string wire encoding and expose an open-string schema for\nclients\n- update model selection and shortcut behavior for model-advertised\neffort values\n\n## Root cause\n`ReasoningEffort` gained a string-backed custom variant, so it could no\nlonger implement `Copy` or rely on derived closed-enum serialization.\nExisting consumers still moved effort values from shared references and\nassumed a fixed built-in value set.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- Local tests and compilation were not run per request; relying on CI.","tree":{"sha":"4ba672273cc2e63806accf34e2fa66ce6c1f9a8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4ba672273cc2e63806accf34e2fa66ce6c1f9a8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8ac304c2997529d3b6fe4be4ba032e0f2dac16af","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIeHICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcNkQAELpIQRgiJ3P6oUmoSv9etem\nrEwsMwJH58Xt3XrU0lJe4vXut6kJWj8MqiS+pEIyG20WMR7+tFvXNzFbtTJedRGh\n8AJC56UKaEJ4b4y5zziLIla35zVVB7QxiQXlHHnWaLs4MB/th5W7Odv1E6gRVJ+p\nwQy+qksZKuZqPCSiTedSXByAWyd6yBMsBZqx+hKRVUczuPyecmjhwL3qAp3rimej\nDJKm6tU4vFL8zYXet2Paxvzew/bDsEa9WiM0WI6Mj9/hI/+vTPtPRSHvrYFS4bFN\nodEx8h5vFfA7SjNSf0EbkhcdWt9tmYM6e3VXwtP+0wI64q0/GVsLUtv8zD773jJr\nbb8eMk1PWb+2T8nNDJOxULTK4qHHpwuqpriQKKaACdmna5KobTmw9su0zq1jh2OA\nOBEXora3R4p2Z7ihVMKulip9tZXjo6ANe1hQh1LuzcFnAdU04t+fpRebCleQ4kyz\nLmcHpOqO5rG8/QCg4B2Pus6aDwhE5ZFI8v+Mf248PbS1wLQoe4qo3m9/h6EcZ33F\nnUM3yr2J+0z10DTbaYH1l4ZmTwIg1fSKHYBh+DJQcWI+gRanxGesFGxxhc4vLLbT\nfjxRg8wEVJYWWkGdRhhwkyQFpH4tp3GaDakpQsIHETY/CSbcAByaD8yLAAyuxXkE\n7XlK5SjX8uMwDuSP/2uf\n=cVY1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4ba672273cc2e63806accf34e2fa66ce6c1f9a8d\nparent 4a70e0ac1b39c6da6863069bebc82ce3513bc8b5\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1780605384 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780605384 -0700\n\n[codex] Support model-defined reasoning efforts (#26444)\n\n## Summary\n- accept non-empty model-defined reasoning effort values while\npreserving built-in effort behavior\n- propagate the non-Copy effort type through core, app-server, TUI,\ntelemetry, and persistence call sites\n- preserve string wire encoding and expose an open-string schema for\nclients\n- update model selection and shortcut behavior for model-advertised\neffort values\n\n## Root cause\n`ReasoningEffort` gained a string-backed custom variant, so it could no\nlonger implement `Copy` or rely on derived closed-enum serialization.\nExisting consumers still moved effort values from shared references and\nassumed a fixed built-in value set.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- Local tests and compilation were not run per request; relying on CI.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T20:36:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ac304c2997529d3b6fe4be4ba032e0f2dac16af","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8ac304c2997529d3b6fe4be4ba032e0f2dac16af","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8ac304c2997529d3b6fe4be4ba032e0f2dac16af/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4a70e0ac1b39c6da6863069bebc82ce3513bc8b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a70e0ac1b39c6da6863069bebc82ce3513bc8b5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4a70e0ac1b39c6da6863069bebc82ce3513bc8b5"}]},{"sha":"4a70e0ac1b39c6da6863069bebc82ce3513bc8b5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRhNzBlMGFjMWIzOWM2ZGE2ODYzMDY5YmViYzgyY2UzNTEzYmM4YjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Matthew Zeng","email":"mzeng@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T20:35:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T20:35:31Z"},"message":"Cleanup experimentalFeature/enablement/set (#26312)\n\n## Why\n\n`experimentalFeature/enablement/set` still allowed several keys that no\nlonger need to be managed through this API. Keeping those keys also\npreserved corresponding special-case logic, including refreshing the\napps list when the `apps` key was enabled.\n\nThe endpoint also rejected an entire request when any key was invalid or\nunsupported. That makes clients brittle when they send a mix of current\nand stale keys, even when the valid entries can still be applied safely.\n\n## What changed\n\n- remove the feature keys that no longer need to be supported by\n`experimentalFeature/enablement/set`\n- remove the corresponding apps-list refresh path and its auth/config\nplumbing\n- ignore and warn on invalid or unsupported keys while still applying\nvalid keys from the same request\n- update the app-server documentation and integration coverage for the\nreduced key set and partial-acceptance behavior\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server experimental_feature_enablement_set` (6\npassed)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server` exercised the changed tests\nsuccessfully; unrelated sandbox-dependent and watcher/timing tests\nfailed locally","tree":{"sha":"7d1b9a0886e5d6810b45be3ff6d942612bb8af35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7d1b9a0886e5d6810b45be3ff6d942612bb8af35"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4a70e0ac1b39c6da6863069bebc82ce3513bc8b5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIeGTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqYEQAIwdiBZ4QeATM00lt65RT1m8\nOZmSFzydjfJhLoUJKNMf1H9QiAb2ggU69cuy31yvjel9bhl7pqLmq48ApRertd0l\ngFpk1lIzlXlgprrh9QrZwIQanMSprqTcxN64DXA8m6KaTJCgKSSY84lGF7AgOsQz\njLpves1dpYxpVA3Ca/8jCvbOV87RJjnjH2xl0fZZsa+IdE4KghTSn3vsh/APcYI6\ne3jEuJgQZhpws690ifKUfRK7Q3Oesst6yA/+UuokvjEJSX4j6136eob+8JLGFglh\newM88aI8f1ng16ESHZ04XXFukGb2GhTeKeDq8Hxpz5sX29Hvl4giP97jkhzeYBWy\nsFANaH73nyNXL+Xn5wDBEtPEnvBhSBYpleis7Zx8J80sIubznDfzjgz4PvWXdi14\nxrkYjsZ5iRrESYK+Bu51OR30pXqM6sJZ6dOUjpkDiJwhqIVB9n1/w8eCuvu+tKlj\n4YlpB4xfWMhT/kW5Wn/M+aZBfZLQ5fWYoazhY3ahHnmCfguTBBZNAkqUMwcmBLii\nKNuRi3nI4ACk6pdmkLDCcPAUkfkfh/14JAKwDEq4Mwju00w2d/Ah6ICicUwLSF+R\n/MfeIc1BBv5OzHBtTXKo2pqu3OmRL/5Ox45aH0sS8OpYX5WXc9lao4NAju9O0nvP\n27OXkpOKA1G7RkE8hqcp\n=f5i/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7d1b9a0886e5d6810b45be3ff6d942612bb8af35\nparent d312a53e2a4419c339c890b79f02b56c19abac85\nauthor Matthew Zeng <mzeng@openai.com> 1780605331 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780605331 -0700\n\nCleanup experimentalFeature/enablement/set (#26312)\n\n## Why\n\n`experimentalFeature/enablement/set` still allowed several keys that no\nlonger need to be managed through this API. Keeping those keys also\npreserved corresponding special-case logic, including refreshing the\napps list when the `apps` key was enabled.\n\nThe endpoint also rejected an entire request when any key was invalid or\nunsupported. That makes clients brittle when they send a mix of current\nand stale keys, even when the valid entries can still be applied safely.\n\n## What changed\n\n- remove the feature keys that no longer need to be supported by\n`experimentalFeature/enablement/set`\n- remove the corresponding apps-list refresh path and its auth/config\nplumbing\n- ignore and warn on invalid or unsupported keys while still applying\nvalid keys from the same request\n- update the app-server documentation and integration coverage for the\nreduced key set and partial-acceptance behavior\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server experimental_feature_enablement_set` (6\npassed)\n- `just test -p codex-app-server` exercised the changed tests\nsuccessfully; unrelated sandbox-dependent and watcher/timing tests\nfailed locally","verified_at":"2026-06-04T20:35:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a70e0ac1b39c6da6863069bebc82ce3513bc8b5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4a70e0ac1b39c6da6863069bebc82ce3513bc8b5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a70e0ac1b39c6da6863069bebc82ce3513bc8b5/comments","author":{"login":"mzeng-openai","id":175741029,"node_id":"U_kgDOCnmYZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/175741029?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/mzeng-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mzeng-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d312a53e2a4419c339c890b79f02b56c19abac85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d312a53e2a4419c339c890b79f02b56c19abac85","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d312a53e2a4419c339c890b79f02b56c19abac85"}]},{"sha":"d312a53e2a4419c339c890b79f02b56c19abac85","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQzMTJhNTNlMmE0NDE5YzMzOWM4OTBiNzlmMDJiNTZjMTlhYmFjODU","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T20:15:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T20:15:50Z"},"message":"Remove response.processed websocket request (#26447)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Responses websocket client no longer needs to send a follow-up\n`response.processed` request after a turn response has already been\nrecorded. Keeping that extra acknowledgement path adds feature-gated\ncontrol flow and a second websocket request shape that no longer carries\nuseful behavior.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Removed the `response.processed` websocket request type and sender.\n- Removed the `responses_websocket_response_processed` feature flag and\nschema entry.\n- Removed turn and remote-compaction plumbing that only tracked response\nIDs to send the acknowledgement.\n- Removed tests that existed solely to cover the deleted feature path.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-api -p codex-features`","tree":{"sha":"119b1169b1eb3789c6f51a0ebcd90548b4ad178f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/119b1169b1eb3789c6f51a0ebcd90548b4ad178f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d312a53e2a4419c339c890b79f02b56c19abac85","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIdz2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkLYQADc1mISaK+EwvU8ipHeBFhCU\nckMyXfXNYidEbY4DZFVrIAgmXMjXK2vTj5Z//qM4XSbzTxBv1USvvBXfYO9tYRs8\nox+5LrtR7fRfuTYl9VMKD3LEw02zO2RYn893gd7UeXBp4rRQU6xyabbaBM5ev1gO\nepmRVHissN4296Z9yfrItXj15cYriQM5uRN0ua8k0SjdAbechQtBOBFc4A134fOA\nyuYPuVnVba3TOdwwSF7L+MG5Mkhl5iw0NVUX7lBZjHNtH7NO3tahxIHLjNEVnN3a\ng4I1sOtT+W5Ox3BILVF9ZnqwXAjol99rIkVKB+peVCRpw9WXWOKPPhB3+OyU/7r4\nnoVeADRcGnieWa5j9UFEe0IL2K1ZprEXwj+DsQRs5ghzDaLw272gVlqmhMV/naYP\nXpNlkiPzxSld9gGmq1+nhWWdfMNrAMZVPRIrSjPuEo6ZPpL+ztBvSvYUhEyZ3HJB\nLoscK+phOUMm0BjFtA2uS8WtLQpkTN0luDPUx+cUTI9GjpqxlhfD6TTr5svVZGWT\nFw6ofSQ1sJHl+1lFQRCDg40ZZ8sZXZVNmOQQNrtNXdkxDKNmwB7TiNeT6LkkxiMJ\nIBmr6b4iLiraXnOu69ks+MIQ76H1CW6sbi95HMrTtSRw5faCqyP5t0bG9yUPNXBv\nYL0rmRIfoIakHuvvi4eu\n=jp9o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 119b1169b1eb3789c6f51a0ebcd90548b4ad178f\nparent f97d5c327538a8fe8580fa4dd9ee22c213780a59\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780604150 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780604150 -0700\n\nRemove response.processed websocket request (#26447)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Responses websocket client no longer needs to send a follow-up\n`response.processed` request after a turn response has already been\nrecorded. Keeping that extra acknowledgement path adds feature-gated\ncontrol flow and a second websocket request shape that no longer carries\nuseful behavior.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Removed the `response.processed` websocket request type and sender.\n- Removed the `responses_websocket_response_processed` feature flag and\nschema entry.\n- Removed turn and remote-compaction plumbing that only tracked response\nIDs to send the acknowledgement.\n- Removed tests that existed solely to cover the deleted feature path.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-api -p codex-features`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T20:15:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d312a53e2a4419c339c890b79f02b56c19abac85","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d312a53e2a4419c339c890b79f02b56c19abac85","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d312a53e2a4419c339c890b79f02b56c19abac85/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f97d5c327538a8fe8580fa4dd9ee22c213780a59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f97d5c327538a8fe8580fa4dd9ee22c213780a59","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f97d5c327538a8fe8580fa4dd9ee22c213780a59"}]},{"sha":"f97d5c327538a8fe8580fa4dd9ee22c213780a59","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY5N2Q1YzMyNzUzOGE4ZmU4NTgwZmE0ZGQ5ZWUyMmMyMTM3ODBhNTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T20:07:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T20:07:53Z"},"message":"build: use ThinLTO for release binaries (#23710)\n\n## Why\n\nFat LTO makes release builds substantially slower without providing\nenough measured runtime benefit to justify the release CI long pole. The\nbuild-profile investigation found that keeping Cargo's default release\n`opt-level=3` and switching from fat LTO to ThinLTO (`3/thin/1`) reduced\na clean `codex-cli` release build from 2073.893 seconds to 1243.172\nseconds, a 40.06% improvement.\n\nThe resulting binary increased from 196.7 MiB to 211.8 MiB (+7.63%).\nMeasured runtime changes were small: the worst image workload median was\n+0.86% and app-server startup was +0.31% relative to fat LTO. ThinLTO\nretains cross-crate optimization while avoiding most of the fat-LTO\nbuild cost.\n\nThis deliberately avoids global size optimization: final-executable\ntesting showed a substantial regression on the image request path, which\nis expected to become more important as image usage grows.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Set the workspace release profile to `lto = \"thin\"`, retaining Cargo's\ndefault release `opt-level=3`.\n- Remove release and CI workflow-specific LTO overrides so\nrelease-profile builds consistently use the workspace setting.\n- Remove the now-unused Windows release workflow input and related\ndiagnostic output.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Confirmed the release profile parses with `cargo metadata --no-deps\n--format-version 1`.\n- CI validates release builds across the supported target matrix.","tree":{"sha":"9898329b91f85f09c48b1a6c3d68d1d0721e9d94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9898329b91f85f09c48b1a6c3d68d1d0721e9d94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f97d5c327538a8fe8580fa4dd9ee22c213780a59","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIdsZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWgMQAJUwwxIFYESZ2LEn/R0HFpOF\nArzXC1tntyaNu1OZTQCEcSap4mJQXgtBWWl5/8Fmfr0FZnKny1LZL6hAmxVacThF\neJ2c1hNYL7/ednifS3ilVkmCdHnqJcrtjIZgMa25eOarvR1qHZJbmKhrxhWwsvTz\nRHIC8F5uIMUyCiT5awSMgHmiOPdNU1U4ZkOCRl4WsJDWWM8Ekc6/gnYLJFc78xRN\nCck33Z/JFVYIfxWAY+6UJd2odfzDRusNEK0RYishRg3JBf+CSHc1TkYOY2X8Gz4W\nHCbjg8JFr41YzbA+htxj9tLHUAvcDIlJRgw+7C5Do0LGaL6wshxZm5lQE0KHIM+C\nlWF8/e56rWsMFbMFCA3b8MFTk4kglYW5Kn7o7pwcsArcc67DgTTrFzEo79zMwNuS\n5BLvGlKTbD82xRECmg/nh+7Vk6xeoum9Rs29B8t6nur1pd4j/qis36jz0iXQ88ZK\nyiRCVwcszJjL0LSo6M+6qsNcpOI0qyi98ooaJWop76SpgefjzHORYFZ5TFYrwmoF\nNZIVLewUvikgbYx3zgyqSTunjejc7LV7Lb3osQpsdDKcZ7JOFU75jM4slia5wrUV\nvx66C1Plkp8d4ao+vB4KKYSLXfSLbxqXFUtNcF1kl5OuLfiC/mArvVXnc24rXC/Z\ncZwwodz06TzpM8++gOQt\n=uHVm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9898329b91f85f09c48b1a6c3d68d1d0721e9d94\nparent 555f8caeff42073fcdc52755491d785adcc81e4a\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780603673 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780603673 +0000\n\nbuild: use ThinLTO for release binaries (#23710)\n\n## Why\n\nFat LTO makes release builds substantially slower without providing\nenough measured runtime benefit to justify the release CI long pole. The\nbuild-profile investigation found that keeping Cargo's default release\n`opt-level=3` and switching from fat LTO to ThinLTO (`3/thin/1`) reduced\na clean `codex-cli` release build from 2073.893 seconds to 1243.172\nseconds, a 40.06% improvement.\n\nThe resulting binary increased from 196.7 MiB to 211.8 MiB (+7.63%).\nMeasured runtime changes were small: the worst image workload median was\n+0.86% and app-server startup was +0.31% relative to fat LTO. ThinLTO\nretains cross-crate optimization while avoiding most of the fat-LTO\nbuild cost.\n\nThis deliberately avoids global size optimization: final-executable\ntesting showed a substantial regression on the image request path, which\nis expected to become more important as image usage grows.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Set the workspace release profile to `lto = \"thin\"`, retaining Cargo's\ndefault release `opt-level=3`.\n- Remove release and CI workflow-specific LTO overrides so\nrelease-profile builds consistently use the workspace setting.\n- Remove the now-unused Windows release workflow input and related\ndiagnostic output.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Confirmed the release profile parses with `cargo metadata --no-deps\n--format-version 1`.\n- CI validates release builds across the supported target matrix.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T20:07:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f97d5c327538a8fe8580fa4dd9ee22c213780a59","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f97d5c327538a8fe8580fa4dd9ee22c213780a59","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f97d5c327538a8fe8580fa4dd9ee22c213780a59/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"555f8caeff42073fcdc52755491d785adcc81e4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/555f8caeff42073fcdc52755491d785adcc81e4a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/555f8caeff42073fcdc52755491d785adcc81e4a"}]},{"sha":"555f8caeff42073fcdc52755491d785adcc81e4a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU1NWY4Y2FlZmY0MjA3M2ZjZGM1Mjc1NTQ5MWQ3ODVhZGNjODFlNGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T20:03:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T20:03:47Z"},"message":"[codex] Fix Windows sandbox build script lint (#26445)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Windows ARM64 Cargo clippy job on `main` is failing because\nworkspace lints deny `clippy::expect_used`, and the\n`codex-windows-sandbox` build script used `expect()` while reading\n`CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`.\n\n## What changed\n\n`codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/build.rs` now returns `Result<(), String>`\nfrom `main()` and converts a missing `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` into an\nexplicit build-script error. The non-Windows early return and Windows\nlinker argument behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just clippy -p codex-windows-sandbox -- -D warnings`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox`","tree":{"sha":"a6f4b0c002f0593fd5de1809de8421ece696b45b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a6f4b0c002f0593fd5de1809de8421ece696b45b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/555f8caeff42073fcdc52755491d785adcc81e4a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIdojCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmPEQAILlabVYYFatrdemx2IZzBAc\nITx8mXIj/Sssphs3NFcEWcdynU4s013mF1RVX0v3tniBjqLi+f3UAKqPpX3veTr2\n6CHYY/xuDY7lubF+mNCaJEll63Q5aHHa16Tl8S2DqZ0uFV05xdL4RWMUDfKJJjff\nuxCLyLBKL/tLNcCmf48eU6N5ehkgEqb1/iS7VepZQXLCIWVdM02FdVMmCg66EG7d\njKZ3YP9rQrMzLGbW1lyHY+tSLeEBKXUugb9UmqHgALP/aVHa+JauWP9nhafVXZEI\nCeqQ66yDmQx1Fr5/vDMfqm5QfguWz1jks2MVWJz1q0KgKjqMVqNKTMX0BGK9ipVn\nXyTHQ8bHDUkx4cevdNAe7Liq2Eu85dTFboL3DiZ3TdRVezwWhvdrCXf8Un8/hoLr\nt5jPMr45Lo+6g4Nxrgb9ed2OJFcNVfxwTszwHsPF35wcrxShvRGqwFG3qZ/TTZ3K\nX8+NKRraVwIbplyXaa3aKre3IrP3aeDcuuRMuQnyH0ialW8/ZtDy/7e/Lsh+oSy/\npUSbCFQ3VVMqy5KnDkkmMDxWBPnmTJmnlmT3tiBmpwIqsz5K1DZ9gmU8v2NFpgLx\npqjN5buM7IM+rIUrfcZl0ZygI+slP3SdstfHNSuTg5nGEhN90lpJcMCVhJ0PNUlD\nwV6OToWLjbGXUU5Y/Sq/\n=jfT2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a6f4b0c002f0593fd5de1809de8421ece696b45b\nparent e64b469bbcf2c2a6bb575ef0a58368f02147e899\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780603427 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780603427 -0700\n\n[codex] Fix Windows sandbox build script lint (#26445)\n\n## Why\n\nThe Windows ARM64 Cargo clippy job on `main` is failing because\nworkspace lints deny `clippy::expect_used`, and the\n`codex-windows-sandbox` build script used `expect()` while reading\n`CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR`.\n\n## What changed\n\n`codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs/build.rs` now returns `Result<(), String>`\nfrom `main()` and converts a missing `CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR` into an\nexplicit build-script error. The non-Windows early return and Windows\nlinker argument behavior are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just clippy -p codex-windows-sandbox -- -D warnings`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T20:03:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/555f8caeff42073fcdc52755491d785adcc81e4a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/555f8caeff42073fcdc52755491d785adcc81e4a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/555f8caeff42073fcdc52755491d785adcc81e4a/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e64b469bbcf2c2a6bb575ef0a58368f02147e899","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e64b469bbcf2c2a6bb575ef0a58368f02147e899","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e64b469bbcf2c2a6bb575ef0a58368f02147e899"}]},{"sha":"e64b469bbcf2c2a6bb575ef0a58368f02147e899","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU2NGI0NjliYmNmMmMyYTZiYjU3NWVmMGE1ODM2OGYwMjE0N2U4OTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T19:43:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T19:43:07Z"},"message":"Route AGENTS.md loading through environment filesystems (#26205)\n\n## Why\n\nWorkspace-specific `AGENTS.md` loading needs to use the selected\nenvironment filesystem so remote workspaces and child agents read\ninstructions from their actual environment instead of the host\nfilesystem. The app-server should report the same instruction sources\nthe initialized thread actually loaded, rather than independently\nrescanning configuration and filesystem state.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Introduce `LoadedAgentsMd` to retain ordered user, project, and\ninternal instructions with their provenance.\n- Load and canonicalize workspace `AGENTS.md` paths through the primary\n`EnvironmentManager` environment, then render the loaded instructions\nwhen constructing turn context.\n- Expose cached loaded instruction sources from initialized threads and\nuse them for app-server start, resume, and fork responses.\n- Preserve global `CODEX_HOME` loading and separator behavior while\nexcluding empty project files that did not supply model-visible\ninstructions.\n- Add integration coverage for CLI injection, selected-environment\nprovenance and rendering, empty environment selection, and cached\nsources on loaded-thread resume.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core agents_md`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nselected_environment_sources_match_model_visible_instructions`\n- `just test -p codex-exec agents_md`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server instruction_sources`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server --status-level fail`","tree":{"sha":"2df8be6d328d691bf8990cea2e09fe8b5288884e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2df8be6d328d691bf8990cea2e09fe8b5288884e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e64b469bbcf2c2a6bb575ef0a58368f02147e899","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIdVLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA01gQAH/7ETVbWehyn342H20Uy/cQ\nb4j+V2/8XBbDmfX/IDYjw7hdOdiAeiEVcCTxTERMgaIK8E7xzbv/OC2MWNcKGg1g\nYc3iW4evAyR0FesRkO2UxD3tFFv/7493+LcmcjSH0HVyN4VTNFD8Ha9kRIBZODNl\n22qUgFdvpKDPTxckg4v2dghoJltNm8grLc93Riyiv7+g5DzgqVKsqqMDB/EF0c0b\nZ55WG6ZJ/A3ia/XnzmFUSfGviFE3aIrDnUYidke5sYp/Z/dlVbaPcM+989EvvVB8\n4Wxv+XRSHJ49dXrQH1VPBNElF+7nk4mFJOmrfXLl/nhLIvllRV7l3pA2jIaf4RQM\nToPtNX36XKmqZhTcgrs2lxrz6k5fYM94OSzK2n/WZF7y+LI0cAXRHq+CWwomfDSI\nSWWFWe7ktYXNRIcEBQ8CXU4o/2MlnmtRW+fzTBLL+hnJVWkwRiPYrm4coQ85/ysx\nif3hUuHhPZ6wzRC4MEImrNqUvl+LDr7iVQYkpr41l/eKgwMaQ6n5+/wiMeIB8+wk\nxSKpkxVvXOW1HV3vdjNBRME7eU9HVoGyMcdaiHKL2tfslhJ5tpBtHnuY4ZehNDrV\nRXstLy15fR0ekl3sX2jto51uCznN/Wbgi42vKYcXbGVv36JcBSaU8Ja2BaPBcLp1\n/aZ0PquxanOU6TxsHHPO\n=AyAG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2df8be6d328d691bf8990cea2e09fe8b5288884e\nparent c3fcb0e7457dc53aa4422ae4356e1fcc2a206ce6\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780602187 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780602187 -0700\n\nRoute AGENTS.md loading through environment filesystems (#26205)\n\n## Why\n\nWorkspace-specific `AGENTS.md` loading needs to use the selected\nenvironment filesystem so remote workspaces and child agents read\ninstructions from their actual environment instead of the host\nfilesystem. The app-server should report the same instruction sources\nthe initialized thread actually loaded, rather than independently\nrescanning configuration and filesystem state.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Introduce `LoadedAgentsMd` to retain ordered user, project, and\ninternal instructions with their provenance.\n- Load and canonicalize workspace `AGENTS.md` paths through the primary\n`EnvironmentManager` environment, then render the loaded instructions\nwhen constructing turn context.\n- Expose cached loaded instruction sources from initialized threads and\nuse them for app-server start, resume, and fork responses.\n- Preserve global `CODEX_HOME` loading and separator behavior while\nexcluding empty project files that did not supply model-visible\ninstructions.\n- Add integration coverage for CLI injection, selected-environment\nprovenance and rendering, empty environment selection, and cached\nsources on loaded-thread resume.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core agents_md`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nselected_environment_sources_match_model_visible_instructions`\n- `just test -p codex-exec agents_md`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server instruction_sources`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server --status-level fail`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T19:43:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e64b469bbcf2c2a6bb575ef0a58368f02147e899","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e64b469bbcf2c2a6bb575ef0a58368f02147e899","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e64b469bbcf2c2a6bb575ef0a58368f02147e899/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c3fcb0e7457dc53aa4422ae4356e1fcc2a206ce6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c3fcb0e7457dc53aa4422ae4356e1fcc2a206ce6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c3fcb0e7457dc53aa4422ae4356e1fcc2a206ce6"}]},{"sha":"c3fcb0e7457dc53aa4422ae4356e1fcc2a206ce6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMzZmNiMGU3NDU3ZGM1M2FhNDQyMmFlNDM1NmUxZmNjMmEyMDZjZTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shijie Rao","email":"shijie.rao@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T19:24:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T19:24:26Z"},"message":"Use Azure artifact signing environment secrets (#25945)\n\n## Why\nWindows release signing should read Azure signing credentials from the\n`azure-artifact-signing` environment instead of the old repo-level\n`AZURE_TRUSTED_SIGNING_*` names. The smoke runs confirmed the\nenvironment secrets resolve with the new `AZURE_ARTIFACT_SIGNING_*`\nnames once the Windows signing job is attached to that environment.\n\n## What Changed\n- Put the real Windows signing job in the `azure-artifact-signing`\nenvironment.\n- Switch the Windows signing action inputs from\n`AZURE_TRUSTED_SIGNING_*` to `AZURE_ARTIFACT_SIGNING_*`.\n- Drop the obsolete `workflow_call.secrets` declarations for the old\nrepo-level secret names; the caller continues to use `secrets: inherit`.\n- Remove the temporary branch-trigger and Windows-only smoke-test\nworkflow changes before finalizing this PR.\n\n## Validation\n- `git diff --check -- .github/workflows/rust-release.yml\n.github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml`\n- `ruby -e 'require \"yaml\"; ARGV.each { |f| YAML.load_file(f); puts\n\"yaml ok: #{f}\" }' .github/workflows/rust-release.yml\n.github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml`","tree":{"sha":"8f60b7f9516342aec53799a6350c7c3d899c4167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8f60b7f9516342aec53799a6350c7c3d899c4167"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c3fcb0e7457dc53aa4422ae4356e1fcc2a206ce6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIdDqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxFgQABjDt0K3EyyY7cGP+s2bZ+C9\nQRocxqmZT7k+ySFEQoRQgrnH8bStvURb1K5uUrwuZiqq9l0ThOGsK5qrqSbNp5jp\n2Np3lzNx5Y1Hb62M7qJ2yjdvM++wBY+1Tx70FMkPLbn2rdz5SXFRFhyKZF97PpZJ\nijKPPYlkPBKJBpZ7YjUOEX80RehhWtlvg+294QP9jWQXN0Er+RV+wxJhshs/2hR9\ngrQ0JjLwkgd+NmOypuSZqaC63cVDwrnbSrwVa5JiLH3xJKmTWoYEcghMqYQO50RI\nELYOXBfIFTaZ9xDk+5GVciVjPiE6PKG5tFMk6ytoiiFk1LLOJwGnsC52gw1Work4\nN2MTut+NdLrKdtkPPCSaky6WXVEWpRTEOJTcx6Pg0D/Sxqli2bzmQGDBKM01HShX\nZo5CtkJsiRvl1oPnL/Rm4Pdc0l2JpkDyJHK3ok6J0Vq2OSxIYieCA1SeGci+BI/H\n/Y8P5qNSAA9YyneZQnD8QzEfIvxYJtDKNPgoaVAjenCjYqksr84Wvt+Quak96J3j\nLgl+AzN8GONSjkCeY4YupfUv1pLdy22nmyguy4VO5gaJHNrlddHb/xioQoua8LSi\nWnsiLOXUYVPvWDctByoznGlzs7XqEut5ELfyEj01UbTPmWlFMr25eF/1DfX6rx0+\n80kL3TuNKPe3oLhsrbbq\n=dwed\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8f60b7f9516342aec53799a6350c7c3d899c4167\nparent 8b1238856b0839cfdb345ee2af9f02e4ee2959f9\nauthor Shijie Rao <shijie.rao@openai.com> 1780601066 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780601066 -0700\n\nUse Azure artifact signing environment secrets (#25945)\n\n## Why\nWindows release signing should read Azure signing credentials from the\n`azure-artifact-signing` environment instead of the old repo-level\n`AZURE_TRUSTED_SIGNING_*` names. The smoke runs confirmed the\nenvironment secrets resolve with the new `AZURE_ARTIFACT_SIGNING_*`\nnames once the Windows signing job is attached to that environment.\n\n## What Changed\n- Put the real Windows signing job in the `azure-artifact-signing`\nenvironment.\n- Switch the Windows signing action inputs from\n`AZURE_TRUSTED_SIGNING_*` to `AZURE_ARTIFACT_SIGNING_*`.\n- Drop the obsolete `workflow_call.secrets` declarations for the old\nrepo-level secret names; the caller continues to use `secrets: inherit`.\n- Remove the temporary branch-trigger and Windows-only smoke-test\nworkflow changes before finalizing this PR.\n\n## Validation\n- `git diff --check -- .github/workflows/rust-release.yml\n.github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml`\n- `ruby -e 'require \"yaml\"; ARGV.each { |f| YAML.load_file(f); puts\n\"yaml ok: #{f}\" }' .github/workflows/rust-release.yml\n.github/workflows/rust-release-windows.yml`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T19:24:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c3fcb0e7457dc53aa4422ae4356e1fcc2a206ce6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c3fcb0e7457dc53aa4422ae4356e1fcc2a206ce6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c3fcb0e7457dc53aa4422ae4356e1fcc2a206ce6/comments","author":{"login":"shijie-oai","id":235382242,"node_id":"U_kgDODgel4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235382242?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/shijie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shijie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8b1238856b0839cfdb345ee2af9f02e4ee2959f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8b1238856b0839cfdb345ee2af9f02e4ee2959f9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8b1238856b0839cfdb345ee2af9f02e4ee2959f9"}]},{"sha":"8b1238856b0839cfdb345ee2af9f02e4ee2959f9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhiMTIzODg1NmIwODM5Y2ZkYjM0NWVlMmFmOWYwMmU0ZWUyOTU5Zjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T18:40:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T18:40:18Z"},"message":"core: allow excluding tool namespaces from code mode (#26320)\n\n## Why\n\nResearch and training setups need to control which tool namespaces\nappear inside code mode's nested `tools` surface without disabling those\ntools entirely. This makes it possible to train against a deliberately\nreduced nested-tool setup while preserving the normal direct and\ndeferred tool paths.\n\n## What\n\n- Extend `features.code_mode` to accept structured configuration while\npreserving the existing boolean syntax.\n- Add an exact `excluded_tool_namespaces` list under\n`[features.code_mode]`:\n\n  ```toml\n  [features.code_mode]\n  enabled = true\n  excluded_tool_namespaces = [\"mcp__codex_apps\", \"multi_agent_v1\"]\n  ```\n\n- Filter matching canonical `ToolName` namespaces when constructing code\nmode's nested router and code-mode-specific direct tool descriptions.\n- Keep excluded tools registered, directly exposed in mixed code mode,\nand discoverable through top-level `tool_search` when otherwise\neligible.\n- Derive deferred nested-tool guidance after namespace filtering so the\n`exec` description does not advertise excluded-only deferred tools.\n- Preserve the boolean/table representation when materializing config\nlocks and update the generated config schema.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-core load_config_resolves_code_mode_config`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlock_contains_prompts_and_materializes_features`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nexcluded_deferred_namespaces_do_not_enable_nested_tool_guidance`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncode_mode_excludes_configured_nested_tool_namespaces`\n- `cargo check -p codex-thread-manager-sample`","tree":{"sha":"56e7ad1bea5a1c8e1a9f26ba9e3819e1e97ed39d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/56e7ad1bea5a1c8e1a9f26ba9e3819e1e97ed39d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8b1238856b0839cfdb345ee2af9f02e4ee2959f9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIcaSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA59cQAG/ZJsUdlahY4IZ1vj0qKVb2\nHS4me2QH8UkvRX2pPQdlCZfehyh8JMim6xatXQ+0xV9QNH3kJ8rJDWO0lSlrbvE5\n0OCr3K0wdqwAXqTo0Mbaob6i9ywskRidll7L+NCePK4YXy8kJhjJmPtDm7FRfmfY\n/bt1uy0+90gEuxZ+cURChQV1GUdzoCOQJP+wEjyRLcOAEGUkY+LVOJBz94HhmYWw\nQ1hnuZtBAcR8YmH24SeT7fHJIuJvFux1pe3hIEyxEe/CzSfAHZs6yCvN+wiNUtvZ\nqkH0nrLsxhUMM+v2Mt5G/jDmtWHPp8pE/Q/fu54EqbkQUjcuXPQOg2BIJt9FwpUK\nJfT81urAOqu4RL98X/AFthemgs7zR8s4rEBAc+8mLLuL6+yIUDmF2rh2oALgFSrc\nQZXe298Lls+Fgrl8778Av/Nq1U+cfCLefQetiL5rIoadeNh+EPBpxqxooxGamzgZ\nZC5nsRMfHwhH1nCXobbYMiIetRVvDa6elJMmTB7lF7fq1Yt93CbSpKyc3rhrmasv\ns4R9OejHKrdlPoYmsh7LoNanV/Bw8mA/cFqd2EKGFOYefo9X6tM8HIFhefwPt7cZ\nR44mKNN7aO4eZCRtqWZRCVpXFNFlhciSBx1xkEaXa5pnFrz2gcff+D5hpH6Nytj9\nWgT2Y+Cww9nToftGBtIn\n=WEAA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 56e7ad1bea5a1c8e1a9f26ba9e3819e1e97ed39d\nparent 9e41f8ddbe087ae6b9bdfb8d5821ab2f09f8c5fe\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1780598418 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780598418 +0000\n\ncore: allow excluding tool namespaces from code mode (#26320)\n\n## Why\n\nResearch and training setups need to control which tool namespaces\nappear inside code mode's nested `tools` surface without disabling those\ntools entirely. This makes it possible to train against a deliberately\nreduced nested-tool setup while preserving the normal direct and\ndeferred tool paths.\n\n## What\n\n- Extend `features.code_mode` to accept structured configuration while\npreserving the existing boolean syntax.\n- Add an exact `excluded_tool_namespaces` list under\n`[features.code_mode]`:\n\n  ```toml\n  [features.code_mode]\n  enabled = true\n  excluded_tool_namespaces = [\"mcp__codex_apps\", \"multi_agent_v1\"]\n  ```\n\n- Filter matching canonical `ToolName` namespaces when constructing code\nmode's nested router and code-mode-specific direct tool descriptions.\n- Keep excluded tools registered, directly exposed in mixed code mode,\nand discoverable through top-level `tool_search` when otherwise\neligible.\n- Derive deferred nested-tool guidance after namespace filtering so the\n`exec` description does not advertise excluded-only deferred tools.\n- Preserve the boolean/table representation when materializing config\nlocks and update the generated config schema.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-features`\n- `just test -p codex-config`\n- `just test -p codex-core load_config_resolves_code_mode_config`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlock_contains_prompts_and_materializes_features`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nexcluded_deferred_namespaces_do_not_enable_nested_tool_guidance`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncode_mode_excludes_configured_nested_tool_namespaces`\n- `cargo check -p codex-thread-manager-sample`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T18:40:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8b1238856b0839cfdb345ee2af9f02e4ee2959f9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8b1238856b0839cfdb345ee2af9f02e4ee2959f9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8b1238856b0839cfdb345ee2af9f02e4ee2959f9/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9e41f8ddbe087ae6b9bdfb8d5821ab2f09f8c5fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e41f8ddbe087ae6b9bdfb8d5821ab2f09f8c5fe","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9e41f8ddbe087ae6b9bdfb8d5821ab2f09f8c5fe"}]},{"sha":"9e41f8ddbe087ae6b9bdfb8d5821ab2f09f8c5fe","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDllNDFmOGRkYmUwODdhZTZiOWJkZmI4ZDU4MjFhYjJmMDlmOGM1ZmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"kbazzi","email":"kbazzi@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T18:24:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T18:24:12Z"},"message":"[codex-analytics] emit forked thread id on initialization (#26248)\n\n## Why\n- Thread initialization analytics do not identify the source thread for\nforked threads.\n- The session viewer needs this lineage to construct thread trees.\n- Depends on openai/openai#987854. Do not release this change before\nthat backend schema change is deployed.\n\n## What Changed\n- Adds optional `forked_from_thread_id` to `codex_thread_initialized`.\n- Populates it from the existing thread fork lineage for app-server and\nin-process subagent initialization paths.\n- Keeps it null for non-forked threads.\n\n## Verification\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-analytics`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_fork_tracks_thread_initialized_analytics`","tree":{"sha":"31deb52d638f15c90169554eee52d91d87bd4f8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/31deb52d638f15c90169554eee52d91d87bd4f8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9e41f8ddbe087ae6b9bdfb8d5821ab2f09f8c5fe","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIcLMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9wMQADy6WEbVAZ0FQGtPZDG9LZcB\nOF/HEZ1NQJfiJo5cGpMqi+MR5X+KnnqLOrJPOKbbT6Z/lnimshTJBKfX2uulPEQp\nh1SejdACbYY3KXBYi+STx6mIvhxCCEQF8QbrpCPzvN9na1Pn+BUcbaZxPdr8BdGz\n4lGppI+Z4kge6PfspwfszFjafYjy0UCfhx5hgtRVJkZDTHU8wWRgdCiYKL24bode\nM1r+b6H4l8IIsc9N2Ei3+zJjjoNXEbAbb/XZErQBDA9i22OV6o8/ignUj9FaQHFI\nai92ANzqLJFXzYNBJpId7gZlPkJ7P61wzlFwrpkFzfiP5ATvf0uomSwRVJX5wK5H\nX0hRwB17cdoLuyvcOw/qL9BSjVf5zQrpdlPI0wLuc7er5l/idnxWLMrS5lz/UEuw\nVPGc58/thWIxsdsL6ow2vOvy/9Quj8IJDJsWoGu49XsEvvFWbqmk7EClam4SRcrd\ncOpXJxbd58Kar6DOD4P6aQtgIuAM6QseAID/hVVtEwIzGrh32zCMX8XxKIjrUgh1\n5koYapYp9qL/AyM2pQiwD8hfBgalODqZ6KB5NbkjmUl9fA7y8VZTqPI5aKqhgpkI\nF2xxCDdtqedkuyErvNt1sOVGqkEEixyUXwwsWj5WhLjD2B56ugBeJf4rygjdumkj\n0kyANgiv1E5VvwB+j2Qe\n=uXAL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 31deb52d638f15c90169554eee52d91d87bd4f8b\nparent c8fdc74b421fb904e11c07886a3a7dc22fa56ed6\nauthor kbazzi <kbazzi@openai.com> 1780597452 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780597452 -0700\n\n[codex-analytics] emit forked thread id on initialization (#26248)\n\n## Why\n- Thread initialization analytics do not identify the source thread for\nforked threads.\n- The session viewer needs this lineage to construct thread trees.\n- Depends on openai/openai#987854. Do not release this change before\nthat backend schema change is deployed.\n\n## What Changed\n- Adds optional `forked_from_thread_id` to `codex_thread_initialized`.\n- Populates it from the existing thread fork lineage for app-server and\nin-process subagent initialization paths.\n- Keeps it null for non-forked threads.\n\n## Verification\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-analytics`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_fork_tracks_thread_initialized_analytics`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T18:24:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e41f8ddbe087ae6b9bdfb8d5821ab2f09f8c5fe","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9e41f8ddbe087ae6b9bdfb8d5821ab2f09f8c5fe","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9e41f8ddbe087ae6b9bdfb8d5821ab2f09f8c5fe/comments","author":{"login":"kbazzi","id":289796993,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUXzgQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289796993?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi","html_url":"https://github.com/kbazzi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c8fdc74b421fb904e11c07886a3a7dc22fa56ed6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c8fdc74b421fb904e11c07886a3a7dc22fa56ed6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c8fdc74b421fb904e11c07886a3a7dc22fa56ed6"}]},{"sha":"c8fdc74b421fb904e11c07886a3a7dc22fa56ed6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM4ZmRjNzRiNDIxZmI5MDRlMTFjMDc4ODZhM2E3ZGMyMmZhNTZlZDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"stefanstokic-oai","email":"stefanstokic@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T18:16:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T18:16:03Z"},"message":"external-agent-migration: avoid mixed MCP transport configs (#26435)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP migration could recursively merge an imported server into an\nexisting same-named Codex server. When one definition used stdio and the\nother used HTTP, this produced an invalid mixed configuration containing\nboth `command` and `url`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Merge MCP configuration at the server level instead of field by field.\n- Preserve an existing same-named Codex MCP server unchanged.\n- Report only MCP servers that would actually be added during detection.\n- Add regression coverage for mixed command/HTTP source configurations.\n- Use neutral fixture names and reserved `example.com` URLs.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server repo_mcp`\n  - 5 tests passed.\n- `just test -p codex-external-agent-migration\nmcp_migration_prefers_command_transport_for_mixed_server_config`\n  - 1 test passed.","tree":{"sha":"de28af57a7791dfa02a055bbe17d83529408e6c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/de28af57a7791dfa02a055bbe17d83529408e6c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c8fdc74b421fb904e11c07886a3a7dc22fa56ed6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIcDjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0m4QAAijJq+NBpTX8N19mHzztDWr\n+lsnNp+qTD4Ose8iCV2+40eT6uqZHGi086yEqm4pezy84thv9QezqoxXNoyDbvME\nniAPfXFMla2u51OcrsVFu5WCHgA6lnfYqiyko58hAFevOr6kaF9Wx/YTL5QQ28CX\nXvUhy0BC3QEF8RxhcAHBahNwrcYgCHx+B66KyZJnSYrAqlwOofv+RckBWgblXx14\n0HtzTSy5cyZDGyRQubw4EGUuKpSPw96d8lUcbSQlTwwVsc7X+6EvaD9vapH/g3c6\nGhrFLjJ6RSkSqtPY2GusLVGtGWHBA6NBswGQ0VDpBpXx7nmwlQZqIILK00Em8IIA\nadyNOF8q+AJWgBxP4HOIBRnZHDNd1MhMLXrmfgHLwfONvfJ65EDKduk1FLxqJpDI\ny424GNO0d6Pm1FzM3Mz+QOAsDmnmMHr+9jw7gqFpfOf+8jtPedVlpT7mnpeDBeYj\nkLXrl8aodvVnOUD6OY3x/s8RFxLVxGlmEntf4S5RW/pVrzXPv/J3DIyvxcrgJfiY\nVsNXwFiORVYn4fvWpDkGFZ/dEpP682+2hCACQK9y5XCg77MieE/Z6q7xVtbvMnlE\nu6NtGfrhQeqOUUbtuS9WBQHrn3ZGW+3bvg8Acv482n5JgxjoD+/CTd5y9SQfmDoP\nnIX7MJV2U6jjoxi5Lbd6\n=NN2t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree de28af57a7791dfa02a055bbe17d83529408e6c9\nparent 881cf191d72da0edfc90cbc9fd5b3c30cb6eb9bc\nauthor stefanstokic-oai <stefanstokic@openai.com> 1780596963 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780596963 -0400\n\nexternal-agent-migration: avoid mixed MCP transport configs (#26435)\n\n## Why\n\nMCP migration could recursively merge an imported server into an\nexisting same-named Codex server. When one definition used stdio and the\nother used HTTP, this produced an invalid mixed configuration containing\nboth `command` and `url`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Merge MCP configuration at the server level instead of field by field.\n- Preserve an existing same-named Codex MCP server unchanged.\n- Report only MCP servers that would actually be added during detection.\n- Add regression coverage for mixed command/HTTP source configurations.\n- Use neutral fixture names and reserved `example.com` URLs.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server repo_mcp`\n  - 5 tests passed.\n- `just test -p codex-external-agent-migration\nmcp_migration_prefers_command_transport_for_mixed_server_config`\n  - 1 test passed.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T18:16:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c8fdc74b421fb904e11c07886a3a7dc22fa56ed6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c8fdc74b421fb904e11c07886a3a7dc22fa56ed6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c8fdc74b421fb904e11c07886a3a7dc22fa56ed6/comments","author":{"login":"stefanstokic-oai","id":278208182,"node_id":"U_kgDOEJUetg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/278208182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/stefanstokic-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"881cf191d72da0edfc90cbc9fd5b3c30cb6eb9bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/881cf191d72da0edfc90cbc9fd5b3c30cb6eb9bc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/881cf191d72da0edfc90cbc9fd5b3c30cb6eb9bc"}]},{"sha":"881cf191d72da0edfc90cbc9fd5b3c30cb6eb9bc","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg4MWNmMTkxZDcyZGEwZWRmYzkwY2JjOWZkNWIzYzMwY2I2ZWI5YmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T18:05:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T18:05:54Z"},"message":"app-server: support -c config overrides (#26436)\n\n## Why\n\nThe standalone `codex-app-server` binary already routed a\n`CliConfigOverrides` value into app-server startup, but its own clap\nargs did not expose the shared `-c/--config` option. That meant\n`codex-app-server -c key=value` was rejected before the existing config\noverride path could run, unlike the main `codex` CLI.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Flatten `CliConfigOverrides` into `AppServerArgs` in\n`codex-rs/app-server/src/main.rs`.\n- Pass parsed overrides to `run_main_with_transport_options` instead of\nalways using `CliConfigOverrides::default()`.\n- Add a binary parser test covering both `-c` and `--config` for the\nstandalone app-server.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\napp_server_accepts_cli_config_overrides`\n\nThe broader `just test -p codex-app-server` run was also attempted. It\ncompiled and ran 812 tests, with 796 passing, but failed in this local\nsandbox on unrelated `sandbox-exec: sandbox_apply: Operation not\npermitted` command-exec/turn integration paths and a skills watcher\ntimeout.","tree":{"sha":"cd4c227362641fa0c9da5ac300c6a8e0f7cf4688","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/cd4c227362641fa0c9da5ac300c6a8e0f7cf4688"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/881cf191d72da0edfc90cbc9fd5b3c30cb6eb9bc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIb6CCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEw4QAGiRLzfg4RC35I/znkooF4R7\nYyKsZv8DB9lf8CCe9Nsx22r+04Wp07tf5uMpAxG0RZ4x/3oRPOV26gxHsueUls9m\n7m4qSoRg/vrtQ1dy1I5Hf3JU/IxVc4lJUb4Dso0/kqu2wjLul4JDq1pC9ySc8XqO\nAxgdd4iKR1bs0u5ZzeD4+fX+qJG4iZl1ghPZ3EwOjB2I50iXEXVjMXPGCDEjEIs/\naWykk+lZNk9cljWVz19yg133acKcntn8hGfYehdqNRDqEXC4nxI6gOC2Dcbx6vsk\nti2nE9vE4Tat22373rkgjZOFlrKDFMQH57Hf1ytae6YfKb6fDAJV3eaa4zpwJ1+R\nUEaCulaawloUPCn/LY1gJDKPmPVt5O9ZqJQO+NN32K9pVmmpLw3TxtrvQFtnNw5o\nTVTLjYRUf27ZlLWNhZrEo6YdjPpLUIhxNSRigzjfUVVQjfQKtheLwmvnBs6e3D8p\n0DPBCOfjW5I44EYfk/7ow4kFxDOBANy9SocVnK/uGHh58J9pNlDMiy/To9sf95RE\nH5VmDvMMYNv7PiHmHU0Z54tfKmbcbZJmH6qMaCk27T/zcm2L91NAhenB1sghYmin\nJdLd1PMExwEo/k4ctYaeGPolSc0uJ03G68uKkB9rzhRE5K4RmRUm3K0H3mAV3qY7\nyPJ18hTSXlcai2MOjWzL\n=yvgc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cd4c227362641fa0c9da5ac300c6a8e0f7cf4688\nparent cdc1d592df7f066c141025cc8ae80bb3202580b6\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780596354 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780596354 +0000\n\napp-server: support -c config overrides (#26436)\n\n## Why\n\nThe standalone `codex-app-server` binary already routed a\n`CliConfigOverrides` value into app-server startup, but its own clap\nargs did not expose the shared `-c/--config` option. That meant\n`codex-app-server -c key=value` was rejected before the existing config\noverride path could run, unlike the main `codex` CLI.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Flatten `CliConfigOverrides` into `AppServerArgs` in\n`codex-rs/app-server/src/main.rs`.\n- Pass parsed overrides to `run_main_with_transport_options` instead of\nalways using `CliConfigOverrides::default()`.\n- Add a binary parser test covering both `-c` and `--config` for the\nstandalone app-server.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\napp_server_accepts_cli_config_overrides`\n\nThe broader `just test -p codex-app-server` run was also attempted. It\ncompiled and ran 812 tests, with 796 passing, but failed in this local\nsandbox on unrelated `sandbox-exec: sandbox_apply: Operation not\npermitted` command-exec/turn integration paths and a skills watcher\ntimeout.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T18:05:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/881cf191d72da0edfc90cbc9fd5b3c30cb6eb9bc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/881cf191d72da0edfc90cbc9fd5b3c30cb6eb9bc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/881cf191d72da0edfc90cbc9fd5b3c30cb6eb9bc/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cdc1d592df7f066c141025cc8ae80bb3202580b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cdc1d592df7f066c141025cc8ae80bb3202580b6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cdc1d592df7f066c141025cc8ae80bb3202580b6"}]},{"sha":"cdc1d592df7f066c141025cc8ae80bb3202580b6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNkYzFkNTkyZGY3ZjA2NmMxNDEwMjVjYzhhZTgwYmIzMjAyNTgwYjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"mpc-oai","email":"mpc@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T17:20:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T17:20:32Z"},"message":"Expose configured marketplace source in plugin list JSON (#26417)\n\n## Summary\n- Follow-up to #25330\n- Add `marketplaceSource` to `codex plugin list --json` entries for\nconfigured marketplaces\n- Keep the existing per-plugin `source` field unchanged; this still\nreports the local plugin source path\n- Include only the configured marketplace `sourceType` and `source` from\n`config.toml`\n- Keep human-readable output unchanged\n- Add CLI coverage for configured local and git marketplace sources\n\nExample:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"source\": {\n    \"source\": \"local\",\n    \"path\": \"/path/to/.codex/.tmp/marketplaces/debug/plugins/sample\"\n  },\n  \"marketplaceSource\": {\n    \"sourceType\": \"git\",\n    \"source\": \"https://example.com/acme/agent-skills.git\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-cli`\n- `just test -p codex-cli plugin_list`","tree":{"sha":"57dbbbc5e2dc89fae7f889dbfc58310eb9b5986f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/57dbbbc5e2dc89fae7f889dbfc58310eb9b5986f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cdc1d592df7f066c141025cc8ae80bb3202580b6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIbPhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAT50QAApEmsUeJdpKJqqOZ2vzfPjZ\niCj2tciy/wjzBqKKv9r4w+wifljEB/LYsYJ30w1fiO4cUf25kNM9bgZ80AS8WZoe\n+hitacd5fW0tRVJR15xNUlryy3vNFSyJMZbwgI/Qw9rmyK3/l4cc2F63wwqynGos\nE5uJx0fhHi9A8wkbQqb0ENtzzsdb541ug2ah6EqwbTXDjkA3T+nNZhzYjG8aZNla\n4Pipw5TKl0kWraHOIflw6q3DIntE5REQXYl5zZ1H4pzmaElXDTTQD3wpUKT0JGfS\nQ8ZpbJwd8M6lu9nG5CwqsaPlfUJAlsIk4CfnyAHHYgyIGTk6Vqkb4722KHiqUPnH\nyPaGPZcoW9YsX1Hx2YXV6xvvy/3flNlk6k7Qg/aCias0x2Eyw8jvB4nhCkVZDuVV\nmLb31+bzxOlMLEBnAMeGau3pZB/3dexmU5eRr2paxs/YW9i1UlHJFw0udEDCrZjK\n3pJ4jMRiBsPYOMjoT5cPkQ1GbLvgXgzWItd83NxMhy8lCBNH8cyHr07so/3llMlJ\nqPb86iU3IP9/WkFn8qcPwtEIm3G3JZM1STSLQ4Sfaz+qDwfcLOY/3oSP4PDAX2a6\nxeye+IeR+erPOmaExPeBwnGBaHNSuYghYzQHquvt6GOVkq1HVJlu6sm4GiAy4Pr2\nuTSNT9xPWwCfLXmi/ysE\n=KyNR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 57dbbbc5e2dc89fae7f889dbfc58310eb9b5986f\nparent cbf62f64cbfdca160e7303536ec6ea464d371281\nauthor mpc-oai <mpc@openai.com> 1780593632 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780593632 -0500\n\nExpose configured marketplace source in plugin list JSON (#26417)\n\n## Summary\n- Follow-up to #25330\n- Add `marketplaceSource` to `codex plugin list --json` entries for\nconfigured marketplaces\n- Keep the existing per-plugin `source` field unchanged; this still\nreports the local plugin source path\n- Include only the configured marketplace `sourceType` and `source` from\n`config.toml`\n- Keep human-readable output unchanged\n- Add CLI coverage for configured local and git marketplace sources\n\nExample:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"source\": {\n    \"source\": \"local\",\n    \"path\": \"/path/to/.codex/.tmp/marketplaces/debug/plugins/sample\"\n  },\n  \"marketplaceSource\": {\n    \"sourceType\": \"git\",\n    \"source\": \"https://example.com/acme/agent-skills.git\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just fix -p codex-cli`\n- `just test -p codex-cli plugin_list`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T17:20:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cdc1d592df7f066c141025cc8ae80bb3202580b6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cdc1d592df7f066c141025cc8ae80bb3202580b6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cdc1d592df7f066c141025cc8ae80bb3202580b6/comments","author":{"login":"mpc-oai","id":278119679,"node_id":"U_kgDOEJPE_w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/278119679?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/mpc-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mpc-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cbf62f64cbfdca160e7303536ec6ea464d371281","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cbf62f64cbfdca160e7303536ec6ea464d371281","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cbf62f64cbfdca160e7303536ec6ea464d371281"}]},{"sha":"cbf62f64cbfdca160e7303536ec6ea464d371281","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNiZjYyZjY0Y2JmZGNhMTYwZTczMDM1MzZlYzZlYTQ2NGQzNzEyODE","commit":{"author":{"name":"stefanstokic-oai","email":"stefanstokic@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T17:13:05Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T17:13:05Z"},"message":"Bound external agent session detection work (#26291)\n\n## Why\n\nExternal agent migration detection parsed and hashed every JSONL session\nfile. For users with many large conversations, launching migration could\nconsume substantial CPU and disk resources.\n\nDetection only needs the most recent sessions for the migration UI, so\nfull-content work should be bounded.\n\n## What\n\n- Use file modification metadata to select the 50 most recent eligible\nsessions before parsing JSONL content.\n- Skip unchanged imported sessions using metadata stored in the import\nledger.\n- Preserve content hashing when metadata indicates a session may have\nchanged.\n- Stream SHA-256 calculation through a 64 KiB buffer instead of loading\nan entire session into memory.\n- Continue detecting older sessions in subsequent batches after newer\nsessions are imported.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `RUST_MIN_STACK=8388608 cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -p\ncodex-external-agent-sessions`\n  - 20 tests passed.\n- Benchmarked release builds against 250 valid JSONL sessions totaling\n501 MiB:\n  - Median detection time decreased from 1,138.8 ms to 47.0 ms.\n  - CPU instructions decreased by 95.8%.\n  - Both versions returned the expected 50 sessions.\n\nThe benchmark used warm filesystem caches and measured the reduction in\nparsing, hashing, and CPU work.","tree":{"sha":"17658af9f1d74a84e77ed3e3af4fa9dabeabed14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/17658af9f1d74a84e77ed3e3af4fa9dabeabed14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cbf62f64cbfdca160e7303536ec6ea464d371281","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIbIhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhMYQAJ5rjUsKXghlOu6HalJI0m9z\noZ4pw4yfBw714fjNyKFu8OQhxQ7YZ0aKzYYcqRDP2cbMT0Qbo663wYhyMo8IEHMz\nQMqdkZpGe7p6ABCFuNeNBnHR30WyxqFLzSDFFbxWd1Yt32eI3xabfaRxqkTd4Wmb\nqf8pd3WsXeByYvVev4C3/H7JJdlCb4YOhM5JBeHGGBK0oI2nsbv/qgSrM7H7Ux4F\nJKUOtPGQTVnD+TKssyUh2pXxv84zb41pX0k8xSiBInZXGe4JE1o1TabzV93B40qL\nwNn7Ge3FsOn7CAMJzGMW8yHAhR59CRwENkzY7EDhcVvkEYGVdk8HvNlQGQW6kW5d\nXnA5U9EIPNHjUl7erAAnH4zV9ROO4/dV1u6flYMr8zGsF9A8afNeFqy6q1EJ0r3x\niBuEsjAe1sa6WTzL9TV11+gTW7w8ziBEvjPJ4nTN6/NXjVRvlr6pkLcPSz2c98tN\ne5Hagqkj1kNu51FiJlHbUcUu1yKvD/99AJAKO7xwtT0lBW+3QnxD05CNY8rNYEc0\nlnfSui3VXeyOdM9bFNBp2eINA0Ji6Ejt6YkiOekgqCRH5cbYN9IQQQIjqy6nt9jA\nBJGXxojpucoCAyiovPdP5Kt6v8Q4UeVlp47B9on0tkfA5M20kkUU25USgCk9bXX3\nfeSacvLglXBN6Kvw426p\n=1EX9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 17658af9f1d74a84e77ed3e3af4fa9dabeabed14\nparent 12e8764a9c61dfc8cc8ba2520a2b7cf3e0500edd\nauthor stefanstokic-oai <stefanstokic@openai.com> 1780593185 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780593185 -0400\n\nBound external agent session detection work (#26291)\n\n## Why\n\nExternal agent migration detection parsed and hashed every JSONL session\nfile. For users with many large conversations, launching migration could\nconsume substantial CPU and disk resources.\n\nDetection only needs the most recent sessions for the migration UI, so\nfull-content work should be bounded.\n\n## What\n\n- Use file modification metadata to select the 50 most recent eligible\nsessions before parsing JSONL content.\n- Skip unchanged imported sessions using metadata stored in the import\nledger.\n- Preserve content hashing when metadata indicates a session may have\nchanged.\n- Stream SHA-256 calculation through a 64 KiB buffer instead of loading\nan entire session into memory.\n- Continue detecting older sessions in subsequent batches after newer\nsessions are imported.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `RUST_MIN_STACK=8388608 cargo nextest run --no-fail-fast -p\ncodex-external-agent-sessions`\n  - 20 tests passed.\n- Benchmarked release builds against 250 valid JSONL sessions totaling\n501 MiB:\n  - Median detection time decreased from 1,138.8 ms to 47.0 ms.\n  - CPU instructions decreased by 95.8%.\n  - Both versions returned the expected 50 sessions.\n\nThe benchmark used warm filesystem caches and measured the reduction in\nparsing, hashing, and CPU work.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T17:13:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cbf62f64cbfdca160e7303536ec6ea464d371281","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cbf62f64cbfdca160e7303536ec6ea464d371281","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cbf62f64cbfdca160e7303536ec6ea464d371281/comments","author":{"login":"stefanstokic-oai","id":278208182,"node_id":"U_kgDOEJUetg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/278208182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/stefanstokic-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"12e8764a9c61dfc8cc8ba2520a2b7cf3e0500edd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/12e8764a9c61dfc8cc8ba2520a2b7cf3e0500edd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/12e8764a9c61dfc8cc8ba2520a2b7cf3e0500edd"}]},{"sha":"12e8764a9c61dfc8cc8ba2520a2b7cf3e0500edd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDEyZTg3NjRhOWM2MWRmYzhjYzhiYTI1MjBhMmI3Y2YzZTA1MDBlZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T16:39:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T16:39:20Z"},"message":"Add saved image path hint to standalone image generation (#25947)\n\n## Why\n\nStandalone image generation returns image bytes to the model, but the\nmodel also needs the host artifact path to reference the generated file\nin follow-up work.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Append the default saved-image path hint alongside the generated image\ntool output.\n- Reuse the existing core image-generation hint text.\n- Pass the thread ID and Codex home directory needed to compute the\nartifact path.\n- Add app-server and extension coverage for the model-visible hint.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nstandalone_image_generation_returns_saved_path_hint_to_model`","tree":{"sha":"23c38cd82374470bd4f3d97115932323f586d4e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/23c38cd82374470bd4f3d97115932323f586d4e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/12e8764a9c61dfc8cc8ba2520a2b7cf3e0500edd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIao4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAP8gQADL9ioAlUXQnBDKPN2C5xYrv\n+TgYPtqa0hWYOERUg8s6xuuX7HEPAPQvNZ2aY0YuP8N8Th17t8pY+qTcvY52pu5R\nF/s6VrI/ArOCrJSwgrIsuSdnK6r/WeH/23JZrckCT3I6FKdQURXa4xoBEYumt8Qd\nCBQwsD4VoPVyXPvuRgVJXt+t5LpteIQ+9r44IAN6F0Qv9Sbuw5elFPN3J5231+LE\nR3/wbRGjHgX3hPPilWcqzJRsZp4gANY6/pCTKt8O8oZLvRB+8cv9Z/5RSWSNHvP8\ndRdv2CUqesURp3hU3iuxGqbJd7cZsQM453JH8cvuBGveRVe+JkDpzdu1YemqM2jh\nkOAQ8sOEQtpaN8skfg/6xnK0Tl3A0SKGyX4fGRiSeVvuiGt68ADMyP0ZrOx+wKPA\nCF4dkdkhbc7kvSuAcwtQ1vWsAEvT3GUNDmD86lAojvDHeEnER51T313ThE7dUGvN\nDryfcTJZUUc61KthHJfaNIXwg97tqS4sNZwU7QtjLGGmGtTdDjheUoAE1a07c3S7\nKP29zd8uW79y+pKIlA1NWDmysi4M2zVdOYnIlmYnzcEIJZxKVAMHDMDxyYLFUW1Z\nlHyCQ43ZDvSHrNta6JEua0stlaUjMtfV2Esx5LgN2+3GaplpcUgHfoYjecEoKXxU\nRnUqBLOVAYoiBDuO8ACc\n=ZyXT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 23c38cd82374470bd4f3d97115932323f586d4e0\nparent 68db0bb5ec67635d3052ddae2ecb35cdea48263e\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1780591160 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780591160 -0700\n\nAdd saved image path hint to standalone image generation (#25947)\n\n## Why\n\nStandalone image generation returns image bytes to the model, but the\nmodel also needs the host artifact path to reference the generated file\nin follow-up work.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Append the default saved-image path hint alongside the generated image\ntool output.\n- Reuse the existing core image-generation hint text.\n- Pass the thread ID and Codex home directory needed to compute the\nartifact path.\n- Add app-server and extension coverage for the model-visible hint.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nstandalone_image_generation_returns_saved_path_hint_to_model`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T16:39:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/12e8764a9c61dfc8cc8ba2520a2b7cf3e0500edd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/12e8764a9c61dfc8cc8ba2520a2b7cf3e0500edd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/12e8764a9c61dfc8cc8ba2520a2b7cf3e0500edd/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"68db0bb5ec67635d3052ddae2ecb35cdea48263e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/68db0bb5ec67635d3052ddae2ecb35cdea48263e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/68db0bb5ec67635d3052ddae2ecb35cdea48263e"}]},{"sha":"68db0bb5ec67635d3052ddae2ecb35cdea48263e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY4ZGIwYmI1ZWM2NzYzNWQzMDUyZGRhZTJlY2IzNWNkZWE0ODI2M2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T16:16:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T16:16:03Z"},"message":"Simplify Codex CLI README (#26313)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe codex-rs README was left over from before we moved the docs into the\ndeveloper site. Its contents were very much out of date, and we received\nsome bug reports about it.","tree":{"sha":"e4f404f0da849a26e58cb1a6b6693350794e7f4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e4f404f0da849a26e58cb1a6b6693350794e7f4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/68db0bb5ec67635d3052ddae2ecb35cdea48263e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIaTDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu4EQABbfmz3TJGCeet6TLqfAjKvY\n14BMCRZ40jgTCKD3V1kf/u2o9o4GjYg3VKe9t5YEdyXhJ+DaKH48u4UlZ8ZoPbdC\nR3S1cdkJcIHIWKSPF+Ee84PkggDfkyEEquRsYV0ouA+XcqEn8OvCJvhEu+hzp/QE\nEVubHYCjA0ic0CCnxQ7wrcsbSloiBGVTVXsMAKZrQNaJTwxP2jfksK/xGYQZ3int\n/Kmq63fAGcuZT6tpc4KNPyN3bBWb4VCCVwg/cnYizND5VRhq7rjP8ZWUyeb2fgNv\nUVMbBtkGpS16Agr7DYdD0vXfkv6WCJmgJxnFrpqcRUlTtTELshjaRNXsqcBUmKzT\nyvRt82aYlxtAzwepZeTRilo5vwr/WahqkHMrX4WSZfsZBgmNOrX3WrkyIEkgu2Jx\nibdvQQVVHcbc/Kpdrts2deZjH1bub/n3oDK1xxRgKDPEV0c0Mgyz7c4Dx05wJCY8\nD1kJRxd/Q/h2x2lypykFH2kQnSuWR2dei6txtTQUsebM0ALBzNQkLKeUQGlEhuTH\nddVvgbThVwP1MXsW14SiOCM8dsVJ6KsFHjRsbllSpYYhj8ZspLZU6NT2aCfHwweD\nrS4s26hHCiOhpZzJsfD3g7T6yaTLI/DyzxQpb3aJHXP2KD5QFVlSjH0ACfLnwWBF\ne2ce/Lg+4oIiVIrVul30\n=w25Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e4f404f0da849a26e58cb1a6b6693350794e7f4b\nparent 4ae7930f58c980c1064f5c2f7a2e38b1058e0410\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780589763 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780589763 -0700\n\nSimplify Codex CLI README (#26313)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe codex-rs README was left over from before we moved the docs into the\ndeveloper site. Its contents were very much out of date, and we received\nsome bug reports about it.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T16:16:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/68db0bb5ec67635d3052ddae2ecb35cdea48263e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/68db0bb5ec67635d3052ddae2ecb35cdea48263e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/68db0bb5ec67635d3052ddae2ecb35cdea48263e/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4ae7930f58c980c1064f5c2f7a2e38b1058e0410","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4ae7930f58c980c1064f5c2f7a2e38b1058e0410","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4ae7930f58c980c1064f5c2f7a2e38b1058e0410"}]},{"sha":"4ae7930f58c980c1064f5c2f7a2e38b1058e0410","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRhZTc5MzBmNThjOTgwYzEwNjRmNWMyZjdhMmUzOGIxMDU4ZTA0MTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Charlie Marsh","email":"charliemarsh@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T15:21:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T15:21:40Z"},"message":"Load plugin hooks without other plugin capabilities (#26272)\n\n## Summary\n\n`hooks/list` only consumes plugin hook declarations, but previously\nloaded every enabled plugin's skills, MCP configuration, apps, and\ncapability summary before discarding them.\n\nIn a local benchmark, this reduced `hooks/list` latency by over 100ms\n(e.g., from 594 to 467ms on startup, and 168 to 16ms when making a\n`hooks/list` call later in the same TUI session). This is on the\ncritical path to rendering the TUI, so every 10s of ms should be eyed\nskeptically (IMO).\n\nThis change adds a hook-specific plugin loading path that preserves\nplugin enablement, remote/local conflict resolution, deterministic\nordering, manifest resolution, and hook-loading warnings while skipping\nunrelated capabilities. (I think there's room for a more general design\nhere that allows you to project the capabilities you need at load-time,\nbut that seems unnecessary right now.)","tree":{"sha":"a808a817fd779703e3c8c236f8d93060c29744c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a808a817fd779703e3c8c236f8d93060c29744c5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4ae7930f58c980c1064f5c2f7a2e38b1058e0410","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIZgECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5LUQAGuD3VKy7qXYVkyG9/8iUPYP\nIwANFWrXHAvjNFoBoPAfGZhxm8jm1lzS2rDKZyfXWKWEUIL2vQ6F6PoCttgTnUeU\nZnGiNlUC79L4E/73pFBJJkomJM4Im0zhp1pamDFRkTuaPXtjz9PHiYUCatUfFAbt\nC6QpyfDskXCf3iKzxSm2WHy78l5d37H/Og3H+fMgA49VHd9oHNRauCcqa8a/0GwD\nVhY01ZYHFw1tXEaNSjWpWfVdT2KVW5/Yo9KGEoHS/irhF3DLgwgwMtE0DfRWGMqB\nnaOGjPIKBGhsiBrqnmEF8DkgurY5/K4f8kKxcgjPlrrTR9QcZ9vICz/XLJZxFWZe\nhIExLal/jRWjWszjPSDmGBcQkyoMStYTGMkpmzr5ThOtYt0PiGvkFlGqob+A2sFM\nj7ch/IgbcpbNefFHjD6qWwb90wu44CdmT12uuxhGisKNsqvEwzBAacGUcXBYKHAh\nIcOsfJ+tNIJkWjlwu02/4BaF1GiJgvo6avk4eMb8jmwM4SPnkuoFOUhjqidX+KVD\n/4ijOLkqm5RkOodSAgI6NlWWLB2PMwoszpyAJTjNoZhU/bH+9V4yJLeV1v3WMQD6\ntRwbmL7wdKEIU6A+Yfio8EEE+5MG1BWR+Uoi7viYBtg5AD2aXoenGY4FpQKADESp\nOVlQGV5bRIk89TesjoH7\n=xlV8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a808a817fd779703e3c8c236f8d93060c29744c5\nparent d81fcdf8ef3f2857db1a51b83a012638a7ecf0fb\nauthor Charlie Marsh <charliemarsh@openai.com> 1780586500 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780586500 -0400\n\nLoad plugin hooks without other plugin capabilities (#26272)\n\n## Summary\n\n`hooks/list` only consumes plugin hook declarations, but previously\nloaded every enabled plugin's skills, MCP configuration, apps, and\ncapability summary before discarding them.\n\nIn a local benchmark, this reduced `hooks/list` latency by over 100ms\n(e.g., from 594 to 467ms on startup, and 168 to 16ms when making a\n`hooks/list` call later in the same TUI session). This is on the\ncritical path to rendering the TUI, so every 10s of ms should be eyed\nskeptically (IMO).\n\nThis change adds a hook-specific plugin loading path that preserves\nplugin enablement, remote/local conflict resolution, deterministic\nordering, manifest resolution, and hook-loading warnings while skipping\nunrelated capabilities. (I think there's room for a more general design\nhere that allows you to project the capabilities you need at load-time,\nbut that seems unnecessary right now.)","verified_at":"2026-06-04T15:21:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4ae7930f58c980c1064f5c2f7a2e38b1058e0410","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4ae7930f58c980c1064f5c2f7a2e38b1058e0410","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4ae7930f58c980c1064f5c2f7a2e38b1058e0410/comments","author":{"login":"charliemarsh-oai","id":282065134,"node_id":"U_kgDOEM_47g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282065134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/charliemarsh-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d81fcdf8ef3f2857db1a51b83a012638a7ecf0fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d81fcdf8ef3f2857db1a51b83a012638a7ecf0fb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d81fcdf8ef3f2857db1a51b83a012638a7ecf0fb"}]},{"sha":"d81fcdf8ef3f2857db1a51b83a012638a7ecf0fb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ4MWZjZGY4ZWYzZjI4NTdkYjFhNTFiODNhMDEyNjM4YTdlY2YwZmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Zanie Blue","email":"zanie@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T15:12:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T15:12:08Z"},"message":"Reduce SQLite contention from OpenTelemetry SDK debug logs (#26396)\n\n## Summary\n\n- skip `opentelemetry_sdk` DEBUG and TRACE events before formatting or\nqueueing them for the SQLite log sink\n- preserve INFO, WARN, and ERROR events from the SDK, along with TRACE\nevents from application targets\n- add a persistence-level regression test for the target and level\npolicy\n\n## Why\n\nOpenTelemetry's batch log processor emits internal\n`BatchLogProcessor.ExportingDueToTimer` meta-events every second per\nCodex process. In measured high-fanout `logs_2.sqlite` databases,\nlow-level `opentelemetry_sdk` events accounted for over 30% of retained\nrows (30-60% on the machines of people I asked to check).\n\nPersisting this SDK bookkeeping across many processes adds substantial\nwrite volume and contention without representing application activity.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-state` (132/132 tests passed, plus bench smoke)\n- `just fix -p codex-state`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"5bf94924bf16cba015fdc8c5a38abc7c834a7c4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5bf94924bf16cba015fdc8c5a38abc7c834a7c4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d81fcdf8ef3f2857db1a51b83a012638a7ecf0fb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIZXICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmYgQAARE+gFaABefGYzNl1dq1AYh\n8+r60BECcNOnImamqUcdAlbuKFxwHge4Wq2V7vQA5cf1xT9mwRb80hK8GNQ1P0n5\nCsHGkPBxIHgfWeWVhj72BFdX0SiaKE7tOplxdgAFcWC3PGizMSGtbG/kNPZohaRZ\njO6r3W5MLDL4P4Kf67m3/dC7LVEVGpcUHY7vaScHs5uT4F+H3WoY7csK32wa23xG\nwpkZN6Er/GZqvAC55pZSdM0AR7tJmbpfJ1S7ijkJsH/cKT0jqqVAEeysf3Wtajm1\nyckj+LLkWxvhPdOmdu908AVDonjO3z4N9x1mkZZG9Kgp6YExZcDs27V/26+LPH0w\nA35MDFbYQ/nbKAtZBkf5Yy0J55+uR/HaavtngaYPw0FuVZdts0fXSnljL4pEv6yh\n9igqoq2GEP/Q95UUG11PvwgFXD+x6cjntUU2AACg6y0NguB87oLM9MHarL9Go8PY\nu1ScyWO2qviCaQLaidXfRW8h2vXME5Him2OdkM3s8cVOWPSvbjIwsOoZcyB+kKXW\nfRBHM0oQqs1v5PHfPmStPue1PdtwWUyF6s5Uwn/Ku3ZPcli2wLQBpTzXhNMiFTPm\n+u3Feb4dGFjL54C+BtXZxsJMUsl3z05BcN7KIi0APPedLXg1t+pFTNQznH+0bP6z\n3HQx+37EMTsmTEPIkbpn\n=sVfJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5bf94924bf16cba015fdc8c5a38abc7c834a7c4a\nparent 7da4af622ffc68d7b687e61ba8f19163af50fab8\nauthor Zanie Blue <zanie@openai.com> 1780585928 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780585928 -0500\n\nReduce SQLite contention from OpenTelemetry SDK debug logs (#26396)\n\n## Summary\n\n- skip `opentelemetry_sdk` DEBUG and TRACE events before formatting or\nqueueing them for the SQLite log sink\n- preserve INFO, WARN, and ERROR events from the SDK, along with TRACE\nevents from application targets\n- add a persistence-level regression test for the target and level\npolicy\n\n## Why\n\nOpenTelemetry's batch log processor emits internal\n`BatchLogProcessor.ExportingDueToTimer` meta-events every second per\nCodex process. In measured high-fanout `logs_2.sqlite` databases,\nlow-level `opentelemetry_sdk` events accounted for over 30% of retained\nrows (30-60% on the machines of people I asked to check).\n\nPersisting this SDK bookkeeping across many processes adds substantial\nwrite volume and contention without representing application activity.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-state` (132/132 tests passed, plus bench smoke)\n- `just fix -p codex-state`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T15:12:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d81fcdf8ef3f2857db1a51b83a012638a7ecf0fb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d81fcdf8ef3f2857db1a51b83a012638a7ecf0fb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d81fcdf8ef3f2857db1a51b83a012638a7ecf0fb/comments","author":{"login":"zanie-oai","id":282067757,"node_id":"U_kgDOENADLQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282067757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/zanie-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zanie-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7da4af622ffc68d7b687e61ba8f19163af50fab8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7da4af622ffc68d7b687e61ba8f19163af50fab8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7da4af622ffc68d7b687e61ba8f19163af50fab8"}]},{"sha":"7da4af622ffc68d7b687e61ba8f19163af50fab8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdkYTRhZjYyMmZmYzY4ZDdiNjg3ZTYxYmE4ZjE5MTYzYWY1MGZhYjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Charlie Marsh","email":"charliemarsh@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T13:53:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T13:53:08Z"},"message":"Optimize unbounded byte scans with memchr (#26265)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR adds `memchr` for some low-hanging performance improvements\n(namely, in MCP stdio, Ollama streaming, and full message-history\nnewline counts).\n\nCodex produced the following release benchmarks:\n\n| Operation | Before | After | Speedup |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| MCP 1 MiB chunked line | 2.172 s | 3.984 ms | 545x |\n| Ollama 1 MiB chunked line | 1.673 s | 2.790 ms | 600x |\n| Count newlines in 10 MiB history | 132.83 ms | 20.05 ms | 6.6x |\n\nWith a \"real\" MCP setup (`ExecutorStdioServerLauncher` started a Python\nMCP server, completed `initialize`, requested `tools/list`, and\ndeserialized a 1 MiB tool description over newline-delimited stdio),\nit's about 16x faster end-to-end:\n\n| Branch | 50 calls | Per call |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `main` | 862.53 ms | 17.25 ms |\n| this branch | 53.89 ms | 1.08 ms |\n\n`memchr` is already in our dependency tree and extremely widely used for\nthis kind of optimized scanning.","tree":{"sha":"475a2a7e2b52ac362ebf742af6a3bdb7443f927e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/475a2a7e2b52ac362ebf742af6a3bdb7443f927e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7da4af622ffc68d7b687e61ba8f19163af50fab8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIYNECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGQgQAB0+lj27zDVKJk0PrvxuRpUp\n58W5xkSn9cKzvNxaKRpkWleJCj5N5ZSHaHRB9ejIWlPT7ldOYUri3k9Dff2/sgqs\nYjDsyCwHVgJ3NDhEdTUT7DpO4MYL/yNl+FSbKQR74MpHoFi290UVDS7pUXePROIg\nAlHkQaJKn86xs+aM5wwp9IoAL2etIX6FFa4CSrzDLkGFahL/qa0mw4K1ApeKq2lo\nTkTX0BcbskSrjTwh60CIcKHPILxDG6WCXahBGUVtVFRRyEuJUFPjf+kcSBZ8R0KJ\nWV6E+r6vCIIvPwiHKAClwRqSLiCGjfQHu5dR4R6Hm62B+4LZRm1hFfhrn823Lp6F\nZ777KTzlDroR83ilOfRDaGzmsRssi4VtFM1edDVb3Q4gS+GIUsjGBzVK0vjN/45V\n+pAQMXGtmNujuLK5VLIBKJ1KbaZeVcu2qA8KrogldTflqnCYLucjghjR+lMVp+qx\n3afXcbVcTpjsZMw08rfpReTAnLaDLnZhXvAoNBZsEt7ew9aUMvc0dkbjL9OUgYLO\njwxtLydxXWuPi+k5WmX5o48jn5Bv+uqqNukpHiEwOey/3odSBcigCYdyrAwsqC5O\ngEywU+BQAZ8zj/nyYTVsI16jiXuBiHRkdBUomaGifpA/y7RVFaiTiUdFJFlDfSee\nob5fhGc77NTCthzBIKqK\n=JsNz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 475a2a7e2b52ac362ebf742af6a3bdb7443f927e\nparent d46a98d31a9c32949580e6e3ce65b85772f3470d\nauthor Charlie Marsh <charliemarsh@openai.com> 1780581188 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780581188 -0400\n\nOptimize unbounded byte scans with memchr (#26265)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR adds `memchr` for some low-hanging performance improvements\n(namely, in MCP stdio, Ollama streaming, and full message-history\nnewline counts).\n\nCodex produced the following release benchmarks:\n\n| Operation | Before | After | Speedup |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| MCP 1 MiB chunked line | 2.172 s | 3.984 ms | 545x |\n| Ollama 1 MiB chunked line | 1.673 s | 2.790 ms | 600x |\n| Count newlines in 10 MiB history | 132.83 ms | 20.05 ms | 6.6x |\n\nWith a \"real\" MCP setup (`ExecutorStdioServerLauncher` started a Python\nMCP server, completed `initialize`, requested `tools/list`, and\ndeserialized a 1 MiB tool description over newline-delimited stdio),\nit's about 16x faster end-to-end:\n\n| Branch | 50 calls | Per call |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `main` | 862.53 ms | 17.25 ms |\n| this branch | 53.89 ms | 1.08 ms |\n\n`memchr` is already in our dependency tree and extremely widely used for\nthis kind of optimized scanning.","verified_at":"2026-06-04T13:53:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7da4af622ffc68d7b687e61ba8f19163af50fab8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7da4af622ffc68d7b687e61ba8f19163af50fab8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7da4af622ffc68d7b687e61ba8f19163af50fab8/comments","author":{"login":"charliemarsh-oai","id":282065134,"node_id":"U_kgDOEM_47g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282065134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/charliemarsh-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d46a98d31a9c32949580e6e3ce65b85772f3470d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d46a98d31a9c32949580e6e3ce65b85772f3470d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d46a98d31a9c32949580e6e3ce65b85772f3470d"}]},{"sha":"d46a98d31a9c32949580e6e3ce65b85772f3470d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ0NmE5OGQzMWE5YzMyOTQ5NTgwZTZlM2NlNjViODU3NzJmMzQ3MGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T13:28:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T13:28:06Z"},"message":"Bridge host-loaded skills into the skills extension (#26172)\n\n## Why\n\nThe skills extension needs to become the path that exposes local host\nskills without losing the behavior already owned by core skill loading.\nHost skill discovery is not just `$CODEX_HOME/skills`: it also includes\nconfig layers, bundled-skill settings, plugin roots, runtime extra\nroots, and the filesystem for the selected primary environment.\n\nRather than making the extension reload host skills and risk drifting\nfrom that authoritative load, this PR bridges the already-loaded\nper-turn skills outcome into the extension. That lets the extension\nadvertise host skills and inject explicit `$skill` prompts while\npreserving the same roots, disabled/hidden state, rendered paths, and\nenvironment-backed file reads that the legacy path uses.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds `HostLoadedSkills` in `core-skills` to wrap the turn's\n`SkillLoadOutcome` and read `SKILL.md` through the filesystem that\nloaded that skill.\n- Stores `HostLoadedSkills` in turn extension data for normal turns and\nreview turns, so the skills extension can consume the loaded host\ncatalog without reloading it.\n- Adds `HostSkillProvider` under `ext/skills/src/provider/host.rs`,\nmapping host-loaded skill metadata into the skills-extension\ncatalog/read contract.\n- Registers the host provider by default from\n`codex_skills_extension::install()`.\n- Preserves host skill metadata such as dependencies, disabled state,\nhidden-from-prompt policy, and slash-normalized display paths.\n- Passes host-loaded skills through `SkillListQuery` and\n`SkillReadRequest` so explicit skill invocation reads only resources\nfrom the loaded host catalog.\n- Adds integration coverage for a real legacy\n`$CODEX_HOME/skills/.../SKILL.md` skill being listed and injected\nthrough the installed extension.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added `installed_extension_loads_host_skills_from_legacy_roots` in\n`ext/skills/tests/skills_extension.rs`.\n- `just test -p codex-skills-extension`","tree":{"sha":"423c41a8da0d135258d71b4243a4b4dc300afc0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/423c41a8da0d135258d71b4243a4b4dc300afc0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d46a98d31a9c32949580e6e3ce65b85772f3470d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIX1mCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8OMQAI2UJ84etYZqqdfocttxPwYM\nM9njwADmwxHQXWlx0wJ4SGp4EpMLtja1F4OUtPmExUep6490pqZa+OljedESn6ba\np2wmBGMyHeb0hqIaRYA8dsOXqyhOBRXT3ZdeFyy+dqw5u4LNeDqeDWcgTmMxBl+t\nC+emqwvdUO6v8JvCyUnOJf+SwTPHqEV0oTYmlqnvBFlkPnIDRv5g8kCYtj+lDTz7\nbmDHbV44OZAfPvwRiRFMWrQa2lYeeLVYXkMiFk6m86MWvbUaPc/pC2p45Y7gwOnC\nfwwf6GtI6Q5Sl7d5WTj+1HMfVJ9KQzMNX3PA2bAlzv7YLUmTB7pdm7+u993Rlclj\n7v4gjlmWp2RyVDCmbmr8uY3qIURBONIZFFmbaz3PrVIiTzLtiOk9S2sv5zb4O5Y7\nXeJA7F2rSixwYTH0CvJzdEW9NgnfKYNia7e9XK3HQTnCPwx+/Ete+lhDYXmTRAcb\n7HokkoGwlFbwJ1m7iiRxcD13ivX8i7jSaukm1Haql5zjgw+8usGLCUYoQtVfQ6eA\nSuFDIuNHD2GCqIkrCmKRzqrrPUsxEAKtUPjApgMwltT2TPK3DEbRDBY9gnZ42WmY\n38j3vuIJB3UqCU8E8BoET/LfbIoCTD2YAxRtBuOaFu+JMORzE5H49Qptya2sGeAL\ne+m7g0L6aYU9Xb73uUfi\n=vY9s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 423c41a8da0d135258d71b4243a4b4dc300afc0a\nparent d297616d3e6a27865fb327e7b4ea3d548f7fdb45\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780579686 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780579686 +0200\n\nBridge host-loaded skills into the skills extension (#26172)\n\n## Why\n\nThe skills extension needs to become the path that exposes local host\nskills without losing the behavior already owned by core skill loading.\nHost skill discovery is not just `$CODEX_HOME/skills`: it also includes\nconfig layers, bundled-skill settings, plugin roots, runtime extra\nroots, and the filesystem for the selected primary environment.\n\nRather than making the extension reload host skills and risk drifting\nfrom that authoritative load, this PR bridges the already-loaded\nper-turn skills outcome into the extension. That lets the extension\nadvertise host skills and inject explicit `$skill` prompts while\npreserving the same roots, disabled/hidden state, rendered paths, and\nenvironment-backed file reads that the legacy path uses.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds `HostLoadedSkills` in `core-skills` to wrap the turn's\n`SkillLoadOutcome` and read `SKILL.md` through the filesystem that\nloaded that skill.\n- Stores `HostLoadedSkills` in turn extension data for normal turns and\nreview turns, so the skills extension can consume the loaded host\ncatalog without reloading it.\n- Adds `HostSkillProvider` under `ext/skills/src/provider/host.rs`,\nmapping host-loaded skill metadata into the skills-extension\ncatalog/read contract.\n- Registers the host provider by default from\n`codex_skills_extension::install()`.\n- Preserves host skill metadata such as dependencies, disabled state,\nhidden-from-prompt policy, and slash-normalized display paths.\n- Passes host-loaded skills through `SkillListQuery` and\n`SkillReadRequest` so explicit skill invocation reads only resources\nfrom the loaded host catalog.\n- Adds integration coverage for a real legacy\n`$CODEX_HOME/skills/.../SKILL.md` skill being listed and injected\nthrough the installed extension.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Added `installed_extension_loads_host_skills_from_legacy_roots` in\n`ext/skills/tests/skills_extension.rs`.\n- `just test -p codex-skills-extension`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T13:28:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d46a98d31a9c32949580e6e3ce65b85772f3470d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d46a98d31a9c32949580e6e3ce65b85772f3470d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d46a98d31a9c32949580e6e3ce65b85772f3470d/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d297616d3e6a27865fb327e7b4ea3d548f7fdb45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d297616d3e6a27865fb327e7b4ea3d548f7fdb45","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d297616d3e6a27865fb327e7b4ea3d548f7fdb45"}]},{"sha":"d297616d3e6a27865fb327e7b4ea3d548f7fdb45","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQyOTc2MTZkM2U2YTI3ODY1ZmIzMjdlN2I0ZWEzZDU0OGY3ZmRiNDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T12:44:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T12:44:45Z"},"message":"Gate automatic idle turns in Plan mode (#26147)\n\n## Why\n\nGoal idle continuation is extension-triggered model-visible work, so it\nshould follow one core-owned rule for when automatic work may start. In\nparticular, it should not jump ahead of queued user/client work, start\nwhile another task is active, or inject a continuation turn while the\nthread is in Plan mode.\n\nKeeping this policy in `try_start_turn_if_idle` avoids passing\n`collaboration_mode` or review-specific state through\n`ThreadLifecycleContributor::on_thread_idle`. Active `/review` is\ncovered by the same active-task gate because Review turns are not\nsteerable.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Teach `Session::try_start_turn_if_idle` to reject automatic idle turns\nin Plan mode, both before reserving an idle turn and after building the\nturn context.\n- Document `CodexThread::try_start_turn_if_idle` as the extension-facing\ngate for automatic idle work, including Plan-mode and active Review-task\nbehavior.\n- Add focused coverage for Plan-mode rejection and active Review-task\nrejection without queuing synthetic input.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core try_start_turn_if_idle`","tree":{"sha":"9067eff35abc997ae121d8885c2cf842280615fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9067eff35abc997ae121d8885c2cf842280615fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d297616d3e6a27865fb327e7b4ea3d548f7fdb45","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIXM9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAARs4QACnfpGVhQsKiJxX2kyz0Zi1j\nPEjS8e5GZk6Ze2Cb4YBfCyP6wGAJeWBQMixDLQ40X6gxz2HQ5sjfbykFHWoYlkuK\n8r87MY4wEqwCbGSMN/acc7wrOlbtmlL35apFF9y+zN1WjVPihptpfjRkf2bdNZTz\nsS5WJA3B7+M8zEafm2k31Vj4IA//Zhu5gEAt5W3mzlFC5J0XxS2JV5HaskoIcFpl\nfkNKn+hQJY0ApwNNITzrfV2gNSxIhMlwZ3n++EIKdrGCnum8zuzIYoDRMQguofJL\nLdQnfpfrnxjv2aY/4TS7LrhiYXtGuBC41fXejuROwRXGQA6prWxzF/0jsv1b1FcH\nWChbXZCkqMBfIkYo+RtI01beWXyM1RRHfAvNPEib9lMwqyImppn4ppmQtWIJhe+R\nIwkBGGuufYtekyo+/8bGEyvcGg2tdqWjSfs6iEkgHkzGqH+Hdljh7QIsl3p+zmCN\ncZNp1EcdFENRWsfEadJjWt07LyGdclyq5dsQ2BlBBnccmPADcrpITsNwrbQYVm98\ny58fIBxlcaMvTH+2YW463+iZfohbXP5Kv896CFNNtjTq+SImC+dT6BlnsAiiNANj\nKTnjXnqp32GtbSQeRWyGYic9I2vIEwIDzOPjlfKN+yqOjulpJOTSwS33G4tw2nHt\nJ0Hja1jgA2iGgcMri1/n\n=ENZF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9067eff35abc997ae121d8885c2cf842280615fc\nparent 16d02ec77c6337ccea02a8c909e05bf3d905f887\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780577085 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780577085 +0200\n\nGate automatic idle turns in Plan mode (#26147)\n\n## Why\n\nGoal idle continuation is extension-triggered model-visible work, so it\nshould follow one core-owned rule for when automatic work may start. In\nparticular, it should not jump ahead of queued user/client work, start\nwhile another task is active, or inject a continuation turn while the\nthread is in Plan mode.\n\nKeeping this policy in `try_start_turn_if_idle` avoids passing\n`collaboration_mode` or review-specific state through\n`ThreadLifecycleContributor::on_thread_idle`. Active `/review` is\ncovered by the same active-task gate because Review turns are not\nsteerable.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Teach `Session::try_start_turn_if_idle` to reject automatic idle turns\nin Plan mode, both before reserving an idle turn and after building the\nturn context.\n- Document `CodexThread::try_start_turn_if_idle` as the extension-facing\ngate for automatic idle work, including Plan-mode and active Review-task\nbehavior.\n- Add focused coverage for Plan-mode rejection and active Review-task\nrejection without queuing synthetic input.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core try_start_turn_if_idle`","verified_at":"2026-06-04T12:44:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d297616d3e6a27865fb327e7b4ea3d548f7fdb45","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d297616d3e6a27865fb327e7b4ea3d548f7fdb45","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d297616d3e6a27865fb327e7b4ea3d548f7fdb45/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"16d02ec77c6337ccea02a8c909e05bf3d905f887","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/16d02ec77c6337ccea02a8c909e05bf3d905f887","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/16d02ec77c6337ccea02a8c909e05bf3d905f887"}]},{"sha":"16d02ec77c6337ccea02a8c909e05bf3d905f887","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE2ZDAyZWM3N2M2MzM3Y2NlYTAyYThjOTA5ZTA1YmYzZDkwNWY4ODc","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-04T10:46:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-04T10:46:02Z"},"message":"chore: calm down (#26367)\n\nPrompt update to address feedback","tree":{"sha":"7ef7de17efe039a4712239770da875004ad7fc6d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7ef7de17efe039a4712239770da875004ad7fc6d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/16d02ec77c6337ccea02a8c909e05bf3d905f887","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIVdqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhbQQACV+L2nZCUYmL57Gif0LAfvk\n6AzBOSv2/U2ysIUUaBdPOsttk1DcT39wj7ACYlIZXnqq5uu5BvN26EqdsXGiZWW/\n9MgRNs80iTFC3EdZfxWbri0Swf+PEVBk717ANWltLf3gag4l6Efng1CpzG6rlrQR\nDmEbdNKxeIG+knB4TPsPC8Orp03rpSfvMq+H7daVXNgHWV/DThAaPTrNtmZLLE5F\nlhEKjRFSITvHTGPeCdxPUNVP6ZsHpyBAOqwlWxT9dCgWnTCbaC8MXmuKuzh8Lvgs\nHEvE6SHTvNcGY90KPhWtFSGc0AESuhHAMPGfmVdyoM+0Jeq+K54MK7I38amScbXY\nErn9UDE3ZsEwXgJZiV/Avr7+BRGLRqBNWhw9VF9pcMzUSD7QldxNyWgUn0A