 -p codex-analytics`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nexplicit_plugin_mentions_track_plugin_used_analytics`\n- `just fix -p codex-analytics`","verified_at":"2026-06-03T23:06:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4d4837c4951375c877986e239304c95ebbe14633","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4d4837c4951375c877986e239304c95ebbe14633","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4d4837c4951375c877986e239304c95ebbe14633/comments","author":{"login":"chrisdong-oai","id":256211597,"node_id":"U_kgDOD0V6jQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256211597?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisdong-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0ed2735d195d149766b242d972f95f3173ebc984","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0ed2735d195d149766b242d972f95f3173ebc984","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0ed2735d195d149766b242d972f95f3173ebc984"}]},{"sha":"0ed2735d195d149766b242d972f95f3173ebc984","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBlZDI3MzVkMTk1ZDE0OTc2NmIyNDJkOTcyZjk1ZjMxNzNlYmM5ODQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Abhinav","email":"abhinav@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T22:33:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T22:33:34Z"},"message":"Use Windows setup marker as completion signal (#26074)\n\n# Why\n\nWhen an organization requires the elevated Windows sandbox, Codex\nlaunches an elevated helper to provision users, configure firewall and\nACL rules, and lock persistent sandbox directories.\n\nWe observed that closing the helper after setup started could leave the\nmachine partially initialized while the TUI still announced **Sandbox\nready**. Model-only turns continued to work, but the first shell command\nretried setup and failed with Windows cancellation error `1223`.\n\nThis was not an enforcement bypass; command execution continued to fail\nclosed. The issue was a false readiness signal: `setup_marker.json` was\nwritten during user provisioning, before the remaining setup stages had\ncompleted.\n\n# What\n\nTreat `setup_marker.json` as the commit record for Windows sandbox\nsetup:\n\n1. Before full or provisioning setup begins, remove the existing marker\nand create the final marker path with a protected ACL.\n2. Keep the marker empty and therefore invalid while setup is in\nprogress. Sandbox users cannot read, modify, or replace it.\n3. Run every synchronous setup stage.\n4. After setup succeeds, write the valid marker contents without\nchanging its ACL.\n5. After the helper exits successfully, verify the existing readiness\ncheck before enabling the sandbox.\n\nIf setup is canceled or fails, the marker remains invalid and Codex\nreports setup as incomplete instead of announcing readiness.\n\nRefresh-only and read-ACL-only helper runs continue to leave the marker\nuntouched. The setup version remains `5` to avoid forcing all existing\nWindows users through elevated setup again.\n\n# Verification\n\n- Added coverage confirming sandbox users cannot read or modify the\nsetup marker after elevated setup.\n- Added coverage confirming a successful helper exit without complete\nsetup artifacts is rejected.\n- Ran `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox`.","tree":{"sha":"7412365e0035b4fb366bdbde02d35bd47918e668","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7412365e0035b4fb366bdbde02d35bd47918e668"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0ed2735d195d149766b242d972f95f3173ebc984","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIKu+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJDIQABBba1GlxJc0Bjyx4j7q/Vnc\nzH+9eY1qBjFxQUHESlqWalS+DviyH4y8oQWcBT8MWg2xqk9PkZhgghE/rNB2uxFd\nU/qKQT8a70Co3z4fHTP5OonDIowAuUF0HGCig7YG/5+nXOTXgtjZgfJlhOV7jPV0\ngTiGuhWIFPkTctwzXwGIijgB6A1Tqs8i4i3+Tf2aCn7poIk1CD5EjEimPiwOenPQ\noaxUnbx5iS9+7cE1Ntjhq+F4d5LJ9RdLkcUS7kbTIFQUwq/W6L5i3KIVaZh8XnQ1\nPCFeprCx8iEPrNXtntEza/V0dyamv5oa9HY1Tq2NXgZaM3Li2zqXJQ6MEwglVyVd\n0bWpXEKi7Qbn3QPuKKj6bi6tFn5IRmAHGSUC3uNX7mT9QceHhWIoYMFhV6yMJzFb\nwaT3Pe/9pLSvjOKWletaHTMCYpy8dfpBlVJhSyww7H6MraBRRf44mV4opW4/Cjdv\nXzcn7wprrf/2l3gfyRtMrh/VSMWCBZZ08QwQsQeQpPnZBFuZM4JPdotJzAvwn/kp\nOKirBai78H6/GzATyVQecHJDSVvnd6JjhWgYfWLItsSxFs1QveMk1bGW3Hl12mZE\nFdgA2AfaN0BDm1Ht8dggVjaRBjZ8xn7Ju7kAzEuNkN7LTwT3QkRnd7JEF9heSsEz\nXSyVyvjScRr1g9Ea0ujG\n=Pgyv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7412365e0035b4fb366bdbde02d35bd47918e668\nparent 14272b21e95ed9a54fae21c27d33d3771a9ee30f\nauthor Abhinav <abhinav@openai.com> 1780526014 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780526014 -0700\n\nUse Windows setup marker as completion signal (#26074)\n\n# Why\n\nWhen an organization requires the elevated Windows sandbox, Codex\nlaunches an elevated helper to provision users, configure firewall and\nACL rules, and lock persistent sandbox directories.\n\nWe observed that closing the helper after setup started could leave the\nmachine partially initialized while the TUI still announced **Sandbox\nready**. Model-only turns continued to work, but the first shell command\nretried setup and failed with Windows cancellation error `1223`.\n\nThis was not an enforcement bypass; command execution continued to fail\nclosed. The issue was a false readiness signal: `setup_marker.json` was\nwritten during user provisioning, before the remaining setup stages had\ncompleted.\n\n# What\n\nTreat `setup_marker.json` as the commit record for Windows sandbox\nsetup:\n\n1. Before full or provisioning setup begins, remove the existing marker\nand create the final marker path with a protected ACL.\n2. Keep the marker empty and therefore invalid while setup is in\nprogress. Sandbox users cannot read, modify, or replace it.\n3. Run every synchronous setup stage.\n4. After setup succeeds, write the valid marker contents without\nchanging its ACL.\n5. After the helper exits successfully, verify the existing readiness\ncheck before enabling the sandbox.\n\nIf setup is canceled or fails, the marker remains invalid and Codex\nreports setup as incomplete instead of announcing readiness.\n\nRefresh-only and read-ACL-only helper runs continue to leave the marker\nuntouched. The setup version remains `5` to avoid forcing all existing\nWindows users through elevated setup again.\n\n# Verification\n\n- Added coverage confirming sandbox users cannot read or modify the\nsetup marker after elevated setup.\n- Added coverage confirming a successful helper exit without complete\nsetup artifacts is rejected.\n- Ran `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox`.","verified_at":"2026-06-03T22:33:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0ed2735d195d149766b242d972f95f3173ebc984","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0ed2735d195d149766b242d972f95f3173ebc984","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0ed2735d195d149766b242d972f95f3173ebc984/comments","author":{"login":"abhinav-oai","id":274334565,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFoDZQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274334565?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/abhinav-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abhinav-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"14272b21e95ed9a54fae21c27d33d3771a9ee30f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/14272b21e95ed9a54fae21c27d33d3771a9ee30f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/14272b21e95ed9a54fae21c27d33d3771a9ee30f"}]},{"sha":"14272b21e95ed9a54fae21c27d33d3771a9ee30f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE0MjcyYjIxZTk1ZWQ5YTU0ZmFlMjFjMjdkMzNkMzc3MWE5ZWUzMGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T22:29:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T22:29:57Z"},"message":"codex-pr-body: avoid confidential references (#26260)\n\n## Why\n\nPR descriptions can be visible outside the context used to generate\nthem. In #23710, a generated description referenced an internal\ndocument, showing that the skill needs an explicit guardrail against\nexposing confidential context.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Updated the `codex-pr-body` guidance to prohibit confidential\nreferences, including codenames and OpenAI-internal URLs.","tree":{"sha":"a0c1f487c14749f131b6fff929b02c2b11ff2b47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a0c1f487c14749f131b6fff929b02c2b11ff2b47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/14272b21e95ed9a54fae21c27d33d3771a9ee30f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIKrlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUPMQAH3tKFDxmfNvqmxYb2kf7CHB\nlUJT0KhME/vtVB1iNpRNkOAET+2Cs9KxeyLGLkuOF63HJRSDboHeMD8ZfzgvPOW1\njUVnB35X9wV15RcwXeyNcPZoq8AMyP0zBw3ojuCR53/rWDnV/zc4Mvx69aHCsx67\naxYtPwsVSZOoSaJP2A/uBgPs/+NNH4S+zBvWMo9Tv881LaMj7DRrX0XFxuHVabh8\nE2h5uRJHIXQ4sQNtLpzk3nWI51C0cttfoP/e20KA5tLcJD7MnlCRIOSF4xZEMgOQ\nBvGJkB28ZLPHQeWZFaUmd7HR5uDslQo/+wH/JlnPmPPdcmwktXpibs1DoZWJ6lKa\nD3lTyWVnDz1p9zw0u6yPZyIlRUFugI7YW9kU/pMjO1rognbxjChzsVMKwi+PQqur\nSmbwL2Oz33dn5ODCqXgFzdllX/G3KzfN5Id3Hbhk+Xnc5JvRPUcxtJ46stp6qIUM\nTYxFLxivyWvqEmIqSemKLHwLSymf/kYsG5IEbAtIL/Blab41R6p1MHdyGffKcgOh\nRSCYjeh8Xc2cEXFNklbwss/7eCuYYGjCsfJoUSsLbPt+MEkas8eZZQeHrso5cFxQ\nZ31EVqfpg7BRa20wPP3tvM3qWEPmgFOMma6r2VwVo5txqGrnfmYlOUN66GK8aIAh\n5MPjO68idBGLxTbhkMuI\n=46/7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a0c1f487c14749f131b6fff929b02c2b11ff2b47\nparent 4231472c03e6c6e3374b1c19ef096ee28476f9dd\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780525797 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780525797 -0700\n\ncodex-pr-body: avoid confidential references (#26260)\n\n## Why\n\nPR descriptions can be visible outside the context used to generate\nthem. In #23710, a generated description referenced an internal\ndocument, showing that the skill needs an explicit guardrail against\nexposing confidential context.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Updated the `codex-pr-body` guidance to prohibit confidential\nreferences, including codenames and OpenAI-internal URLs.","verified_at":"2026-06-03T22:29:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/14272b21e95ed9a54fae21c27d33d3771a9ee30f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/14272b21e95ed9a54fae21c27d33d3771a9ee30f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/14272b21e95ed9a54fae21c27d33d3771a9ee30f/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4231472c03e6c6e3374b1c19ef096ee28476f9dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4231472c03e6c6e3374b1c19ef096ee28476f9dd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4231472c03e6c6e3374b1c19ef096ee28476f9dd"}]},{"sha":"4231472c03e6c6e3374b1c19ef096ee28476f9dd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQyMzE0NzJjMDNlNmM2ZTMzNzRiMWMxOWVmMDk2ZWUyODQ3NmY5ZGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T22:25:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T22:25:50Z"},"message":"Rewrite oversized tool outputs during remote compaction (#26251)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen trying to fit history under compaction limit rewrite output items\ninstead of removing them entirely. Otherwise we're breaking\nincrementality in relation to the previous response.","tree":{"sha":"c11231d04e762df91b3a61b619274496db2df726","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c11231d04e762df91b3a61b619274496db2df726"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4231472c03e6c6e3374b1c19ef096ee28476f9dd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIKnuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC7AQAJ2Ff8qvmkWVel1cG4VtOMeW\nX4qIQUjP+raeOYv7iTdv2owBcjszv9mfAvc9fAh1vK48Q46OJCyT8mv+SMnKtDnB\nK9NOLUwA6/jNfcdDye8gxcW3J8x8KTVvXDtdZhm+hl/MOUgEilPTAkQ9YGI1DI+J\n19RMN3HUpMcJ2iWbdI3kHq7QJBmGdvJmI6t4ccQJ5UxQC+KMFgX2/Hu/uQCPA1tX\n28Yl+M2ASXpCb/qrnvNhdUM5M0u0x92hrJY/2R+6W+QcKNgvi/lgFeGM4M/frI28\ncqVuJDz0bWnmqVe9W37+Ywx9Fi3CjiGjfQVO3b/YHFcEpwE4Np4PX/BNsexCsepQ\nwtVTBas3kcdn4ZoydU7bKGY44FJbD+luR78uf5AalvGwG50sB+HltTrNmQM87xzS\ng0t2ie8r57pJoDrPnTFdFtfC9JH7rEKnRwLgzaT4JPawHv7lxzRha/nYdZxYTMO1\nM5W3XihKT0VPLE2j/vObRukqtfrqqIw2X5/pRrpcVpF1xYLiLHZjMNtKIJTr2HYb\n07Ldcw+o+YXrr+/T6DbULPwH57FCMOJX+KPsup8KsmxNXgWlgPbd8QsHi8Zz3NXW\nvVFZ4CQ+EwVawm8u/EPBQC2LmqItkdyr6g3PdNFazT8EXHuX0INyNoeFGYDB+9M5\n8Umy5wpLUa3bp9TmHp5X\n=CV1m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c11231d04e762df91b3a61b619274496db2df726\nparent 11bceb8f8bfdd8723da10bdcaa767a19d92a2a57\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1780525550 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780525550 -0700\n\nRewrite oversized tool outputs during remote compaction (#26251)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen trying to fit history under compaction limit rewrite output items\ninstead of removing them entirely. Otherwise we're breaking\nincrementality in relation to the previous response.","verified_at":"2026-06-03T22:25:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4231472c03e6c6e3374b1c19ef096ee28476f9dd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4231472c03e6c6e3374b1c19ef096ee28476f9dd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4231472c03e6c6e3374b1c19ef096ee28476f9dd/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"11bceb8f8bfdd8723da10bdcaa767a19d92a2a57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/11bceb8f8bfdd8723da10bdcaa767a19d92a2a57","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/11bceb8f8bfdd8723da10bdcaa767a19d92a2a57"}]},{"sha":"11bceb8f8bfdd8723da10bdcaa767a19d92a2a57","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDExYmNlYjhmOGJmZGQ4NzIzZGExMGJkY2FhNzY3YTE5ZDkyYTJhNTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T22:24:40Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T22:24:40Z"},"message":"feat: catalog multi-agent v2 config (#26254)\n\n## Why\n\nModel metadata can now select multi-agent v2 even when a user has not\nenabled `features.multi_agent_v2` in their config. Some existing configs\nstill set the legacy `agents.max_threads` knob for v1 multi-agent\nbehavior, so treating every v2 runtime as incompatible with\n`agents.max_threads` would break users whose only v2 signal came from\nthe model catalog.\n\nThe incompatible configuration is specifically enabling\n`features.multi_agent_v2` while also setting `agents.max_threads`.\nCatalog-forced v2 should use the v2 concurrency setting and ignore the\nlegacy v1 cap instead of rejecting the config.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Split config validation from runtime concurrency calculation:\n`effective_agent_max_threads` now just returns the effective cap for the\nresolved multi-agent runtime.\n- Added explicit validation for `features.multi_agent_v2` +\n`agents.max_threads` at session startup.\n- Preserved catalog-selected v2 behavior when `features.multi_agent_v2`\nis disabled, so existing configs with `agents.max_threads` keep\nstarting.\n- Updated model-runtime selector coverage so a catalog v2 model still\nexposes v2 tools even when `agents.max_threads` is set and the config\nflag is disabled.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-core --lib`\n- `just test -p codex-core --lib -E\n\"test(multi_agent_v2_feature_rejects_agents_max_threads) |\ntest(catalog_v2_allows_agents_max_threads_when_feature_disabled)\"`","tree":{"sha":"ab621c0a57e5ed671c92ba331ef9ba5399b992a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ab621c0a57e5ed671c92ba331ef9ba5399b992a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/11bceb8f8bfdd8723da10bdcaa767a19d92a2a57","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIKmoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVHAQAJi33D3zNHg0VX/yhLigleM3\nnEjCnYpMaddodiCCHNVttx3yAMDpZeKzBuSodRJDqC3zwT2Syo4OFNRw97Cm1LHL\n6SMgWKL96p/NL7HuTudp8+VZvcleFInACA0o8F1A0MuhdIej7BAEaxq+jjU7xJkh\nB9/gYw+vrL9u+QANMVbJ5+Ab/h6xKpReFXHgWuD5h81dHtaxKxF4sLCFLmIZIMQN\nAJ9B7OyJDSok2wJtRRedPJGBBlWZBLfvRv1VVdkvJ4DVk+Ypva6XbQGXNhiL64y+\ndSIxxpQ7daFvK/hRCHWS+oc0zDcII8x1PZ26jKsT5AVgPyT0B+YJ6lxanMfVbrWr\nGnmRqdbdqW9qoU/yocydajvmkQI3H+wnVoTua9OlC42FEv4nBizwDPgWXySO9Ws5\nNn4+27/wQHVXpYuau9WIdWaElEG7Ue+3ZrlnGohGuthkoJvZTS2CzimEoW/PIkM1\nSn0Mf6HV6qWqNYX0OnJpUz0fNRQ64h3hCYTn81r4WGCrgSwiOtMakTd++bQ1lA8C\nQb3B9djjvYTZsIMG4Zh1ZSlN0JgxRa/TpYqmWxXaxpAZH8MM39X3UF4+aewfqNso\nXpRyme4Qsd4NMj8/6Rf3AZ0GZ+gx3+Kga7GhVFb+c0GVjsRsucsY4Gj7WLXjqf/S\n4uCnqE1JljesUbav+PGJ\n=a9oA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ab621c0a57e5ed671c92ba331ef9ba5399b992a4\nparent 2ca3810005f61bb033ccf6c48111e2aa4536b0e4\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780525480 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780525480 +0200\n\nfeat: catalog multi-agent v2 config (#26254)\n\n## Why\n\nModel metadata can now select multi-agent v2 even when a user has not\nenabled `features.multi_agent_v2` in their config. Some existing configs\nstill set the legacy `agents.max_threads` knob for v1 multi-agent\nbehavior, so treating every v2 runtime as incompatible with\n`agents.max_threads` would break users whose only v2 signal came from\nthe model catalog.\n\nThe incompatible configuration is specifically enabling\n`features.multi_agent_v2` while also setting `agents.max_threads`.\nCatalog-forced v2 should use the v2 concurrency setting and ignore the\nlegacy v1 cap instead of rejecting the config.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Split config validation from runtime concurrency calculation:\n`effective_agent_max_threads` now just returns the effective cap for the\nresolved multi-agent runtime.\n- Added explicit validation for `features.multi_agent_v2` +\n`agents.max_threads` at session startup.\n- Preserved catalog-selected v2 behavior when `features.multi_agent_v2`\nis disabled, so existing configs with `agents.max_threads` keep\nstarting.\n- Updated model-runtime selector coverage so a catalog v2 model still\nexposes v2 tools even when `agents.max_threads` is set and the config\nflag is disabled.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo check -p codex-core --lib`\n- `just test -p codex-core --lib -E\n\"test(multi_agent_v2_feature_rejects_agents_max_threads) |\ntest(catalog_v2_allows_agents_max_threads_when_feature_disabled)\"`","verified_at":"2026-06-03T22:24:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/11bceb8f8bfdd8723da10bdcaa767a19d92a2a57","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/11bceb8f8bfdd8723da10bdcaa767a19d92a2a57","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/11bceb8f8bfdd8723da10bdcaa767a19d92a2a57/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2ca3810005f61bb033ccf6c48111e2aa4536b0e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2ca3810005f61bb033ccf6c48111e2aa4536b0e4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2ca3810005f61bb033ccf6c48111e2aa4536b0e4"}]},{"sha":"2ca3810005f61bb033ccf6c48111e2aa4536b0e4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJjYTM4MTAwMDVmNjFiYjAzM2NjZjZjNDgxMTFlMmFhNDUzNmIwZTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T21:29:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T21:29:52Z"},"message":"[codex] Split Python runtime release workflow (#26226)\n\n## Why\n\nPython SDK releases pin an exact `openai-codex-cli-bin` version, so all\neight platform runtime wheels must be available on PyPI before the SDK\npackage is built and published. PyPI does not support reusable workflows\nas Trusted Publishers, which means OIDC-backed publishing must run from\neach top-level release workflow.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add reusable `python-runtime-build.yml` to prepare and upload all\neight runtime wheels without publishing\n- add top-level `python-runtime-release.yml` for manual runtime\npublication before updating an SDK pin\n- have `python-sdk-release.yml` publish and verify the prepared runtime\nwheels from its own top-level trusted job before building the SDK\n- verify PyPI exposes exactly the expected eight runtime wheels before\neither release workflow continues\n\n## PyPI configuration\n\n- keep the trusted publisher for\n`.github/workflows/python-sdk-release.yml` with environment `pypi`\n- add a trusted publisher for\n`.github/workflows/python-runtime-release.yml` with environment `pypi`\n- no trusted publisher is needed for\n`.github/workflows/python-runtime-build.yml`\n\n## Validation\n\n- parsed all three workflow YAML files\n- validated all embedded shell blocks with `bash -n`\n- no local tests run; relying on online CI","tree":{"sha":"e547e8843e27a5e379fd4458457c7049feb7301b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e547e8843e27a5e379fd4458457c7049feb7301b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2ca3810005f61bb033ccf6c48111e2aa4536b0e4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIJzQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/8YQAATrnXP2irhOOxP6qiWvr5QB\ni9VYl9vNk2exTHcyAW9c21Mp7FX86Wblw5MRH0DdLTS89cpHaLggkVBLf/D6Wqjz\nA0KMjfS9OVsE7otpAa3Na3V98EVm14J0j9PZ3uKsfb8iZgYNiRGUacr8uhTtsDpY\nxAuXxRp4NTqlP1RxEAX5TNlHNGtCLtGMoR8WOkQLpfuPZ0fTwuzPzH8OMWudzSll\nQRPDPqrPQtBUxoeEIdeVZY+KwaSJ3ucgxDPtXNckJqTF7NJTmh2HjY2tZoq9B/wD\nkacUMHVkiQqbsH5KGhjoWKRK6JvTwdjReqGO6Js7rIwIHw3WGUolXmiM0iQ/WnY5\nyR+wk8eKY969dZyjlAdKJ99mYu6Unt4PKd9Lx81eEnkzua3EHeJ+pQZZoQISLpZ1\n0ST8NoOgC1grH/bz/q3e/FYUjmrdKq1Vm3GFmwWoPS5qpmlw0YuCoqS3HuGNgj1H\ncM4Wgt5qMms7uCC804N4XpW9ya8j/8l/zE7VR165B0Bnkj4bcZenpIWLnwGNWeNa\n3UGuQDrRsMEfy1byJ7pbmR+QszNF9R7l0+DU2QB4a0uIcH62GLPXYiKPjknXL6La\nIOLmtVg1GjTrr1b4IwAKQUHXfrS4kJzy1a8T2nu13lbLQFNPtih5mgKz8E/Jl0vG\nCRa49jKTdNSOEK4ZL/vw\n=2QKh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e547e8843e27a5e379fd4458457c7049feb7301b\nparent 0eb7e6d79b44b95d4aa6b22759322efcccde3521\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1780522192 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780522192 -0700\n\n[codex] Split Python runtime release workflow (#26226)\n\n## Why\n\nPython SDK releases pin an exact `openai-codex-cli-bin` version, so all\neight platform runtime wheels must be available on PyPI before the SDK\npackage is built and published. PyPI does not support reusable workflows\nas Trusted Publishers, which means OIDC-backed publishing must run from\neach top-level release workflow.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add reusable `python-runtime-build.yml` to prepare and upload all\neight runtime wheels without publishing\n- add top-level `python-runtime-release.yml` for manual runtime\npublication before updating an SDK pin\n- have `python-sdk-release.yml` publish and verify the prepared runtime\nwheels from its own top-level trusted job before building the SDK\n- verify PyPI exposes exactly the expected eight runtime wheels before\neither release workflow continues\n\n## PyPI configuration\n\n- keep the trusted publisher for\n`.github/workflows/python-sdk-release.yml` with environment `pypi`\n- add a trusted publisher for\n`.github/workflows/python-runtime-release.yml` with environment `pypi`\n- no trusted publisher is needed for\n`.github/workflows/python-runtime-build.yml`\n\n## Validation\n\n- parsed all three workflow YAML files\n- validated all embedded shell blocks with `bash -n`\n- no local tests run; relying on online CI","verified_at":"2026-06-03T21:29:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2ca3810005f61bb033ccf6c48111e2aa4536b0e4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2ca3810005f61bb033ccf6c48111e2aa4536b0e4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2ca3810005f61bb033ccf6c48111e2aa4536b0e4/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0eb7e6d79b44b95d4aa6b22759322efcccde3521","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0eb7e6d79b44b95d4aa6b22759322efcccde3521","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0eb7e6d79b44b95d4aa6b22759322efcccde3521"}]},{"sha":"0eb7e6d79b44b95d4aa6b22759322efcccde3521","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBlYjdlNmQ3OWI0NGI5NWQ0YWE2YjIyNzU5MzIyZWZjY2NkZTM1MjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T21:02:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T21:02:55Z"},"message":"Restore Windows coverage for code-mode image generation exposure (#25960)\n\n## Summary\n\nRestore Windows coverage for standalone image generation in code mode.\n\nThe previous test executed a V8-backed code-mode cell on Windows CI,\nwhere that runtime path is intentionally excluded because it is\nunreliable. The test was then ignored entirely on Windows, removing\nuseful coverage.\n\nThis splits the test into two checks:\n\n- All platforms verify that `image_gen__imagegen` is exposed to the\nmodel when image generation is configured for code mode only.\n- Non-Windows platforms continue to execute the full V8-backed flow and\nverify that the nested image-generation call succeeds.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server standalone_image_generation`\n\nResult: 3 tests passed, plus the required bench smoke check.","tree":{"sha":"064f073b6f3f0bf8822c01ca81c4dc87a768e6b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/064f073b6f3f0bf8822c01ca81c4dc87a768e6b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0eb7e6d79b44b95d4aa6b22759322efcccde3521","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIJaACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArO0QAHg0tah9OPg2AuQ5HAQ1UbwE\nyvdKEVgaCGwZl9geuXFWtCdbE/nAoelIsZtmK7p9oIT70AJwqUmuF4zmqu6GtfO1\nngxTfreZ28adqyI5VSjtwtMo54tVkK6fKVKryx8OOAysQV+7alCR/QST7eYnXcfq\nBp4F6H1SPHoK36qrw6+LixYXzLTuCwndXY+QfZ7Y+gobymcc8l6pXHe86ltTfjZU\nZ/VOjo6UWYetVGVKiHCGnLKuNtb+C4Ex8X35vanBkvP8qdEKAmctS18j6k+MC5dM\n9/JrnJHxAhrW73V1VWAs1tXc+SLMC9hV4T+QOu92MLRjFZVe/527hqKdyhuhZZGq\nG+/prYfMEk7FQhLBCnn+Nh/NI6TREXkvBEYZn1iap08qLIhALsrJuH3hn1yCeJCy\ni3rfk2P0pmU9MCJJ2doX2e4qk/7D8aYcSxw726FueJfz6PztgJTQVYVu3C8dsDJL\nlVrgD/3TeXbKHwXwYPGpF0kq+o+5rsOXpWSrqJIPwcHlLXeqKH4i6VqWYjn1/FVX\n9RuNCaZO8f+Jo+MlCXAGiTyeWOmgzBRtTAO4nEwAkyObLrvkU4edZPOn68R/XBcV\nYmW46H01DbThPWQur9mnsTTkpDEmj0agU9xVgMA7YDK0mPHSAB9A2YC/pNGL1ewe\n489CPLQLcZwK9HWtpX5l\n=n082\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 064f073b6f3f0bf8822c01ca81c4dc87a768e6b0\nparent d8121f93c8df2e9066e929128886cae2fc81782b\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1780520575 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780520575 -0700\n\nRestore Windows coverage for code-mode image generation exposure (#25960)\n\n## Summary\n\nRestore Windows coverage for standalone image generation in code mode.\n\nThe previous test executed a V8-backed code-mode cell on Windows CI,\nwhere that runtime path is intentionally excluded because it is\nunreliable. The test was then ignored entirely on Windows, removing\nuseful coverage.\n\nThis splits the test into two checks:\n\n- All platforms verify that `image_gen__imagegen` is exposed to the\nmodel when image generation is configured for code mode only.\n- Non-Windows platforms continue to execute the full V8-backed flow and\nverify that the nested image-generation call succeeds.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server standalone_image_generation`\n\nResult: 3 tests passed, plus the required bench smoke check.","verified_at":"2026-06-03T21:02:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0eb7e6d79b44b95d4aa6b22759322efcccde3521","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0eb7e6d79b44b95d4aa6b22759322efcccde3521","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0eb7e6d79b44b95d4aa6b22759322efcccde3521/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d8121f93c8df2e9066e929128886cae2fc81782b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d8121f93c8df2e9066e929128886cae2fc81782b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d8121f93c8df2e9066e929128886cae2fc81782b"}]},{"sha":"d8121f93c8df2e9066e929128886cae2fc81782b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQ4MTIxZjkzYzhkZjJlOTA2NmU5MjkxMjg4ODZjYWUyZmM4MTc4MmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T19:56:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T19:56:54Z"},"message":"Fix forked thread name inheritance (#26075)\n\nFixes #25950.\n\n## Why\nForking a renamed thread could fall back to the source thread's\nfirst-prompt title because the fork path did not preserve the source's\nexplicit name. That meant fork-of-renamed-fork flows could show stale\nsidebar labels even though the user had renamed the parent.\n\n## What changed\n`thread/fork` now reads the source thread's distinct `name`, normalizes\nit, persists it onto materialized forks, and applies it to the returned\nAPI thread. Because the source `name` already excludes first-prompt\npseudo-titles, forks inherit only an explicit user rename instead of\nstale generated metadata.","tree":{"sha":"fc558320b96c43aeda0e61c370cfd87f06ba06df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/fc558320b96c43aeda0e61c370cfd87f06ba06df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d8121f93c8df2e9066e929128886cae2fc81782b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIIcGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAERgQAEvk1ILkzl4Tqs80uFPCdy6u\nEyRQww0t21fK0Ike/IwUblWTeKhn/tmYUebqVVk0TNlNwDp6ZK06kbY7MLq0dru+\nmJizOjgZspxSYaabiX2E5DblaRteGapNykY9Emo6JsGay1LynQSF1WecBpgFGsBI\nZcxZSVwvWwLg3TQCYvd1h2ltoKuprfip1ZiuL0DKnMyfq27hRCadXS75yJJS4VNz\nuTab62kV5/IGRxWB250+aZLD6fhoBUZe25w7iVWeHz8IJ92prphByyQjblvqpopc\nYXAUSFY5e2J4aQyEan7Vz7372cF98tYMFXh2Cn8iTfaAeJJydN3UJKOyFLxcCkVm\nKxcd5x+9wJ2GdQ5fmV7FZu2X7a1xSR1jym+Bv5qvqFfxDxl27tlxnXIN6evjYGDi\n3YpzoSAhKap9poB555OV9G/JF9LPq/UlW4rxYRjAQ1dJKKDp5TLa9F3nrLZVpLjz\n0zVTKN5sr9KA/0zV4smUb+LkQD+k4sdT1FZxVCKd0NOrBsafk6hvd2L/eC9+vtkm\npDult2ynDzywZbaSCo3/JrNHQXZp8S3bztxEjiizjv/iRoee3lbHMos2vlfZyYPI\n6aQ7MuzGWPrRviaIZ6naGDzEhmHzexkJ6fqtlIW6Guop2ps9ANB34i1UxGSsZzVe\nXEdtTALQMDUhYsAr5GQz\n=waI0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fc558320b96c43aeda0e61c370cfd87f06ba06df\nparent a2ebe07b39823945aaedd4e1acbd70316ca13f1d\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780516614 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780516614 -0700\n\nFix forked thread name inheritance (#26075)\n\nFixes #25950.\n\n## Why\nForking a renamed thread could fall back to the source thread's\nfirst-prompt title because the fork path did not preserve the source's\nexplicit name. That meant fork-of-renamed-fork flows could show stale\nsidebar labels even though the user had renamed the parent.\n\n## What changed\n`thread/fork` now reads the source thread's distinct `name`, normalizes\nit, persists it onto materialized forks, and applies it to the returned\nAPI thread. Because the source `name` already excludes first-prompt\npseudo-titles, forks inherit only an explicit user rename instead of\nstale generated metadata.","verified_at":"2026-06-03T19:56:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d8121f93c8df2e9066e929128886cae2fc81782b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d8121f93c8df2e9066e929128886cae2fc81782b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d8121f93c8df2e9066e929128886cae2fc81782b/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a2ebe07b39823945aaedd4e1acbd70316ca13f1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a2ebe07b39823945aaedd4e1acbd70316ca13f1d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a2ebe07b39823945aaedd4e1acbd70316ca13f1d"}]},{"sha":"a2ebe07b39823945aaedd4e1acbd70316ca13f1d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEyZWJlMDdiMzk4MjM5NDVhYWVkZDRlMWFjYmQ3MDMxNmNhMTNmMWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"dhruvgupta-oai","email":"dhruvgupta@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T19:55:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T19:55:11Z"},"message":"[profile-switcher][rust] -- [1/2] Add app-server account session protocol (#25469)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds the app-server v2 `accountSession/*` protocol used by the Desktop\nprofile switcher and the backend account metadata client needed to\npopulate workspace choices.\n\nThis is the protocol layer only. The app-server lifecycle and\nconsolidated saved-session storage are split into a follow-up PR.\n\n## Rust Stack\n\n1. This PR\n2. [openai/codex#25383](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25383) adds\napp-server session lifecycle behavior and consolidated saved-session\nstorage.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Generated app-server schema fixtures are included from the existing\ngeneration flow in the lifecycle PR where the routes are registered.\n- Did not run tests per requested scope.","tree":{"sha":"bc24ad7fe594f10762f58e6a568222d95b329034","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bc24ad7fe594f10762f58e6a568222d95b329034"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a2ebe07b39823945aaedd4e1acbd70316ca13f1d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIIafCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZQUQAKEBZ2jp/MEMUyhboGDsg4oy\n4r3vBZVUKg3htN4s9CrlZf8QYxtFP3bvPSE9+xhC61CdXeShOTZPQRThRD30G0C/\nX67CBAKzqxurVaJivSTOtGOp9razO2385pc8sxJ/QVG6zfHKYidle1lqvDI1OVL0\nb0MKkPGXLe31GYnzbH54Fr+1bhwSorkaNNJoMikjmhvlcA1to+tDPBLS22CNb2Wb\nn2mOskDU3QLNk5dITbnqElTQpH5EFJx+Z9cGNVSuu7FX+wcAMEq4E1K+NE1rLHgR\nRENLetKEJs13k7n3qph9MmF0bpwEb6oxV9b6uhlhh7uIxDAhoH8nV9Q6IvvU5cnk\nsqG6LVS24O0Gng0GGdxrO8T/8NZPrgyIyYJKcw03k6ExHZ46C8CzvU1lL7y0XLLy\nZuXv6/l7NcWOYW6JwAQYQpy3ScxuPrL8cfkkDU6porQCrksKMBbEowefjbdRXVJI\nTRWzC5FeQKPhKHyMa+wwgOgYBbgI4AG/ysoUpcM262WSXFKox4PRzbDFEYw1RN2F\nJ+e8ELV5RdHB1Rw+seYBIoffNX3xkMhe6/Tuwa2MhrzEiOyv/vhQpqOb+riWCvNp\nx9yYZ1E7cI1EDTJFF8IKolR2IUd6zAs7wVCPHjfL23KXFeSKh/88eczNWyBe0k9O\nxvn8tqu00NWnlDfRCYRq\n=NyCb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bc24ad7fe594f10762f58e6a568222d95b329034\nparent 57ab4c89e05d13b81722780ffc50eee0ea6cf445\nauthor dhruvgupta-oai <dhruvgupta@openai.com> 1780516511 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780516511 +0530\n\n[profile-switcher][rust] -- [1/2] Add app-server account session protocol (#25469)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds the app-server v2 `accountSession/*` protocol used by the Desktop\nprofile switcher and the backend account metadata client needed to\npopulate workspace choices.\n\nThis is the protocol layer only. The app-server lifecycle and\nconsolidated saved-session storage are split into a follow-up PR.\n\n## Rust Stack\n\n1. This PR\n2. [openai/codex#25383](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/25383) adds\napp-server session lifecycle behavior and consolidated saved-session\nstorage.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Generated app-server schema fixtures are included from the existing\ngeneration flow in the lifecycle PR where the routes are registered.\n- Did not run tests per requested scope.","verified_at":"2026-06-03T19:55:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a2ebe07b39823945aaedd4e1acbd70316ca13f1d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a2ebe07b39823945aaedd4e1acbd70316ca13f1d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a2ebe07b39823945aaedd4e1acbd70316ca13f1d/comments","author":{"login":"dhruvgupta-oai","id":247462758,"node_id":"U_kgDODr_7Zg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247462758?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhruvgupta-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/dhruvgupta-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhruvgupta-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhruvgupta-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhruvgupta-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhruvgupta-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhruvgupta-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhruvgupta-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhruvgupta-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhruvgupta-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhruvgupta-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"57ab4c89e05d13b81722780ffc50eee0ea6cf445","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/57ab4c89e05d13b81722780ffc50eee0ea6cf445","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/57ab4c89e05d13b81722780ffc50eee0ea6cf445"}]},{"sha":"57ab4c89e05d13b81722780ffc50eee0ea6cf445","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU3YWI0Yzg5ZTA1ZDEzYjgxNzIyNzgwZmZjNTBlZWUwZWE2Y2Y0NDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T19:49:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T19:49:58Z"},"message":"Expose local image paths to models (#25944)\n\n## Why\n\nLocal image attachments include image bytes, but the adjacent\nmodel-visible label omits the source path. Exposing the path lets\nmodel-selected workflows refer back to the intended local image\nexplicitly.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Include an escaped `path` attribute in model-visible local image\nopening tags.\n- Reuse the path-aware marker generator in rollout coverage.\n- Update protocol, replay, and rollout coverage for the new request\nshape.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-core skips_local_image_label_text`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncopy_paste_local_image_persists_rollout_request_shape`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"c7c1ffb742c761098e6ab20fb5eaea2c44dbbdc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c7c1ffb742c761098e6ab20fb5eaea2c44dbbdc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/57ab4c89e05d13b81722780ffc50eee0ea6cf445","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIIVmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAcMQAA2x9PO7ziJWMLGqtWG40Q+b\nCcDY5s0zKMBrhZtGMBhg7hjmb2S7IjMsWJWEePOusf1utOxx64kAbpxqKbZoLR+r\nBOcLwIH2/2Un8wxtZbkBJp11ualW1EBgcUds8GLrkLHU4XGfd2SAiAaEzQVnyg0d\nP5pq3bNGJk4Sb278l/ZEkdlwDH5x3hPehSw/aVevMuS6II6hrRyTl7FAR7PIAG7u\n/4YmWAwdzqbgLhch3HGzaSoaf5WecnnC9h2aRUmMl+ClpMQbV0UR9xKt6zwllNeV\nmWUgUat61QdnCOAub8dAd77tdFm4Hn4PHRln3Be4RbGGVEW2fojLDDSPviDlgSMx\n+tPer+hR+yl1oX7yBOl4ryk1Kc+am3l0EhuHLFpQm17OT4lbqgQiwbeRz9EuKjZ+\nUyMHoY17Ufo0NytHMb7D2KjHEHgVbySx6HSTMpXNujzSSSnPgOLifH3B93hR6i9d\nZEmLWi4G4wHdzDci+yQ/PwUjy+rTpfcOpVnUSU2fw8s8gOPS1WTJdRWtSZ2WG5j+\nbFy2S09zDJmNdjlhDYVcSGqyzxmpKzeg+/MIa2935AJSh7LWXfxJz2HSiu1P2QBV\nf6eTpQHH68OiXSlbaChML0hQyMmhpxSIbBUZKHhfrBIsh3/wO4HrrzGNa1Fk6hPj\nv142YaY9UdNOvgi9JD/R\n=7O94\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c7c1ffb742c761098e6ab20fb5eaea2c44dbbdc6\nparent aeac226d16523875a3fc77f61d6edcd2943155fc\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1780516198 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780516198 +0000\n\nExpose local image paths to models (#25944)\n\n## Why\n\nLocal image attachments include image bytes, but the adjacent\nmodel-visible label omits the source path. Exposing the path lets\nmodel-selected workflows refer back to the intended local image\nexplicitly.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Include an escaped `path` attribute in model-visible local image\nopening tags.\n- Reuse the path-aware marker generator in rollout coverage.\n- Update protocol, replay, and rollout coverage for the new request\nshape.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-core skips_local_image_label_text`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncopy_paste_local_image_persists_rollout_request_shape`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-03T19:49:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/57ab4c89e05d13b81722780ffc50eee0ea6cf445","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/57ab4c89e05d13b81722780ffc50eee0ea6cf445","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/57ab4c89e05d13b81722780ffc50eee0ea6cf445/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"aeac226d16523875a3fc77f61d6edcd2943155fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/aeac226d16523875a3fc77f61d6edcd2943155fc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/aeac226d16523875a3fc77f61d6edcd2943155fc"}]},{"sha":"aeac226d16523875a3fc77f61d6edcd2943155fc","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFlYWMyMjZkMTY1MjM4NzVhM2ZjNzdmNjFkNmVkY2QyOTQzMTU1ZmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Ning","email":"ericning@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T19:39:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T19:39:13Z"},"message":"Preserve remote plugin default prompts (#25887)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Read `default_prompts` from remote plugin release metadata.\n- Prefer the plural prompt list over legacy `default_prompt`.\n- Fall back to `default_prompt` as a single-item list for backward\ncompatibility.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server`","tree":{"sha":"36b18809a60695f05dcc68f576319f3657b3c859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/36b18809a60695f05dcc68f576319f3657b3c859"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/aeac226d16523875a3fc77f61d6edcd2943155fc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIILhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAI+wQAID8sPqEllaEPHNto7wTrhbu\nxMKej0NGXSIlRNaiZ4jzAGtki/XOZW40QNiE8swr2wGcqalkqVtoJ1XDIEtiT+LR\nV6JivQV3wSv+TNakSDQe8loJOJNAXHHcKd/prUNKvqvj1DzraRb4rCtWokkyzs3/\nmF0wXGcw+YHjcWuQMIc37H3N1kMrOiV0H5ADfFPutr1odcnYTArxdKlqMOcHXcel\nN65/dml1ilhg5QSXHk34G62Xr3WVeo1vmNgCgzNxyT/9x0FpghZLSyNQ1E1ptFyQ\nbu5QYRJt7B5fDJ6etkrkUTMHXa6nxKF9ult4klXy9N8CX/27j38VDKdOT07mYoak\nvZCK+eQPyfkzainYiQ/p9lF1M2iMc1WeN67Qqltcmrc7PYJoNCasTVGKg1r4N1KX\nTXZ4ZsohwGFPF/fKLNALMEiO+4gQLUrdbkhdUF89/j0MTrPtcASqZVm1PP/Uj5NW\nSEIydyMuRC7IQdZjaS8dptvA0jsQWfU0dt6YRAk0PsM51w7VgKaNY25Nw7xm675e\nH4PWyRB0K952ICAJfL+pKRz3cz+NOYAtpkLWzz/ycq94/jntytdxynMgGpcoL83X\nL03q9YuNdXNff3GZZB8TTFm7/esb5e9a5zdrz7wb7Urf01Tyv7qAZTqeL6ogLnj/\n4Vfd0T5M0TyCuOxd5d66\n=BkFG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 36b18809a60695f05dcc68f576319f3657b3c859\nparent 10b408080a1009ca99be50cf8bc3fe45dfe7223b\nauthor Eric Ning <ericning@openai.com> 1780515553 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780515553 -0700\n\nPreserve remote plugin default prompts (#25887)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Read `default_prompts` from remote plugin release metadata.\n- Prefer the plural prompt list over legacy `default_prompt`.\n- Fall back to `default_prompt` as a single-item list for backward\ncompatibility.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server`","verified_at":"2026-06-03T19:39:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/aeac226d16523875a3fc77f61d6edcd2943155fc","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/aeac226d16523875a3fc77f61d6edcd2943155fc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/aeac226d16523875a3fc77f61d6edcd2943155fc/comments","author":{"login":"ericning-o","id":182030612,"node_id":"U_kgDOCtmRFA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182030612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o","html_url":"https://github.com/ericning-o","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ericning-o/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"10b408080a1009ca99be50cf8bc3fe45dfe7223b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/10b408080a1009ca99be50cf8bc3fe45dfe7223b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/10b408080a1009ca99be50cf8bc3fe45dfe7223b"}]},{"sha":"10b408080a1009ca99be50cf8bc3fe45dfe7223b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDEwYjQwODA4MGExMDA5Y2E5OWJlNTBjZjhiYzNmZTQ1ZGZlNzIyM2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T19:14:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T19:14:14Z"},"message":"[codex] Pin Python SDK to runtime 0.137.0a4 (#26216)\n\n## Summary\n- pin the Python SDK runtime to `openai-codex-cli-bin==0.137.0a4`\n- refresh generated protocol artifacts from `rust-v0.137.0-alpha.4`\n- refresh `sdk/python/uv.lock` with all eight published runtime wheels\n\n## Runtime publication\n- published `openai-codex-cli-bin==0.137.0a4` through the\n`python-sdk-release` workflow\n- includes macOS, manylinux, musllinux, and Windows wheels\n- publication run:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26905608531\n\n## Validation\n- ran `just fmt`\n- generated artifacts from the `rust-v0.137.0-alpha.4` release wheel\n- ran `uv lock --check --default-index https://pypi.org/simple`\n- did not run tests locally, per request; CI provides the test signal","tree":{"sha":"d1ed244dac1595c696cd1298c2819f6a2eddecaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d1ed244dac1595c696cd1298c2819f6a2eddecaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/10b408080a1009ca99be50cf8bc3fe45dfe7223b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIH0GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgzkQAHCTJs/fJbEkaHebLhKJjVok\nEbZBFg6QA7aEllNds0Bq6IGglq0Bxsue8jjjE2UIGxM0nPWXhvIUcD6SyJl6CjuA\n5H5UBCDdz+eN8rrfjH3CTNoq7vguu9NLgkJJ/v0qWO/OA61AvuEU0BVagkJIf2FM\nddWFCoCbs8ApTVPWwicuBAc6uAxDQhFBdH5oN8h/VzdT7PaSwWlGeAsD0s8GWTyu\nRovYkqoNZ4/nK0qs3/9+8lVt50oAj8Ev1sxX9Pq+d8qU0HPCGMdzaYJg4oqBUSvt\ntN15SmVVjbFoWQGhIEnC0G/m9EKI1EcFKV0qZ/hTHu2uqG+sn9t+LLoFs2qeOp5r\n0or6RiUocYecVQEqEse608yNsFFE8AZqX0NbGnOtRLwDxlAD8jwbdzfOrB5MYcye\nTQwLOqNbg0MLDlxAXAB+dMzspHR/PSRklVmn693RXP8eU0lf+S+0WrHw5DiI1P4Q\nIbvXjiYFAgPHveXZrkOc2hViSd/wNH7zCadsWJPoAdh9uQ9rU+uZMEjVTjUcQeqQ\n7YSF7tgMiUxDzxQsuaJo3ae/dbh7bhiR2nNtvkUy19EqGz4Xl2MBRiCzy8WwbSiL\nGWtHZhQzWHMlQf1l6oBsGZTtRZBp1TtDMBtE3rAUtWW5pfAQiw5wwZBvGEo4uG4Z\nfkYETX/wM9WZq72bk8P5\n=KcjY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d1ed244dac1595c696cd1298c2819f6a2eddecaf\nparent 2d5c264ebc26c276ca6cc312389abde453ca69aa\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1780514054 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780514054 -0700\n\n[codex] Pin Python SDK to runtime 0.137.0a4 (#26216)\n\n## Summary\n- pin the Python SDK runtime to `openai-codex-cli-bin==0.137.0a4`\n- refresh generated protocol artifacts from `rust-v0.137.0-alpha.4`\n- refresh `sdk/python/uv.lock` with all eight published runtime wheels\n\n## Runtime publication\n- published `openai-codex-cli-bin==0.137.0a4` through the\n`python-sdk-release` workflow\n- includes macOS, manylinux, musllinux, and Windows wheels\n- publication run:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/26905608531\n\n## Validation\n- ran `just fmt`\n- generated artifacts from the `rust-v0.137.0-alpha.4` release wheel\n- ran `uv lock --check --default-index https://pypi.org/simple`\n- did not run tests locally, per request; CI provides the test signal","verified_at":"2026-06-03T19:14:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/10b408080a1009ca99be50cf8bc3fe45dfe7223b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/10b408080a1009ca99be50cf8bc3fe45dfe7223b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/10b408080a1009ca99be50cf8bc3fe45dfe7223b/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2d5c264ebc26c276ca6cc312389abde453ca69aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2d5c264ebc26c276ca6cc312389abde453ca69aa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2d5c264ebc26c276ca6cc312389abde453ca69aa"}]},{"sha":"2d5c264ebc26c276ca6cc312389abde453ca69aa","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJkNWMyNjRlYmMyNmMyNzZjYTZjYzMxMjM4OWFiZGU0NTNjYTY5YWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T18:29:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T18:29:36Z"},"message":"[codex] Copy user Bazel settings into Codex worktrees (#25925)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex-created linked worktrees do not include ignored files from the\nmain worktree. Bazel users who keep local overrides in `user.bazelrc`\ntherefore lose those settings in every new worktree.\n\nThe setup must also work on Windows and must not overwrite a file that\nalready exists in the worktree.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe checked-in Codex environment now invokes\n`.codex/environments/setup.py`. The script resolves the main worktree\nand current worktree, then uses\n`copy_from_main_worktree_to_worktree(repo_relative_path)` to copy\nignored files into new worktrees without overwriting existing\ndestinations.\n\n`main()` currently copies `user.bazelrc`. Additional repository-relative\npaths can be added as further calls to the same helper.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran the setup script in a linked worktree and confirmed it handles a\nmissing main-worktree `user.bazelrc`.\n- Verified the helper copies a main-worktree file, preserves an existing\nworktree file, and creates parent directories for a nested path.","tree":{"sha":"d52718ac0a9730f93b6a826a612feb1358fa7eb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d52718ac0a9730f93b6a826a612feb1358fa7eb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2d5c264ebc26c276ca6cc312389abde453ca69aa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIHKQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhlwQABgPm3bV5NMkz5E1IZcHEzta\nEzLr2AquyonxBfSwtcGCYcWDE5nCS15dGYRTBVZmx10QIGMMxsOQnygL7GG4bi8t\n8VxfDSX0YfCHaZerDQd95lOzgCzBCn2PT6OWmxakhdLk8djCJw/Ost1OwVicXCcq\nz1KKhVED7uk0XDGKvIFnSAhpJ2wKGJb653f0snPs/nGeZreFTEMnD+AnpoViiimc\nWp7Cm95/EIVbevwQf94dObQj0wlJr2TqmK0qZ70gWFoZkL6QsMGuo4RD7b21/uB3\nqUqXmoSK1bgMWql4c0fe9s8PT1VvcYnD9QSJl7XHTyaQCWi0uyYd2QePRhflW1VW\nR/Urz0HTCwbE/Qvc/Y8Yo4omcfPjR7udqwjHRdYmD3TQyFovYOlo/eydTS6I0fR7\n/X1lFFa2K90quku8bRMYlsuSh/W2vvisik80Hz77ULi3FBlPGl/ohaMv8t2uIIdy\nnZP5YNj4TQiCzxv4utZ6cLUEkP5L3+Px8dV24ArfcSD5QbBaggdA7JXGz6jLYiR2\nsQZhiP5EV4Pz/MRjWc/eXHVWq+fVSzGx8to5DKvR7YwQZXMeBbQXSdTJnX2y8wft\nYUViCnah1sGseWFBi4GCBD8ayp/oNO6TthkJmqV1yrODTRm3sOQSSRhq8ZVuvhf7\n1MQ8CXh6jXpj9RfC7xz2\n=Ymn0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d52718ac0a9730f93b6a826a612feb1358fa7eb4\nparent 52b359b24913ddab5d12d42f2f113b0e63843063\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1780511376 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780511376 +0000\n\n[codex] Copy user Bazel settings into Codex worktrees (#25925)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex-created linked worktrees do not include ignored files from the\nmain worktree. Bazel users who keep local overrides in `user.bazelrc`\ntherefore lose those settings in every new worktree.\n\nThe setup must also work on Windows and must not overwrite a file that\nalready exists in the worktree.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe checked-in Codex environment now invokes\n`.codex/environments/setup.py`. The script resolves the main worktree\nand current worktree, then uses\n`copy_from_main_worktree_to_worktree(repo_relative_path)` to copy\nignored files into new worktrees without overwriting existing\ndestinations.\n\n`main()` currently copies `user.bazelrc`. Additional repository-relative\npaths can be added as further calls to the same helper.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Ran the setup script in a linked worktree and confirmed it handles a\nmissing main-worktree `user.bazelrc`.\n- Verified the helper copies a main-worktree file, preserves an existing\nworktree file, and creates parent directories for a nested path.","verified_at":"2026-06-03T18:29:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2d5c264ebc26c276ca6cc312389abde453ca69aa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2d5c264ebc26c276ca6cc312389abde453ca69aa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2d5c264ebc26c276ca6cc312389abde453ca69aa/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"52b359b24913ddab5d12d42f2f113b0e63843063","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52b359b24913ddab5d12d42f2f113b0e63843063","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/52b359b24913ddab5d12d42f2f113b0e63843063"}]},{"sha":"52b359b24913ddab5d12d42f2f113b0e63843063","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUyYjM1OWIyNDkxM2RkYWI1ZDEyZDQyZjJmMTEzYjBlNjM4NDMwNjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T17:41:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T17:41:41Z"},"message":"core: stop threading SandboxPolicy through exec (#25700)\n\n## Why\n\n#25450 attempts a broad `SandboxPolicy` removal across several unrelated\nsurfaces, which makes it hard to review and still leaves new helper code\nmoving legacy policies around. This PR is a narrower alternative:\nmigrate only the exec-side Windows sandbox plumbing so the review can\nfocus on one production path and one compatibility boundary.\n\nThe goal is to stop threading `SandboxPolicy` through exec code without\nexpanding the migration into app-server, protocol, telemetry, config, or\nsession behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Removed `ExecRequest::compatibility_sandbox_policy()`.\n- Changed the Windows restricted-token and elevated filesystem override\nhelpers to accept `PermissionProfile` plus the split filesystem/network\npolicies instead of a `SandboxPolicy`.\n- Kept the remaining legacy projection local to the writable-root\ncomparison that still needs to compare split policy behavior against the\nlegacy Windows backend model.\n- Rejected restricted split filesystem policies that still grant\nfull-disk writes before using the Windows restricted-token backend,\npreserving the previous clear-failure behavior for profiles that project\nto `ExternalSandbox`.\n- Updated the Windows sandbox override tests to exercise the new call\nshape and cover the full-write split-profile regression.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core windows_restricted_token`\n- `just test -p codex-core windows_elevated`","tree":{"sha":"a112ab263889e583142e9841c141bf514db71d60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a112ab263889e583142e9841c141bf514db71d60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/52b359b24913ddab5d12d42f2f113b0e63843063","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIGdVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/9QQABGDaYJuwNEbvnf1Np7IFljN\nHnd9hwD3XmKkrZwUepS6SzHjNCVq5r+Kh5jmuf7JbE9FN311aHYth6tVklKRe8h8\nTRCIlXvr/wLUQyw5AIluUhai+wwphHAX8pEOdSq3p0TTLEcCFr0A1KrPOJKccIkB\nkDk9VWd9PEEWqtBG6/ShQl893J7wQZ2PMcAIWSXcQZgOriJ9oyOWiw4niEug+7ya\n3r2064eCsFMNEWbLrSaM9d0o97qRxPsQ7UKc26GyjYIWV0wSTuK0QmW/v6W8yarH\nRvr7nWQ5D20GmnKdqrSlwsbWlPE/90cW9VscYdTikNQ3/GCNy7ELF5aGgF+ZQpry\nR3oI3qxuWYi+bQASrKUJGXCuuMClSt79sdntKGUVg3KoRJzpAevEE5ugwW09se7U\n89d/FxrG3PqYb9QHARMHSby3VNaszAvZLkiiVPt4zjlFk7mMV/phd7C0yZI5A+yI\nGafrKMJeMGfAYGegS7Kl0nkpLI3cU8t2sdM7LTnEFIdUXYzHXpOhY7DEpRwalMtq\nTHQcdLSF/ho3vcQJKDUP/jTHG1rfU4/XbKUgPkHjEVMe1KUmGpnJo/1Phj9XNxSW\n0QseYXyX7jci4IHCIQ1ko6jFKA7Txy3862uZE12c/24dYZfpCkZTvHQlKCAZEiHq\nk+87Yuz5D3ordLy+r95X\n=EODR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a112ab263889e583142e9841c141bf514db71d60\nparent a2a9e767f7fc5c4fa9dc6c91c6907612dda72cf3\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1780508501 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780508501 -0700\n\ncore: stop threading SandboxPolicy through exec (#25700)\n\n## Why\n\n#25450 attempts a broad `SandboxPolicy` removal across several unrelated\nsurfaces, which makes it hard to review and still leaves new helper code\nmoving legacy policies around. This PR is a narrower alternative:\nmigrate only the exec-side Windows sandbox plumbing so the review can\nfocus on one production path and one compatibility boundary.\n\nThe goal is to stop threading `SandboxPolicy` through exec code without\nexpanding the migration into app-server, protocol, telemetry, config, or\nsession behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Removed `ExecRequest::compatibility_sandbox_policy()`.\n- Changed the Windows restricted-token and elevated filesystem override\nhelpers to accept `PermissionProfile` plus the split filesystem/network\npolicies instead of a `SandboxPolicy`.\n- Kept the remaining legacy projection local to the writable-root\ncomparison that still needs to compare split policy behavior against the\nlegacy Windows backend model.\n- Rejected restricted split filesystem policies that still grant\nfull-disk writes before using the Windows restricted-token backend,\npreserving the previous clear-failure behavior for profiles that project\nto `ExternalSandbox`.\n- Updated the Windows sandbox override tests to exercise the new call\nshape and cover the full-write split-profile regression.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core windows_restricted_token`\n- `just test -p codex-core windows_elevated`","verified_at":"2026-06-03T17:41:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52b359b24913ddab5d12d42f2f113b0e63843063","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/52b359b24913ddab5d12d42f2f113b0e63843063","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52b359b24913ddab5d12d42f2f113b0e63843063/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a2a9e767f7fc5c4fa9dc6c91c6907612dda72cf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a2a9e767f7fc5c4fa9dc6c91c6907612dda72cf3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a2a9e767f7fc5c4fa9dc6c91c6907612dda72cf3"}]},{"sha":"a2a9e767f7fc5c4fa9dc6c91c6907612dda72cf3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEyYTllNzY3ZjdmYzVjNGZhOWRjNmM5MWM2OTA3NjEyZGRhNzJjZjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T16:36:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T16:36:50Z"},"message":"Fix multiline paste in /goal edit (#26047)\n\nFixes #26025.\n\n## Why\n`/goal edit` opens `CustomPromptView`, which did not use the paste-burst\nhandling that protects the main composer when terminals deliver paste as\nrapid key events. On Windows terminals, the first pasted newline could\nbe treated as Enter-to-submit, truncating the goal edit and leaving the\nrest of the paste behind.\n\n## What\nThis reuses `PasteBurst` in `CustomPromptView` as a lightweight\nEnter-suppression detector for paste-like key streams. Characters still\ninsert directly, explicit paste still goes through the view paste path,\nand ordinary text entry still submits on Enter.","tree":{"sha":"047c20c30ea5ee0ce12232814cd8dd3849a953ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/047c20c30ea5ee0ce12232814cd8dd3849a953ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a2a9e767f7fc5c4fa9dc6c91c6907612dda72cf3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIFgiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsSgQACnXVU9Ip0dVL2iwlzDTZC9I\n/CLUDun9aIWIDn+ZwLbAnfllkJ0t+vwVReykcCHjImUev9LcLLP1bPWJNCf2AyoS\nj9HPEWw6CGmqiQX+ynmMzotZyqJDUgh8JCWO6Ypncr+Ct46jghHVZzf5Q7+DVe33\nlvlp8805GfEzwvN9aks85vTTgg07pLi+jovX3hsrbjV/IaT38+hnRMcZKGFJ/uz5\nlVV/TnpKfE3viHDIED7wjnDzQGDvm7fzSmOoL3ja68mU8eJ5rBq0jKKyDn9kpina\nzEBEowmbR4IeDWldNUfj/mtPwLX0WdwXjyqNMRrBdnJSD/tWrTNj1OmaKcJU0yTB\nUF2it/9X6cfqpOotOk/9qvtT1+GVyJ4h9gL29qyJYFSYc0olNLrZoykG0wZMZv51\nNYYiV+wIKI0U46+nFeY+cT43Mm1gFmXioIQIf71DkwEAH54I2mu6oXpuMGTyPCrt\naqGbRkPIUacEKRy1IGHRr7R5sYLH8Wr1OVDMndsMDhOcyiSc8aBxKhDmQzDwxcrA\nmo+VtPVrjD2zP5SoL1mnTmYMFLREhh8+9saHZN27nwGsv4AsEkKGtJFGJo0LKib5\nqfuDHCuNWnMdivfoJJmYe+PtADcbhFAuQj7xKtV56A3Qp48gUVq3WvPrFgz004Nv\n/wdanARGp6SJJ7pZEgrL\n=NdjP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 047c20c30ea5ee0ce12232814cd8dd3849a953ba\nparent 8030c3697019b32dd0fc2b232cea0c2c2574fe9d\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1780504610 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780504610 -0700\n\nFix multiline paste in /goal edit (#26047)\n\nFixes #26025.\n\n## Why\n`/goal edit` opens `CustomPromptView`, which did not use the paste-burst\nhandling that protects the main composer when terminals deliver paste as\nrapid key events. On Windows terminals, the first pasted newline could\nbe treated as Enter-to-submit, truncating the goal edit and leaving the\nrest of the paste behind.\n\n## What\nThis reuses `PasteBurst` in `CustomPromptView` as a lightweight\nEnter-suppression detector for paste-like key streams. Characters still\ninsert directly, explicit paste still goes through the view paste path,\nand ordinary text entry still submits on Enter.","verified_at":"2026-06-03T16:36:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a2a9e767f7fc5c4fa9dc6c91c6907612dda72cf3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a2a9e767f7fc5c4fa9dc6c91c6907612dda72cf3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a2a9e767f7fc5c4fa9dc6c91c6907612dda72cf3/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8030c3697019b32dd0fc2b232cea0c2c2574fe9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8030c3697019b32dd0fc2b232cea0c2c2574fe9d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8030c3697019b32dd0fc2b232cea0c2c2574fe9d"}]},{"sha":"8030c3697019b32dd0fc2b232cea0c2c2574fe9d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDgwMzBjMzY5NzAxOWIzMmRkMGZjMmIyMzJjZWEwYzJjMjU3NGZlOWQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-03T16:36:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-03T16:36:10Z"},"message":"feat: guard git enrichment (#26175)\n\nSkip turn git metadata enrichment when a turn has remote or multiple\nexecutors, so we do not report the orchestrator checkout as executor\nworkspace metadata.\n\nTest: `just test -p codex-core` (blocked by existing\n`Session::conversation_id` compile error in `close_agent.rs`).","tree":{"sha":"55d0e96ead3c64d48f71661b81d50322111ed93c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/55d0e96ead3c64d48f71661b81d50322111ed93c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8030c3697019b32dd0fc2b232cea0c2c2574fe9d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqIFf6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvU4QAKQ4w0j8nRJD0Abudsx42YOG\nhz704c76OH8ajn0gSksU6orYagRiz4uka9zxwACVY97wV5hCR4QQBgWldKOet3d8\nsjMqzlN8efcblT5ifyFG1aTL7Y0xTo4kGnW1kN9wgGDehciQglDvSl3AixAAcn/b\nKUxsSt5EDK/KGVoYSoIF9IErb5ddBU/7Lf1nD9YMR0KlVYcyd5jT6NCZ/hVRX41n\nAVvvNA5pAKc63tKKMHqgyAsQzcacZvRqelh4t2nXcYOD+c6vX0V0kGMJbKZFPV3e\nvghTMzoHLFh7/+ItRQyahWXvBAXbubaeN8C0K85U1G1CJ6IkHnJYfB8IIS0YxUpO\nVujrjHkDUMJ/SC4fBRvsHziC3dYLvO1cSVO5K2VHVKyIHiHiFkO7OFU//G+fgtpI\npjOupo62wrKMCm1xwuGLDNajL6Hi1MkxGX+zAHgtDCWSJ30CZPdg6dqYfR+P6gtP\neJuqMoUkXpKXEQ4Otf062WAZG8TQYPvIlqrHqfGttG42wa313I6TNyf1eCS5lKWC\nJ+PrjZbf6nbpxsTezczTu/c3EaV3p8cY8wVk713jFftS2mLW/JdqjK8KLXN+67kp\nlvZqdtUYeigGAYiHzetoZla0hWA6AVdXACXfdm+7BePsvL5Pxh0opocFm4cao/Ul\ng9P1Mv6HFIc0IsxVRCqq\n=/I1h\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 55d0e96ead3c64d48f71661b81d50322111ed93c\nparent 99c9be1d30ea78fad24d9eca8daa3526592a77b5\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1780504570 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780504570 +0200\n\nfeat: guard git enrichment (#26175)\n\nSkip turn git metadata enrichment when a turn has remote or multiple\nexecutors